export const entries = [{"id":"ab / a","latin":"ab / a","headword":"ab / a","letter":"a","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"from; away from (+ abl.); by (agent)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"abdere","latin":"abdere","headword":"abdere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to hide; conceal","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi cum eum somnus oppressisset, pāstor quīdam nōmine Cācus, ferōx viribus, bovēs pulcherrimōs ē grege rapere et praedam in spēluncam suam abdere voluit.","reading":"SACRA HERCULIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"abest","latin":"abest","headword":"abest","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is absent; is away","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus nōn adest, sed abest.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Iūlium vocāte, ancillae!\" Syra: \"Sed dominus in oppidō est.\" Aemilia: \"Ō, iam rūrsus abest Iūlius!\" Dēlia: \"Age!","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"ablativus","latin":"ablātīvus","headword":"ablātīvus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ablative","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Cāsus nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Sex.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Nōminātīvus, genetīvus, dativus, accūsātīvus, vocātīvus, ablātīvus.","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"aborigines","latin":"Aborīginēs, -um","headword":"Aborīginēs","letter":"a","pos":"noun m. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"the first inhabitants of Italy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aborīginēs Italiae incolae prīmī fuērunt, quōrum rēx Sāturnus tantā iūstitiā fuisse dīcitur ut neque servīret quisquam sub illō neque quidquam suum proprium habēret, sed omnia commūnia omnibus essent.","reading":"ABORĪGINĒS ET RĒGĒS LATIĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"abrogare","latin":"abrogāre","headword":"abrogāre","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to repeal; take away (by vote)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīs ātrociōribusque — crēdō — aliīs memorātīs, incēnsam multitūdinem perpulit ut imperium rēgī abrogāret exsulēsque esse iubēret L.","reading":"RĒGĒS EXĀCTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"accendere","latin":"accendere","headword":"accendere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to light; kindle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lucernas accendite, servi!\"","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"accidit","latin":"accidit","headword":"accidit","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"happens","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic Quīntus, quī exitum tabulae studiōsē exspectat, interrogat: \"Quid tum accidit?\"","reading":"ĪCARVS IN MARE CADIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"accipit","latin":"accipit","headword":"accipit","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"receives; gets","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fēminae quārum virī magnam pecūniam habent multa ōrnāmenta ā virīs suīs accipiunt.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"Pāstor canī suō cibum dat: canis ā pāstōre cibum accipit.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"accumbere","latin":"accumbere","headword":"accumbere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to recline (at table)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quot convīvae in singulīs lectīs accumbunt?","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"accusat","latin":"accūsat","headword":"accūsat","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"accuses; blames","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus Dāvum accūsat: 'Pecūnia tua in sacculō Dāvī est.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"accusativus","latin":"accūsātīvus","headword":"accūsātīvus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"accusative","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Cāsus nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Sex.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Nōminātīvus, genetīvus, dativus, accūsātīvus, vocātīvus, ablātīvus.","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"acerbus","latin":"acerbus","headword":"acerbus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"bitter; sharp","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At Paulā vīnum gustāns 'Hoc vīnum' inquit 'nimis acerbum est: os mihi contrahitur.","reading":"CĒNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"achaicus","latin":"Achāicus, -a, -um","headword":"Achāicus","letter":"a","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"Achaean; of the Achaean League","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lēgātī Rōmānī ab Achaeīs pulsī sunt Corinthī, missī ut eās cīvitātēs quae sub dīcione Philippī fuerant ab Achāicō conciliō sēcernerent.","reading":"BELLVM ACHAEVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"acies","latin":"aciēs, -ēī","headword":"aciēs","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"battle-line","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Exercitus ita īnstrūctus aciēs appellātur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"latin":"Rōmānus clāmōre undique ortō sē circumventum esse sēnsit, et ante in frontem lateraque pugnārī coeptum est quam satis īnstruerētur aciēs aut expedīrī arma stringīque gladiī possent.","reading":"LACVS TRĀSŪMENNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"acta","latin":"ācta, -ōrum","headword":"ācta","letter":"a","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"deeds; records","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Atque ego sciō, Quirītēs, quī postquam cōnsulēs factī sunt, et ācta maiōrum et Graecōrum mīlitāria praecepta legere coepērunt.","reading":"METELLVS ET MARIVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"activus","latin":"āctīvus","headword":"āctīvus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"active","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ad","latin":"ad","headword":"ad","letter":"a","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"to; towards","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ab oppidō Tusculō ad vīllam Iūliī nōn longa via est.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"adest","latin":"adest","headword":"adest","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is present; is here","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus nōn adest, sed abest.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"adhuc","latin":"adhūc","headword":"adhūc","letter":"a","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"still; up to now","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus adhūc dormit.","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"administer","latin":"administer, -trī","headword":"administer","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"assistant; accomplice","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi cum multa dē administrandō imperiō dissererent, Iugurtha inter aliās rēs iacit 'oportere quīnquenniī cōnsulta et dēcrēta omnia rescindī, nam per eōs annōs Micipsam parum animō valuisse.' Tum 'idem' Hiempsal 'placēre sibi' respondit, 'nam ipsum illum tribus proximīs annīs adoptātiōne in rēgnum pervēnisse!' Quod verbum in pectus Iugurthae altius quam quisquam rātus erat dēscendit.","reading":"MORS HIEMPSALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"admittere","latin":"admittere","headword":"admittere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to let in; admit","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī quis vīllam intrāre vult, iānuam pulsat et extrā iānuam exspectat, dum iānitor forēs aperit eumque in vīllam admittit.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"adoptatio","latin":"adoptātiō, -ōnis","headword":"adoptātiō","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"adoption","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Igitur rēx, ubi ea quae fāma accēperat ex litterīs imperātōris ita esse cognōvit, cum virtūte tum grātiā virī permōtus, flēxit animum suum et Iugurtham beneficiīs vincere aggressus est, statimque eum adoptāvit et testāmentō pariter cum fīliīs hērēdem īnstituit.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"adstare","latin":"adstāre","headword":"adstāre","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to stand by (with dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum omnēs hīs malīs perturbārentur, dī Penātēs, quōs Aenēās sēcum Trōiā extulerat, noctū in somnīs eī vīsī sunt ante lectum adstāre in līmine iānuae atque hīs dictīs cōnsōlārī: \"Nōs quī tē, Dardaniā incēnsā, per mare tumidum secūtī sumus, nōs īdem posterōs tuōs in caelum tollēmus imperiumque urbī eōrum dabimus.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"adulescens","latin":"adulēscēns","headword":"adulēscēns","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"young man","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius adulēscēns vīgintī duōrum annōrum erat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"adulescentia","latin":"adulēscentia, -ae","headword":"adulēscentia","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"youth; young manhood","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quibus rēbus Micipsa tametsī initiō laetus fuerat exīstimāns virtūtem Iugurthae rēgnō suō glōriae fore, tamen, postquam hominem adulēscentem — exāctā suā aetāte et parvīs līberīs — magis magisque crēscere intellegit, vehementer eō negōtiō permōtus multa cum animō suō volvēbat.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"adulter","latin":"adulter, -erī","headword":"adulter","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"adulterer","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ubi obstinātam vidēbat neque mortis quidem metū inclīnārī, addit ad metum dēdecus: cum mortuā iugulātum servum nūdum positūrum sē esse, ut in sordidō adulteriō necāta dīcerētur!","reading":"LŪCRĒTIA VIOLĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"adulterinus","latin":"adulterīnus, -a, -um","headword":"adulterīnus","letter":"a","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"false; counterfeit","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quem ille casū ministrum oblātum prōmissīs onerat impellitque utī tamquam suam vīsēns domum eat, portārum clāvēs adulterīnās paret — nam vērae ad Hiempsalem referēbantur; 'cēterum, ubi rēs postulāret, sē ipsum cum magnā manū ventūrum.'","reading":"MORS HIEMPSALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"adultus","latin":"adultus, -a, -um","headword":"adultus","letter":"a","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"grown up; mature","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"advena","latin":"advena, -ae","headword":"advena","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"newcomer; stranger","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēgīna, ut prīmum ex altā turrī vīdit classem plēnīs vēlīs prōcēdere, ter quaterque pulchrum pectus manū percutiēns et comās scindēns 'Prō, Iuppiter!' ait 'Abībit advena, et rēgnō nostrō illūserit?","reading":"ROGUS DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"advenit","latin":"advenit","headword":"advenit","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"arrives; comes to","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce Iūlius ad vīllam advenit.","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"latin":"Sextus, quī ante Mārcum et Titum ad lūdum advēnit, prīmus lūdum intrat.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"adventus","latin":"adventus, -ūs","headword":"adventus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"arrival","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Turnus, rēx Rutulōrum, cui Lāvīnia ante adventum Aenēae sponsa fuerat, moleste patiēns advenam sibi praelātum esse, simul Aenēae Latīnōque bellum intulerat.","reading":"TRŌIĀNĪ ET LATĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"adverbium","latin":"adverbium","headword":"adverbium","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"adverb","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"adversarius","latin":"adversārius, -ī","headword":"adversārius","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"opponent; enemy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Longō apud Trebiam adversus eum vēnit.","reading":"BELLA IN ĪTALIĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"adversus","latin":"adversus","headword":"adversus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"adverse; hostile","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Caelum nūbilum suspiciēns gubernātor optat ut ventus in adversum vertātur.","reading":"IN MARĪ TVSCŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"aedes","latin":"aedēs, -is","headword":"aedēs","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"temple; (pl.) house","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ex aedibus sacrīs forī Rōmānī minima quidem, sed veterrima est aedēs Iānī, quae ad īnfimum Argīlētum sita est.","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"aedificare","latin":"aedificāre","headword":"aedificāre","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to build","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Posteā Rōmānī nōbilissimī in Palātiō habitāvērunt, ibīque post Iūliī Caesaris aetātem Augustus, Tiberius, Caligula aliīque prīncipēs Rōmānī domōs magnificās sibi aedificāvērunt.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"aedilicius","latin":"aedīlicius, -a, -um","headword":"aedīlicius","letter":"a","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"of aedile rank","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cōnsūmpsērunt ultrā centum quīnquāgintā mīlia hominum, virōs cōnsulārēs quattuor et vīgintī, praetōriōs septem, aedīliciōs sexāgintā, senātōrēs ferē ducentōs.","reading":"BELLVM CĪVĪLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"aedilitas","latin":"aedīlitās, -ātis","headword":"aedīlitās","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"aedileship","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cōnsūmpsērunt ultrā centum quīnquāgintā mīlia hominum, virōs cōnsulārēs quattuor et vīgintī, praetōriōs septem, aedīliciōs sexāgintā, senātōrēs ferē ducentōs.","reading":"BELLVM CĪVĪLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"aeger","latin":"aeger","headword":"aeger","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"sick; ill","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homō quī ventrem malum habet cibum sūmere nōn potest, neque is sānus, sed aeger est.","reading":"SĀNVS ET AEGER","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Quīntus dīcit sē aegrum esse.' Diodōrus: 'Sī aeger est, in lūdum īre nōn potest.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"aegrotat","latin":"aegrōtat","headword":"aegrōtat","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is ill; is sick","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Medicus interrogat: \"Quis aegrōtat?\" Iūlius: \"Meus Quīntus fīlius aegrōtat; ambulāre nōn potest.\" Medicus: \"Cūr ambulāre nōn potest?\" Iūlius: \"Quia pēs eius aeger est.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"aegrotus","latin":"aegrōtus","headword":"aegrōtus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"sick; ill","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puer aegrōtus iterum iterumque super lectum sē convertit nec dormīre potest, sīve in latere dextrō cubat sīve in latere sinistrō.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"aeneus","latin":"aēneus, -a, -um","headword":"aēneus","letter":"a","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"of bronze","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"aequabilitas","latin":"aequābilitās, -ātis","headword":"aequābilitās","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"evenness; equality","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed et in rēgnīs nimis expertēs sunt cēterī commūnis iūris et cōnsiliī; et in optimātium dominātū vix particeps lībertātis potest esse multitūdō, cum omnī cōnsiliō commūnī ac potestāte careat; et cum omnia per populum geruntur, quamvīs iūstum atque moderātum, tamen ipsa aequābilitās est inīqua, cum habet nūllōs gradūs dignitātis...'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"aequinoctium","latin":"aequinoctium","headword":"aequinoctium","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"equinox","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ante diem octāvum kalendās Aprīlēs (id est diē octāvō ante kalendās Aprīlēs) nox atque diēs aequī sunt; is diēs \"aequinoctium\" dīcitur.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"aequor","latin":"aequor, -oris","headword":"aequor","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sea; level surface","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trōiānī igitur, paucīs relictīs, hanc quoque sēdem dēseruērunt et rūrsus vastum aequor classe percurrēbant.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"aerarium","latin":"aerārium, -ī","headword":"aerārium","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"treasury","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aedēs Sāturnī est aerārium populī Rōmānī, id est locus ubi pecūnia pūblica dēpōnitur ac servātur.","reading":"AEDĒS FORĪ RŌMĀNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"aesculetum","latin":"aesculētum, -ī","headword":"aesculētum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"oak forest","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"quāle portentum neque mīlitāris / Daunias lātīs alit aesculētīs / nec Iubae tellūs generat, leōnum / ārida nūtrīx.","reading":"INTEGER VĪTAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"aestas","latin":"aestās","headword":"aestās","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"summer","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tempora annī sunt quattuor: aestās et hiems, vēr et autumnus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"aestimat","latin":"aestimat","headword":"aestimat","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"values; reckons","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Nāvigāre necesse est\" aiunt, et mercātōrēs, quī ipsī mare adīre nōn audent, haec adiciunt: \"Vīvere est necesse!\" Mercātōrēs mercēs suās magnī aestimant, vītam nautārum parvī aestimant.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"aevum","latin":"aevum, -ī","headword":"aevum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"age; everlasting time","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"africus","latin":"Africus, -ī","headword":"Africus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"south-west wind","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aeolus, ubi haec audīvit, cavum montem hastā impellit, ac ventī velut agmine factō ex antrō ruunt: Eurus Notusque et Africus terrās mariaque turbant et vastōs fluctūs ad lītora volvunt.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"age! / agite!","latin":"age! / agite!","headword":"age! / agite!","letter":"a","pos":"interjection","posGroup":"interjection","english":"come! come on!","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ager","latin":"ager","headword":"ager","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"field","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ager quī multum frūmentī aliāsve frūgēs ferre potest, fertilis esse dīcitur.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"agmen","latin":"agmen","headword":"agmen","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"marching column","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Signum legiōnis est aquilā argenteā, quae in itinere ante agmen fertur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"agnoscere","latin":"agnōscere","headword":"agnōscere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to recognise","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dum haec nārrat itemque dē cāsū Aenēae et Ascanīī puerī quaerit, ex urbe vēnit Helēnus cum multīs comitibus; quī cīvēs suōs laetus āgnōscit eōsque in urbem ad convīvium magnificum invītat.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"agricola","latin":"agricola","headword":"agricola","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"farmer","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī agrōs arant ac frūmentum serunt et metunt, agricolae appellantur.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"ala","latin":"āla","headword":"āla","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wing","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"alacer","latin":"alacer, -cris, -cre","headword":"alacer","letter":"a","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"eager; brisk","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"albus","latin":"albus","headword":"albus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"white","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"alere","latin":"alere","headword":"alere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"feed; nourish","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī māter īnfantem suum ipsa alere nōn potest sīve vult, īnfāns ab aliā muliere alitur, quae eī in locō mātris est.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"ales","latin":"āles, -itis","headword":"āles","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bird","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"alienus","latin":"aliēnus","headword":"aliēnus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"another's; foreign; another’s; belonging to someone else","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mulier quae aliēnum īnfantem alit nūtrīx appellātur.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"altaria","latin":"altāria, -ium","headword":"altāria","letter":"a","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"high altar","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Circum stant ārae, et sacerdōs crīnibus passīs deōs Īnferōs invocat, dum ipsa Dīdō moritūra iuxtā altāria precātur.","reading":"ROGUS DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"alter","latin":"alter","headword":"alter","letter":"a","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"the one; the other","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Alter puer dormit, alter vigilat.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"altus","latin":"altus","headword":"altus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"high; deep","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sōl altus in caelō est nec nūbibus operītur.'","reading":"QVĪNTVS INTERROGAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"amat","latin":"amat","headword":"amat","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"loves","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius Aemiliam amat, quia ea pulchra et bona fēmina est.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Aemilia laeta nōn est, quia Iūlius abest; nam Aemilia virum suum amat.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"ambulare","latin":"ambulāre","headword":"ambulāre","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"walk; to walk","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Initiō pater eum sustinēbit ac manū dūcet; mox vērō īnfāns sōlus ambulāre incipiet neque ā parentibus sustinēbitur neque manū dūcētur.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"latin":"In Iudaeā Iēsus nōn sōlum faciēbat ut caecī vidērent, surdī audīrent, mūtī loquerentur, vērum etiam verbīs efficiēbat ut mortuī surgerent et ambulārent.","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA IN NĀVĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"ambulat","latin":"ambulat","headword":"ambulat","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"walks","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius nōn in viā ambulat, servī eum portant.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Pater fīliōs salūtat: 'Salvēte, fīliī!' et ā fīliīs salūtātur: 'Salvē, pater!' Iūlius ambulat ad ōstium, quod ab ōstiāriō aperītur.","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"amica","latin":"amīca","headword":"amīca","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"girlfriend; (female) friend","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Est Mēdus, quī cum Lȳdiā, amīcā suā, ambulat.","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"Inter eōs hominēs quī nāvēs cōnscendunt est Mēdus, quī ex Italiā proficīscitur cum amīcā suā Lȳdia.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"amicitia","latin":"amīcitia","headword":"amīcitia","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"friendship","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam etsī rāra est vēra amīcitia ac fidēs, nōn omnēs amīcī sunt falsī seu īnfīdī.","reading":"DĒ VĒRĪS AMĪCĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"amictus","latin":"amictus, -ūs","headword":"amictus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cloak; mantle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Erat illī amictus ex Tyriā purpurā et ēnsis gemmīs fulgēns, mūnera Dīdōnis.","reading":"NŪNTIUS DEŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"amicus","latin":"amīcus","headword":"amīcus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"friend","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus amīcus Mēdī nōn est, nam servus bonus et servus malus nōn amīcī, sed inimīcī sunt.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"amor","latin":"amor","headword":"amor","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"love","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Venus enim mala uxor est, quae aliōs deōs amat praeter coniugem suum Vulcānum.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"amphitheatrum","latin":"amphitheātrum, -ī","headword":"amphitheātrum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"amphitheatre","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hōrum omnium operum nihil paene restat, nam post mortem Nerōnis imperātor Flāvius Vespasiānus in locō stagnī clārissimum amphitheātrum exstrūxit, quod ā nōmine prīncipis amphitheātrum Flāvium appellātur; atque Titus et Trāiānus in ipsō locō domūs aureae thermās suās collocāvērunt.","reading":"VRBIS INCENDIVM ET DOMVS AVREA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"amplecti","latin":"amplectī","headword":"amplectī","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to embrace; cling to","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iam bis corpus eius medium amplectuntur, bis collō longa corpora sua circumdant.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"amplitudo","latin":"amplitūdō, -inis","headword":"amplitūdō","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"greatness; distinction","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fuit enim profectō quibusdam summīs virīs quaedam ad amplitūdinem et ad glōriam et ad rēs magnās bene gerendās dīvīnitus adiūncta fortūna.","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"ancile","latin":"ancīle, -is","headword":"ancīle","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sacred shield of Mars","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ancilla","latin":"ancilla","headword":"ancilla","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"maidservant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēlia nōn est fīlia Aemiliae, Dēlia ancilla Aemiliae est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"anfractus","latin":"anfractus, -ūs","headword":"anfractus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"winding; circuit","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"anguis","latin":"anguis, -is","headword":"anguis","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"snake; serpent","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"angustiae","latin":"angustiae, -ārum","headword":"angustiae","letter":"a","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"narrow pass; defile","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic, clausus locōrum angustiīs, noctū sine ūllō dētrīmentō exercitūs sē expedīvit, Fabiōque, callidissimō imperātōrī, dedit verba.","reading":"BELLA IN ĪTALIĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"anima","latin":"anima","headword":"anima","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"breath; spirit; soul","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum homō spīrat, anima in pulmōnēs intrat et rūrsus ex pulmōnibus exit.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"annus","latin":"annus","headword":"annus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"year","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Annus in duodecim mēnsēs dīviditur, quibus haec sunt nōmina: Iānuārius, mēnsis prīmus; Februārius, secundus; Mārtius, tertius; Aprīlis, quārtus; Maius, quīntus; Iūnius, sextus; Iūlius, septimus; Augustus, octāvus; September, nōnus; Octōber, decimus; November, ūndecimus; December, mēnsis duodecimus ac postrēmus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"ante","latin":"ante","headword":"ante","letter":"a","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"before; in front of","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ursus est ante Iūlium, Dāvus post eum est.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"antiquitas","latin":"antīquitās, -ātis","headword":"antīquitās","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"antiquity; the past","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pompēius quī nōn modo eōrum hominum quī nunc sunt glōriam, sed etiam antīquitātis memoriam virtūte superārit, quae rēs est quae cuiusquam animum in hāc causā dubium facere possit?","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"antiquus","latin":"antīquus","headword":"antīquus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"old; ancient","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce duo librī Latīnī: liber antīquus et liber novus.","reading":"LIBER TVVS LATĪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"antrum","latin":"antrum, -ī","headword":"antrum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cave; cavern","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nec vērō tālia passus est Ulixēs, nam cum Polyphēmus carne vīnōque implētus per antrum iacēret, nōs longam hastam acūtam in oculō eius, quem sōlum in mediā fronte habēbat, dēfīximus: ita tandem sociōs necātōs ultī sumus. — Sed fugite, ō miserī, fugite, nē quis necem ulcīscātur, ac fūnēs nāvium incīdite!","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"anulus","latin":"ānulus","headword":"ānulus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ring","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ānulus cum gemmā ōrnāmentum pulchrum est.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"Ānulus aureus multō pulchrior est quam ānulus ferreus.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"anus","latin":"anus","headword":"anus","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"old woman","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sequuntur epigrammata quibus deridentur feminae, praecipue anus, ut Laecania et Paula:","reading":"DĒ MĀRTIĀLĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"aperire","latin":"aperīre","headword":"aperīre","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to open","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Servus cuius officium est forēs aperīre et claudere ac vīllam dominī cūstōdīre, ōstiārius vel iānitor appellātur.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"aperit","latin":"aperit","headword":"aperit","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"opens","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra ōstium aperit et in cubiculum intrat, neque ōstium post sē claudit.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"latin":"Quīntus quiētus super lectum iacet nec oculōs aperit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"apertus","latin":"apertus","headword":"apertus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"open","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"appellare","latin":"appellāre","headword":"appellāre","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"call; address by name","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mulier quae aliēnum īnfantem alit nūtrīx appellātur.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"appellativus","latin":"appellātīvus","headword":"appellātīvus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"common (of a noun)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Nōmen quid est?' Discipulus: 'Pars ōrātiōnis cum cāsū, corpus aut rem propriē significāns; aut enim ūnīus nōmen est et proprium dīcitur, aut multōrum et appellātīvum.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"apponere","latin":"appōnere","headword":"appōnere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to serve; set before","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"apud","latin":"apud","headword":"apud","letter":"a","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"at the house of; with","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius sōlus nōn est, nam quattuor servī apud eum sunt.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"aqua","latin":"aqua","headword":"aqua","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"water","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In eō est aqua.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Pāstor ovī nigrae et ovibus albīs aquam et cibum dat.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"aquae ductus","latin":"aquae ductus, -ūs","headword":"aquae ductus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"aqueduct","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aqua, cuius magna cōpia ā lavantibus cōnsūmitur, ē montibus in thermās dēdūcitur per longōs aquae ductūs, quōrum veterrimus, aqua Appia, in urbem inducta est ab Appiō Claudiō Caecō, quī etiam viam Appiam ā portā Capēnā ad urbem Capuam mūniendam cūrāvit.","reading":"VRBS MARMOREA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"aquila","latin":"aquila","headword":"aquila","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"eagle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aquila est magna avis fera, quae parvās avēs capit et ēdit.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Signum legiōnis est aquilā argenteā, quae in itinere ante agmen fertur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"aquilo","latin":"Aquilō, -ōnis","headword":"Aquilō","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"north wind","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Namque tibi nūntiō sociōs tuōs salvōs esse classemque relātam et in tūtum locum āctam versīs Aquilōnibus.","reading":"VENUS GENETRĪX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"arat","latin":"arat","headword":"arat","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"ploughs","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Agricola arāns post arātrum ambulat.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"aratrum","latin":"arātrum","headword":"arātrum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"plough","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Agricola arāns post arātrum ambulat.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"arbiter","latin":"arbiter, -trī","headword":"arbiter","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"judge; arbitrator","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"arbitrari","latin":"arbitrārī","headword":"arbitrārī","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to think; suppose","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tabellārius enim canem ā iānitōre solūtum esse arbitrātur.","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"arbitrium","latin":"arbitrium, -ī","headword":"arbitrium","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"will; judgement","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quō magis cupiēbat eum Hannibal opprimī: quem sī remōvisset, faciliora sibi cētera fore arbitrabātur.","reading":"APVD PRŪSIAM ET MORS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"arbor","latin":"arbor","headword":"arbor","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tree","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In campō est collis. (Collis est mōns parvus.) In colle arbor est.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Vērē campī nova herba operiuntur, arborēs novīs foliīs ōrnantur, avēs, quae hieme tacent, rūrsus canere incipiunt.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"arcessit","latin":"arcessit","headword":"arcessit","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sends for; summons","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius, quī cum Sȳrō servō in ātriō est, imperat: \"I ad oppidum, Syre, atque medicum arcesse!\" Medicus Tusculī habitat.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"arcus","latin":"arcus","headword":"arcus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In exercitibus Rōmānīs etiam Hispānī et Gallī multī mīlitant, quī et alia arma et arcūs sagittāsque ferunt.'","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"area","latin":"ārea, -ae","headword":"ārea","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"open space; arena","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ad spectāculum cōnsēderant, et praecō cum tubicine, ut mōs est, in mediam āream prōcessit et tubā silentiō factō ita prōnūntiat: 'Senātus Rōmānus et T.","reading":"ISTHMIA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"argentum","latin":"argentum","headword":"argentum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"silver","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rosae et līlia et alia multa flōrum genera in mēnsā sparsa sunt inter vāsa et pōcula argentea; nec enim quidquam nisi argentum mēnsam decet virī nōbilis. (Argentum quidem minōris pretiī est quam aurum, nec vērō quisquam ex vāsīs aureīs cēnat nisi hominēs dīvitissimī atque glōriōsī, ut rēgēs Orientīs.)","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"arma","latin":"arma","headword":"arma","letter":"a","pos":"noun (n. pl.); noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"weapons; arms","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Scūtum et gladius et pīlum sunt arma mīlitis Rōmānī.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Auxilia sunt peditēs equitēsque ex prōvinciīs, quī arma leviōra, sīcut arcus sagittāsque, ferunt.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"armentum","latin":"armentum, -ī","headword":"armentum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"herd of cattle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hercules in ea loca, Geryone monstrō interemptō, bovēs mīrā speciē ēgisse nārrātur ac prope Tiberim fluvium, quem prae sē armentum agēns nandō trānsierat, fessus viā in herbā recubuisse.","reading":"SACRA HERCULIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"armilla","latin":"armilla, -ae","headword":"armilla","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bracelet; armlet","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Additur fābula Tarpēiam mercēdem ab Sabīnīs postulāvisse \"id quod in sinistrīs manibus habērent\" (nam Sabīnī aureās armillās magnī ponderis bracchiō laevō gemmōsque ānulōs habēbant); ergō Sabīnōs prō aureīs dōnīs scūta in eam coniēcisse.","reading":"BELLVM SABINVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"arvum","latin":"arvum, -ī","headword":"arvum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"field; ploughland","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"arx","latin":"arx, arcis","headword":"arx","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"citadel; height","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ea Capitōliī pars quae spectat ad septentriōnēs, ardua atque mūrīs firmīs mūnīta, arx dīcitur.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"as","latin":"as (assis)","headword":"as","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"an as (a small Roman coin)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister, quī verba Mārcī nōn audit, ex sacculō suō duōs nummōs prōmit, assem et dēnārium, et 'Ecce' inquit nummōs ostendēns, 'as et dēnārius.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"ascendit","latin":"ascendit","headword":"ascendit","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"climbs; goes up","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ascende in arborem, Quīnte!' Quīntus in arborem ascendit; iam is suprā Mārcum in arbore est.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"asciscere","latin":"ascīscere","headword":"ascīscere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to admit; adopt","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"aspicit","latin":"aspicit","headword":"aspicit","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"looks at; gazes at","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quae nūllam aut parvam pecūniam habent ōrnāmenta aspiciunt tantum, nōn emunt.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"asserere","latin":"asserere","headword":"asserere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to claim; assert","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūliō Caesare et Marciō Philippō cōnsulibus sescentēsimō quīnquāgēsimō nōnō annō ab urbe conditā, cum prope alia omnia bella cessārent, in Ītaliā gravissimum bellum Picentēs, Marsī Paelīgnīque mōvērunt, quī, cum annīs numerōsīs iam populō Rōmānō oboedīrent, tum lībertātem sibi aequam asserere coepērunt.","reading":"BELLVM SOCIĀLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"astrologus","latin":"astrologus, -ī","headword":"astrologus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"astronomer; student of the stars","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Neque multō posteā Eudoxus astrologus in terrā Graeciā nōbilitātus est, Lacedaemoniīque ab Athēniēnsibus apud Corinthum superātī duce Phormiōne; et M.","reading":"SŌCRATĒS ET CAMILLUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"asylum","latin":"asȳlum, -ī","headword":"asȳlum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"place of refuge; sanctuary","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deinde, nē vāna urbis magnitūdō esset, multitūdinem fīnitimōrum in urbem recēpit, cum sub monte Capitōlīnō inter duōs lūcōs asȳlum aperuisset.","reading":"ROMVLVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"ater","latin":"āter","headword":"āter","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"dark; black","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"atrium","latin":"ātrium","headword":"ātrium","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"atrium; hall; entrance hall; entrance-hall","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In vīllā Iūliī magnum ātrium est cum impluviō.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Aemilia cum Dēliā ē peristȳlō in ātrium intrat, laeta; ad Iūlium adit eumque salūtat.","reading":"ROSA IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"attonitus","latin":"attonitus, -a, -um","headword":"attonitus","letter":"a","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"thunderstruck; astonished","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aenēās vērō obmūtuit amēns, tantō imperiō deōrum attonitus.","reading":"NŪNTIUS DEŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"auctor","latin":"auctor, -ōris","headword":"auctor","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"founder; originator","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Incertum est — quis enim rem tam veterem prō certō affirmet? — hīcine fuerit Lāvīniae fīlius an fīlius ille māior, Creūsā mātre nātus, Ascanius sīve Iūlus appellātus, quem gēns Iūlia auctōrem nōminis suī esse dīcit.","reading":"ALBA CONDITA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"auctoritas","latin":"auctōritās, -ātis","headword":"auctōritās","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"authority; influence","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Custōdibus armātīs corpus saepsit; neque enim ad iūs regnī quicquam praeter vim habēbat, ut quī neque populī iussū neque auctōribus patribus regnāret.","reading":"L. IŪNIUS BRŪTUS, LĪBERĀTOR POPULĪ RŌMĀNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"audax","latin":"audāx","headword":"audāx","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"bold; daring","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quoniam igitur aliae viae clausae erant, ille vir audāx per āera effugere cōnstituit.\"","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"audit","latin":"audit","headword":"audit","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"hears; listens to","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius Quīntum nōn audit neque venit.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Mēdus Dāvum vocat: 'Dāve!' sed Dāvus Mēdum nōn audit neque venit.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"auferre","latin":"auferre","headword":"auferre","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to carry off; steal","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"aufugere","latin":"aufugere","headword":"aufugere","letter":"a","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to run away; escape","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"augur","latin":"augur, -uris","headword":"augur","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"augur; reader of bird-signs","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inde ab augure dēductus in arcem, in lapide ad merīdiem versus cōnsēdit.","reading":"NVMA POMPILIVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"augurium","latin":"augurium, -ī","headword":"augurium","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"omen; augury","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Accēpisse id augurium laeta dīcitur Tanaquil, mulier perīta caelestium prōdigiōrum, ut plērīque Etrūscī.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"aula","latin":"aula, -ae","headword":"aula","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"palace; court","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī saltem īnfantem dē tē habērem, sī quī parvulus Aenēās in aulā meā lūderet quī memoriam tuī referret, nōn omnīnō dēserta vidērer…'","reading":"NŪNTIUS DEŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"aureus","latin":"aureus","headword":"aureus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"golden","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce ānulus aureus gemmātus, quem amīcus meus prope centum nummīs emit mihi.\" Lȳdia manum extendēns digitum aureō ōrnātum gubernātōrī ostendit.","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"auriga","latin":"aurīga","headword":"aurīga","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"charioteer","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed ex novissimis circensibus maestus abii, cum ille auriga cui plerique spectatores favebant ex curru lapsus equis procurrentibus occisus esset.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"auris","latin":"auris","headword":"auris","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ear","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"aurora","latin":"aurōra, -ae","headword":"aurōra","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dawn","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iam aurōra ab oriente rubēbat, cum procul humilēs collēs appāruērunt.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"aurum","latin":"aurum","headword":"aurum","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gold","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aurum est magnī pretiī sīcut gemmae.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"latin":"Bacchus deus, quī ob quoddam beneficium rēgī bene volēbat, \"Dabō tibi,\" inquit, \"quidquid optāverīs.\" Midās: \"Ergō dā mihi potestātem quidquid tetigerō in aurum mūtandī.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"auspicium","latin":"auspicium, -ī","headword":"auspicium","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bird-omen; auspices; omen (from birds)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ergō inter frātrēs convēnit ut Rōmulus in Palātiō, Remus in Aventīnō auspicārētur.","reading":"RŌMA CONDITA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"},{"latin":"Hostīliō Mancīnō cōnsule sacrificante pullī ex caveā ēvolāvērunt; cōnscendentī deinde nāvem, ut in Hispāniam proficīscerētur, accidit vōx: 'Manē, Mancīne!' Quae auspicia trīstia fuisse ēventū probātum est: victus enim ā Numantīnīs et castrīs exūtus, cum spēs nūlla servandī exercitūs esset, pācem cum hīs fēcit ignōminiōsam, quam ratam esse senātus vetuit.","reading":"HISPĀNIA PĀCĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"auster","latin":"Auster, -trī","headword":"Auster","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"south wind","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trōiā profugī Hesperiam sīve Italiam, terram antīquam, petēbāmus, cum turbidus Auster nōs disiēcit atque paucōs nostrum hīc ad vestrās ōrās compulit.","reading":"DĪDŌ RĒGĪNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"aut","latin":"aut","headword":"aut","letter":"a","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"or","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quae nūllam aut parvam pecūniam habent ōrnāmenta aspiciunt tantum, nōn emunt.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"autem","latin":"autem","headword":"autem","letter":"a","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"however; but","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus autem bonus servus est, neque is Mēdum amat.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"autumnus","latin":"autumnus","headword":"autumnus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"autumn","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tempora annī sunt quattuor: aestās et hiems, vēr et autumnus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"auxilium","latin":"auxilium","headword":"auxilium","letter":"a","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"help; aid; (pl.) auxiliary troops","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sine mē tibi auxilium ferre!'","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"latin":"Praetereā magna auxilia exercituī adiunguntur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"avaritia","latin":"avāritia, -ae","headword":"avāritia","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"greed; avarice","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vīdit autem vir omnium callidissimus in magnō sē fore perīculō, nisi quid prōvīdisset, propter avāritiam Crētēnsium: magnam enim sēcum pecūniam portābat, dē quā sciēbat exīsse fāmam.","reading":"APVD ANTIOCHVM ET IN CRĒTĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"avarus","latin":"avārus","headword":"avārus","letter":"a","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"greedy; miserly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Orontēs: 'Midās est nōmen rēgis, dē quō haec tabulā nārrat: in quādam urbe Asiae ōlim vīvēbat rēx quīdam avārus, nōmine Midās, quī nihil magis optābat dīvitiās...' Iūlius, quī tabulam audīre nōn vult, Orontem interpellat: 'Nōn Midās,' inquit, 'sed Mēdus est nōmen servī meī, quī heri...' Orontēs vērō, minimē turbātus, nārrāre pergit:","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"avidus","latin":"avidus, -a, -um","headword":"avidus","letter":"a","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"greedy; eager","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At contrā paucī, quibus bonum et aequum dīvitiīs cārius erat, subveniendum Adherbalī et Hiempsalis mortem sevērē vindicandam cēnsēbant; sed ex omnibus maximē Aemilius Scaurus, homō nōbilis, impiger, factiōsus, avidus potentiae, honōris, dīvitiārum, cēterum vitia sua callidē occultāns.","reading":"ADHERBAL RŌMAM PROFĪCĪSCITUR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"avis","latin":"avis","headword":"avis","letter":"a","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bird","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aquila est magna avis fera, quae parvās avēs capit et ēdit.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Quis est tam liber quam avis quae trāns montēs, vallēs, flūmina, maria volāre potest?","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"avunculus","latin":"avunculus","headword":"avunculus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"uncle (mother's brother)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Frāter Aemiliae est avunculus līberōrum.","reading":"DĒ FAMILIĀ ET NŌMINIBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"avus","latin":"avus, -ī","headword":"avus","letter":"a","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"grandfather","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"baculum","latin":"baculum","headword":"baculum","letter":"b","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stick; staff","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius baculum suum in mēnsā pōnit.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Dominus servōs malōs baculō verberat; itaque servī malī dominum et baculum eius timent.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"balneum","latin":"balneum","headword":"balneum","letter":"b","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bath","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ex agrīs reversus Iūlius continuō balneum petit, atque aqua calida, tum frīgida lavātur.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"barba","latin":"barba, -ae","headword":"barba","letter":"b","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"beard","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sordidam barbam crīnēsque cruentōs gerēbat et vulnera illa quae plūrima circum mūrōs Trōiae accēperat.","reading":"SOMNIVM AENĒAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"barbarus","latin":"barbarus","headword":"barbarus","letter":"b","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"barbarian; foreign","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Germānī sunt hominēs barbarī quī Germāniam incolunt.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"basilica","latin":"basilica, -ae","headword":"basilica","letter":"b","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"basilica; public hall","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aedificia pūblica amplissima sunt duae basilicae, Aemilia et Iūlia.","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"basium","latin":"bāsium","headword":"bāsium","letter":"b","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"kiss","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"beatus","latin":"beātus","headword":"beātus","letter":"b","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"happy; blessed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"bellum","latin":"bellum, -ī","headword":"bellum","letter":"b","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"war","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Germānī hostēs Rōmānōrum sunt, ac bellum est inter Germānōs et Rōmānōs.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Hīs verbīs maximō gaudiō affectī sumus, nam post longum bellum omnēs pācem dēsīderāmus.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"bellus","latin":"bellus","headword":"bellus","letter":"b","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"pretty; fine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"belua","latin":"bēlua, -ae","headword":"bēlua","letter":"b","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wild beast","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quō in locō cum esset silvestris bēluae sustentātus ūberibus pastōrēsque eum sustulissent et in agrēstī cultū labōreque aluissent, perhibētur, ut adolēverit, et corporis vīribus et animī ferōcitāte tantum cēterīs praestitisse ut omnēs quī tum eōs agrōs ubi hodiē est haec urbs incolēbant aequō animō illī libenterque pārērent.","reading":"DĒ VETERE RĒ PŪBLICĀ RŌMĀNĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"beneficium","latin":"beneficium","headword":"beneficium","letter":"b","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"kindness; favour","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ergō omnēs mihi grātī sunt prō beneficiīs.\"","reading":"DĒ VĒRĪS AMĪCĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"bestia","latin":"bēstia","headword":"bēstia","letter":"b","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"beast; animal","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Equus et asinus, leō et lupus, canis et ovis bēstiae sunt.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"bibere","latin":"bibere","headword":"bibere","letter":"b","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to drink","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In convīviīs suīs sanguinem bibere solent, ut rūmor est.' Aemilia: 'Nōn omnēs vērī sunt rūmōrēs quī afferuntur super Chrīstiānīs.' Fabia: 'Nec omnēs īnfantēs expositī pereunt.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"bibit","latin":"bibit","headword":"bibit","letter":"b","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"drinks","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ovis nigra ovēs albās relinquit et rīvum petit; aquam bibit ē rīvō, et in silvam intrat!","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"biduum","latin":"bīduum, -ī","headword":"bīduum","letter":"b","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"two days","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"biennium","latin":"biennium, -ī","headword":"biennium","letter":"b","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"period of two years","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque cum essem biennium versātus in causīs et iam in forō celebrātum meum nōmen esset, Rōmā sum profectus.'","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"bona","latin":"bona, -ōrum","headword":"bona","letter":"b","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"goods; property","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"bonus","latin":"bonus","headword":"bonus","letter":"b","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"good","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus bonus servus est: pecūniam meam nōn habet.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Bonus es magister!' Magister laetus 'Vērum est quod dīcitis' inquit, 'ego bene recitō ac bonus sum magister, at vōs male recitātis ac malī discipulī estis!'","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ DORMIENTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"bos","latin":"bōs","headword":"bōs","letter":"b","pos":"noun (m./f.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"ox; cow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus: \"Bōs īrātus cornū mē pulsāvit!\"","reading":"MARCVS Ā PATRE INTERROGĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"bracchium","latin":"bracchium","headword":"bracchium","letter":"b","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"arm","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Corpus hūmānum quattuor membra habet: duo bracchia et duo crūra.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"brevi","latin":"brevī","headword":"brevī","letter":"b","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"soon; in a short time","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Brevī hūc redībō neque sine tē, Ariadna, in patriam revertar.","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"brevis","latin":"brevis","headword":"brevis","letter":"b","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"short","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūr tam brevis est gladius?'","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Februārius brevior est quam cēterī ūndecim mēnsēs: is mēnsis annī brevissimus est.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"breviter","latin":"breviter","headword":"breviter","letter":"b","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"briefly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister breviter respondet: 'Semel.'","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"cadit","latin":"cadit","headword":"cadit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"falls","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce rāmus cum puerō et nīdō et pullīs ad terram cadit!","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Hieme nōn sōlum imber, sed etiam nix dē caelō cadit.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"caducus","latin":"cadūcus, -a, -um","headword":"cadūcus","letter":"c","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"falling; perishable","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Infrā autem iam nihil est nisi mortāle et cadūcum — praeter animōs mūnere deōrum hominum generī datōs; supra Lūnam sunt aeterna omnia.","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"caedere","latin":"caedere","headword":"caedere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to cut down; kill","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"caedo","latin":"caedō","headword":"caedō","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to kill; cut down","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tanta ibi caedēs hostium facta est ut meminisse horream.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"caelites","latin":"caelitēs, -um","headword":"caelitēs","letter":"c","pos":"noun m. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"the gods of heaven","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ad quem ut vēnī, complexus mē senex collacrimāvit aliquantōque post suspexit ad caelum et 'Grātēs' inquit 'tibi agō, summe Sōl, vōbīsque, reliquī caelitēs, quod, ante quam ex hāc vītā migrō, cōnspiciō in meō rēgnō et hīs tēctīs P.","reading":"APUD MASINISSAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"caelum","latin":"caelum","headword":"caelum","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sky; heaven; heavens","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Caelum est suprā terram.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Aemilia ad fenestram it caelumque spectat.","reading":"QVĪNTVS INTERROGAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"caerimonia","latin":"caerimōnia, -ae","headword":"caerimōnia","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ceremony; rite","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Idemque Pompīlius et auspiciīs maiōribus inventīs ad prīstinum numerum duo augurēs addidit, et sacrīs ē prīncipum numerō pontificēs quīnque praefēcit, et animōs ardentēs cōnsuētūdine et cupiditāte bellandī religiōnum caerimōniīs mītigāvit, adiūnxītque praetereā flāminēs, Saliōs virginēsque Vestālēs omnēsque partēs religiōnis statuit sānctissimē.","reading":"DĒ VETERE RĒ PŪBLICĀ RŌMĀNĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"calamitas","latin":"calamitās, -ātis","headword":"calamitās","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"disaster; misfortune; defeat","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque cum continuae calamitātēs Rōmānīs displicērent, dēcrēvit senātus ut ā maritimīs proeliīs recēderētur et tantum sexāgintā nāvēs ad praesidium Italiae salvae essent.","reading":"BELLVM PŪNICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"},{"latin":"Quadrienniō cum gravī tamen calamitāte hoc bellum tractum est.","reading":"BELLVM SOCIĀLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"calceus","latin":"calceus","headword":"calceus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shoe","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"calidus","latin":"calidus","headword":"calidus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"hot; warm","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aestāte diēs longī sunt, sōl lūcet, āēr calidus est.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"callis","latin":"callis, -is","headword":"callis","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mountain path","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"campus","latin":"campus, -ī","headword":"campus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"field; plain; Campus Mārtius","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ā colle Quirīnālī et ā monte Capitōlīnō usque ad Tiberim flūmen campus Mārtius patet.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"candidus","latin":"candidus","headword":"candidus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"white; bright","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hodiē manē vestīmenta Mārcī munda erant atque tam candida quam nix nova, nunc vērō sordida et ūmida sunt.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"candor","latin":"candor, -ōris","headword":"candor","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"brightness; whiteness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ea vīta via est in caelum et in hunc coetum eōrum quī iam vīxērunt et corpore laxātī illum incolunt locum quem vidēs' — erat autem is splendidissimō candōre inter flammās circus ēlūcēns — 'quem vōs, ut ā Graecīs accēpistis, \"orbem lacteum\" nuncupātis.'","reading":"MORS ET VĪTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"canis","latin":"canis","headword":"canis","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dog","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pāstor nōn sōlus est in campō, nam canis niger cum eō est et centum ovēs: ūna ovis nigra et ūndēcentum ovēs albae.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Equus et asinus, leō et lupus, canis et ovis bēstiae sunt.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"canit","latin":"canit","headword":"canit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sings; crows; plays (music)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puella laeta rīdet et canit.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Ecce gallus canit: 'Cucurru!","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"cantat","latin":"cantat","headword":"cantat","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sings","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlia cantat: 'Lalla.' Iūlia laeta est.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"capit","latin":"capit","headword":"capit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"catches; takes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aquila est magna avis fera, quae parvās avēs capit et ēdit.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"capitulum","latin":"capitulum","headword":"capitulum","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"chapter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In capitulō prīmō mīlle vocābula sunt.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"caput","latin":"caput","headword":"caput","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"head","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In corpore ūnum caput est, nōn duo capita.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"carcer","latin":"carcer","headword":"carcer","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"prison","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Intuēre illam aquilam quae in magnum orbem circum carcerem nostrum volat!","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"cardo","latin":"cardō","headword":"cardō","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hinge","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"carere","latin":"carēre","headword":"carēre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"lack; be without (+ abl.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Īnfāns neque somnō neque cibō carēre potest.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"caritas","latin":"caritās, -ātis","headword":"caritās","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"affection; loyalty","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ubi eō ventum est, Turnum ex somnō excitātum circumsistunt custōdēs; comprehensīsque servīs, quī caritāte dominī vim parābant, cum gladiī abditī ex omnibus locīs aedium prōtraherentur, ēnimvērō manifēsta rēs vīsa est, iniectaeque Turnō catēnae.","reading":"TURNUS HERDONIUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"caro","latin":"carō","headword":"carō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"meat; flesh","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homō sex diēs cibō carēre potest, nec tamen famē moritur.' Iūlius: 'Dubitō num ego tam diū famem ferre possim.' Cornēlius: 'Id nōn negō, sed multō molestior est sitis quam famēs.'","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"carpentum","latin":"carpentum, -ī","headword":"carpentum","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"two-wheeled carriage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi eī in carpentō sedentī cum uxōre aquilā repente dēlāpsa pilleum aufert, superque carpentum volitāns rūrsus, velut dīvīnitus missa, capitī aptē repōnit; inde sublīmis abit.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"carpit","latin":"carpit","headword":"carpit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"picks; plucks","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus: \"Carpe rosās, Iūlia!\" Iūlia rosās carpit et cum quīnque rosīs ex hortō venit.","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Quid agit Iūlia?' Aemilia: 'Rosās carpit in hortō.'","reading":"ROSA IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"carus","latin":"cārus","headword":"cārus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"dear; expensive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"casa","latin":"casa, -ae","headword":"casa","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cottage; hut","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Palātium prīmum mūnītum est, sed ea moenia quadrāta, quibus Rōmulus, prīmus rēx Rōmānōrum, Palātium mūnīvisse dīcitur, iam prīdem periērunt, neque ūlla casa restat ex illā urbe antīquissimā, quae ā fōrmā moenium \"Rōma quadrāta\" appellābātur, praeter \"casam Rōmulī\" strāmentō tēctam.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"castellum","latin":"castellum, -ī","headword":"castellum","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fort; stronghold","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cōnsulēs usque ad Carthāginem prōcessērunt, multīsque castellīs vāstātīs, Manlius victor Rōmam rediit et vīgintī septem mīlia captīvōrum redūxit, Atīlius Regulus in Āfricā remānsit.","reading":"BELLVM PŪNICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"castitas","latin":"castitās, -ātis","headword":"castitās","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"chastity; purity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tarquinium mala libīdō Lūcrētiae per vim stuprandae capit; cum fōrmā tum spectāta castitās incitat.","reading":"LŪCRĒTIA VIOLĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"castra","latin":"castra","headword":"castra","letter":"c","pos":"noun (n. pl.); noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"camp","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Castra sunt mīlitum oppidum.'","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Vesperī exercitūs locō ad dēfendendum idōneō castrā pōnit, quae vāllō et fossā circumdantur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"casus","latin":"cāsus","headword":"cāsus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"case (of a noun); case","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Cāsus nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Sex.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Nōminātīvus, genetīvus, dativus, accūsātīvus, vocātīvus, ablātīvus.","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"catena","latin":"catēna","headword":"catēna","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"chain","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iānitor intrā iānuam sedet cum cane, quī prope tam ferōx est quam lupus; itaque necesse est eum catēnā vincīre.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"caterva","latin":"caterva, -ae","headword":"caterva","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"crowd; company","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec mīranda dum Aenēās intuētur, dum stupet et fīxus in locō haeret, Dīdō rēgīna, fōrmā pulcherrima, ad templum incessit magnā iuvenum catervā comitāta.","reading":"DĪDŌ RĒGĪNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"cauda","latin":"cauda","headword":"cauda","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tail","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Piscis quī natat caudam movet.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"causa","latin":"causa","headword":"causa","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cause; reason","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Certē nōn sine causā Sextus tē pulsāvit.","reading":"MARCVS Ā PATRE INTERROGĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"cautus","latin":"cautus","headword":"cautus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"cautious; careful","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Semper cautus estō!","reading":"ĪCARVS IN MARE CADIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"cavus","latin":"cavus, -a, -um","headword":"cavus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"hollow","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hoc sēnsit Polyphēmus, sed cum eōs capere nōn posset, clāmōrem horribilem sustulit, quō mare et terrae contremuērunt atque penitus resonuit mōns cavus.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"cella","latin":"cella, -ae","headword":"cella","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"inner chamber (of a temple)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postrēmō Domitiānus templum Iovis Capitōlīnī incendīō cōnsūmptum refēcit atque tantīs dīvitiīs exōrnāvit ut nihil magnificentius fierī posset: aurō et gemmīs splendet tēctum, quod plūrimīs columnīs ē marmore pulcherrimō factīs sustinētur; intus in cellā, templō clausus post forēs aurō opertās, ingēns simulācrum Iovis in altā sēde sedentis positum est.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"cena","latin":"cēna","headword":"cēna","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dinner; main meal","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dum ille vestem novam induit, Cornēlius et Orontēs et hospitēs eius cum uxōribus Fabiā et Paulā adveniunt. (Hospitēs sunt amīcī quōrum alter alterum bene recipit domum suam, etiam sī inexspectātī vēnerint.) Hodiē autem hospitēs Iūliī exspectātī veniunt, nam eōs vocāvit ad cēnam. (Cēna est cibus quem circiter hōrā nōnā vel decimā sūmunt.)","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"censor","latin":"cēnsor, -ōris","headword":"cēnsor","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"censor","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Claudius cēnsor aquam Appiam indūxit et viam Appiam strāvit.","reading":"SAMNĪTĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"census","latin":"cēnsus, -ūs","headword":"cēnsus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"census; valuation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In quārtā classe cēnsūs quīnque et vīgintī mīlium; totidem centuriae factae.","reading":"CENSVS INSTITVTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"centum","latin":"centum","headword":"centum","letter":"c","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"a hundred","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In familiā sunt centum servī.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Iūlius respondet: 'Centum.'","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"centuria","latin":"centuria, -ae","headword":"centuria","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"company of a hundred; squadron","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eōdem tempore et centuriae trēs equitum cōnscrīptae sunt: \"Ramnēnsēs\" ab Rōmulō, ab T.","reading":"BELLVM SABINVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"centurio","latin":"centuriō, -ōnis","headword":"centuriō","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"centurion","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Centuriōnēs armātī Mettium circumsistunt.","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"cera","latin":"cēra","headword":"cēra","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wax","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Necesse est tē stilum gravius in cēram premere.' (Discipulī in cērā scrībunt, nam tabulae eōrum cērā operiuntur.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"latin":"Dominus cēram aspiciēns signum magistrī cognōscit — est enim parva eius imāgō — et 'Missā est' inquit 'ā magistrō Diodōrō.","reading":"EPISTVLA ADVENIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"cerebrum","latin":"cerebrum","headword":"cerebrum","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"brain","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Post frontem est cerebrum.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"certamen","latin":"certāmen","headword":"certāmen","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"contest; struggle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fabia: \"Sextus quidem hodie naso turgido atque cruento e ludo rediit, cum certavisset cum quibusdam pueris qui eum laeserant.\" Aemilia: \"Cum pueri ludunt, haud multum interest inter ludum et certamen.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"certare","latin":"certāre","headword":"certāre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to contend; fight","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"certus","latin":"certus","headword":"certus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"certain; sure","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn certus sum!' Titus nōn certus, sed incertus est, et respōnsum incertum dat magistrō.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"cervus","latin":"cervus, -ī","headword":"cervus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stag; deer","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ceteri","latin":"cēterī","headword":"cēterī","letter":"c","pos":"adjective (pl.)","posGroup":"adjective","english":"the rest; the others","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In Āfricā ūnus fluvius magnus est: Nīlus; cēterī fluviī Āfricae parvī sunt.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Ubi sunt cēterī nummī?","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"chronicus","latin":"chronicus, -a, -um","headword":"chronicus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"chronological; librī chronicī; chronicles","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"cibus","latin":"cibus","headword":"cibus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"food","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cibus ovium est herba, quae in campō est.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Īnfāns multās hōrās dormit, nōn sōlum nocte sed etiam diē; nam longus somnus īnfantī tam necessārius est quam cibus.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"cingulus","latin":"cingulus, -ī","headword":"cingulus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"belt; zone","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cernis autem eandem terram quasi quibusdam redimītam et circumdatam cingulīs, ē quibus duōs maximē inter sē dīversōs et caelī verticibus ipsīs ex utrāque parte subnīxōs obriguisse pruīnā vidēs, medium autem illum et maximum sōlis ārdōre torrērī.","reading":"ANGUSTIAE TERRĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"cinis","latin":"cinis, -eris","headword":"cinis","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ashes; remains","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"circuitus","latin":"circuitus, -ūs","headword":"circuitus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"circuit; circumference","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Carthāgō, in circuītū vīgintī tria mīlia passuum patēns, magnō labōre obsessa et per partēs capta est, prīmum ā Mancīnō lēgātō, deinde ā Scīpiōne cōnsule, cui extrā sortem Āfrica prōvincia data erat.","reading":"BELLVM PVNICVM TERTIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"circum","latin":"circum","headword":"circum","letter":"c","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"around","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Circum oppida mūrī sunt.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"circumvehi","latin":"circumvehī","headword":"circumvehī","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to sail around (a place)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Italia, quam tū iam propinquam esse rēris, longō cursū ā tē dīviditur: prius circum Siciliam tibi nāvigandum est quam in illā terrā urbem condere poteris.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"circus","latin":"circus, -ī","headword":"circus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"the circus; racecourse; racetrack; circus","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Alter circus posteā in campō Mārtiō aedificātus est et circus Flāminius appellātus ā nōmine C.","reading":"VRBS MARMOREA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"civitas","latin":"cīvitās, -ātis","headword":"cīvitās","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"state; city; citizenship","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cīvitāte ita auctā, Rōmulus centum senātōrēs creāvit, sīve quia is numerus satis erat, sīve quia sōlī centum cīvēs nōbilēs erant quī senātōrēs creārī possent.","reading":"ROMVLVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"clades","latin":"clādēs, -is","headword":"clādēs","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"defeat; disaster","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec est nōbilis ad Trāsūmennum pugna atque inter paucās memorāta populī Rōmānī clādēs.","reading":"LACVS TRĀSŪMENNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"clamat","latin":"clāmat","headword":"clāmat","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"shouts; calls out; calls; cries out","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Albīnus clāmat: \"Ōrnāmenta!","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"In aurem puerī dormientis magnā vōce clāmat: 'Mārce!","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"clamor","latin":"clāmor","headword":"clāmor","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shout; cry","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At subitō silentium clāmōre et strepitū maximō rumpitur, nam Mārcus in cubiculō suō, quod iuxtā cubiculum Quīntī est, magnā vōce clāmat et forem manibus pedibusque percutit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"claritudo","latin":"clāritūdō, -inis","headword":"clāritūdō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"renown; distinction","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Scīpiōnis, quī tum Rōmānīs imperātor erat, et mōrem hostium cognōvit, multō labōre multāque cūrā, praetereā modestissimē pārendō et saepe obviam eundō perīculīs, in tantam clāritūdinem brevī pervēnit ut nostrīs vehementer cārus, Numantīnīs maximō terrōrī esset.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"clarus","latin":"clārus","headword":"clārus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"bright; clear","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"classiarius","latin":"classiārius, -ī","headword":"classiārius","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"marine; sailor","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Classī paucīs diēbus erant dēcrētūrī.","reading":"APVD PRŪSIAM ET MORS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"classis","latin":"classis, -is","headword":"classis","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fleet","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postrēmō, cum tam cārum esset frūmentum ac pānis ut multī inopia cibī necessāriī perīrent, populus Rōmānus ūnō ōre postulāvit ut ūniversa classis Rōmāna ad hostēs illōs audācissimōs mitterētur.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"},{"latin":"Ō sociī, ēripite nōs ē perīculō!\" Prīmus Palīnūrus prōram ad laevam vertit, et cūncta classis rēmīs ventīsque laevam petīvit.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"claudere","latin":"claudere","headword":"claudere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to close; shut","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Servus cuius officium est forēs aperīre et claudere ac vīllam dominī cūstōdīre, ōstiārius vel iānitor appellātur.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"claudit","latin":"claudit","headword":"claudit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"closes; shuts","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra ōstium aperit et in cubiculum intrat, neque ōstium post sē claudit.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"latin":"Quīntus oculōs claudit atque dormit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"clausus","latin":"clausus","headword":"clausus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"closed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"clavis","latin":"clāvis","headword":"clāvis","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"key","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce clāvis cubiculī.'","reading":"RESPŌNSVM IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"clemens","latin":"clēmēns","headword":"clēmēns","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"merciful; gentle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemiliā autem marītō suō suādet ut clēmēns sit: 'Nōlī, Iūlī, Mēdum cruciāre, sī eum invēnerīs.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"clementia","latin":"clēmentia, -ae","headword":"clēmentia","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mercy; clemency","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nihil eā lēgātiōne perfectum est, Perseō rēgium nōmen omnī vī amplectente, Paulō 'ut sē suaque omnia in fidem et clēmentiam populī Rōmānī permitteret' tendente.","reading":"PERSEVS CAPTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"clipeus","latin":"clipeus, -ī","headword":"clipeus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"round shield","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"clivus","latin":"clīvus, -ī","headword":"clīvus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"slope; steep street","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Multae viae ex omnibus urbis partibus in forum ferunt, ut Argīlētum, Sacra via, Nova via, vīcus Tuscus, vīcus Iūgārius, atque clīvus Capitōlīnus, quō imperātōrēs triumphantes in Capitōlium ascendunt. (\"Clīvus\" dīcitur via quae in clīvō montis facta est.) In summā Sacrā viā īnfrā clīvum Palātīnum est arcus Titī, dē quō mox dīcendum erit, et templum Iovis Stātōris.","reading":"AEDĒS FORĪ RŌMĀNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"coalescere","latin":"coalēscere","headword":"coalēscere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to grow together; unite","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēbus dīvīnīs rīte factīs vocātāque ad concilium multitūdine, quae coalēscere in ūnum populum nōn poterat nisi lēgibus, Rōmulus iūra dedit.","reading":"ROMVLVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"cocus","latin":"cocus","headword":"cocus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cook","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"(Servus cuius negōtium est cibum coquere atque cōnficere in culīnā, cocus appellātur.","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"coetus","latin":"coetus, -ūs","headword":"coetus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gathering; assembly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quārē, quoniam dē rē pūblicā quaerimus, hoc prīmum videāmus: quid sit id ipsum quod quaerimus.' Cum approbāvisset Laelius, 'Est igitur' inquit Āfricānus 'rēs pūblica \"rēs populī\", populus autem nōn omnis hominum coetus quōquō modō congregātus, sed coetus multitūdinis iūris cōnsēnsū et ūtilitātis commūniōne sociātus...'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"cogito","latin":"cōgitō","headword":"cōgitō","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"think","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūr nōn cōgitās antequam respondēs?' Mārcus: 'Semper cōgitō antequam respondeō.' Magister: 'Ergō puer stultus es, Mārce!","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"cognomen","latin":"cognōmen","headword":"cognōmen","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"surname; family name","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Virō Rōmānō tria nōmina sunt. 'Lūcius' est praenōmen, id est nōmen prīmum; 'Balbus' cognōmen est.","reading":"DĒ FAMILIĀ ET NŌMINIBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"cognomentum","latin":"cognōmentum, -ī","headword":"cognōmentum","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"surname; additional name","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Posteā Pythagorās Samius in Italiam vēnit, Tarquinī fīliō regnum obtinente, cui cognōmentum Superbus fuit; iīsdemque temporibus occīsus est Athēnīs ab Harmodiō et Aristogītōne Hipparchus, Pīsistratī fīlius, Hippiae tyrannī frāter.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"cognoscere","latin":"cognōscere","headword":"cognōscere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to recognize; find out; to learn","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia: 'Nēmō tibi quidquam scrībet dē rēbus urbānīs, nisi prius ipse epistulam scrīpserīs.' Orontēs: 'Opus nōn est epistulās exspectāre, nam facile aliquid novī per nūntiōs cognōscere potes.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"cognoscit","latin":"cognōscit","headword":"cognōscit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"recognises; gets to know","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus est, sed difficile est eum cognōscere, nam sordidus est et sanguis dē nāsō eius fluit.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"cohorrescere","latin":"cohorrēscere","headword":"cohorrēscere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to shudder; be terrified","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quem ubi agnōvī, equidem cohorruī; sed ille 'Ades' inquit 'animō et omitte timōrem, Scīpiō, et quae dīcam trade memoriae!'","reading":"APUD MASINISSAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"cohors","latin":"cohors","headword":"cohors","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cohort","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"colit","latin":"colit","headword":"colit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"cultivates; farms","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque pecus maiōris pretiī est quam frūmentum, et quī pecus pāscit plūs pecūniae facit quam quī agrōs colit.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"collega","latin":"collēga, -ae","headword":"collēga","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"colleague in office","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lūcrētium Tricipitīnum collēgam sibi fēcit, Lūcrētiae patrem; quō morbō mortuō iterum M.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"collis","latin":"collis, -is","headword":"collis","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hill","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In campō est collis. (Collis est mōns parvus.) In colle arbor est.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"collum","latin":"collum","headword":"collum","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"neck","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ānulus digitum Aemiliae ōrnat, margarītae collum eius ōrnant.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"Lupus collum ovis petit dentibus ...","reading":"LPVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"colonia","latin":"colōnia, -ae","headword":"colōnia","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"colony; settlement","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Et continuātō in alterum annum tribūnātū, lēgibus agrāriīs lātīs effēcit ut complūrēs colōniae in Italiā dēdūcerentur et ūna in solō dīrutae Carthāginis, quō ipse triumvir creātus colōniam dēdūxit.","reading":"LĒGĒS AGRĀRIAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"colonus","latin":"colōnus","headword":"colōnus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tenant farmer","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Colōnus est agricola quī nōn suōs, sed aliēnōs agrōs prō absente dominō colit et mercēdem dominō solvit prō agrīs.","reading":"VĪNEAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"columna","latin":"columna","headword":"columna","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"column; pillar","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Marītus et uxor inter columnās et signa ambulant.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"coma","latin":"coma, -ae","headword":"coma","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hair of the head","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cui Pyrrhus \"Nunc morere!\" inquit, senemque trementem et in sanguine fīliī lābentem ad ipsam āram trāxit, ubi laevā comam eius prehendēns dextrā ensem sustulit atque in latere rēgis dēfīxit!","reading":"MORS PRIAMĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"comes","latin":"comes","headword":"comes","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"companion","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Crās Dāvus eum comitābitur; is certē bonus comes erit.'","reading":"RESPŌNSVM IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"comis","latin":"cōmis, -e","headword":"cōmis","letter":"c","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"courteous; kindly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"comitatur","latin":"comitātur","headword":"comitātur","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"accompanies","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postquam Dāvus puerum ex ātriō dūxit, dominus 'Haec omnia' inquit 'facta sunt, quod Mēdus heri domō fugit nec hodiē Mārcum in lūdum euntem et illinc redeuntem comitārī potuit.","reading":"RESPŌNSVM IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"comitia","latin":"comitia, -ōrum","headword":"comitia","letter":"c","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"assembly of the people","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī cum comitia habēret, Ancum Marcium rēgem populus creāvit; patrēs fuēre auctōrēs.","reading":"ANCVS MARCIUS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"commentarius","latin":"commentārius, -ī","headword":"commentārius","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"notebook; commentary","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Satis autem vīsum est in hōc commentāriō dē temporibus paucōrum hominum dīcere, ex quōrum aetātibus dē plūribus quoque, quōs nōn nōminārēmus, haud difficilis coniectūra fierī posset.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"committere proelium","latin":"committere proelium","headword":"committere proelium","letter":"c","pos":"phrase","posGroup":"other","english":"to join battle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"communicare","latin":"commūnicāre","headword":"commūnicāre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to share; make common","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quārē, quoniam dē rē pūblicā quaerimus, hoc prīmum videāmus: quid sit id ipsum quod quaerimus.' Cum approbāvisset Laelius, 'Est igitur' inquit Āfricānus 'rēs pūblica \"rēs populī\", populus autem nōn omnis hominum coetus quōquō modō congregātus, sed coetus multitūdinis iūris cōnsēnsū et ūtilitātis commūniōne sociātus...'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"communio","latin":"commūniō, -ōnis","headword":"commūniō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sharing; community","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quārē, quoniam dē rē pūblicā quaerimus, hoc prīmum videāmus: quid sit id ipsum quod quaerimus.' Cum approbāvisset Laelius, 'Est igitur' inquit Āfricānus 'rēs pūblica \"rēs populī\", populus autem nōn omnis hominum coetus quōquō modō congregātus, sed coetus multitūdinis iūris cōnsēnsū et ūtilitātis commūniōne sociātus...'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"communis","latin":"commūnis","headword":"commūnis","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"common (of gender)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Genera nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Quattuor.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Masculīnum, ut hic magister; fēminīnum, ut haec fēmina; neutrum, ut hoc scamnum; commūne, ut hic et haec sacerdōs.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"commutatio","latin":"commūtātiō, -ōnis","headword":"commūtātiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"change; reversal","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed ubi Rōmam lēgātī vēnēre et ex praeceptō rēgis hospitibus aliīsque, quōrum ea tempestāte in senātū auctōritās pollēbat, magna mūnera mīsēre, tanta commūtātiō incessit ut ex maximā invidiā in grātiam et favōrem nōbilitātis Iugurtha venīret!","reading":"ADHERBAL RŌMAM PROFĪCĪSCITUR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"comoedia","latin":"cōmoedia","headword":"cōmoedia","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"comedy; play","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nuper spectavi comoediam Plauti de Amphitryone, duce Graecorum, cuius uxor Alcmena ab ipso Iove amabatur.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"comparat","latin":"comparat","headword":"comparat","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"compares","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister litterās Titī comparat cum litterīs Mārcī, et 'Litterae vestrae,' inquit, 'aequē foedae sunt: tū, Tite, neque pulchrius neque foedius scrībis quam Mārcus.'","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"comparatio","latin":"comparātiō, -ōnis","headword":"comparātiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"comparison; preparation","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Comparātiōnis gradūs quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Trēs.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Positīvus, ut doctus; comparātīvus, ut doctior; superlātīvus, ut doctissimus.' Magister: 'Quae nōmina comparantur?' Discipulus: 'Appellātīva dumtaxat quālitātem aut quantitātem significantiā.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"},{"latin":"Mithridātēs autem omne reliquum tempus nōn ad oblīviōnem veteris bellī, sed ad comparātiōnem novī contulit.","reading":"DĒ GENERE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"comparativus","latin":"comparātīvus","headword":"comparātīvus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"comparative","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Comparātiōnis gradūs quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Trēs.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Positīvus, ut doctus; comparātīvus, ut doctior; superlātīvus, ut doctissimus.' Magister: 'Quae nōmina comparantur?' Discipulus: 'Appellātīva dumtaxat quālitātem aut quantitātem significantiā.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"complecti","latin":"complectī","headword":"complectī","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to embrace","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus eam complectitur et 'Terge oculōs!' inquit, 'Amīcus tuus, quī tē amō, tēcum sum.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"complere","latin":"complēre","headword":"complēre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to fill; man","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Graecī enim, cum urbem vī expugnāre nōn possent, dolō ūsī sunt: equum ingentem ē lignō fabricāvērunt eumque mīlitibus armātīs complēvērunt, quibus praefectī erant Ulixēs et Pyrrhus, Achillis fīlius.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"complorare","latin":"complōrāre","headword":"complōrāre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to bewail; lament","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Viriāthus ā prōditōribus, cōnsiliō Servīliī Caepiōnis, interfectus est et ab exercitū suō multum complōrātus ac nōbiliter sepultus, vir duxque magnus et per quattuordecim annōs quibus cum Rōmānīs bellum gessit frequentius superior.","reading":"HISPĀNIA PĀCĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"comploratio","latin":"complōrātiō, -ōnis","headword":"complōrātiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lamentation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Movet ferōcī iuvenī animum complōrātiō sorōris in victōriā suā tantōque gaudiō pūblicō.","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"computare","latin":"computāre","headword":"computāre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"calculate; reckon","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"computo","latin":"computō","headword":"computō","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"compute; count up","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Titus digitīs computat: '... quattuor ... octō ... duodecim ... sēdecim: quattuor sēstertiī sunt sēdecim assēs.' Magister: 'Et decem dēnāriī quot sēstertiī sunt?' Titus: 'Quadrāgintā.' Magister: 'Quot dēnāriī sunt duodequinquāgintā sēstertiī?' Titus magistrō interrogantī nihil respondet.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"conari","latin":"cōnārī","headword":"cōnārī","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to try; attempt","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"conatur","latin":"cōnātur","headword":"cōnātur","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"tries; attempts","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"concentus","latin":"concentus, -ūs","headword":"concentus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"harmony; concord","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc' inquam 'quis est quī complet aurēs meās tantus et tam dulcis sonus?' 'Hic est' inquit Āfricānus 'ille quī intervāllīs coniūnctus imparibus, sed tamen prō ratā parte ratiōne distīnctīs, impulsū et mōtū ipsōrum orbium efficitur, et acūta cum gravibus temperāns variōs aequābiliter concentūs efficit.","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"concilium","latin":"concilium, -ī","headword":"concilium","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"assembly; council; league","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ita sōlus rēx duārum gentium factus Aenēās, ut animōs Aborīginum sibi conciliāret, utramque gentem eōdem nōmine 'Latīnōs' appellāvit.","reading":"TRŌIĀNĪ ET LATĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"},{"latin":"Lēgātī Rōmānī ab Achaeīs pulsī sunt Corinthī, missī ut eās cīvitātēs quae sub dīcione Philippī fuerant ab Achāicō conciliō sēcernerent.","reading":"BELLVM ACHAEVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"concubina","latin":"concubīna, -ae","headword":"concubīna","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"concubine","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dein Micipsa fīlius rēgnum sōlus obtinuit, Mastanabalem et Hiempsalem ex sē genuit, Iugurthamque, fīlium Mastanabalis frātris — quem Masinissa, quod ortus ex concubīnā erat, prīvātum dērelīquerat — eōdem cultū quō līberōs suōs domī habuit.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"concupiscere","latin":"concupīscere","headword":"concupīscere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to desire greatly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"concursus","latin":"concursus, -ūs","headword":"concursus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"running together; riotous gathering","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Post aliquot annōs rēx Tatius Lāvīniī, cum ad sacrificium eō vēnisset, concursū factō interfectus est.","reading":"FIDENATES ET VEIENTES VICTI","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"condere","latin":"condere","headword":"condere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to found (a city); hide","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Prīmum in Thrāciam vectī sunt ibīque in lītore curvō novam urbem condere volēbant.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"conditor","latin":"conditor, -ōris","headword":"conditor","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"founder","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Factum est trīcēsimō ferē annō post Lāvīnium conditum.","reading":"ALBA CONDITA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"conficit","latin":"cōnficit","headword":"cōnficit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"makes; completes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ālās quoque cōnficere possum, quamquam opus haud facile est.\"","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"confidere","latin":"cōnfidere","headword":"cōnfidere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to trust (+ dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Posthāc servō Graecō numquam cōnfīdam, neque enim fide meā dignī sunt: īnfīdī et nēquam sunt omnēs!","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"confitetur","latin":"cōnfitētur","headword":"cōnfitētur","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"confesses","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūr nōndum mihi respondistī?\" Ita repente interrogātus Mēdus sē pecūniam ē sacculō dominī surripuisse cōnfitētur.","reading":"ĀNVLVS POLYCRATIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"confligere","latin":"cōnflīgere","headword":"cōnflīgere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to clash; do battle; to fight; engage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fabius Maximus dictātor adversus Hannibalem missus nōllet aciē cum eō cōnflīgere, M.","reading":"FABIVS MAXIMVS CVNCTĀTOR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"},{"latin":"Cum Cimbrīs itaque cōnflīxit et duōbus proeliīs ducenta mīlia hostium cecīdit, octōgintā mīlia cēpit et ducem eōrum Teutobodum; propter quod meritum absēns quīntō cōnsul est factus.","reading":"BELLVM CIMBRICVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"confluentes","latin":"cōnfluentēs, -ium","headword":"cōnfluentēs","letter":"c","pos":"noun m. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"river-junction","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ubi Aniēnem fluvium trānsiit, ad cōnfluentēs collocat castra.","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"confugere","latin":"cōnfugere","headword":"cōnfugere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to flee for refuge","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At anguēs in summam arcem ad simulācrum Minervae cōnfugiunt ibīque sub clipeō deae latent.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"confusio","latin":"cōnfūsiō, -ōnis","headword":"cōnfūsiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"confusion; disorder","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec cōnstitūtiō prīmum habet aequābilitātem quandam magnam, quā carēre diūtius vix possunt līberī, deinde firmitūdinem — quod et illa prīma facile in contrāria vitia convertuntur, ut exsistat ex rēge dominus, ex optimātibus factiō, ex populō turba et cōnfūsiō.'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"coniectura","latin":"coniectūra, -ae","headword":"coniectūra","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"conjecture; inference","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Satis autem vīsum est in hōc commentāriō dē temporibus paucōrum hominum dīcere, ex quōrum aetātibus dē plūribus quoque, quōs nōn nōminārēmus, haud difficilis coniectūra fierī posset.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"coniugatio","latin":"coniugātiō","headword":"coniugātiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"conjugation","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"coniugium","latin":"coniugium, -ī","headword":"coniugium","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"marriage; wedlock","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nisi certum mihi esset nūllī virō mē coniugio iungere, postquam prīmus amor mē morte fefellit, huius ūnīus amōrī forsitan succumbere potuī!","reading":"FLAMMA AMŌRIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"coniunctio","latin":"coniūnctiō","headword":"coniūnctiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"conjunction","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"coniunctivus","latin":"coniūnctīvus","headword":"coniūnctīvus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"subjunctive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"coniunx","latin":"coniūnx","headword":"coniūnx","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"spouse; husband / wife","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cupīdō est fīlius Veneris et Mārtis, quamquam Venus Mārtis coniūnx nōn est, sed alterīus deī, cui nōmen est Vulcānus.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"coniuratio","latin":"coniūrātiō, -ōnis","headword":"coniūrātiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"conspiracy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Catilīna, bis repulsam in petitione cōnsulātūs passus, cum Lentulō praetōre et Cethēgō et complūribus aliīs coniūrāvit dē caede cōnsulum et senātūs, incendīs urbis et opprimendā rē pūblicā, exercitū quoque in Etrūriā comparātō.","reading":"FĪNIS MITHRIDĀTIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"consecrare","latin":"cōnsecrāre","headword":"cōnsecrāre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to consecrate; dedicate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn rēx igitur, sed cōnsul Rōmānus hoc templum augustum Iovī Optimō Maximō, summō deō populī Rōmānī, et Iūnōnī et Minervae, duābus maximīs deābus, cōnsecrāvit.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"conservator","latin":"cōnservātor, -ōris","headword":"cōnservātor","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"preserver; guardian","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Sed quō sīs, Āfricāne, alacrior ad tuendam rem pūblicam, sīc habētō: omnibus quī patriam cōnservāverint, adiūverint, auxerint, certum esse in caelō dēfīnītum locum, ubi beātī aevō sempiternō fruantur.","reading":"MORS ET VĪTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"consideratio","latin":"cōnsīderātiō, -ōnis","headword":"cōnsīderātiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"consideration; contemplation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dein, cum essent perpauca inter sē ūnō aut alterō spatiō collocūtī Scīpiōnīque eōrum adventus periūcundus et pergrātus fuisset, placitum est ut in apricō maximē prātulō locō, quod erat hībernum tempus annī, cōnsīderent.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"considit","latin":"cōnsīdit","headword":"cōnsīdit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sits down","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cōnsīde!' Sextus in sellā cōnsīdit.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"consilium","latin":"cōnsilium","headword":"cōnsilium","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"plan; purpose","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is laetus Ōstia profectus est cum mercibus pretiōsīs quās omnī pecūniā suā in Italiā ēmerat, eō cōnsiliō ut eās maiōre pretiō in Graeciā vēnderet.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"consistit","latin":"cōnsistit","headword":"cōnsistit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"stops; halts; takes a stand","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Multae fēminae quae in hāc viā ambulant ante tabernam Albīnī cōnsistunt, nam fēminae ōrnāmentīs dēlectantur.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"consolari","latin":"cōnsōlārī","headword":"cōnsōlārī","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to comfort","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In patriam īmus, ubi multī amīcī nōs opperiuntur.' Hīs verbīs Mēdus amīcam suam trīstem cōnsōlātur.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"consolor","latin":"cōnsōlor","headword":"cōnsōlor","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to comfort","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Graviter vulnerātus in castrā portātus est, ubi in manibus meīs ex vulnere mortuus est, postquam mē ōrāvit ut per litterās parentēs suōs dē morte fīliī cōnsōlārer.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"consonans","latin":"cōnsonāns","headword":"cōnsonāns","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"consonant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Litterae sunt aut vōcālēs aut cōnsonantēs: vōcālēs sunt Ā, Ē, I, Ō, V, Y; cēterae sunt cōnsonantēs. (Etiam I et V cōnsonantēs sunt in vocābulīs IAM, VEL, vōs, QVAM, cet.)","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"conspicit","latin":"cōnspicit","headword":"cōnspicit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"catches sight of; notices","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum cruōrem in faciē eius cōnspiciēns exclāmat pater: \"Ō mī fīlī!","reading":"MARCVS Ā PATRE INTERROGĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"conspicuus","latin":"cōnspicuus, -a, -um","headword":"cōnspicuus","letter":"c","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"conspicuous; notable","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Novitās dīvitiaeque eum cōnspicuum faciēbant Rōmānīs, et ipse fortūnam suam adiuvābat benignē alloquendō, cōmiter invītandō, beneficiīsque quōs poterat sibi conciliandō, dōnec in rēgiam quoque dē eō fāma perlāta est.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"constantia","latin":"cōnstantia, -ae","headword":"cōnstantia","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"firmness; constancy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque cōnstat utrumque poētam antīquissimum nōn multō post Troiam captam, sed multō ante Rōmam conditam vīxisse.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"constat","latin":"cōnstat","headword":"cōnstat","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"costs (with a price)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus Albīnum interrogat: \"Quot nummīs cōnstat ānulus in quō gemma est?\" Albīnus Mēdō ānulum gemmātum ostendit.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"constitutio","latin":"cōnstitūtiō, -ōnis","headword":"cōnstitūtiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"constitution; ordering","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Āfricānus, hic Paulī fīlius, fēriīs Latīnīs Tūditānō cōnsule et Aquīliō, cōnstituisset in hortīs esse familiārissimīque eius ad eum frequenter per eōs diēs ventitātūrī sē esse dīxissent, Latīnīs ipsīs māne ad eum prīmus sorōris fīlius vēnit Q.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"consuetudo","latin":"cōnsuētūdō, -inis","headword":"cōnsuētūdō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"custom; habit","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quam nē aliēnō arbitriō dīmineret, memor prīstinārum virtūtum, venēnum quod semper sēcum habēre cōnsuērat sūmpsit.","reading":"APVD PRŪSIAM ET MORS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"consul","latin":"cōnsul, -ulis","headword":"cōnsul","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"consul","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ille vērō, cum nōndum sacrāvisset novum templum, Rōmā expulsus est ā Iūniō Brūtō, atque prō rēge duō cōnsulēs populō Rōmānō praepositī sunt.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"},{"latin":"Cōnsulēs tunc Rōmae erant P.","reading":"SAGVNTVM OPPVGNĀTVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"consulatus","latin":"cōnsulātus, -ūs","headword":"cōnsulātus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"consulship","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hinc cōnsulēs coepēre, prō ūnō rēge duo, hāc causā creātī, ut, sī ūnus malus esse voluisset, alter eum habēns potestātem similem coercēret.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"consumere","latin":"cōnsūmere","headword":"cōnsūmere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to consume; destroy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postrēmō Domitiānus templum Iovis Capitōlīnī incendīō cōnsūmptum refēcit atque tantīs dīvitiīs exōrnāvit ut nihil magnificentius fierī posset: aurō et gemmīs splendet tēctum, quod plūrimīs columnīs ē marmore pulcherrimō factīs sustinētur; intus in cellā, templō clausus post forēs aurō opertās, ingēns simulācrum Iovis in altā sēde sedentis positum est.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"contemnere","latin":"contemnere","headword":"contemnere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to despise","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tanta enim erat vīs et audācia eōrum, ut vim Rōmānōrum contemnentēs etiam portūs Italiae oppugnārent.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"contio","latin":"contiō, -ōnis","headword":"contiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"assembly; public meeting","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīs immortālibus perfectīs operibus, cum Rōmulus cōntiōnem mīlitum in campō Mārtiō habēret, subitō coorta tempestās cum magnō fragōre tonitribusque tam dēnsō nimbō rēgem operuit ut cōnspectum eius mīlitibus abstulerit.","reading":"ROMVLVS CONSECRATVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"contra","latin":"contrā","headword":"contrā","letter":"c","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"against","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ariadna igitur, antequam Thēseus labyrinthum intrāvit, ad eum accessit et sīc loquī coepit: 'Contrā Mīnōtaurum sōlus proficīscī nōn potes.","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"contremescere","latin":"contremēscere","headword":"contremēscere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to tremble greatly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hoc sēnsit Polyphēmus, sed cum eōs capere nōn posset, clāmōrem horribilem sustulit, quō mare et terrae contremuērunt atque penitus resonuit mōns cavus.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"contumelia","latin":"contumēlia, -ae","headword":"contumēlia","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"insult; abuse","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ferōx Tullia, quae Arruntī Tarquiniō nūpta erat, aegrē ferēbat nihil māteriae in virō neque ad cupiditātem neque ad audāciam esse; alterum Tarquinium admīrārī, \"eum virum esse\" dīcere, spernere sorōrem quod virō audācī nūpta ipsa audāciā cāreret; nimis verbōrum contumēliīs parcere dē virō ad frātrem, dē sorōre ad virum.","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"contumeliosus","latin":"contumēliōsus, -a, -um","headword":"contumēliōsus","letter":"c","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"insulting; abusive","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"conubium","latin":"cōnūbium, -ī","headword":"cōnūbium","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"marriage; union; right of intermarriage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Egō per hās lacrimās, per dextram tuam, per cōnūbium nostrum tē ōrō: sī quid bene dē tē meruī, aut sī tibi dulce fuit quidquam meum, miserēre meī et mūtā iam mentem!","reading":"NŪNTIUS DEŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"},{"latin":"Sed cum novus populus mulieribus carēret neque virīs Rōmānīs cum fīnitimīs cōnūbia essent, Rōmulus ex cōnsiliō patrum lēgātōs ad vīcīnās gentēs mīsit, quī societātem cōnūbiumque novō populō peterent.","reading":"SABINAE RAPTAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"convenit","latin":"convenit","headword":"convenit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"fits; suits","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Illud ōrnāmentum nōn tam pulchrum est quam hoc, neque illa gemma tanta est quanta haec.\" Mēdus: \"Tanta gemma ad tam parvum ānulum nōn convenit.\"","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"conventus","latin":"conventus, -ūs","headword":"conventus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"assembly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Isthmiōrum lūdicrum aderat tempus, semper frequēns — cum propter spectāculī studium, tum quia Graeciae is mercātus erat; tum vērō nōn ad solitōs modo ūsūs undique convēnerant, sed exspectātiōne ērectī, quī deinde status futūrus Graeciae, quae sua fortūna esset.","reading":"ISTHMIA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"conversio","latin":"conversiō, -ōnis","headword":"conversiō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"turning; revolution","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hunc ut comitēs cōnsequuntur Veneris alter, alter Mercuriī cursūs, in īnfimōque orbe Lūna radiīs sōlis accēnsa convertitur.","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"convincere","latin":"convincere","headword":"convincere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to convict; prove guilty","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"conviva","latin":"convīva","headword":"convīva","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"guest at dinner; guest at a banquet","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ante convīvium trīclīnium flōribus exōrnātur et vestis pretiōsa super lectōs sternitur.","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"},{"latin":"Nōn sōlum dē cibō et pōtiōne est sermō convīvārum.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"convivium","latin":"convīvium","headword":"convīvium","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dinner party; banquet","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ante convīvium trīclīnium flōribus exōrnātur et vestis pretiōsa super lectōs sternitur.","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"copiae","latin":"cōpiae, -ārum","headword":"cōpiae","letter":"c","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"troops; forces; supplies","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inter cōnsulēs ita cōpiae dīvīsae: Semprōniō datae legiōnēs duae et sociōrum sēdecim mīlia peditum, equitēs mīlle octingentī, nāvēs longae centum sexāgintā.","reading":"EXCIDIVM SAGVNTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"coquere","latin":"coquere","headword":"coquere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to cook","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"(Servus cuius negōtium est cibum coquere atque cōnficere in culīnā, cocus appellātur.","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"cor","latin":"cor","headword":"cor","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"heart","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In pectore cor et pulmōnēs sunt.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"corona","latin":"corōna, -ae","headword":"corōna","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"crown","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīs enim magistrātibus lēgātī Carthāginiēnsēs Rōmam vēnērunt, quī senātuī populōque Rōmānō grātiās agerent quod cum iīs pācem fēcissent, ob eamque rem corōnā aureā eōs dōnārent simulque peterent ut obsidēs eōrum Fregellīs essent captīvīque redderentur.","reading":"ZAMA ET FVGA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"corpus","latin":"corpus","headword":"corpus","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"body","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Corpus hūmānum quattuor membra habet: duo bracchia et duo crūra.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"corrigit","latin":"corrigit","headword":"corrigit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"corrects","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister stilō suō addit litterās quae dēsunt; ita menda corrigit.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"corripere","latin":"corripere","headword":"corripere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to seize; snatch up","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inde rēctā viā Laocoontem petunt; et prīmum parva duōrum fīliōrum corpora complexī membra eōrum tenera edunt, tum patrem ipsum, quī miserīs fīliīs auxiliō veniēbat, corripiunt.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"corvus","latin":"corvus, -ī","headword":"corvus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"raven; also a boarding-hook","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Valerius tribūnus mīlitum obtulit, et cum prōcessisset armātus, corvus eī suprā dextrum bracchium sēdit.","reading":"POST VRBEM CAPTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"cotidie","latin":"cotīdiē","headword":"cotīdiē","letter":"c","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"daily; every day","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"“Aspice hanc vītem: tot et tantae ūvae magnam vīnī cōpiam prōmittunt, ac vīnum bonum futūrum esse exīstimō, nam sōl duōs iam mēnsēs prope cotīdiē lūcet usque ā māne ad vesperum.","reading":"PĀSTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"crassus","latin":"crassus","headword":"crassus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"fat; thick; stout","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rāmus quī nīdum sustinet nōn crassus, sed tenuis est.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Vir quī ab Aemiliā amābātur Crassus Dīves nōminābātur.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"credere","latin":"crēdere","headword":"crēdere","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to believe; trust (with dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"credit","latin":"crēdit","headword":"crēdit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"believes; trusts","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magistrō recitante, Mārcus dormīvit!\" Iūlius Mārcum dormīvisse dīcit, nec vērō māter id crēdit.","reading":"MARCVS MENTĪTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"crimen","latin":"crīmen, -inis","headword":"crīmen","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"charge; crime","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hāc lēge duumvirī creātī sunt, iūdicēs sevērissimī, quī sē tam grave crīmen negligere posse nōn rēbantur, et Horātium condemnāvērunt.","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"crinis","latin":"crīnis, -is","headword":"crīnis","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hair","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"cruciare","latin":"cruciāre","headword":"cruciāre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to torture","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Profectō eum verberābō atque omnibus modīs cruciābō, sī eum invēnerō priusquam Italiam relīquerit.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"cruciatus","latin":"cruciātus, -ūs","headword":"cruciātus","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"torture","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inter haec senex iuvenem amplexus, spolia Curiātiōrum fīxa eō locō quī nunc \"pilā Horātiā\" appellātur ostentāns, \"Huncine\" aiēbat \"quem modo decorātum ovantemque victōriā incēdentem vīdistis, Quirītēs, eum vīnctum inter verbera et cruciātūs vidēre potestis?","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"crudelis","latin":"crūdēlis","headword":"crūdēlis","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"cruel","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sānē pater crūdēlis fuit Mānlius, sed illō suppliciō cēterī mīlitēs dēterrēbantur nē officium dēsererent.'","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"crudelitas","latin":"crūdēlitās, -ātis","headword":"crūdēlitās","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cruelty","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed nec dī nec hominēs aut ipsam aut fīliōs ā crūdēlitāte rēgis dēfendunt: Amūlius Vestālem vīnctam in custōdiam dat, puerōs in fluvium mittī iubet.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"cruentus","latin":"cruentus","headword":"cruentus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"bloody; bloodstained","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nūper Mārcus sōlus rediit, sed pater fīlium suum redeuntem vix cognōvit neque eum ōsculātus est ut solet, nam Mārcus nōn modo ūmidus erat quod per imbrem ambulāverat, sed etiam sordidus atque cruentus quod humī iacuerat et ā Sextō pulsātus erat.'","reading":"SYRA NĀRRAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"crus","latin":"crūs","headword":"crūs","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"leg; shin","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Bracchium membrum est et crūs membrum est.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Syra: 'Ego nōn mīror pedem tuum aegrum esse, quod dē tam altā arbore cecidistī; at mīror tē crūs nōn frēgisse.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"crux","latin":"crux","headword":"crux","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cross","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"cubare","latin":"cubāre","headword":"cubāre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to lie (in bed); to lie; recline","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trīstis sum, quod mihi necesse est intus cubāre, dum aliī puerī foris lūdunt.","reading":"SYRA NĀRRAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"cubat","latin":"cubat","headword":"cubat","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"lies; is lying down","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus quiētus in lectō suō cubat; is bene dormit.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"cubiculum","latin":"cubiculum","headword":"cubiculum","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bedroom; room","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In vīllā sunt multa cubicula.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"In cubiculō suō est.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"cui?","latin":"cui?","headword":"cui?","letter":"c","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"to whom?","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In cubiculō suō est.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"cuius?","latin":"cuius?","headword":"cuius?","letter":"c","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"whose?","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cuius servus est Dāvus?","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Cuius est haec taberna?","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"culmen","latin":"culmen, -inis","headword":"culmen","letter":"c","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"summit; roof-top","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"culpa","latin":"culpa, -ae","headword":"culpa","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fault; blame","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nec eā culpā omnium Albānōrum est: ducem secūtī sunt, et vōs, sī ego inde agmen abdūcere voluissem, recūsāssētis.","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"cum","latin":"cum","headword":"cum","letter":"c","pos":"preposition; conjunction","posGroup":"preposition","english":"with (+ abl.); with; when; since","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius in vīllā suā habitat cum magnā familiā.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Duo servī lectīcam cum dominō portant.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"cunae","latin":"cūnae","headword":"cūnae","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cradle (plural)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūnae sunt cūnābula īnfantīs.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"cupido","latin":"cupīdō, -inis","headword":"cupīdō","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"desire; passion","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"cupidus","latin":"cupidus","headword":"cupidus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"eager; desirous","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Post expugnātiōnem urbis Mīnōs, cupidus aurī atque sanguinis, nōn modo magnam pecūniam, sed etiam hominēs vīvōs ab Athēniēnsibus postulāverat.","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"latin":"Ad hōc Syrā \"Ergō\" inquit, \"quoniam tam cupidus es audiendī, reliquam tabulam tibi nārrābō:","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"cur?","latin":"cūr?","headword":"cūr?","letter":"c","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"why?","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia Quīntum interrogat: 'Cūr Iūlia plōrat?'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"curare","latin":"cūrāre","headword":"cūrāre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"care for; look after; to care for; see to it that","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī aeger erit, ipsa eum cūrābō tōtamque noctem apud eum vigilābō; nēmō īnfantem aegrum tam bene cūrāre potest quam māter ipsa.\"","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"curia","latin":"cūria, -ae","headword":"cūria","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"senate-house","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūxtā basilicam Aemiliam, in eā forī parte quae dīcitur Comitium, locāta est Cūria, id est aedificium quō senātus Rōmānus convenīre solet.","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"currit","latin":"currit","headword":"currit","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"runs","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Currite in hortum, puerī, et vocāte eam!' Quīntus currit.","reading":"ROSA IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"latin":"Dum pāstor in herbā dormit, ovis nigra ab ovibus albīs abit et ad rīvum currit.","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"curvus","latin":"curvus, -a, -um","headword":"curvus","letter":"c","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"curved; bending","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"custodia","latin":"custōdia, -ae","headword":"custōdia","letter":"c","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"guard; custody","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed nec dī nec hominēs aut ipsam aut fīliōs ā crūdēlitāte rēgis dēfendunt: Amūlius Vestālem vīnctam in custōdiam dat, puerōs in fluvium mittī iubet.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"custodire","latin":"cūstōdīre","headword":"cūstōdīre","letter":"c","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to guard","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Servus cuius officium est forēs aperīre et claudere ac vīllam dominī cūstōdīre, ōstiārius vel iānitor appellātur.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"custos","latin":"custōs, custōdis","headword":"custōs","letter":"c","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"guard; watchman","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"dactylus","latin":"dactylus","headword":"dactylus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dactyl (– ˘ ˘)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"daedalus","latin":"Daedalus","headword":"Daedalus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"Daedalus; the craftsman","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum rēx īrātus cēpit Daedalum, quī fīlum cōnfēcerat et Ariadnae dederat, eumque in labyrinthum inclūdī iussit ūna cum eius Īcarō fīliō; vērum pater et fīlius mīrābilī modō ē labyrinthō fūgērunt.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"dapes","latin":"dapēs, -um","headword":"dapēs","letter":"d","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"feast; rich food","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"dat","latin":"dat","headword":"dat","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"gives","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius mālum ē saccō sūmit et sē vertit ad Mārcum: 'Ecce mālum tuum, Mārce.' Iūlius Mārcō mālum dat.","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"dativus","latin":"datīvus","headword":"datīvus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dative","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Cāsus nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Sex.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Nōminātīvus, genetīvus, dativus, accūsātīvus, vocātīvus, ablātīvus.","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"dea","latin":"dea","headword":"dea","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"goddess","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nēmō deōrum peior marītus est quam Iuppiter, neque ūlla dea peior uxor est quam Venus.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"debet","latin":"dēbet","headword":"dēbet","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"owes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia: 'Cūr nōn solvis pecūniam quae magistrō dēbētur?","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"decem","latin":"decem","headword":"decem","letter":"d","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"ten","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"declamitare","latin":"dēclāmitāre","headword":"dēclāmitāre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to practise declamation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Commentābar dēclāmitāns — sīc enim nunc loquimur — idque faciēbam multum etiam Latīnē, sed Graecē saepius, vel quod Graeca ōrātiō plūra ōrnāmenta suppeditāns cōnsuētūdinem similiter Latīnē dīcendī afferēbat, vel quod ā Graecīs summīs doctōribus, Graecē dīcerem, neque corrigī possem neque docērī.'","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"declinare","latin":"dēclīnāre","headword":"dēclīnāre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to decline; inflect","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Per hōs omnium generum nōmina, prōnōmina, participia dēclīnantur.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"declinatio","latin":"dēclīnātiō","headword":"dēclīnātiō","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"declension","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"decor","latin":"decor, -ōris","headword":"decor","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"beauty; grace","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum hīs verbīs sē āvertēns dīvīnō decōre fulsit.","reading":"VENUS GENETRĪX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"decorus","latin":"decōrus, -a, -um","headword":"decōrus","letter":"d","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"handsome; comely","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"decus","latin":"decus, -oris","headword":"decus","letter":"d","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"honour; glory; ornament","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Posteā inter tot annōs, tot bella, bīna tantum spolia opīma capta sunt: adeō rāra fuit fortūna id decus adipīscendī.","reading":"SPOLIA OPIMA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"decutere","latin":"dēcutere","headword":"dēcutere","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to strike off; knock down","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"dedecus","latin":"dēdecus, -oris","headword":"dēdecus","letter":"d","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"disgrace; shame","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ubi obstinātam vidēbat neque mortis quidem metū inclīnārī, addit ad metum dēdecus: cum mortuā iugulātum servum nūdum positūrum sē esse, ut in sordidō adulteriō necāta dīcerētur!","reading":"LŪCRĒTIA VIOLĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"deducere","latin":"dēdūcere","headword":"dēdūcere","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to lead down; draw off","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In eā valle ōlim magna palūs erat, quae tum dēmum siccāta est cum aqua palūdis in flūmen dēdūcerētur per cloācam subterrāneam, quae appellātur \"cloāca Maxima\".","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"deesse","latin":"deesse","headword":"deesse","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to fail; be lacking (+ dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"defendere","latin":"dēfendere","headword":"dēfendere","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to defend","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Baebium in Āfricam mittunt ad percontandōs Carthāginiēnsēs 'pūblicōne cōnsiliō Hannibal Saguntum oppugnāsset?' et, sī (id quod factūrī vidēbantur) fatērentur ac dēfenderent pūblicō cōnsiliō factum, ut indīcerent populō Carthāginiēnsī bellum.","reading":"EXCIDIVM SAGVNTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"defendit","latin":"dēfendit","headword":"dēfendit","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"defends","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum exercitus Germānōrum castra oppugnat, Rōmānī castra dēfendunt: vallum ascendunt ac pīla in Germānōs iaciunt.","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"defendo","latin":"dēfendō","headword":"dēfendō","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to defend","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vesperī exercitūs locō ad dēfendendum idōneō castrā pōnit, quae vāllō et fossā circumdantur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"defensor","latin":"dēfēnsor, -ōris","headword":"dēfēnsor","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"defender","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aenēās vērō, cupidus cīvibus inclūsīs auxilium ferendī, per forēs occultās in rēgiam penetrat atque dēfēnsōribus sē adiungit.","reading":"MORS PRIAMĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"deferre","latin":"deferre","headword":"deferre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to carry down; drive off course","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"deiurare","latin":"dēiūrāre","headword":"dēiūrāre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to swear by","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In veteribus scrīptīs neque mulierēs Rōmānae per Herculem dēiūrant neque virī per Castorem.","reading":"DĒ IVRE IVRANDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"delectantur","latin":"dēlectantur","headword":"dēlectantur","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"are delighted (with)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Multae fēminae quae in hāc viā ambulant ante tabernam Albīnī cōnsistunt, nam fēminae ōrnāmentīs dēlectantur.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"delectat","latin":"dēlectat","headword":"dēlectat","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"delights; pleases","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vidēte rosās meās!\" Iūlia laeta est, rosae eam dēlectant.","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"\"Audāx quidem est cōnsilium tuum\" inquit Īcarus, \"sed omne cōnsilium fugiendī mē dēlectat, ac tū id quod semel excōgitāvistī perficere solēs.\"","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"delet","latin":"dēlet","headword":"dēlet","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"erases; deletes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēlē illam litteram!' Mārcus stilum vertit et litteram H dēlet.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"deliberatio","latin":"dēlīberātiō, -ōnis","headword":"dēlīberātiō","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"deliberation; debate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Utinam, Quirītēs, virōrum fortium atque innocentium cōpiam tantam habērētis ut haec vōbīs dēlīberātiō difficilis esset, quemnam potissimum tantīs rēbus ac tantō bellō praeficiendum putārētis!","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"deliciae","latin":"dēliciae","headword":"dēliciae","letter":"d","pos":"noun (f. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"darling; pet; delight","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lucernis accensis, Iulius librum Catulli proferri iubet, tum \"Incipiam\" inquit \"a carmine de morte passeris quem Lesbia in deliciis habuerat:","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"delictum","latin":"dēlictum, -ī","headword":"dēlictum","letter":"d","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fault; crime","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cōnsōlantur aegram animī āvertendō noxam ab coāctā in auctōrem dēlictī: 'mentem peccāre, nōn corpus, et unde cōnsilium fūerit, culpam abesse.' 'Vōs' inquit 'vīderitis quid illī dēbeātur!","reading":"RĒGĒS EXĀCTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"delphinus","latin":"delphīnus","headword":"delphīnus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dolphin","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At certē nōn tam fēlīx eris quam Arīōn, quī delphīnō servātus est.\"","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"demens","latin":"dēmēns, -entis","headword":"dēmēns","letter":"d","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"mad; out of one's mind","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In lītus ēiectum, egentem tē excēpī et — dēmēns — partem rēgnī dedī, classem āmissam restituī, sociōs ā morte servāvī!","reading":"QUERELLA DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"demonstrare","latin":"dēmōnstrāre","headword":"dēmōnstrāre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to show; prove","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Posteā Chrīstus ipse plānē dēmōnstrāvit sē esse fīlium Deī, nam discipulōs docēbat, quōrum magna turba eum sequēbātur, aegrōsque sānābat...\"","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA IN NĀVĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"denarius","latin":"dēnārius","headword":"dēnārius","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"denarius (a Roman coin)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister, quī verba Mārcī nōn audit, ex sacculō suō duōs nummōs prōmit, assem et dēnārium, et 'Ecce' inquit nummōs ostendēns, 'as et dēnārius.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"dens","latin":"dēns","headword":"dēns","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tooth","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn sānus est dēns quī colōrem nigrum habet.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"depellere","latin":"dēpellere","headword":"dēpellere","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to drive off; repel","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"deponens","latin":"dēpōnens","headword":"dēpōnens","letter":"d","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"deponent","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Genera verbōrum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Quattuor.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Āctīva, passīva, neutra, dēpōnentia.'","reading":"DĒ VERBŌ ET ADVERBIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"deridere","latin":"dērīdēre","headword":"dērīdēre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to mock; laugh at","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Prōcēde in vīllam!\" Sīc iānitor virum territum dērīdet.","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"desciscere","latin":"dēscīscere","headword":"dēscīscere","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to desert; revolt","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"deserit","latin":"dēserit","headword":"dēserit","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"abandons; deserts","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"desiderium","latin":"dēsīderium, -ī","headword":"dēsīderium","letter":"d","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"longing; desire","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Noster autem exercitus, tametsī urbem ex Tigrānis rēgnō cēperat et proeliīs ūsus erat secundīs, tamen nimiā longinquitāte locōrum ac dēsīderiō suōrum commovēbātur.","reading":"DĒ MAGNITŪDINE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"desilit","latin":"dēsilit","headword":"dēsilit","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"jumps down","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hoc sōlum precor!\" Nautae precibus eius ita permōtī sunt ut manūs quidem ab eō abstinērent; sed tamen imperāvērunt ut statim in mare dēsilīret!","reading":"FĀBVLA ARĪONIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"desinit","latin":"dēsinit","headword":"dēsinit","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"stops; ceases","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēsine, magister!' Magister puerum verberāre dēsinit et 'Ad sellam tuam redī!' inquit, 'atque cōnsīde!'","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"despicio","latin":"dēspiciō","headword":"dēspiciō","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to despise; look down on","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed tum litterās et studiōsōs litterārum dēspiciēbam.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"despicit","latin":"dēspicit","headword":"dēspicit","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"looks down on","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Īcarus dēspiciēns multitūdinem īnsulārum mīrātus est: \"Ō, quot parvae īnsulae in marī ingentī sunt!\" Daedalus vērō \"Illae īnsulae\" inquit \"haud parvae sunt, quamquam parvae esse videntur.","reading":"ĪCARVS IN MARE CADIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"deterrere","latin":"dēterrēre","headword":"dēterrēre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to deter; frighten off","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nē servō quidem iniūriam facere oportet, sed necesse est servōs īnfīdōs aut fugitīvōs sevērē pūnīre; nec enim quidquam nisi poena sevēra eius generis servōs ā maleficiīs dēterrēre atque in officiō tenēre potest.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"detrimentum","latin":"dētrīmentum, -ī","headword":"dētrīmentum","letter":"d","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"loss; damage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic, clausus locōrum angustiīs, noctū sine ūllō dētrīmentō exercitūs sē expedīvit, Fabiōque, callidissimō imperātōrī, dedit verba.","reading":"BELLA IN ĪTALIĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"deus","latin":"deus","headword":"deus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"god","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mercurius nōn homō, sed deus est.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Nam ego adsum, quamquam nec videor nec audior.' Deus ab hominibus nec vidētur nec audītur.","reading":"NAVTAE ET NEPTŪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"dexter","latin":"dexter","headword":"dexter","letter":"d","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"right; on the right","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puer territus pedēs nōdōs aspicit et 'Quid hoc est?' inquit; 'Pēs dexter multō maior est quam pēs laevus!'","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"dictator","latin":"dictātor, -ōris","headword":"dictātor","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dictator; commander with royal power","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Albānī Mettium Fūfētium dictātōrem creant.","reading":"TVLLVS HOSTILIVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"dictatura","latin":"dictātūra, -ae","headword":"dictātūra","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dictatorship","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōnō annō post rēgēs exāctōs, cum gener Tarquinī ad iniūriam socerī vindicandam ingentem collēgisset exercitum, nova Rōmae dignitās est creāta, quae dictātūra appellātur, maior quam cōnsulātus.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"dictitare","latin":"dictitāre","headword":"dictitāre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to say repeatedly; keep saying","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inde Tarquinius regnāre coepit, cui 'Superbō' cognōmen datum est, quia socerum suum sepelīrī prohibuit, 'Rōmulum quoque īnsēpultum periisse' dictitāns, et quōs Serviī rēbus favisse crēdēbat interēmit.","reading":"L. IŪNIUS BRŪTUS, LĪBERĀTOR POPULĪ RŌMĀNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"dies","latin":"diēs","headword":"diēs","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"day","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ūnus annus duodecim mēnsēs vel trecentōs sexāgintā quīnque diēs habet.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"difficilis","latin":"difficilis","headword":"difficilis","letter":"d","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"difficult; hard","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus: 'At id quod ego interrogor nimis difficile est.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"difficultas","latin":"difficultās, -ātis","headword":"difficultās","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"difficulty","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīs difficultātibus circumventus, ubi videt neque per vim neque īnsidiīs opprimī posse hominem tam acceptum populāribus, quod erat Iugurtha manū prōmptus et appetēns glōriae mīlitāris, statuit eum obiectāre perīculīs et eō modō fortūnam temptāre.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"digitus","latin":"digitus","headword":"digitus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"finger","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ānulus digitum Aemiliae ōrnat, margarītae collum eius ōrnant.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"dilacerare","latin":"dīlacerāre","headword":"dīlacerāre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to tear apart; rip to pieces","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ita omnia in duās partēs abstracta sunt, rēs pūblica, quae media fuerat, dīlacerāta.","reading":"CĪVITĀS DĪLACERĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"dilectus","latin":"dīlēctus, -ūs","headword":"dīlēctus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"levy; recruiting; recruitment","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hadrūmētī reliquōs ē fugā collēgit, novīs dīlēctibus paucīs diēbus multōs contrāxit.","reading":"ZAMA ET FVGA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"},{"latin":"Gulussa, Masinissae filius, nūntiāvit 'Carthāgine dīlēctūs agī, classem comparārī et haud dubiē bellum struī.' Cum Catō suādēret ut hīs bellum indīcerētur, P.","reading":"BELLVM PVNICVM TERTIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"diligere","latin":"dīligere","headword":"dīligere","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"love; cherish; to love; be fond of","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"dimicatio","latin":"dīmicātiō, -ōnis","headword":"dīmicātiō","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fight; struggle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Priusquam dīmicārent, foedus ictum est inter Rōmānōs et Albānōs hīs lēgibus, ut cuius populī cīvēs eō certāmine vīcissent, is alterī populō cum bonā pāce imperitāret.","reading":"TRIGEMINORVM PVGNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"discedit","latin":"discēdit","headword":"discēdit","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"leaves; departs; goes away","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Sūme sacculum tuum et discēde, bone serve!' Dāvus sacculum suum sūmit et discēdit.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Iūlia rosās pulchrās in hortō videt et ab Aemiliā discēdit.","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"discere","latin":"discere","headword":"discere","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"learn","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"discernere","latin":"discernere","headword":"discernere","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to distinguish; discern","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Palīnūrus, optimus gubernātor, rēctum cursum tenēre nōn poterat neque diem noctemque discernere, cum nec sōl interdiū nec stēllae noctū appārērent.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"discipulus","latin":"discipulus","headword":"discipulus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pupil; student; disciple","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus magistrum metuit, Diodōrus enim magister sevērus est, quī discipulōs suōs virga verberat; eō modo magister sevērus discipulōs improbōs pūnīre solet.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"latin":"Discipulus quī nec stultus nec piger est, sed prūdēns atque industrius, multās rēs ā magistrō discere potest.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"discit","latin":"discit","headword":"discit","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"learns","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"disco","latin":"discō","headword":"discō","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"learn","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī paulum aut nihil discere potest, stultus esse dīcitur.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"discrimen","latin":"discrīmen, -inis","headword":"discrīmen","letter":"d","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"crisis; danger; distinction; difference","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Per variōs cāsūs, per tot discrīmina rērum tendimus in Latium, sedēs ubi fāta quietās ostendunt: illīc fās regna resurgere Trōiae.","reading":"LĪTUS ĀFRICAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"latin":"Quoniam geminī erant nec aetātis discrīmen inter eōs fierī poterat, necesse fuit deōs cōnsulere.","reading":"RŌMA CONDITA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"disertus","latin":"disertus, -a, -um","headword":"disertus","letter":"d","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"eloquent","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ōrātor omnium quī Rōmae fuērunt disertissimus M.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"disputatio","latin":"disputātiō, -ōnis","headword":"disputātiō","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"discussion; argument","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed possumus audīre aliquid, an sērius vēnimus?' [Philus:] 'Nihil est adhūc disputātum, et, quoniam disputāre integrum est, libenter tibi, Laelī, dē eō dissertāre concesserō.' [Laelius:] 'Immō vērō tē audiāmus.'","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"diuturnitas","latin":"diuturnitās, -ātis","headword":"diuturnitās","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"long duration","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Et placuit nē imperium longius quam annuum habērent, nē per diuturnitātem potestātis īnsolentiōrēs redderentur, sed civīlēs semper essent, quī sē post annum scīrent futūrōs esse prīvātōs.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"dives","latin":"dīves","headword":"dīves","letter":"d","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"rich","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pater Iūliī, quī iam mortuus est, magnam pecūniam habēbat multāsque vīllās magnificās possidēbat praeter domum Rōmānam: is homō dīves erat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"latin":"Iūlius aspicit agricolās quī in agrīs et in vīneīs opus faciunt, gaudēns quod ipse, ut dominus dīves, in agrīs nōn labōrat.","reading":"VĪNEAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"divisio","latin":"dīvīsiō, -ōnis","headword":"dīvīsiō","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"division; distribution","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In dīvīsiōne, quae pars Numidiae Mauretaniam attingit, agrō virīsque opulentior, Iugurthae trāditur; illam alteram, quae portuōsior et aedificiīs magis exōrnāta erat, Adherbal possēdit.","reading":"ADHERBAL RŌMAM PROFĪCĪSCITUR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"divitiae","latin":"dīvitiae","headword":"dīvitiae","letter":"d","pos":"noun (f. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"riches; wealth","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Subitō mercātor ē dīvitissimō pauperrimus factus est.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"divortium","latin":"dīvortium, -ī","headword":"dīvortium","letter":"d","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"divorce","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Carvīlius Rūga prīmus Rōmae dē amīcōrum sententiā dīvortium cum uxōre fēcit, quod matrimōniō sterilis esset iūrāssetque apud cēnsōrēs 'uxōrem sē līberum quaerundōrum causā habēre'; eōdemque annō Cn.","reading":"PHILIPPVS ĀD LŪCĪLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"doceo","latin":"doceō","headword":"doceō","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"teach","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"docet","latin":"docet","headword":"docet","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"teaches","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister, quī puerōs legere docet, ipse et librōs Latīnōs et Graecōs legere potest, nam is utramque linguam scit.","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"doctor","latin":"doctor, -ōris","headword":"doctor","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"teacher","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Atque hōc Sōsilō Hannibal litterārum Graecārum ūsus est doctōre.","reading":"DĒ SCRĪPTŌRIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"doctus","latin":"doctus","headword":"doctus","letter":"d","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"learned; skilled","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister est vir doctus; puerī adhūc indoctī sunt.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"latin":"Magister: 'Comparātiōnis gradūs quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Trēs.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Positīvus, ut doctus; comparātīvus, ut doctior; superlātīvus, ut doctissimus.' Magister: 'Quae nōmina comparantur?' Discipulus: 'Appellātīva dumtaxat quālitātem aut quantitātem significantiā.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"dolere","latin":"dolēre","headword":"dolēre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to hurt; ache","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque ē lectō surgere cōnātur, sed pēs dēnuō dolēre incipit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"dolet","latin":"dolet","headword":"dolet","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"hurts; gives pain; causes pain","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus: 'Sed dēns nōn dolet; ergō dēns aeger nōn est.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Quīntus dormīre nōn potest, quod et caput et pēs eī dolet.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"dolus","latin":"dolus, -ī","headword":"dolus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"trick; stratagem","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"domina","latin":"domina","headword":"domina","letter":"d","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mistress; lady","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia domina Dēliae est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"dominatus","latin":"dominātus, -ūs","headword":"dominātus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rule; domination","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed et in rēgnīs nimis expertēs sunt cēterī commūnis iūris et cōnsiliī; et in optimātium dominātū vix particeps lībertātis potest esse multitūdō, cum omnī cōnsiliō commūnī ac potestāte careat; et cum omnia per populum geruntur, quamvīs iūstum atque moderātum, tamen ipsa aequābilitās est inīqua, cum habet nūllōs gradūs dignitātis...'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"dominus","latin":"dominus","headword":"dominus","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"master; lord","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius dominus Mēdī est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Dāvus, quī dominum suum nōn videt, Mēdum interrogat: 'Quid est, Mēde?'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"donum","latin":"dōnum","headword":"dōnum","letter":"d","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gift","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Num opus est mē plūs dīcere?' Amor dōnum est Veneris.","reading":"AMOR IŪLIĪ ET AEMILIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"dormire","latin":"dormīre","headword":"dormīre","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sleep","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vix ūnam hōram dormīre poterimus, sī īnfāns vāgiet.","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"dormit","latin":"dormit","headword":"dormit","letter":"d","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sleeps","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Respondet Mārcus: 'Pater dormit.'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Quīntus in cubiculō parvō dormit.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"duae","latin":"duae","headword":"duae","letter":"d","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"two (fem.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēlia et Syra duae ancillae sunt.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"ductor","latin":"ductor, -ōris","headword":"ductor","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"leader","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mettius ille est ductor itineris huius, Mettius īdem huius auctor bellī, Mettius foederis Rōmānī Albānīque ruptor!\"","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"dulcis","latin":"dulcis","headword":"dulcis","letter":"d","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"sweet","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"dum","latin":"dum","headword":"dum","letter":"d","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"while; as long as; until","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ergō vōs hōram tōtam tacitī stāte, dum ego sedēns partem librī posteriōrem recitō!","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ DORMIENTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"latin":"Dum ille vestem novam induit, Cornēlius et Orontēs et hospitēs eius cum uxōribus Fabiā et Paulā adveniunt. (Hospitēs sunt amīcī quōrum alter alterum bene recipit domum suam, etiam sī inexspectātī vēnerint.) Hodiē autem hospitēs Iūliī exspectātī veniunt, nam eōs vocāvit ad cēnam. (Cēna est cibus quem circiter hōrā nōnā vel decimā sūmunt.)","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"duo","latin":"duo","headword":"duo","letter":"d","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"two","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"duodecim","latin":"duodecim","headword":"duodecim","letter":"d","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"twelve","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In mūrō Rōmānō duodecim portae sunt.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Annus in duodecim mēnsēs dīviditur, quibus haec sunt nōmina: Iānuārius, mēnsis prīmus; Februārius, secundus; Mārtius, tertius; Aprīlis, quārtus; Maius, quīntus; Iūnius, sextus; Iūlius, septimus; Augustus, octāvus; September, nōnus; Octōber, decimus; November, ūndecimus; December, mēnsis duodecimus ac postrēmus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"duodequadraginta","latin":"duodēquadrāgintā","headword":"duodēquadrāgintā","letter":"d","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"thirty-eight","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trīgintā et octō sunt duodēquadrāgintā.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"duodequinquaginta","latin":"duodequinquāgintā","headword":"duodequinquāgintā","letter":"d","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"forty-eight","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trīgintā et octō sunt duodēquadrāgintā.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"duumviri","latin":"duumvirī, -ōrum","headword":"duumvirī","letter":"d","pos":"noun m. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"two men appointed as judges","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēx, nē ipse rem tam trīstem iūdicāret ac secundum iūdicium suppliciī auctor esset, cōnsiliō populī advocātō, \"Duumvirōs\" inquit, \"quī Horātiō perduelliōnem iūdicent, secundum lēgem faciō.\" Horrenda lēgis verba haec erant: \"Duumvirī perduelliōnem iūdicent.","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"dux","latin":"dux","headword":"dux","letter":"d","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"leader; commander","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī exercitum dūcit dux exercitus est.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Ante proelium dux exercitiīs mīlitēs suōs hortātur ut fortiter pugnent.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"eam","latin":"eam","headword":"eam","letter":"e","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"her (acc.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus respondet: 'Iūlia plōrat, quia Mārcus eam pulsat.'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"ebrius","latin":"ēbrius","headword":"ēbrius","letter":"e","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"drunk","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nimium pōtāvistī, ēbrius es.","reading":"INTER PŌCVLA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"ecce!","latin":"ecce!","headword":"ecce!","letter":"e","pos":"interjection","posGroup":"interjection","english":"look! here is!","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"edepol","latin":"edepol","headword":"edepol","letter":"e","pos":"interjection","posGroup":"interjection","english":"by Pollux!","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nusquam igitur scrīptum invenīre est — apud idōneōs quidem scrīptōrēs — aut 'mehercle' fēminam dīcere aut 'mecastor' virum; 'edepol' autem, quod iūs iūrandum per Pollūcem est, et virō et fēminae commūne est.","reading":"DĒ IVRE IVRANDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"edit","latin":"ēdit","headword":"ēdit","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"eats","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aquila est magna avis fera, quae parvās avēs capit et ēdit.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"efferre","latin":"efferre","headword":"efferre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to carry out; lift up","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aenēās vērō, rūrsus armīs sūmptīs, \"Mēne putās\" inquit \"tē relictō pedem hinc efferre posse?","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"effigies","latin":"effigiēs, -ēī","headword":"effigiēs","letter":"e","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"image; likeness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rogō ingentī in rēgiā ērēctō, rēgīna locum flōribus et fronde exōrnat; super rogum exuviās et ēnsem relictum effigiemque Aenēae in torō locat.","reading":"ROGUS DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"effugit","latin":"effugit","headword":"effugit","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"escapes; flees from","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"egens","latin":"egēns, -entis","headword":"egēns","letter":"e","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"needy; destitute","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ipse ignōtus, egēns per Libyam errō ex Eurōpā atque Asiā pulsus…'","reading":"VENUS GENETRĪX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"ego","latin":"ego","headword":"ego","letter":"e","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"I","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister interrogat: 'Cūr tū sōlus es, Sexte?' 'Ego sōlus sum, quod cēterī discipulī omnēs absunt,' respondet Sextus.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"egredi","latin":"ēgredī","headword":"ēgredī","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to go out; leave","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nautae nec marī turbidō nec marī tranquillō nāvigāre possunt; itaque in portū ventum secundum opperiuntur. (Ventus secundus est ventus quī ā tergō flat.) Ventō secundō nāvēs ē portū ēgrediuntur: vēla ventō implentur ac nāvēs plēnīs vēlīs per mare vehuntur.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"egreditur","latin":"ēgreditur","headword":"ēgreditur","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"goes out; leaves","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"egressus","latin":"ēgressus, -ūs","headword":"ēgressus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"going out; departure","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Bomilcar mātūre rēgis mandāta exsequitur, et per hominēs tālis negōtiī artificēs itinera ēgressūsque eius, postrēmō loca atque tempora cūncta explōrat; deinde, ubi rēs postulābat, īnsidiās tendit.","reading":"IVGVRTHA RŌMAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"elephantus","latin":"elephantus, -ī","headword":"elephantus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"elephant","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Commissā mox pugnā, cum iam Pyrrhus fugeret, elephantōrum auxiliō vīcit, quōs incognitōs Rōmānī expāvērunt.","reading":"PYRRHUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"eligere","latin":"ēligere","headword":"ēligere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to choose; pick out","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ex malīs minimum ēligere oportet.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"elucubrare","latin":"ēlūcubrāre","headword":"ēlūcubrāre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to polish by night; work over","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deinceps inde multae, quās nōs dīligenter ēlabōrātās et tamquam ēlūcubrātās afferēbāmus.'","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"eluvio","latin":"ēluviō, -ōnis","headword":"ēluviō","letter":"e","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"flood; deluge","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīn etiam sī cupiat prōlēs illa futūrōrum hominum deinceps laudēs ūnius cuiusque nostrum ā patribus acceptās posterīs prōdere, tamen propter ēluviōnēs exustiōnēsque terrārum, quās accidere tempore certō necesse est, nōn modo nōn aeternam, sed nē dīturnam quidem glōriam assequī possumus.'","reading":"ANGUSTIAE TERRĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"emit","latin":"emit","headword":"emit","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"buys","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Emite ōrnāmenta!\"","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"emptor","latin":"emptor, -ōris","headword":"emptor","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"buyer","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed postquam Rōmā ēgressus est, fertur saepe eō tacitūs respiciēns postrēmō dīxisse: 'urbem vēnālem et mātūre peritūram, sī emptōrem invēnerit!'","reading":"IVGVRTHA RŌMAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"epigramma","latin":"epigramma","headword":"epigramma","letter":"e","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"epigram","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum vero Cornelius \"Bene quidem\" inquit \"et iocose scripsit Catullus, nec tamen versus eius comparandi sunt cum epigrammatis sale plenis quae Martialis in inimicos scripsit.","reading":"DĒ MĀRTIĀLĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"epistula","latin":"epistula","headword":"epistula","letter":"e","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"letter (message); letter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Cum pater tuus abest, oportet tē epistulās ad eum scrībere.'","reading":"EPISTVLA AD PATREM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"latin":"Iūlius cotīdiē epistulās ad Aemiliam scrībēbat, in quibus pulchritūdō eius laudābātur verbīs magnificīs, ac cum epistulīs rosās aliōsque flōrēs pulcherrimōs eī mittere solēbat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"eques","latin":"eques, equitis","headword":"eques","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"horseman; cavalryman","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Aemilius pīlum tantum fert, is enim pedēs est, nōn eques.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"[Ex Periochā librī XXI:] Hannibal, superātō Pyrēnaeō saltū, per Galliam ad Alpēs vēnit, et labōriōsō per eās trānsitū dēscendit in Ītaliam, et ad Tīcīnum flūmen Rōmānōs equestrī proeliō fūdit; in quō vulnerātum P.","reading":"ITER HANNIBALIS IN ĪTALIAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"equitatus","latin":"equitātus, -ūs","headword":"equitātus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cavalry","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hāc igitur, quā dīximus, aetāte cum patre in Hispāniam profectus est, cuius post obitum, Hasdrubale imperātōre suffectō, equitātuī omnī praefuit.","reading":"IN HISPĀNIAM ET AD ALPĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"equus","latin":"equus","headword":"equus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"horse","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Equus quī Cornēlium vehit pulcher est.","reading":"MĒDVS ET CORNĒLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"error","latin":"error, -ōris","headword":"error","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wandering; error","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quaecumque es, sīs nōbīs fēlīx et doceās nōs quō sub caelō et quibus in ōrīs versēmur; namque ignārī et hominum et locōrum errāmus, postquam ventō et fluctibus hūc āctī sumus.","reading":"VENUS GENETRĪX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"erubescere","latin":"ērubēscere","headword":"ērubēscere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to blush; grow red","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hoc audiens erubescit Paula atque ceteri convivae risum vix tenent.","reading":"DĒ MĀRTIĀLĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"esse","latin":"esse","headword":"esse","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to be (ero; eris; erit)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"est","latin":"est","headword":"est","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rōma in Italiā est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"et","latin":"et","headword":"et","letter":"e","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"and","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Italia et Graecia in Eurōpā sunt.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"etiam","latin":"etiam","headword":"etiam","letter":"e","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"also; even","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fīliī, quī iam nōn sōlum māla, sed etiam pira habent, laetī sunt.","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"eum","latin":"eum","headword":"eum","letter":"e","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"him (acc.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius eum nōn audit, quia dormit.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"eurus","latin":"Eurus, -ī","headword":"Eurus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"east wind","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aeolus, ubi haec audīvit, cavum montem hastā impellit, ac ventī velut agmine factō ex antrō ruunt: Eurus Notusque et Africus terrās mariaque turbant et vastōs fluctūs ad lītora volvunt.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"eventus","latin":"ēventus, -ūs","headword":"ēventus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"outcome","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Licinius Crassus cōnsul, cui mandātum erat, in Macedoniam trānsiit, levibusque expedītiōnibus, equestribus proeliīs, in Thessaliā cum Perseō, quem Cotys, rēx Thrāciae, adiuvābat, parum prosperō ēventū pugnāvit.","reading":"PERSEVS VICTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"evertere","latin":"ēvertere","headword":"ēvertere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to overthrow; demolish","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"evocare","latin":"ēvocāre","headword":"ēvocāre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to call out; summon","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ex / e","latin":"ex / e","headword":"ex / e","letter":"e","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"out of; from (+ abl.); from","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"exagitare","latin":"exagitāre","headword":"exagitāre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to harass; drive about","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Marcius Coriolānus, exagitātus vexātusque ā tribūnīs plēbis, ad Volscōs, quī tum hostēs erant, ā rē pūblicā dēscīvit bellumque populō Rōmānō fēcit.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"excedere","latin":"excēdere","headword":"excēdere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to leave; go out (with abl.)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quod cum Trōiānī profugī cognōvissent, cito ē terrā scelerātā excēdere cōnstituērunt.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"excellens","latin":"excellēns, -entis","headword":"excellēns","letter":"e","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"outstanding; excellent","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"excerpere","latin":"excerpere","headword":"excerpere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to pick out; excerpt","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"excessus","latin":"excessus, -ūs","headword":"excessus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"departure; death","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Sīc ille, cum ūndēquādrāgintā annōs summā in pāce concordiāque rēgnāvisset (sequāmur enim potissimum Polybium nostrum, quō nēmō fuit in exquīrendīs temporibus dīligentior), excessit ē vītā, duābus praeclārissimīs ad dīturnitātem reī pūblicae rēbus cōnfirmātīs: religiōne atque clēmentiā.'","reading":"DĒ VETERE RĒ PŪBLICĀ RŌMĀNĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"excitat","latin":"excitat","headword":"excitat","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"wakes; rouses","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus ad puerum dormientem adit eumque excitat.","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"excusat","latin":"excūsat","headword":"excūsat","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"excuses","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus sē et Titum excūsāre cōnātur: \"At pugnāvimus cum puerō maiōre.","reading":"MARCVS Ā PATRE INTERROGĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"exemplum","latin":"exemplum","headword":"exemplum","letter":"e","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"example","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus: 'Quārē igitur tot numerōs difficilēs discimus?' Magister: 'Quia necesse est computāre scīre, ut multīs exemplīs tibi dēmōnstrāre possum.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"exercitus","latin":"exercitus, -ūs","headword":"exercitus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"army","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Germānī exercitum nostrum oppugnant.'","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Exercitus Rōmānus ūniversus cōnstat ex legiōnibus duodētrīgintā, quae in dēnās cohortēs dīviduntur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"exhaurire","latin":"exhaurīre","headword":"exhaurīre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to drain; empty","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ergō pōcula exhaurīte, amīcī!","reading":"CĒNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"exiguus","latin":"exiguus","headword":"exiguus","letter":"e","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"small; scanty","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"exitus","latin":"exitus","headword":"exitus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"exit; way out","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"exornare","latin":"exōrnāre","headword":"exōrnāre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to decorate; adorn","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic Aemilia 'Necesse est' inquit 'paulisper famem sitimque ferre, dum cibus coquitur et trīclīnium exōrnātur.'","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"exorsus","latin":"exōrsus, -ūs","headword":"exōrsus","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"beginning; opening","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dē vestrī imperiī dignitāte atque glōriā, quoniam is est exōrsus ōrātiōnis meae, vidēte quem vōbīs animum suscipiendum putētis.","reading":"DĒ GENERE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"expeditio","latin":"expedītiō, -ōnis","headword":"expedītiō","letter":"e","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"expedition","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Licinius Crassus cōnsul, cui mandātum erat, in Macedoniam trānsiit, levibusque expedītiōnibus, equestribus proeliīs, in Thessaliā cum Perseō, quem Cotys, rēx Thrāciae, adiuvābat, parum prosperō ēventū pugnāvit.","reading":"PERSEVS VICTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"experiri","latin":"experīrī","headword":"experīrī","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to try; experience","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Praestat tōtam Siciliam longō cursū circumīre quam semel Scyllam īnfōrmem vidēre et saxa illa resonantia experīrī.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"expetere","latin":"expetere","headword":"expetere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to seek; demand","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"explicare","latin":"explicāre","headword":"explicāre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to disentangle; free oneself; to free; extricate; to explain","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ille simul manibus sē explicāre cōnātur, simul clāmōrēs horrendōs ad caelum tollit.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"},{"latin":"Quā oppugnātiōne cum neglēctōs ab ūnā parte mūrōs duo tribūnī temere cum cohortibus suīs irrūpissent et ab oppidānīs graviter caederentur, ā Scīpiōne Aemiliānō explicātī sunt.","reading":"BELLVM PVNICVM TERTIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"explorator","latin":"explōrātor, -ōris","headword":"explōrātor","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"scout; spy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Valerius Laevīnus, quī cum explōrātōrēs Pyrrhī cēpisset, iussit eōs per castra ūt dūcī, ostendī omnem exercitum, tumque dīminī renūntiārent Pyrrhō quaecumque ā Rōmānīs agerentur.","reading":"PYRRHUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"expugnare","latin":"expugnāre","headword":"expugnāre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to storm; take by assault","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cartalam, urbem opulentam, caput gentis eius, expugnat dīripitque.","reading":"HANNIBAL IMPERĀTOR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"expugnat","latin":"expugnat","headword":"expugnat","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"storms; captures","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hostēs castra nostra expugnāre nōn possunt.'","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"exsequiae","latin":"exsequiae, -ārum","headword":"exsequiae","letter":"e","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"funeral; funeral rites","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vtque vident habitum, 'Quae lūctūs causa?' requīrunt, 'Cui paret exsequiās, quōve sit icta malō?' Illa diū reticet pudibundaque cēlat amictū ōra; fluunt lacrimae more perennis aquae.","reading":"HOSTIS PRŌ HOSPITE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"exsilium","latin":"exsilium, -iī","headword":"exsilium","letter":"e","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"exile","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ut plūribus metum iniceret, iūdicia per sē sōlus exercēbat, perque eam causam occīdere aut exsiliō agere poterat nōn suspectōs modo aut invīsōs, sed etiam eōs unde nihil aliud quam praedam spērāre posset.","reading":"L. IŪNIUS BRŪTUS, LĪBERĀTOR POPULĪ RŌMĀNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"exsistere","latin":"exsistere","headword":"exsistere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to arise; emerge","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec cōnstitūtiō prīmum habet aequābilitātem quandam magnam, quā carēre diūtius vix possunt līberī, deinde firmitūdinem — quod et illa prīma facile in contrāria vitia convertuntur, ut exsistat ex rēge dominus, ex optimātibus factiō, ex populō turba et cōnfūsiō.'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"exspectare","latin":"exspectāre","headword":"exspectāre","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to wait (for)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī quis vīllam intrāre vult, iānuam pulsat et extrā iānuam exspectat, dum iānitor forēs aperit eumque in vīllam admittit.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"exspectat","latin":"exspectat","headword":"exspectat","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"waits for; expects","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puerī Iūlium exspectant.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"exstruere","latin":"exstruere","headword":"exstruere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to build up; erect","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Antequam illae basilicae exstrūctae sunt, tabernae in forō erant: tabernae veterēs eō locō ubi basilica Iūlia sita est, tabernae novae in locō basilicae Aemiliae.","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"exsul","latin":"exsul, -ulis","headword":"exsul","letter":"e","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"exile","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Spernentibus Etrūscīs Lucumōnem \"exsule advena ortum\", Tanaquil eam indignitātem ferre nōn potuit, oblītaque amōris patriae, dummodo virum honōrātum vidēret, cōnsilium migrandī ab Tarquiniīs cēpit.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"exter","latin":"exter, -era, -erum","headword":"exter","letter":"e","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"foreign; outside","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"exurere","latin":"exūrere","headword":"exūrere","letter":"e","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to burn up; destroy by fire","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"exustio","latin":"exustiō, -ōnis","headword":"exustiō","letter":"e","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"burning up; conflagration","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīn etiam sī cupiat prōlēs illa futūrōrum hominum deinceps laudēs ūnius cuiusque nostrum ā patribus acceptās posterīs prōdere, tamen propter ēluviōnēs exustiōnēsque terrārum, quās accidere tempore certō necesse est, nōn modo nōn aeternam, sed nē dīturnam quidem glōriam assequī possumus.'","reading":"ANGUSTIAE TERRĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"exuviae","latin":"exuviae, -ārum","headword":"exuviae","letter":"e","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"spoils; cast-off clothing","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rogō ingentī in rēgiā ērēctō, rēgīna locum flōribus et fronde exōrnat; super rogum exuviās et ēnsem relictum effigiemque Aenēae in torō locat.","reading":"ROGUS DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"faber","latin":"faber","headword":"faber","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"craftsman; smith","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī rēs ferreās vel ligneās facit, faber appellātur.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"fabricare","latin":"fabricāre","headword":"fabricāre","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to build; construct","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Graecī enim, cum urbem vī expugnāre nōn possent, dolō ūsī sunt: equum ingentem ē lignō fabricāvērunt eumque mīlitibus armātīs complēvērunt, quibus praefectī erant Ulixēs et Pyrrhus, Achillis fīlius.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"fabula","latin":"fābula","headword":"fābula","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"story; tale","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fābulās tuās Graecās audīre nōlumus.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"facies","latin":"faciēs","headword":"faciēs","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"face; appearance","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn modo vestīs, sed etiam faciēs et manūs et genua sordida sunt.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"facilis","latin":"facilis","headword":"facilis","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"easy","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"facilitas","latin":"facilitās, -ātis","headword":"facilitās","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ease; affability","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ac prīmum quanta innocentia dēbent esse imperātōrēs! quanta deinde in omnibus rēbus temperantia! quanta fide, quanta facilitāte, quanto ingeniō, quanta hūmānitāte!","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"facinus","latin":"facinus, -oris","headword":"facinus","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"deed; crime","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"factio","latin":"factiō, -ōnis","headword":"factiō","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"faction; party","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mōs partium et factiōnum ac deinde omnium malārum artium Rōmae ortus est ōtiō atque abundantia eārum rērum quae prīma mortālēs dūcunt.","reading":"CĪVITĀS DĪLACERĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"factiosus","latin":"factiōsus, -a, -um","headword":"factiōsus","letter":"f","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"factional; intriguing","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eā tempestāte exercitū nostrō fuēre complūrēs novī atque nōbilēs, quibus dīvitiae bonō honestōque potiōrēs erant, factiōsī domī, potentēs apud sociōs, clārī magis quam honestī; quī Iugurthae nōn mediocrem animum pollicitandō accendēbant, 'sī Micipsa rēx occidisset, fore utī sōlus imperiī Numidiae potīrētur: in ipsō maximam virtūtem, Rōmae omnia vēnālia esse!'","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"facultas","latin":"facultās, -ātis","headword":"facultās","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"means; resources","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum hōc — exhāustīs iam patriae facultātibus — cupīvit impraesentiārum bellum compōnere, quō valentior posteā congrederētur.","reading":"ZAMA ET FVGA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"fallit","latin":"fallit","headword":"fallit","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"deceives; tricks","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia vērō, quae tabellam Mārcī esse crēdit, ā fīliō suō improbō fallitur.","reading":"MARCVS MENTĪTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"falsus","latin":"falsus","headword":"falsus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"false","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"falx","latin":"falx","headword":"falx","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sickle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Falx est īnstrūmentum quō agricola mētit.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"fames","latin":"famēs","headword":"famēs","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hunger","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homō sex diēs cibō carēre potest, nec tamen famē moritur.' Iūlius: 'Dubitō num ego tam diū famem ferre possim.' Cornēlius: 'Id nōn negō, sed multō molestior est sitis quam famēs.'","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"familia","latin":"familia","headword":"familia","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"household; family","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius, Aemilia, Mārcus, Quīntus, Iūlia, Syra, Dāvus, Dēlia Mēdusque sunt familia Rōmāna.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"familiaris","latin":"familiāris, -is","headword":"familiāris","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"friend; intimate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quod in familiā nostrā fuit, praestitit utī in omnibus bellīs adesset vōbīs: nōs utī per ōtium tūtī sīmus, in vestrā manū est, patrēs cōnscrīptī.","reading":"ADHERBAL RŌMAM PROFĪCĪSCITUR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"famula","latin":"famula, -ae","headword":"famula","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"maidservant","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Famulae eam collāpsam suscipiunt, in marmoreum thalamum referunt et in lectō pōnunt.","reading":"QUERELLA DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"fascis","latin":"fascis, -is","headword":"fascis","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bundle of rods (carried before a magistrate)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"fatalis","latin":"fātālis, -e","headword":"fātālis","letter":"f","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"ordained by fate; fatal","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"fatetur","latin":"fatētur","headword":"fatētur","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"confesses; admits","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus, quī iam nōn audet mentīrī, nihil negat, sed omnia fatētur: 'Rēctē dīcis, pater.","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"fax","latin":"fax, facis","headword":"fax","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"torch","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"felix","latin":"fēlīx","headword":"fēlīx","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"happy; lucky","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At certē nōn tam fēlīx eris quam Arīōn, quī delphīnō servātus est.\"","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"femina","latin":"fēmina","headword":"fēmina","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"woman","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia fēmina Rōmāna est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"femininum","latin":"fēminīnum","headword":"fēminīnum","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"feminine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"femininus","latin":"fēminīnus","headword":"fēminīnus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"feminine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Genera nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Quattuor.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Masculīnum, ut hic magister; fēminīnum, ut haec fēmina; neutrum, ut hoc scamnum; commūne, ut hic et haec sacerdōs.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"fenestra","latin":"fenestra","headword":"fenestra","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"window","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vīlla duo ōstia et multās fenestrās habet.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Āēr frīgidus cubiculum Mārcī intrat, fenestra enim aperta est.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"fera","latin":"fera","headword":"fera","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wild beast","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Leō et lupus sunt bēstiae ferae, quae aliās bēstiās capiunt et edunt.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"feriae","latin":"fēriae, -ārum","headword":"fēriae","letter":"f","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"holiday; festival","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dabant enim hae fēriae tibi facultātem ad explicandās tuās litterās.' Tum ille: 'Mihi vērō omne tempus est ad meōs librōs vacuum; numquam enim sunt illī occupātī.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"ferocitas","latin":"ferōcitās, -ātis","headword":"ferōcitās","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fierceness; ferocity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quō in locō cum esset silvestris bēluae sustentātus ūberibus pastōrēsque eum sustulissent et in agrēstī cultū labōreque aluissent, perhibētur, ut adolēverit, et corporis vīribus et animī ferōcitāte tantum cēterīs praestitisse ut omnēs quī tum eōs agrōs ubi hodiē est haec urbs incolēbant aequō animō illī libenterque pārērent.","reading":"DĒ VETERE RĒ PŪBLICĀ RŌMĀNĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"ferre","latin":"ferre","headword":"ferre","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to carry; bring","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Catēna cōnstat ē multīs ānulīs ferreīs, quī inter sē coniunguntur.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"ferrum","latin":"ferrum","headword":"ferrum","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"iron","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lignum est māteria dūra, sed minus dūra quam ferrum.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"fert","latin":"fert","headword":"fert","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"carries; bears","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Mīles est vir quī scūtum et gladium et pīlum fert.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"fertilis","latin":"fertilis","headword":"fertilis","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"fertile","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ager quī multum frūmentī aliāsve frūgēs ferre potest, fertilis esse dīcitur.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"ferus","latin":"ferus","headword":"ferus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"wild","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"fervens","latin":"fervēns, -entis","headword":"fervēns","letter":"f","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"burning; passionate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed ōrātor adulēscēns, cum ōrātiōnis genere ferventī ac vehementī ūterētur, adeō in dīcendō omnēs nervōs contendēbat ut brevī vōx vīrēsque eum dēicerent; ergō aliquamdiū dē forō dēcēdere atque in Graeciam Asiamque prōicīscī cōnstituit, ut vōcem remitteret atque ōrātiōnī abundantī moderārētur.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"fessus","latin":"fessus","headword":"fessus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"tired; weary","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dominus autem fessus nōn est, nam is nōn ambulat.","reading":"MĒDVS ET CORNĒLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Pāstor, quī fessus est, oculōs claudit et dormit.","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"fictilis","latin":"fictilis, -e","headword":"fictilis","letter":"f","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"earthen; made of clay","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Imperāvit quam plūrimās venēnātās serpentēs vīvās colligī eāsque in vāsa fictilia conicī.","reading":"APVD PRŪSIAM ET MORS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"fides","latin":"fidēs","headword":"fidēs","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"faith; trust","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam etsī rāra est vēra amīcitia ac fidēs, nōn omnēs amīcī sunt falsī seu īnfīdī.","reading":"DĒ VĒRĪS AMĪCĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"fidicen","latin":"fidicen","headword":"fidicen","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lyre-player; musician","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is fidicen nōbilissimus fuit quī tam pulchrē canēbat ut bēstiae ferae, nātūram suam oblīta, accēderent, ut eum canentem audīrent, ac rapidī fluviī cōnsisterent, nē strepitū cantum eius turbārent.","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"fiducia","latin":"fīdūcia, -ae","headword":"fīdūcia","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"confidence","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Multōrum rēgum populōrumque cāsibus cognita populī Rōmānī clēmentia nōn modo spem tibi, sed prope certam fīdūciam salūtis praebet.'","reading":"PERSEVS ANTE CONSVLEM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"fidus","latin":"fīdus","headword":"fīdus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"faithful; loyal","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cēterum fābulam male intellēxistī, nec enim dēbilis fuit Paris nec fīdus servus Priamī; nam rēx eī imperāverat ut Paridem interficeret, et quidquid dominus imperāvit, servō faciendum est.'","reading":"INTER PŌCVLA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"figit","latin":"fīgit","headword":"fīgit","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"fixes; fastens","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"filia","latin":"fīlia","headword":"fīlia","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"daughter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlia est fīlia Iūliī et Aemiliae.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Iūlius et Aemilia sunt parentēs trium līberōrum: duōrum fīliōrum et ūnīus fīliae.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"filius","latin":"fīlius","headword":"fīlius","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"son","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus fīlius Iūliī est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Cupīdō est fīlius Veneris et Mārtis, quamquam Venus Mārtis coniūnx nōn est, sed alterīus deī, cui nōmen est Vulcānus.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"filum","latin":"fīlum","headword":"fīlum","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"thread","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ego vērō tibi auxilium feram: ecce fīlum ā Daedalō factum, quod tibi viam mōnstrābit.","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"latin":"Tum rēx īrātus cēpit Daedalum, quī fīlum cōnfēcerat et Ariadnae dederat, eumque in labyrinthum inclūdī iussit ūna cum eius Īcarō fīliō; vērum pater et fīlius mīrābilī modō ē labyrinthō fūgērunt.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"firmamentum","latin":"firmāmentum, -ī","headword":"firmāmentum","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"support; strengthening","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed tamen alterīus partis perīculum, Sertōriānae atque Hispāniēnsis, quae multō plūs firmāmentī ac rōboris habēbat, Cn.","reading":"DĒ GENERE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"firmitudo","latin":"firmitūdō, -inis","headword":"firmitūdō","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"firmness; stability","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec cōnstitūtiō prīmum habet aequābilitātem quandam magnam, quā carēre diūtius vix possunt līberī, deinde firmitūdinem — quod et illa prīma facile in contrāria vitia convertuntur, ut exsistat ex rēge dominus, ex optimātibus factiō, ex populō turba et cōnfūsiō.'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"fiscus","latin":"fiscus, -ī","headword":"fiscus","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"treasury; public purse","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"flagitare","latin":"flagitāre","headword":"flagitāre","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to demand eagerly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"flagitium","latin":"flagitium, -ī","headword":"flagitium","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shameful act; outrage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fautōrēs lēgātōrum, praetereā senātūs magna pars, grātiā dēprāvāta, Adherbalis dicta contemnere, Iugurthae virtūtem extollere laudibus; grātiā, voce, dēnique omnibus modīs prō aliēnō scelere et flagitiō sua quasi prō glōriā nītēbantur.","reading":"ADHERBAL RŌMAM PROFĪCĪSCITUR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"flamen","latin":"flāmen, -inis","headword":"flāmen","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"flamen; priest of a single god","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed quia in cīvitāte bellicōsā plūrēs Rōmulī quam Numae similēs rēgēs fore putābat, itūrōsque ipsōs ad bella, nē rēge absente sacra negligerentur, Iovī assiduum sacerdōtem creāvit quī \"flāmen Diālis\" appellātus est.","reading":"NVMA POMPILIVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"flare","latin":"flāre","headword":"flāre","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to blow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Statim sequitur tonitrus cum imbre, et simul magnus ventus flāre incipit.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"flere","latin":"flēre","headword":"flēre","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to weep; cry","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"florere","latin":"flōrēre","headword":"flōrēre","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to flourish; be at one's prime","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"flos","latin":"flōs","headword":"flōs","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"flower","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"fluctus","latin":"flūctus","headword":"flūctus","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wave","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tempestās est magnus ventus quī mare turbat ac flūctus facit quī altiōrēs sunt quam nāvēs.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"flumen","latin":"flūmen","headword":"flūmen","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"river","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Flūmen Rhēnus Germāniam ā Galliā dīvidit.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Quī agrōs prope Nīlum flūmen colunt, bis terve in annō metere possunt.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"fluvius","latin":"fluvius","headword":"fluvius","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"river","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nīlus fluvius est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"focus","latin":"focus, -ī","headword":"focus","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hearth","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"foederatus","latin":"foederātus, -a, -um","headword":"foederātus","letter":"f","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"allied by treaty","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sīc Hannibal, minor quīnque et vīgintī annīs nātus, imperātor factus, proximō trienniō omnēs gentēs Hispāniae bellō subēgit, Saguntum, foederātam cīvitātem, vī expugnāvit, trēs exercitūs maximōs comparāvit.","reading":"IN HISPĀNIAM ET AD ALPĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"foeditas","latin":"foeditās, -ātis","headword":"foeditās","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"foulness; baseness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quō enim dūcere hunc iuvenem potestis ubi nōn sua decora eum ā tantā foeditāte suppliciī dēfendant?\"","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"foedus","latin":"foedus, -eris","headword":"foedus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective; noun n.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"ugly; foul; treaty; compact; alliance","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra nōn est fēmina pulchra, neque pulcher est nāsus eius, sed foedus est.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Puella sē in speculō videt et sē interrogat: 'Estne foedus nāsus meus?' Nāsus eius autem fōrmōsus nōn est.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"folium","latin":"folium","headword":"folium","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"leaf","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"fons","latin":"fōns, fontis","headword":"fōns","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"spring; fountain","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"foris","latin":"foris","headword":"foris","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"door; door-leaf; (pl.) doors","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Foris duōs cardinēs habet, in quibus vertī potest; cum foris in cardinibus vertitur, iānua aperītur aut clauditur.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"formosus","latin":"fōrmōsus","headword":"fōrmōsus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"beautiful; handsome","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puella sē in speculō videt et sē interrogat: 'Estne foedus nāsus meus?' Nāsus eius autem fōrmōsus nōn est.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"latin":"Quia ea virgō proba ac fōrmōsa erat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"forte","latin":"forte","headword":"forte","letter":"f","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"by chance","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fābulamne dē lupō et agnō, quī forte ad eundem rīvum vēnērunt, an tabulam dē puerō quī cupīvit regere equōs quī currum Solīs per caelum trahunt?'","reading":"TABVLĀ POSTVLĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"fortis","latin":"fortis","headword":"fortis","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"brave; strong","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mīles fortis hostem nōn metuit, sed sine metū impetum in hostem facit.","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Discipulus quamque litteram cuiusque vocābulī sīc legit: 'M-I mī, L-Ē-S lēs: mī-lēs; R-Ō Rō, M-Ā ma, N-V-S nus: Rō-ma-nus ...' Ita quodque vocābulum cuiusque sententiae ā discipulō legitur. (In hāc sententia vocābulum fortiter novum est, sed quī vocābulum fortis scit, hoc vocābulum quoque intellegit, nam mīles fortis est mīles quī fortiter pugnat.)","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"fortiter","latin":"fortiter","headword":"fortiter","letter":"f","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"bravely","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quōmodo parvus discipulus hanc sententiam lēgit: Mīles Rōmānus fortiter pugnat?","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"latin":"Ante proelium dux exercitiīs mīlitēs suōs hortātur ut fortiter pugnent.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"fortitudo","latin":"fortitūdō, -inis","headword":"fortitūdō","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bravery; courage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc Aenēās sōlus in antrum Sibyllae vātis penetrāvit; quae eum sēcum ad Īnferōs dūxit, ubi pater Anchīsēs multa nārrāvit dē futūrō imperiō Rōmānō et dē fortitūdine Rōmānōrum; tum, postquam fīliō mīrantī virōs Rōmānōs fortissimōs ostendit usque ad Iūlium Caesarem, hīs verbīs Rōmānōs admonuit: 'Tū regere imperiō populōs, Rōmāne, mementō!","reading":"POST DĪDŌNEM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"},{"latin":"Sī vērum est — quod nēmō dubitat — ut populus Rōmānus omnēs gentēs virtūte superārit, nōn est īnfitiandum Hannibalem tantō praestitisse cēterōs imperātōrēs prūdentiā, quantō populus Rōmānus antecēdat fortitūdine cūnctās nātiōnēs.","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"fortuna","latin":"fortūna","headword":"fortūna","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fortune; luck","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hoc nōs docet fortūna illīus tyrannī.","reading":"ĀNVLVS POLYCRATIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"fortunatus","latin":"fortūnātus, -a, -um","headword":"fortūnātus","letter":"f","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"fortunate; blessed","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mē quoque per multōs similīs fortūna labōrēs iactātam hāc dīvum voluit cōnsistere terrā.","reading":"DĪDŌ RĒGĪNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"fossa","latin":"fossa","headword":"fossa","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ditch; trench","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Circum castra fossā et vallum longum et altum est.'","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Vesperī exercitūs locō ad dēfendendum idōneō castrā pōnit, quae vāllō et fossā circumdantur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"fragor","latin":"fragor, -ōris","headword":"fragor","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"crash; thunder","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Parentēs expavidī ignem aquā restinguere properant; at pater Anchīsēs laetus Iovem invocat, subitōque fragōre ā laevā gravis tonat, et simul stēlla dē caelō lāpsa multā cum lūce per tenebrās currit.","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"frangere","latin":"frangere","headword":"frangere","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to break; wreck","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra: 'Nōlī hoc mīrārī: Mārcus forem frangere cōnātur, quod aliter exīre nōn potest.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"frater","latin":"frāter (fratris)","headword":"frāter","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"brother","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sextus: 'At frāter tuus saepe laudātur, Mārce.' Magister: 'Rēctē dīcis, Sexte: Quīntus bonus discipulus est, et industrius et prūdēns.' Quīntus ā magistrō laudātur, quamquam abest.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"fremitus","latin":"fremitus, -ūs","headword":"fremitus","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"roar; murmur","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quārtō post diē quam cum rēge est pugnātum, cum in circō lūdī fierent, murmur repentē populum tōtā spectācula pervāsit 'pugnātum in Macedoniā et dēvictum rēgem esse'; dein fremitus incrēvit; postrēmō clāmor, plausus, velut certō nūntiō victōriae allātō, est exortus.","reading":"PERSEVS VICTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"fretum","latin":"fretum","headword":"fretum","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"strait; channel","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus et Lȳdia ventō secundō per mare Īnferum nāvigāre pergunt ad fretum Siculum (id est fretum quō Sicilia ab Italiā disiungitur).","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA IN NĀVĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"fretus","latin":"frētus, -a, -um","headword":"frētus","letter":"f","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"relying on; trusting (+ abl.)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Adherbal, tametsī Rōmam lēgātōs mīserat quī senātum docērent dē caede frātris et fortūnīs suīs, tamen frētus multitūdine mīlitum parābat armīs contendere.","reading":"MORS HIEMPSALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"frigidus","latin":"frīgidus","headword":"frīgidus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"cold","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hiems tempus frīgidum est.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"latin":"Āēr frīgidus cubiculum Mārcī intrat, fenestra enim aperta est.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"frons","latin":"frōns, frondis","headword":"frōns","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"forehead; leaf; foliage","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Suprā oculōs frōns est.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"fructus","latin":"frūctus, -ūs","headword":"frūctus","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fruit; produce; profit","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"frui","latin":"fruī","headword":"fruī","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to enjoy (+ abl.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius frontem contrahit et 'Agricola' inquit 'ipse nōn sum, sed multīs agricolīs praesum ac dīligenter cūrō ut colōnī agrōs meōs bene cōlant.' Orontēs, quī vīta rūstica nōn fruitur, 'Prūdenter facis' inquit 'quod agrōs ipse nōn colis.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"frumentum","latin":"frūmentum","headword":"frūmentum","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"grain; wheat","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In agrīs frūmentum crēscit vērē et aestāte.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"},{"latin":"Quoniam igitur propter vim atque multitūdinem praedōnum nē mare Tuscum quidem tūtum erat, frūmentī ex Siciliā et ex Āfricā Rōmam advehēbātur.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"frustra","latin":"frūstrā","headword":"frūstrā","letter":"f","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"in vain","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tālibus verbīs nauta mercātōrem maestum cōnsōlārī cōnātur, sed frūstrā, nam ille prōtinus \"Nōlī mē monēre\" inquit, \"quī ipse imperāvistī ut mercēs meae iacērentur!\"","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"fuga","latin":"fuga","headword":"fuga","letter":"f","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"flight; escape","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Crās tibi nārrābō dē fugā eōrum, hodiē plūs temporis ad nārrandum nōn habeō: iam hōram cōnsūmpsī in nārrandō.\"","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"fugare","latin":"fugāre","headword":"fugāre","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to rout; put to flight","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"fugit","latin":"fugit","headword":"fugit","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"flees","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Mīles Rōmānus, quī hostem armātum accurrere videt, nōn ab eō fugit, sed armīs sē dēfendit.","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"fugitivus","latin":"fugitīvus","headword":"fugitīvus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"runaway; fugitive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornēlius: 'Etiam sī adhūc Rōmae latet, difficile erit servum fugitīvum in tantā urbe reperīre.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"fulgor","latin":"fulgor, -ōris","headword":"fulgor","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"radiance; brightness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deinde est hominum generī prosperus et salūtāris ille fulgor quī dīcitur \"Iovis\"; tum rutilus horribilisque terrīs quem \"Martium\" dīcitis.'","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"fulmen","latin":"fulmen, -inis","headword":"fulmen","letter":"f","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"thunderbolt","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"fumus","latin":"fūmus, -ī","headword":"fūmus","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"smoke","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūxtā haec loca surgit Aetna, mōns ingēns, unde fūmus flammaeque ad caelum eduntur, interdum etiam saxa lapidēsque cum fragōre horribilī ab īmō fundō emittuntur.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"fundere","latin":"fundere","headword":"fundere","letter":"f","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to pour","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"funis","latin":"fūnis, -is","headword":"fūnis","letter":"f","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rope; cable","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"futurus","latin":"futūrus","headword":"futūrus","letter":"f","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"future; about to be","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"gallus","latin":"gallus","headword":"gallus","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cockerel; rooster","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce gallus canit: 'Cucurru!","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"gaudet","latin":"gaudet","headword":"gaudet","letter":"g","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"rejoices; is glad","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Medicus: \"Puer spīrat et cor eius palpitat.\" Aemilia gaudet quod fīlius vīvit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"gemitus","latin":"gemitus, -ūs","headword":"gemitus","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"groan; lament","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quem cum Aenēās interrogāvisset \"quae fortūna esset patriae?\", magnō cum gemitū haec respondit: \"Vēnit summa diēs et inēlūctābile tempus Dardaniae.","reading":"SOMNIVM AENĒAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"gemma","latin":"gemma","headword":"gemma","letter":"g","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gem; jewel","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce taberna Rōmāna, in quā gemmae et margarītae multae sunt.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"gena","latin":"gena","headword":"gena","letter":"g","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cheek","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Īnfrā oculōs genae sunt.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"gener","latin":"gener, -erī","headword":"gener","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"son-in-law","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vōs tamen cum virīs Rōmānīs in mātrimōniō eritis, in societāte fortūnārum omnium et — quō nihil cārius est generī hūmānō — līberōrum.","reading":"SABINAE RAPTAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"genetivus","latin":"genetīvus","headword":"genetīvus","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"genitive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Cāsus nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Sex.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Nōminātīvus, genetīvus, dativus, accūsātīvus, vocātīvus, ablātīvus.","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"genitor","latin":"genitor, -ōris","headword":"genitor","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"father; begetter","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc Aenēās genitōrem Anchīsēn āmīsit; ille enim cōnfectus aetāte ē vītā excessit nequīquam ex tantīs perīculīs ēreptus.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"genus","latin":"genus","headword":"genus","letter":"g","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gender; kind","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"gerundium","latin":"gerundium","headword":"gerundium","letter":"g","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gerund (a verbal noun)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"gerundivum","latin":"gerundīvum","headword":"gerundīvum","letter":"g","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gerundive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"glacies","latin":"glaciēs","headword":"glaciēs","letter":"g","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ice","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In Germāniā hiemēs frīgidiōrēs sunt quam in Italiā: altā nive operītur tōta terra et lacūs glaciē operiuntur; hieme Germānī puerī super glaciem lacuum lūdere possunt.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"gladiator","latin":"gladiātor","headword":"gladiātor","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gladiator; swordsman","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Modo in amphitheatro certamen magnificum spectavi: plus trecenti gladiatores certabant.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"gladius","latin":"gladius","headword":"gladius","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sword","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Mīles est vir quī scūtum et gladium et pīlum fert.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"globosus","latin":"globōsus, -a, -um","headword":"globōsus","letter":"g","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"spherical; round","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homines enim sunt hāc lēge generātī, quī tuērentur illum globum quem in hōc templō medium vidēs, quae \"terra\" dīcitur, iīsque animus datus est ex illīs sempiternīs ignibus quae \"sīdera\" et \"stellās\" vocātis, quae globōsae et rotundae, dīvīnīs animātae mentibus, circōs suōs orbēsque cōnficiunt celeritāte mīrābilī.","reading":"MORS ET VĪTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"gloria","latin":"glōria","headword":"glōria","letter":"g","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"glory","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Eō tempore Thēseus, vir patriae amāns atque glōriae cupidus, Athēnīs vīvēbat.","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"gracilis","latin":"gracilis","headword":"gracilis","letter":"g","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"slender; slim","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Omnēs pulchritūdinem tuam laudant.' Tum vērō fōrmam eius spectāns: 'At minus gracilis es quam tunc: eō enim tempore gracilior erās quam hoc signum Veneris.'","reading":"AMOR IŪLIĪ ET AEMILIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"gracilitas","latin":"grācilitās, -ātis","headword":"grācilitās","letter":"g","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"slenderness; thinness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Erat eō tempore in nōbīs summa grācilitās et īnfirmitās corporis, prōcērum et tenue collum; quī habitus et quae fīgūra nōn procul abesse putātur ā vītae perīculō, sī accēdit labor et laterum magna contentiō.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"gradus","latin":"gradus","headword":"gradus","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"degree; step","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Comparātiōnis gradūs quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Trēs.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Positīvus, ut doctus; comparātīvus, ut doctior; superlātīvus, ut doctissimus.' Magister: 'Quae nōmina comparantur?' Discipulus: 'Appellātīva dumtaxat quālitātem aut quantitātem significantiā.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"graece","latin":"Graece","headword":"Graece","letter":"g","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"in Greek","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Zēnō est servus doctus quī et Latīnē et Graecē scit.","reading":"EPISTVLA AD PATREM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"graecus","latin":"Graecus","headword":"Graecus","letter":"g","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"Greek","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sparta est oppidum Graecum.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Etiam peristȳlum magnum et pulchrum in vīllā est. 'Peristȳlum' est vocābulum Graecum.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"grammatica","latin":"grammatica","headword":"grammatica","letter":"g","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"grammar","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"gravida","latin":"gravida","headword":"gravida","letter":"g","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"pregnant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōlī mē ab uxōre gravidā rapere!","reading":"PĀSTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"gravis","latin":"gravis","headword":"gravis","letter":"g","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"heavy; serious","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Quod gladius brevis nōn tam gravis est quam gladius longus.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"gremium","latin":"gremium","headword":"gremium","letter":"g","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lap; bosom","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"grex","latin":"grex","headword":"grex","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"flock; herd","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"gubernator","latin":"gubernātor, -ōris","headword":"gubernātor","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"helmsman; pilot; steersman; captain","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In puppī sedet gubernātor, quī nāvem gubernat.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Hic gubernātor, quī sermōnem eōrum exaudīvit, \"Tanta\" inquit \"ūnīus deī potestās nōn est.","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"gurges","latin":"gurges, -itis","headword":"gurges","letter":"g","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"whirlpool; abyss","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"gustare","latin":"gustāre","headword":"gustāre","letter":"g","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to taste","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"habet","latin":"habet","headword":"habet","letter":"h","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"has; holds","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam in sacculō habet.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"habitabilis","latin":"habitābilis, -e","headword":"habitābilis","letter":"h","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"habitable","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vidēs habitārī in terrā rārīs et angustīs in locīs et in ipsīs quasi maculīs ubi habitātur vāstās sōlitūdinēs interiectās, eōsque quī incolunt terram nōn modo interruptōs ita esse ut nihil inter ipsōs ab aliīs ad aliōs mānāre possit, sed partim oblīquōs, partim trānsversōs, partim etiam adversōs stāre vōbīs — ā quibus exspectāre glōriam certē nūllam potestis!'","reading":"ANGUSTIAE TERRĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"habitat","latin":"habitat","headword":"habitat","letter":"h","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"lives; dwells","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius in magnā vīllā habitat.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Vīlla ubi Iūlius habitat prope Tusculum est.","reading":"MĒDVS ET CORNĒLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"hasta","latin":"hasta","headword":"hasta","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"spear; lance","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus: 'Num Aemilius et hastam et pīlum fert?'","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"haurire","latin":"haurīre","headword":"haurīre","letter":"h","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to draw (water); bail out","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nāvis aqua implērī incipit, neque enim nautae satis multum aquae haurīre possunt.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"hebes","latin":"hebes, -etis","headword":"hebes","letter":"h","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"dull; blunt","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"hendecasyllabus","latin":"hendecasyllabus","headword":"hendecasyllabus","letter":"h","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hendecasyllable (eleven-syllable verse)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"herba","latin":"herba","headword":"herba","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"grass; herb","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cibus ovium est herba, quae in campō est.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Vērē campī nova herba operiuntur, arborēs novīs foliīs ōrnantur, avēs, quae hieme tacent, rūrsus canere incipiunt.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"hereditas","latin":"hērēditās, -ātis","headword":"hērēditās","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"inheritance","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic autem, velut hērēditāte relictum, odium paternum ergā Rōmānōs sīc cōnservāvit ut prius animam dēpōneret quam id dēposuerit — quī quidem, cum patriā pulsus esset et aliēnārum opum indigeret, numquam dēstiterit animō bellāre cum Rōmānīs.","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"heres","latin":"hērēs, -edis","headword":"hērēs","letter":"h","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"heir","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lucumō superfuit patrī bonōrum omnium hērēs.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"hexameter","latin":"hexameter","headword":"hexameter","letter":"h","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hexameter (six-foot verse)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"hic","latin":"hīc","headword":"hīc","letter":"h","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"here","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus: 'Pater nōn hīc est, sed Mārcus hīc est.'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"hic/haec/hoc","latin":"hīc/haec/hoc","headword":"hīc/haec/hoc","letter":"h","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"this (one)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"hiems","latin":"hiems","headword":"hiems","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"winter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tempora annī sunt quattuor: aestās et hiems, vēr et autumnus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"hodie","latin":"hodiē","headword":"hodiē","letter":"h","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"today","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus cubiculum intrāns interrogat: 'Quōmodo sē habet pēs tuus hodiē?' Quīntus respondet: 'Pēs male sē habet, nec pēs tantum, sed etiam caput et bracchium dolet.","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"latin":"Hodiē manē vestīmenta Mārcī munda erant atque tam candida quam nix nova, nunc vērō sordida et ūmida sunt.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"honestas","latin":"honestās, -ātis","headword":"honestās","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"honour; integrity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Claudius, Vergīniī cuiusdam (quī honestīs iam stīpendiīs contrā Latīnōs in monte Algidō mīlitāverat) fīliam virginem corrumpere voluit; quam pater occīdit, nē stuprum ā decemvirō sustinēret, et regressus ad mīlitēs mōvit tumultum.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"honos","latin":"honōs, -ōris","headword":"honōs","letter":"h","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"honour; glory","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dum fluviī in maria current, dum sīdera in caelum surgent, semper honōs tuus laudēsque manēbunt, quaecumque terrae mē vocant.' Sīc fātus Īlionēō aliīsque amīcīs dextram dedit.","reading":"DĪDŌ RĒGĪNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"hora","latin":"hōra","headword":"hōra","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hour","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Diēs in duodecim hōrās dīviditur.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"horror","latin":"horror, -ōris","headword":"horror","letter":"h","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"horror; shuddering","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At tum prīmum saevus horror Aenēam perfūdit: nam cum rēgem senem ex crūdēlī vulnere morientem vidēret, vēnit eī in mentem ipsīus pater senex Anchīsēs et uxor Creūsa et parvus fīlius Ascanius, quōs sōlōs domī dēseruerat.","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"hortus","latin":"hortus","headword":"hortus","letter":"h","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"garden","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce vīlla et hortus Iūliī.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"hospes","latin":"hospes","headword":"hospes","letter":"h","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"guest; host","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"hospitium","latin":"hospitium, -ī","headword":"hospitium","letter":"h","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hospitality; guest-friendship","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eum cōnsēnsum deōsque cōnsociātōs laudābat Servius inter prīmōrēs Latīnōrum, cum quibus pūblicē prīvātimque hospitia amīcitiāsque iūnxerat.","reading":"CENSVS INSTITVTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"hostia","latin":"hostia, -ae","headword":"hostia","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sacrificial victim","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Multās hostiās ante ārās tibi immolābimus!'","reading":"VENUS GENETRĪX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"latin":"'Pater meus' inquit 'Hamilcar, puerulō mē, utpote nōn amplius novem annōs nātō, in Hispāniam imperātor proficīscēns Carthāgine Iovī Optimō Maximō hostiās immolāvit.","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"hostis","latin":"hostis","headword":"hostis","letter":"h","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"enemy","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nūllus hostis Rōmam expugnāre potest.'","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Nē hoc fīat, legiōnēs Rōmānae hīc sunt ac tamdiū remanēbunt dum hostis armātus seu citrā seu ultrā Dānuvium ūllus reliquus erit.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"humanitas","latin":"hūmānitās, -ātis","headword":"hūmānitās","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"humanity; kindness; culture","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ac prīmum quanta innocentia dēbent esse imperātōrēs! quanta deinde in omnibus rēbus temperantia! quanta fide, quanta facilitāte, quanto ingeniō, quanta hūmānitāte!","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"humus","latin":"humus","headword":"humus","letter":"h","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ground; earth","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sordidus est quod humī iacuit; humus enim propter imbrem ūmida et sordida est.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"iacet","latin":"iacet","headword":"iacet","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"lies (down)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"iactor","latin":"iactor","headword":"iactor","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"be tossed; be thrown about","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nauta, quī flūctibus iactātur ac mergitur: 'Flūctibus iactor ac mergor!","reading":"NAVTAE ET NEPTŪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"iactura","latin":"iactūra","headword":"iactūra","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"loss; throwing overboard","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Gubernātor: \"Iactūra mercium nāvis servāta est.\" Mercātor: \"Rēctē dīcis: meae mercēs ēiectae sunt, ut nāvis tua salva esset!\" Gubernātor: \"Mercēs iēcimus ut nōs omnēs salvī essēmus.","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"iam","latin":"iam","headword":"iam","letter":"i","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"now; already","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iam Iūlia nōn cantat, sed plōrat: 'Uhuhū!'","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"ianitor","latin":"iānitor","headword":"iānitor","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"doorkeeper; porter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Servus cuius officium est forēs aperīre et claudere ac vīllam dominī cūstōdīre, ōstiārius vel iānitor appellātur.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"latin":"Iūlius, quī canem lātrāre audīvit, iānitōrem ātrium intrantem interrogat: 'Quis advenit?'","reading":"EPISTVLA ADVENIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"ianua","latin":"iānua","headword":"iānua","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"door","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic Titus ad lūdum advēnit et iānuam pulsat antequam intrat: discipulus nōn statim intrat, sed prīmum iānuam pulsat; tum lūdum intrat et magistrum salūtat: 'Salvē, magister!' Magister: 'Ō Tite!","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"latin":"Iānua vīllae ē duābus foribus cōnstat.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"ianus","latin":"Iānus, -ī","headword":"Iānus","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"Janus; his temple; open in war","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"icarus","latin":"Īcarus","headword":"Īcarus","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"Icarus; son of Daedalus","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Īcarus autem, quī cōnsilium patris ignōrābat, humī cōnsēdit et \"Fessus sum\" inquit \"ambulandō in hōc labyrinthō quem ipse nōbīs aedificāvistī, pater.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"idoneus","latin":"idōneus","headword":"idōneus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"suitable; fit","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum agmen ad hostēs pervēnit, sī tempus et locus idōneus est ad pugnandum, cohortēs in trēs ōrdinēs īnstruuntur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"idus","latin":"īdūs","headword":"īdūs","letter":"i","pos":"noun (f. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"the Ides (thirteenth or fifteenth day)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Diēs tertius decimus post kalendās \"Īdūs\" nōminātur.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"ignarus","latin":"ignārus","headword":"ignārus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"ignorant; unaware","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Gubernātor: \"Ignārus quidem es sī illum ignōrās.","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"ignis","latin":"ignis","headword":"ignis","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fire","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Tum pater, puerum ōsculātus, \"Parātī sumus ad volandum\" inquit, \"sed prius hoc tē moneō: vola post mē in mediō inter caelum et terram, nam sī in īnfimō aere prope terram volābis, pennae ūmidae fīent; sīn volābis in āere prope caelum, ignis sōlis cēram molliet et pennās ūret.","reading":"ĀLAE CONFICIWNTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"ignominiosus","latin":"ignōminiōsus, -a, -um","headword":"ignōminiōsus","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"disgraceful; shameful","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hostīliō Mancīnō cōnsule sacrificante pullī ex caveā ēvolāvērunt; cōnscendentī deinde nāvem, ut in Hispāniam proficīscerētur, accidit vōx: 'Manē, Mancīne!' Quae auspicia trīstia fuisse ēventū probātum est: victus enim ā Numantīnīs et castrīs exūtus, cum spēs nūlla servandī exercitūs esset, pācem cum hīs fēcit ignōminiōsam, quam ratam esse senātus vetuit.","reading":"HISPĀNIA PĀCĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"ignoscere","latin":"ignōscere","headword":"ignōscere","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to forgive (+ dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nimis clēmentēs sunt mulierēs, quae tam facile virīs nēquissimīs ignōscunt!","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"ille/illa/illud","latin":"ille/illa/illud","headword":"ille/illa/illud","letter":"i","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"that (one); he; she; it","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"illecebra","latin":"illecebra, -ae","headword":"illecebra","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"enticement; lure","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Suīs tē oportet illecebrīs ipsa virtūs trahat ad vērum decus.","reading":"DĒ GLŌRIĀ AETERNĀ ET ANIMŌ IMMORTĀLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"imbecillus","latin":"imbecillus, -a, -um","headword":"imbecillus","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"weak; feeble","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"imber","latin":"imber","headword":"imber","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rain; shower; rain-shower","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hieme nōn sōlum imber, sed etiam nix dē caelō cadit.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"immanitas","latin":"immānitās, -ātis","headword":"immānitās","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"savagery; cruelty","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Simulatque enim sē īnflexit hic rēx in dominātum iniūstiōrem, fit continuō tyrannus, quō neque taetrius neque foedius nec dīs hominibusque invīsius animāl ūllum cōgitārī potest — quī, quamquam figūra est hominis, mōrum tamen immānitāte vāstissimās vincit bēluās!","reading":"DĒ VETERE RĒ PŪBLICĀ RŌMĀNĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"immensus","latin":"immēnsus, -a, -um","headword":"immēnsus","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"boundless; immense","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi ēgressī Trōiānī, quibus ab immēnsō prope errōre nihil praeter arma et nāvēs supererat, cum praedam ex agrīs agerent, Latīnus rēx Aborīginēsque, quī tum ea tenēbant loca, ad arcendam vim advenārum armātī ex urbe atque agrīs concurrunt.","reading":"TRŌIĀNĪ ET LATĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"imminuere","latin":"imminuere","headword":"imminuere","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to lessen; reduce","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Praecipuē ita patrum numerō imminūtō, statuit nūllōs in patrēs legere, ut paucitāte ipsā senātus contemptior esset.","reading":"L. IŪNIUS BRŪTUS, LĪBERĀTOR POPULĪ RŌMĀNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"immo","latin":"immō","headword":"immō","letter":"i","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"on the contrary; no indeed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Immō fōrmōsus est nāsus tuus.' Iūlia sē vertit.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"immolare","latin":"immolāre","headword":"immolāre","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to sacrifice","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Paulō post animī Trōiānōrum rē horrendā turbātī sunt: dum Laocoōn ad āram taurum immolat, subitō duo anguēs ingentēs ab īnsulā Tenedō per mare tranquillum ad lītus natant.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"immortalis","latin":"immortālis","headword":"immortālis","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"immortal","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Immortālis est fīlius Deī sīcut pater eius, vīvus.","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"immunis","latin":"immūnis, -e","headword":"immūnis","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"exempt (from service)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hōc minōre cēnsū reliquam multitūdinem habuit; inde ūna centuria facta est immūnis mīlitiā.","reading":"CENSVS INSTITVTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"impensa","latin":"impēnsa, -ae","headword":"impēnsa","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"expense; cost","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"imperare","latin":"imperāre","headword":"imperāre","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to order; command (+ dat.); command (with dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus, quī legere nōn didicit, Lȳdiae librum reddit et rogat ut aliquid sibi lēgat; quae continuō librum ēvolvit et \"Legam tibi\" inquit \"dē virō claudō cui imperāvit ut surgeret et tolleret lectum suum et ambulāret.\"","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"imperat","latin":"imperat","headword":"imperat","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"commands; orders; orders (with dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia imperat: \"Mārce et Quīnte!","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Venī in hortum, Iūlia!' Iūlia imperat: 'Claude ōstium!' Ancilla pāret.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"imperator","latin":"imperātor, -ōris","headword":"imperātor","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"commander; general","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hostibus proeliō victīs, dux ā mīlitibus imperātor salūtātur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"latin":"Cum hōc Hasdrubale foedus renovāverat populus Rōmānus: 'ut fīnis utrīusque imperiī esset amnis Hibērus, Saguntīnīsque mediīs inter imperia duōrum populōrum lībertās servārētur.' In Hasdrubalis locum haud dubia rēs fuit quīnam successūrus esset, quia extemplō iuvenis Hannibal in praetōrium dēlātus imperātorque ingentī omnium clāmōre atque assēnsū appellātus erat.","reading":"IŪS IŪRANDVM HANNIBALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"imperium","latin":"imperium","headword":"imperium","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"empire; command","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ubi est imperium Rōmānum?","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Prōvincia est pars imperiī Rōmānī, ut membrum pars corporis est; Rōma enim caput imperiī est, prōvinciae membra sunt.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"impetrare","latin":"impetrāre","headword":"impetrāre","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to obtain; win by asking","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Id facile impetrāvērunt.","reading":"SPOLIA OPIMA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"impetus","latin":"impetus","headword":"impetus","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"charge; attack","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Ecce portae aperiuntur atque equitātus noster in hostēs impetum facit.","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"impiger","latin":"impiger","headword":"impiger","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"diligent; active","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sextus: 'Ego frequentēs epistulās ad patrem meum absentem scrībō.' Sextus puer probus est ac tam impiger quam apis.","reading":"EPISTVLA AD PATREM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"impius","latin":"impius, -a, -um","headword":"impius","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"impious; wicked","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēgnum autem Tyrī habēbat frāter Dīdōnis Pygmaliōn, rēx impius atque scelestus.","reading":"VENUS GENETRĪX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"implicare","latin":"implicāre","headword":"implicāre","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to entangle; involve","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornelius: \"Alter alterum in rete implicare conatur, nam qui reti implicitus est non potest se defendere et sine mora interficitur, nisi tam fortiter pugnavit ut spectatores eum vivere velint.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"impluvium","latin":"impluvium","headword":"impluvium","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"water-basin in the atrium","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In vīllā Iūliī magnum ātrium est cum impluviō.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"improbus","latin":"improbus","headword":"improbus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"bad; naughty; wicked","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus puer probus nōn est; Mārcus est puer improbus!'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Servus quī servum accūsat improbus est!' Mēdus tacet.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"imprudens","latin":"imprūdēns, -entis","headword":"imprūdēns","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"unaware; imprudent","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quārē, sī quid amīcē dē Rōmānīs cōgitābis, nōn imprūdenter fēceris sī mē cēlāris; cum quidem bellum parābis, tē ipsum frūstrāberis sī nōn mē in eō principem posueris.'","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"impudentia","latin":"impudentia, -ae","headword":"impudentia","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shamelessness; effrontery","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Baebium tribūnum plēbis magnā mercēde parat, cuius impudentia contrā iūs et iniūriās omnēs mūnītus foret.","reading":"IVGVRTHA RŌMAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"impunitas","latin":"impūnitās, -ātis","headword":"impūnitās","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"licence; unchecked freedom","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is dedit operam — sī modo id cōnsequī potuit — ut nimis redundantēs nōs et superfluentēs iuvenīlī quādam dīcendī impūnitāte et licentiā reprimeret et quasi extrā rīpās diffluentēs coercēret.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"in","latin":"in","headword":"in","letter":"i","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"in; on (+ ablative); into; on (+ abl.); on","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rōma in Italiā est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"In sacculō eius est pecūnia.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"incendium","latin":"incendium, -ī","headword":"incendium","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fire; conflagration","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deinde idem templum iterum et tertium sacrātum est, cum post incendia refectum esset.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"inceptum","latin":"inceptum, -ī","headword":"inceptum","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"undertaking; plan","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Interim haud longē ā marī prope Cirtam oppidum utrīusque exercitus cōnsēdit, et quia diēī extrēmum erat, proelium nōn inceptum.","reading":"CIRTA OBSESSA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"incertus","latin":"incertus","headword":"incertus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"uncertain; unsure","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn certus sum!' Titus nōn certus, sed incertus est, et respōnsum incertum dat magistrō.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"incipit","latin":"incipit","headword":"incipit","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"begins","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Autumnus ā Septembrī incipit.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"latin":"Mārcus īrātus Titum pulsāre incipit, sed magister 'Dēsine, Mārce!' inquit, 'Titus tibi mālum dare nōn potest, at ego tibi mālum dare possum, nisi hic et nunc Titō librum reddis!' Mārcus Titō librum reddit.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"includit","latin":"inclūdit","headword":"inclūdit","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"shuts in; locks up","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dūc eum in cubiculum eius, Dāve, atque inclūde eum!","reading":"RESPŌNSVM IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"inclutus","latin":"inclutus, -a, -um","headword":"inclutus","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"famous; renowned","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iam tum erat inclutum fānum Diānae Ephesī; id commūniter ā cīvitātibus Asiae factum fāma ferēbat.","reading":"CENSVS INSTITVTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"incolumis","latin":"incolumis","headword":"incolumis","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"unharmed; safe","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Plērīque autem mīlitēs nostrī ex tantō proeliō incolumēs sunt.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"incolumitas","latin":"incolumitās, -ātis","headword":"incolumitās","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"safety","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Octāviī prōnūntiātum est per praecōnem 'rēgiōs puerōs Macedonāsque aliōs quī Samothrācae essent, sī transīrent ad Rōmānōs, incolumitātem lībertātemque et sua omnia servātūrōs quae aut sēcum habērent aut in Macedoniā relīquissent.' Ad hanc vōcem trānsitiō omnium facta est, nōminaque dabant ad C.","reading":"PERSEVS CAPTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"incolunt","latin":"incolunt","headword":"incolunt","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"inhabit","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Germānī sunt hominēs barbarī quī Germāniam incolunt.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"incommodum","latin":"incommodum, -ī","headword":"incommodum","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"disadvantage; loss","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lūcullus, quī tamen aliquā ex parte iīs incommodīs medērī fortasse potuisset, vestrō iussū coāctus — quod imperiī diuturnitātī modum statuendum vetere exemplō putāvistis — partem mīlitum quī iam stīpendiīs cōnfectī erant dīmīsit, partem M'.","reading":"DĒ MAGNITŪDINE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"inconspectus","latin":"incōnspectus, -a, -um","headword":"incōnspectus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"unexamined; not properly considered","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"incredibilis","latin":"incrēdibilis, -e","headword":"incrēdibilis","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"incredible","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc iam incrēdibilis fāma iīs allāta est: Helēnum, Priamī fīlium, rēgnō Ēpīrī potītum esse atque Andromachēn, viduam Hectoris, uxōrem dūxisse!","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"incursio","latin":"incursiō, -ōnis","headword":"incursiō","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"raid; invasion","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Igitur Latīnī, cum quibus Tullō rēgnante foedus ictum erat, sustulerant animōs, et cum incursiōnem in agrum Rōmānum fēcissent, repetentibus rēs Rōmānīs superbē respōnsum reddunt — ōtiōsum Rōmānum rēgem inter lānā et ārās rēgnum āctūrum esse ratī.","reading":"ANCVS MARCIUS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"indicium","latin":"indicium, -ī","headword":"indicium","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"evidence; disclosure","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cassius, quī tum praetor erat, ad Iugurtham mitterētur eumque, datā fidē pūblicā, Rōmam dūceret, ut eius indiciō patefierent dēlicta eōrum et reliquōrum quī pecūniae acceptae accūsābantur.","reading":"IVGVRTHA RŌMAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"indignatio","latin":"indignātiō, -ōnis","headword":"indignātiō","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"indignation; resentment","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rōmulus vērō indignātiōnem dissimulāns lūdōs parat Neptūnō; deinde fīnitimōs ad spectāculum vocārī iubet.","reading":"SABINAE RAPTAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"indignitas","latin":"indīgnitās, -ātis","headword":"indīgnitās","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"outrage; indignity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī ubi in Āfricam trānsiērunt, acceptīs quōs imperāverant trecentīs obsidibus et armīs omnibus īnstrūmentīsque bellī, cum ex auctōritāte patrum iubērentur in alium locum sēdēs transferre, dum ā marī decem mīlia passuum nec minus recessissent, Carthāginiēnsēs indignitāte reī ad bellum compulsī sunt.","reading":"BELLVM PVNICVM TERTIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"indignus","latin":"indignus","headword":"indignus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"unworthy; disgraceful","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Intellegisne factum tuum indignum esse?","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"indoctus","latin":"indoctus","headword":"indoctus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"unlearned; ignorant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister est vir doctus; puerī adhūc indoctī sunt.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"indoles","latin":"indolēs, -is","headword":"indolēs","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"natural character; disposition","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haud displicet rēs Tullō, quamquam cum indole, tum spē victōriae ferōcior erat.","reading":"TRIGEMINORVM PVGNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"industria","latin":"industria, -ae","headword":"industria","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"diligence; energy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pompēium interfectus est, quem adulēscentem Sulla atque annōs ūnum et vīgintī nātum, cognitā eius industriā, exercitibus praefēcerat, ut secundus ā Sullā habērētur.","reading":"BELLVM CĪVĪLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"industrius","latin":"industrius","headword":"industrius","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"industrious; hard-working","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Discipulus quī nec stultus nec piger est, sed prūdēns atque industrius, multās rēs ā magistrō discere potest.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"inermis","latin":"inermis","headword":"inermis","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"unarmed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus autem gladium brevem, quem adhūc sub veste occultāvit, ēdūcit et \"Equidem\" inquit \"nōn inermīs occīdar.","reading":"IN MARĪ TVSCŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"inertia","latin":"inertia, -ae","headword":"inertia","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"idleness; inactivity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī ubi prīmum adolēvit, pollēns vīribus, decōrā faciē, sed multō maximē ingeniō validus, nōn sē luxuī neque inertiae corrumpendum dedit, sed, utī mōs gentis illīus est, equitāre, iaculārī, cursū cum aequalibus certāre; et, cum omnēs glōriā anteīret, omnibus tamen cārus esse.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"infandus","latin":"īnfandus, -a, -um","headword":"īnfandus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"unspeakable; monstrous","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mōnstrum īnfandum est Cyclōps ille nōmine Polyphēmus, quī carne et sanguine hominum miserōrum vēscitur!","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"infans","latin":"īnfāns (infantis)","headword":"īnfāns","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"infant; baby","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Parvulus īnfāns in cūnīs cubāre solet.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"inferi","latin":"īnferī","headword":"īnferī","letter":"i","pos":"noun (m. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"the underworld; the dead","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī hoc vērum est, prīnceps omnium deōrum est deus tuus; neque enim ūllus deus Rōmānus hominem mortālem ab Īnferīs suscitāre potest; nē Iuppiter quidem tantam potestātem habet, etsī ille deus maximus habētur.\"","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"infestus","latin":"īnfēstus","headword":"īnfēstus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"hostile (to; + dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ōlim cūncta maria tam īnfēstā erant praedōnibus ut nēmō nāvigāret sine maximō perīculō mortis aut servitūtis.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"infidus","latin":"īnfidus","headword":"īnfidus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"faithless","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"infinitus","latin":"infīnītus, -a, -um","headword":"infīnītus","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"boundless; endless","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Intereā Cimbrī et Teutonēs, quōrum cōpia adhūc infīnīta erat, ad Ītaliam trānsiērunt.","reading":"BELLVM CIMBRICVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"inflammare","latin":"īnflammāre","headword":"īnflammāre","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to kindle; set on fire","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīs dictīs animum sorōris amōre īnflammāvit et mentī dubiae spem dedit atque pudōrem solvit.","reading":"FLAMMA AMŌRIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"informis","latin":"īnfōrmis, -e","headword":"īnfōrmis","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"shapeless; hideous","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Praestat tōtam Siciliam longō cursū circumīre quam semel Scyllam īnfōrmem vidēre et saxa illa resonantia experīrī.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"ingenium","latin":"ingenium","headword":"ingenium","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"nature; talent; wit","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ovidius poeta, qui ingenium mulierum tam bene noverat quam ipsae mulieres, rationem reddit hoc versu: 'Spectatum veniunt, veniunt spectentur ut ipsae!'\"","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"ingens","latin":"ingēns","headword":"ingēns","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"huge; vast","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"inimicus","latin":"inimīcus","headword":"inimīcus","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"enemy","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus amīcus Mēdī nōn est, nam servus bonus et servus malus nōn amīcī, sed inimīcī sunt.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"iniquitas","latin":"inīquitās, -ātis","headword":"inīquitās","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"injustice; unfairness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam vel rēx aequus et sapiēns, vel dēlēctī ac prīncipēs cīvēs, vel ipse populus, quamquam id est minimē probandum, tamen, nūllīs interiectīs inīquitātibus aut cupiditātibus, posse vidētur aliquō esse nōn incertō statū.","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"innocentia","latin":"innocentia, -ae","headword":"innocentia","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"integrity; innocence","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Utinam, Quirītēs, virōrum fortium atque innocentium cōpiam tantam habērētis ut haec vōbīs dēlīberātiō difficilis esset, quemnam potissimum tantīs rēbus ac tantō bellō praeficiendum putārētis!","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"inopia","latin":"inopia","headword":"inopia","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"scarcity; want","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ita maxima inopia frūmentī facta est, quam ob rem pretium frūmentī semper crēscēbat.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"insatiabilis","latin":"īnsatiābilis, -e","headword":"īnsatiābilis","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"insatiable","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Duodecim mīlia sē Sullae dēdidērunt, cēterī in aciē, in castrīs, in fugā īnsatiābilī īrā victōrum cōnsūmptī sunt.","reading":"BELLVM CĪVĪLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"insciens","latin":"īnsciēns, -entis","headword":"īnsciēns","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"not knowing; unaware","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Gortȳniī templum magnā cūrā custōdiunt, nōn tam ā cēterīs quam ab Hannibale, nē ille īnscientibus iīs tolleret sēcumque dūceret.","reading":"APVD ANTIOCHVM ET IN CRĒTĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"insidiae","latin":"īnsidiae, -ārum","headword":"īnsidiae","letter":"i","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ambush; treachery; trap","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed īnfēlīx Dīdō noctem variō sermōne trahēbat, multa super Priamō rogitāns, super Hectore multa: 'Immo, age, et ā prīmā dīc, hospes, orīgine nōbīs īnsidiās' inquit 'Danaum cāsūsque tuōrum errōrēsque tuōs.","reading":"CONVĪVIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"latin":"Sed latrōnēs ob praedam āmissam īrātī geminīs īnsidiās fēcērunt et, cum Rōmulus vī sē dēfendisset, Remum cēpērunt et captum rēgī Amūliō trādidērunt falsō accūsantēs 'in Numitōris agrōs ab iīs impetūs fierī; inde coāctā iuvenum manū hostīlem in modum praedās agere!' Sīc Numitōrī ad supplicium Remus dēditur.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"insidiator","latin":"īnsidiātor, -ōris","headword":"īnsidiātor","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ambusher; assassin","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīs difficultātibus circumventus, ubi videt neque per vim neque īnsidiīs opprimī posse hominem tam acceptum populāribus, quod erat Iugurtha manū prōmptus et appetēns glōriae mīlitāris, statuit eum obiectāre perīculīs et eō modō fortūnam temptāre.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"insolentia","latin":"īnsolentia, -ae","headword":"īnsolentia","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"arrogance; excess","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deinde, victōriīs dīvitiīsque subnīxus, exsultābat īnsolentiā neque suōs mōrēs regere poterat neque suōrum libīdinēs.'","reading":"DĒ VETERE RĒ PŪBLICĀ RŌMĀNĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"instruo","latin":"īnstruō","headword":"īnstruō","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to draw up; arrange","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum agmen ad hostēs pervēnit, sī tempus et locus idōneus est ad pugnandum, cohortēs in trēs ōrdinēs īnstruuntur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"insula","latin":"īnsula","headword":"īnsula","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"island","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Corsica īnsula est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"'In īnsulā Crēta ōlim vīvēbat mōnstrum terribile, Mīnōtaurus, cui caput taurī, corpus virī erat.","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"integer","latin":"integer","headword":"integer","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"whole; intact; unbroken","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"inter","latin":"inter","headword":"inter","letter":"i","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"between; among","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Via Appia est inter Rōmam et Brundisium; via Latīna inter Rōmam et Capuam; via Flāminia inter Rōmam et Arīminum; via Aurēlia inter Rōmam et Genuam; via Aemilia inter Arīminum et Placentiam.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"interdum","latin":"interdum","headword":"interdum","letter":"i","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sometimes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"interiectio","latin":"interiectiō","headword":"interiectiō","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"interjection","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"interitus","latin":"interitus, -ūs","headword":"interitus","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"death; destruction","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam vel rēx aequus et sapiēns, vel dēlēctī ac prīncipēs cīvēs, vel ipse populus, quamquam id est minimē probandum, tamen, nūllīs interiectīs inīquitātibus aut cupiditātibus, posse vidētur aliquō esse nōn incertō statū.","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"internicio","latin":"interniciō, -ōnis","headword":"interniciō","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"slaughter; destruction","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Caepiō ā Cimbrīs et Teutonibus et Tīgurīnīs et Ambrōnibus, quae erant Germānōrum et Gallōrum gentēs, victī sunt iuxtā flūmen Rhodanum ingentī interniciōne; etiam castra sua et magnam partem exercitūs perdidērunt.","reading":"BELLVM CIMBRICVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"interregnum","latin":"interrēgnum, -ī","headword":"interrēgnum","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"period between two kings","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēnī simul quīnōs diēs imperitābant, quōrum prīncipēs, quī \"interrēgēs\" nōminābantur, cum īnsignibus imperiī erant.","reading":"INTERREGNVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"interrex","latin":"interrēx, -rēgis","headword":"interrēx","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"regent between two kings","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēnī simul quīnōs diēs imperitābant, quōrum prīncipēs, quī \"interrēgēs\" nōminābantur, cum īnsignibus imperiī erant.","reading":"INTERREGNVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"interrogat","latin":"interrogat","headword":"interrogat","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"asks; questions","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia interrogat: 'Quis mē vocat?'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"interrogo","latin":"interrogō","headword":"interrogō","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"ask; question","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister Titum interrogat.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"intervallum","latin":"intervallum, -ī","headword":"intervallum","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gap; interval","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iam aliquantum spatiī ex eō locō ubi pugnātum est aufūgerat, cum respiciēns videt Curiātiōs magnīs intervāllīs sequentēs, ūnum haud procul ab sēsē abesse.","reading":"TRIGEMINORVM PVGNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"interventus","latin":"interventus, -ūs","headword":"interventus","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"interruption; arrival","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Num sermōnem vestrum aliquem dīrēmit noster interventus?' 'Minimē vērō!' Āfricānus; 'sōlēs enim tē haec studiōsē investīgāre quae sunt in hōc genere, dē quō īnstituerat paulō ante Tubērō quaerere; Rutilius quidem noster etiam sub ipsīs Numantiae moenibus solēbat, mēcum interdum eius modī aliquid conquīrere.' 'Quae rēs tandem inciderat?' inquit Philus.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"intrat","latin":"intrat","headword":"intrat","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"enters; goes into","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ovis nigra ovēs albās relinquit et rīvum petit; aquam bibit ē rīvō, et in silvam intrat!","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Āēr frīgidus cubiculum Mārcī intrat, fenestra enim aperta est.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"intueri","latin":"intuērī","headword":"intuērī","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to look at; gaze at","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"intuetur","latin":"intuētur","headword":"intuētur","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"looks at; watches","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"investigare","latin":"investīgāre","headword":"investīgāre","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to investigate; search out","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Num sermōnem vestrum aliquem dīrēmit noster interventus?' 'Minimē vērō!' Āfricānus; 'sōlēs enim tē haec studiōsē investīgāre quae sunt in hōc genere, dē quō īnstituerat paulō ante Tubērō quaerere; Rutilius quidem noster etiam sub ipsīs Numantiae moenibus solēbat, mēcum interdum eius modī aliquid conquīrere.' 'Quae rēs tandem inciderat?' inquit Philus.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"invictus","latin":"invictus, -a, -um","headword":"invictus","letter":"i","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"unconquered","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōnne tibi in mentem venit quī hostēs nōs cingant: Gaetūlī Numidaeque, gentēs invictae, et frāter tuus Pygmaliōn, quī Tyrō bellum minātur?","reading":"FLAMMA AMŌRIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"invidet","latin":"invidet","headword":"invidet","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"envies (with dative)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Cum Arīōn, nōbilissimus suī temporis fidicen, ex Italiā in Graeciam nāvigāret magnāsque dīvitiās sēcum habēret, nautae pauperēs, quī hominī dīvitī invidēbant, eum necāre cōnstituērunt.","reading":"FĀBVLA ARĪONIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"invidia","latin":"invidia, -ae","headword":"invidia","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"envy; hatred; unpopularity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi tam ātrox invidia in Turnum orta est, gladiīs in mediō positīs, ut sine iūdiciō — novō genere suppliciī — dēiectus in aquam, crāte super iniectā, mergerētur.","reading":"TURNUS HERDONIUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"iratus","latin":"īrātus","headword":"īrātus","letter":"i","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"angry","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus: 'Ssst!' Mārcus īrātus est.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"is/ea/id","latin":"is/ea/id","headword":"is/ea/id","letter":"i","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"he; she; it; this; that","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"it","latin":"it","headword":"it","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"goes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius ab oppidō ad vīllam suam it.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"itaque","latin":"itaque","headword":"itaque","letter":"i","pos":"adverb; conjunction","posGroup":"verb","english":"therefore; and so","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dominus servōs malōs baculō verberat; itaque servī malī dominum et baculum eius timent.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Pāstor duōs pedēs habet, itaque pāstor ambulāre potest.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"iubet","latin":"iubet","headword":"iubet","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"orders; bids","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius servum suum Tusculum īre iubet atque medicum arcessere.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"iudex","latin":"iūdex, -icis","headword":"iūdex","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"judge","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"iudicium","latin":"iūdicium, -ī","headword":"iūdicium","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"judgement; decision","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Id metuēns et memor veteris bellī quod ad Trōiam prō cārīs Argīs gesserat — nōndum oblīta erat causam īrae ac dolōris: iūdicium Paridis, quī Venerem deam pulcherrimam esse iūdicāverat — Trōiānōs per mare tōtum iactātōs longē ā Latiō arcēbat.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"iugerum","latin":"iūgerum, -ī","headword":"iūgerum","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"a measure of land (about ¼ hectare)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīnctius Cincinnātus dictātor est factus, quī agrum quattuor iūgerum possidēns manibus suīs colēbat.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"},{"latin":"Deinde, cum minus agrī esset quam quod dīvidī posset sine offēnsā etiam plēbis — quoniam eōs ad cupiditātem amplum modum spērandī incitāverat — lēgem sē iūgerum prōmulgātūrum ostendit: 'ut iīs quī Semprōniā lēge agrum accipere dēbērent, pecūnia quae rēgis Attalī fuisset dīviderētur.' Hērēdem autem populum Rōmānum relīquerat Attalus, rēx Pergamī, Eumenis fīlius.","reading":"LĒGĒS AGRĀRIAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"iugulum","latin":"iugulum, -ī","headword":"iugulum","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"throat","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"iugum","latin":"iugum, -ī","headword":"iugum","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"yoke; sub iugum mittere; to send under the yoke","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum cōnsulēs ingentī dēdecōre victī sunt et sub iugum missī.","reading":"SAMNĪTĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"iungit","latin":"iungit","headword":"iungit","letter":"i","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"joins; connects","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ius iurandum","latin":"iūs iūrandum","headword":"iūs iūrandum","letter":"i","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"oath; sworn formula","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nusquam igitur scrīptum invenīre est — apud idōneōs quidem scrīptōrēs — aut 'mehercle' fēminam dīcere aut 'mecastor' virum; 'edepol' autem, quod iūs iūrandum per Pollūcem est, et virō et fēminae commūne est.","reading":"DĒ IVRE IVRANDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"iusta","latin":"iūsta, -ōrum","headword":"iūsta","letter":"i","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"funeral rites","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postquam illī mōre rēgiō iūsta magnificē fēcerant, rēgulī in ūnum convēnērunt, ut inter sē dē cūnctīs negōtiīs disceptārent.","reading":"MORS HIEMPSALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"iustitia","latin":"iūstitia, -ae","headword":"iūstitia","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"justice","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aborīginēs Italiae incolae prīmī fuērunt, quōrum rēx Sāturnus tantā iūstitiā fuisse dīcitur ut neque servīret quisquam sub illō neque quidquam suum proprium habēret, sed omnia commūnia omnibus essent.","reading":"ABORĪGINĒS ET RĒGĒS LATIĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"iuvencus","latin":"iuvencus, -ī","headword":"iuvencus","letter":"i","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"young bull","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ille, immolātīs ex mōre iuvencīs, Aenēam ad Phoebī templum manū dūxit, deinde dīvīnō ex ōre haec fātus est: \"Nāte deā!","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"iuventus","latin":"iuventūs, -ūtis","headword":"iuventūs","letter":"i","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"youth","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Huius fīlius in prīmā iuventūte periit; sōla in rēgiā erat fīlia, nōmine Lavīnia, iam mātūra virō.","reading":"ABORĪGINĒS ET RĒGĒS LATIĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"kalendae","latin":"kalendae","headword":"kalendae","letter":"k","pos":"noun (f. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"the Kalends (first day of the month); the Kalends (first of the month)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Diēs mēnsis prīmus \"kalendae\" nōminātur.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"latin":"K litterā, quae frequēns est in linguā Graeca, littera Latīna rārissima est, nam K in ūnō vocābulō Latīnō tantum reperītur, id est kalendae (itemque in praenōmine Kaesō, quod praenōmen Rōmānōrum rārissimum est).","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"labefactare","latin":"labefactāre","headword":"labefactāre","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to shake; undermine","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī patre Marte nātus cum Remō frātre dīcitur ab Amūliō, rēge Albānō, ob labefactandī rēgnī timōrem ad Tiberim expōnī iussus esse.","reading":"DĒ VETERE RĒ PŪBLICĀ RŌMĀNĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"labes","latin":"lābes, -is","headword":"lābes","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stain; disgrace","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"labi","latin":"lābī","headword":"lābī","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to slip; slide; fall","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ille trīstīs mercēs suās dē nāve lābī et in mare mergī videt.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"labrum","latin":"labrum","headword":"labrum","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lip","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"labyrinthus","latin":"labyrinthus","headword":"labyrinthus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"labyrinth; maze","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In magnō labyrinthō habitābat.'","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"latin":"Tum rēx īrātus cēpit Daedalum, quī fīlum cōnfēcerat et Ariadnae dederat, eumque in labyrinthum inclūdī iussit ūna cum eius Īcarō fīliō; vērum pater et fīlius mīrābilī modō ē labyrinthō fūgērunt.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"lac","latin":"lac (lactis)","headword":"lac","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"milk","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Īnfāns lac mammae bibit.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"lacertus","latin":"lacertus","headword":"lacertus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"(upper) arm","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Igne cēram molliam, cērā mollī pennās iungam et in lacertīs fīgam.\"","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"lacessere","latin":"lacessere","headword":"lacessere","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to provoke; challenge","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Bellum grave et perīculōsum vestrīs vectīgālibus ac sociīs ā duōbus potentissimīs rēgibus īnfertur, Mithridāte et Tigrāne, quōrum alter relictus, alter lacessītus occasionem sibi ad occupandam Asiam oblātam esse arbitrātur.","reading":"DĒ GENERE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"lacrima","latin":"lacrima","headword":"lacrima","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tear","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puella lacrimat: in oculīs eius sunt lacrimae.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"latin":"Puerum Rōmānum sine lacrimīs dolōrem patī decet.'","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"lacrimat","latin":"lacrimat","headword":"lacrimat","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"weeps; cries","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puella lacrimat: in oculīs eius sunt lacrimae.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"lacteus","latin":"lacteus, -a, -um","headword":"lacteus","letter":"l","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"milky","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ea vīta via est in caelum et in hunc coetum eōrum quī iam vīxērunt et corpore laxātī illum incolunt locum quem vidēs' — erat autem is splendidissimō candōre inter flammās circus ēlūcēns — 'quem vōs, ut ā Graecīs accēpistis, \"orbem lacteum\" nuncupātis.'","reading":"MORS ET VĪTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"laedere","latin":"laedere","headword":"laedere","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to hurt; injure","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Marcus vero, si quis eum laedere vult, ipse se defendere potest.\" Fabia: \"Item Sextus scit se defendere, dummodo cum singulis certet.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"laetari","latin":"laetārī","headword":"laetārī","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to rejoice; rejoice; be glad","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At nōn possum laetārī quod omnēs meās Rōmānās relinquō.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"laetatur","latin":"laetātur","headword":"laetātur","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"rejoices (deponent)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"laetor","latin":"laetor","headword":"laetor","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"rejoice; be glad (deponent)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sextus: 'Nōnne tū laetāris, Mārce, quod frāter tuus etiam absēns ā magistrō laudātur?' Mārcus: 'Ego nōn laetor cum frāter meus laudātur!","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"laetus","latin":"laetus","headword":"laetus","letter":"l","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"happy; glad","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus: 'St!' Mārcus laetus nōn est.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"laevus","latin":"laevus","headword":"laevus","letter":"l","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"left; on the left","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puer territus pedēs nōdōs aspicit et 'Quid hoc est?' inquit; 'Pēs dexter multō maior est quam pēs laevus!'","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"lapis","latin":"lapis, -idis","headword":"lapis","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stone","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"laqueus","latin":"laqueus, -ī","headword":"laqueus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"noose","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Līctor, colliga manūs!\" Accesserat līctor iniciēbatque laqueum collō.","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"largitio","latin":"largītiō, -ōnis","headword":"largītiō","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bribery; lavish giving","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postquam rēx fīnem loquendī fēcit, lēgātī Iugurthae, largītiōne magis quam causā frētī, paucīs respondent: 'Hiempsalem ob saevitiam suam ab Numidīs interfectum; Adherbalem ultrō bellum īnferentem, postquam superātus sit, querī quod iniūriam facere nequīvisset!","reading":"ADHERBAL RŌMAM PROFĪCĪSCITUR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"lascivia","latin":"lascīvia, -ae","headword":"lascīvia","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"licence; wantonness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed ubi illa formīdō mentibus dēcessit, scīlicet ea quae rēs secundae amant, lascīvia atque superbia, incessēre.","reading":"CĪVITĀS DĪLACERĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"latebra","latin":"latebra, -ae","headword":"latebra","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hiding-place; retreat","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"latere","latin":"latēre","headword":"latēre","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to hide; lurk","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Crēdō eum apud puellam Rōmānam latēre.' Orontēs: 'Ergō numquam reperiētur, nam vērum est quod scrīpsit Ovidius in librō quī vocātur Ars amandī: Quot caelum stēllās, tot habet tua Rōma puellās.'","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"latine","latin":"Latīne","headword":"Latīne","letter":"l","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"in Latin","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nescīs Latīnē scrībere!","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"latinus","latin":"Latīnus","headword":"Latīnus","letter":"l","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"Latin","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ubi quoque vocābulum Latīnum est.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"latrare","latin":"lātrāre","headword":"lātrāre","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to bark","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"latrat","latin":"lātrat","headword":"lātrat","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"barks","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"latro","latin":"latrō, -ōnis","headword":"latrō","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"robber; bandit","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ita vīribus corporum auctīs iam nōn ferās tantum petēbant, sed in latrōnēs praedam facientēs impetūs faciēbant pāstōribusque praedam dīvidēbant.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"latus","latin":"lātus","headword":"lātus","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"side; flank","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra iuxtā lectum ad latus puerī laevum cōnsīdit eumque sīc cōnsōlātur: 'Nōlī trīstīs esse quod hīc intus cubās: immō laetāre tē nōn inclūsum esse in cubiculō ut frātrem tuum!","reading":"SYRA NĀRRAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"laudare","latin":"laudāre","headword":"laudāre","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"praise; to praise","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"laudat","latin":"laudat","headword":"laudat","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"praises","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pulchritūdō Veneris ab omnibus laudātur.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"laudo","latin":"laudō","headword":"laudō","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"praise","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister Titum et Sextum laudat: 'Vōs rēctē respondētis, Tite et Sexte.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"lautus","latin":"lautus","headword":"lautus","letter":"l","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"washed; bathed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed brevī lautus erit.' Tum Iūlius lautus et novā veste indūtus intrat et amīcōs salvēre iubet: 'Salvēte, amīcī!","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"lavat","latin":"lavat","headword":"lavat","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"washes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus prīmum manus lavat, deinde faciem.","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"lectica","latin":"lectīca","headword":"lectīca","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"litter; sedan-chair","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dominus in lectīcā est.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"lectissimus","latin":"lēctissimus, -a, -um","headword":"lēctissimus","letter":"l","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"picked; elite","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hāc pugnā Mithridātēs cognitā septuāgintā mīlia lēctissima ex Asiā Archelaō mīsit, contrā quem iterum Sulla commīsit.","reading":"BELLVM MITHRIDĀTICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"lectus","latin":"lectus","headword":"lectus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bed; couch","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In trīclīniō sunt trēs lectī, lectus summus, medius, īmus, et mēnsā in mediō.","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"legatus","latin":"lēgātus, -ī","headword":"lēgātus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"envoy; lieutenant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"legio","latin":"legiō, -ōnis","headword":"legiō","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"legion","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Exercitus Rōmānus ūniversus cōnstat ex legiōnibus duodētrīgintā, quae in dēnās cohortēs dīviduntur.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"latin":"Sex in eum annum dēcrētae legiōnēs et classis quanta parārī posset.","reading":"EXCIDIVM SAGVNTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"legit","latin":"legit","headword":"legit","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"reads","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quōmodo parvus discipulus hanc sententiam lēgit: Mīles Rōmānus fortiter pugnat?","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"legitimus","latin":"lēgitimus, -a, -um","headword":"lēgitimus","letter":"l","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"lawful; legitimate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum illō simul iūsta ac lēgitima rēgna occīdērunt.","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"lembus","latin":"lembus, -ī","headword":"lembus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"small boat","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēmētrium est portus in prōmunturiō quōdam Samothrācae; ibi lembus stābat.","reading":"PERSEVS CAPTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"lenire","latin":"lēnīre","headword":"lēnīre","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to soften; soothe; calm","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ardeam Rutulī habēbant, gens — ut in eā regiōne et in eā aetāte — dīvitiīs praepotēns; eaque ipsa causa bellī fuit, quod rēx Rōmānus cum ipse dītārī volēbat (exhaustō aerāriō magnificentia pūblicōrum operum), tum praedā lēnīre populārium animōs studēbat, quī sē in servilī opere tam diū habitōs ab rēge indignābantur.","reading":"LŪCRĒTIA VIOLĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"leo","latin":"leō","headword":"leō","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lion","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Equus et asinus, leō et lupus, canis et ovis bēstiae sunt.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"levat","latin":"levat","headword":"levat","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"lifts; raises","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"levis","latin":"levis","headword":"levis","letter":"l","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"light (in weight)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pedēs, quī pedibus it multaque alia arma fert, gladium longum et gravem ferre nōn potest; itaque gladius eius brevis et levis est — brevior et levior quam is quī ab equite fertur.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"libellus","latin":"libellus","headword":"libellus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"little book; scroll","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed ipsa male nārrō: ex libellō recitābō tibi aliquid.\"","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"libenter","latin":"libenter","headword":"libenter","letter":"l","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"gladly; willingly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Libenter faciam\" inquit Iulius, \"sed iam nimis obscurum est hoc triclinium; in tenebris legere non possum.","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"liber","latin":"liber","headword":"liber","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"book","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus, Quīntus Iūliaque sunt trēs līberī.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Mārcus cum servō ātrium intrat, ubi parentēs sedent līberōs exspectantēs.","reading":"DISCESSVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"liberator","latin":"līberātor, -ōris","headword":"līberātor","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"liberator; deliverer","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Caput obnūbe — līberātōris urbis huius!","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"liberi","latin":"līberī","headword":"līberī","letter":"l","pos":"noun (m. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"children (free-born)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus, Quīntus Iūliaque sunt trēs līberī.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"libertas","latin":"lībertās, -ātis","headword":"lībertās","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"freedom; liberty","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dīxistī tē mortem servitūtī praeferre.\" Gubernātor: \"Haud sciō an ego ita dīxerim, sed profectō lībertās mihi vīta cārior est.","reading":"IN MARĪ TVSCŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"},{"latin":"Illī lībertātem imminūtam cīvium Rōmānōrum nōn tulērunt — vōs ēreptam vītam neglegētis?","reading":"DĒ GENERE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"libido","latin":"libīdō, -inis","headword":"libīdō","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"desire; lust","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tarquinium mala libīdō Lūcrētiae per vim stuprandae capit; cum fōrmā tum spectāta castitās incitat.","reading":"LŪCRĒTIA VIOLĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"libra","latin":"lībra, -ae","headword":"lībra","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pound (a weight)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornēlium Rūfīnum, quī bis cōnsul et dictātor fuerat, senātū mōvērunt: causamque istī notae subscrīpsērunt 'quod eum comperissent argentī factī cēnae grātiā decem pondō lībrās habēre.'","reading":"PHILIPPVS ĀD LŪCĪLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"licentia","latin":"licentia, -ae","headword":"licentia","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"licence; unrestrained freedom","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quā tū audācia, mē vīvō, vocāre ausus es patrēs aut sēde cōnsīdere mea?\" Cum ille ferōciter ad haec — \"sē patris suī tenēre sēdem: fīlium rēgis multō potiōrem rēgnī hērēdem esse quam servum; illum satis diū per licentiam illūsisse dominīs\" — clāmor ab utriusque fautōribus oritur et concursus populī fīēbat in cūriam.","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"licere","latin":"licēre","headword":"licēre","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to be allowed (licet; it is allowed)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"licet","latin":"licet","headword":"licet","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"it is allowed; one may","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In lectulō dormīre licet, hic in lūdō nōn licet dormīre!'","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ DORMIENTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"lictor","latin":"līctor, -ōris","headword":"līctor","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lictor; attendant of a magistrate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Et ut hominēs agrestēs novum rēgem verērentur, ipse sē īnsignibus imperiī augustiōrem fēcit: cum vestem purpuream induit, tum līctōrēs duodecim sūmpsit, quī fascēs et secūrēs ante eum gerentēs īrent.","reading":"ROMVLVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"lignum","latin":"lignum","headword":"lignum","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wood","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lignum est māteria dūra, sed minus dūra quam ferrum.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"lilium","latin":"līlium","headword":"līlium","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lily","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"limen","latin":"līmen","headword":"līmen","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"threshold","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sub foribus est līmen, in quō SALVĒ scrīptum est.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"limes","latin":"līmes, -itis","headword":"līmes","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"path; boundary","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Quae cum dīxisset, \"Egō vērō\" inquam \"Āfricāne, sīquidem bene meritīs dē patriā quasi līmes ad caelī aditum patet, quamquam ā pueritiā vestīgiīs ingressus patris et tuīs decōrī vestrō nōn dēfuī, nunc tamen tantō praemiō exposītō ēnītar multō vigilantius!\" Et ille: \"Ille vērō ēnītere et sīc habētō: nōn esse tē mortālem, sed corpus hoc.","reading":"DĒ GLŌRIĀ AETERNĀ ET ANIMŌ IMMORTĀLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"linea","latin":"līnea","headword":"līnea","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"line; necklace","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Etiam līnea cum margarītīs ōrnāmentum est.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"lingua","latin":"lingua","headword":"lingua","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tongue; language","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In ōre lingua et dentēs īnsunt.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Magnī discipulī litterās Graecās et linguam Graecam discunt.","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"littera","latin":"littera","headword":"littera","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"letter (of the alphabet); pl. writing; letter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"A et B litterae sunt.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"In lūdō puerī numerōs et litterās discunt.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"litterae","latin":"litterae","headword":"litterae","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"a letter; epistle (written message)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōlō hās litterās legere, nam certē poscit pecūniam quam eī dēbeō.","reading":"EPISTVLA ADVENIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"litus","latin":"lītus","headword":"lītus","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shore; beach; coast","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ariadna igitur in lītus dēscendit atque hūc et illūc currēns cum lacrimīs capillum et vestem scindēbat, ut eae quae maerent agere solent — ita maerēbat virgō quae ā virō, quem ante omnēs amābat, sōla erat inter ferās īnsulae sīcut agnus timidus inter lupōs.'","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"lituus","latin":"lituus, -ī","headword":"lituus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"augur’s curved staff; curved trumpet","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"longinquitas","latin":"longinquitās, -ātis","headword":"longinquitās","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"distance; remoteness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Noster autem exercitus, tametsī urbem ex Tigrānis rēgnō cēperat et proeliīs ūsus erat secundīs, tamen nimiā longinquitāte locōrum ac dēsīderiō suōrum commovēbātur.","reading":"DĒ MAGNITŪDINE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"longinquus","latin":"longinquus, -a, -um","headword":"longinquus","letter":"l","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"far off; distant","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quō factō patrem suum dē rē certiōrem fēcit, quī sine morā terram illam longinquam quaerendam esse cēnsuit.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"longus","latin":"longus","headword":"longus","letter":"l","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"long","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tiberis fluvius nōn tam longus est quam fluvius Padus.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Pīlum nōn tam longum est quam hastā, neque gladius peditis tam longus est quam gladius equitis.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"loqui","latin":"loquī","headword":"loquī","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to speak; speak","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dum ille loquitur, Mēdus occidentem spectat et nūbēs ātrās procul suprā mare orīrī videt; simul mare tranquillum esse dēsinit. 'Nōn serēnum est caelum,' inquit, 'Ecce nūbēs ātrae ...' Gubernātor statim loquī dēsinit et nūbēs spectat; tum caelum aspiciēns exclāmat: 'Quid (malum!) hoc est?","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Simul īnfāns plūra verba discet et mox rēctē loquī sciet.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"lucerna","latin":"lucerna","headword":"lucerna","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lamp","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lucernas accendite, servi!\"","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"lucet","latin":"lūcet","headword":"lūcet","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"shines; is light","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aestāte diēs longī sunt, sōl lūcet, āēr calidus est.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"lucrum","latin":"lucrum","headword":"lucrum","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"profit; gain","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ita spērābat sē magnum lucrum factūrum esse.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"luctus","latin":"lūctus, -ūs","headword":"lūctus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"grief; mourning","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Plūrima corpora sternuntur per viās et per domōs, ubīque lūctus et pavor.","reading":"SOMNIVM AENĒAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"lucus","latin":"lūcus, -ī","headword":"lūcus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sacred grove","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ludibrium","latin":"lūdibrium, -ī","headword":"lūdibrium","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mockery; laughing-stock","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is tum ab Tarquiniīs Delphōs ductus est, lūdibrium vērius quam comes.","reading":"TEMPLUM IOVIS ET ŌRĀCULUM DELPHICUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"ludit","latin":"lūdit","headword":"lūdit","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"plays","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque puella lūdit cum cane suā Margarītā.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"ludus","latin":"lūdus","headword":"lūdus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"school; game; play","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Illīc est lūdus puerōrum.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"lugere","latin":"lūgēre","headword":"lūgēre","letter":"l","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to mourn; grieve","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Illo occiso spectatores plaudere desierunt ac lugere coeperunt.\"","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"lumen","latin":"lūmen, -inis","headword":"lūmen","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"light","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tālia exclāmāns omnem domum gemitū complēbat — cum subitō mīrābile prōdigium vīsum est: namque inter manūs maestōrum parentum lūmen in summō culminī appāruit, neque flamma puerō nocēbat!","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"luna","latin":"lūna","headword":"lūna","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"moon","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nocte sōl nōn lūcet, sed lūna et stēllae lūcent.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"lupa","latin":"lupa, -ae","headword":"lupa","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"she-wolf","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum aqua recēdēns alveum, in quō expositī erant puerī, in siccō relīquisset, lupa sitiēns ex montibus ad puerīlem vāgītum cursum flēxit.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"lupus","latin":"lupus","headword":"lupus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wolf","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In silvā est lupus.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Equus et asinus, leō et lupus, canis et ovis bēstiae sunt.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"lustrum","latin":"lūstrum, -ī","headword":"lūstrum","letter":"l","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"purification; five-year period","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi īnstrūctum exercitum omnem suovetaurīlibus lūstrāvit; ita cēnsuī fīnis factus est idque \"lustrum condere\" appellātum.","reading":"CENSVS INSTITVTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"lux","latin":"lūx","headword":"lūx","letter":"l","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"light","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lūna ipsa suam lūcem nōn habet; lūx lūnae ā sōle venit; itaque lūna nōn tam clāra est quam sōl.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"luxus","latin":"luxus, -ūs","headword":"luxus","letter":"l","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"luxury; excess","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"maceria","latin":"māceria, -ae","headword":"māceria","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"garden wall","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēx ipse nocte mediā cum tribus cōnsciīs fugae per posticum aedium in propinquum cubiculō hortum atque inde, māceriam aegrē trānsgressus, ad mare pervēnit.","reading":"PERSEVS CAPTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"machina","latin":"māchina, -ae","headword":"māchina","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"machine; engine","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aut hōc inclūsī lignō occultantur Achīvī, aut haec in nostrōs fabricāta est māchina mūrōs...","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"machinari","latin":"māchinārī","headword":"māchinārī","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to contrive; plot","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quam rem Tarquinius aegrē ferēns cōnfestim Turnō necem māchinātur, ut eundem terrōrem quō cīvium animōs domī oppresserat Latīnīs iniceret.","reading":"TURNUS HERDONIUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"macula","latin":"macula, -ae","headword":"macula","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stain; blot; disgrace","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"maeret","latin":"maeret","headword":"maeret","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"grieves; mourns","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"maestus","latin":"maestus","headword":"maestus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"sad; sorrowful","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn mīrum est eum maestum esse.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"magister","latin":"magister","headword":"magister","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"teacher; master","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister lūdī est vir Graecus, cui nōmen est Diodōrus.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"latin":"Magister puerōs numerōs et litterās docet.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"magnitudo","latin":"magnitūdō, -inis","headword":"magnitūdō","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"greatness; size","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed satis hōc locō dictum est dē magnitūdine et pulchritūdine urbis Rōmae.","reading":"ORBIS CAPVT","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"magnus","latin":"magnus","headword":"magnus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"big; great; large","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nīlus fluvius magnus est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"In flūminibus et in maribus magnus numerus piscium est.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"maior","latin":"māior","headword":"māior","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"greater; bigger","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus maior est quam Iūlia et minor quam Mārcus.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"maiores","latin":"maiōrēs, -um","headword":"maiōrēs","letter":"m","pos":"noun m. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ancestors","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"malum","latin":"mālum","headword":"mālum","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"apple","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius mālum ē saccō sūmit et sē vertit ad Mārcum: 'Ecce mālum tuum, Mārce.' Iūlius Mārcō mālum dat.","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"latin":"Māter fīliō suō aegrōtantī pānem et mālum dat, sed ille, quī multum esse solet, hodiē nec pānem nec mālum est.","reading":"DISCESSVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"malus","latin":"malus","headword":"malus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"bad; wicked","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus est malus servus quī nummōs dominī in sacculō suō habet.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"mamma","latin":"mamma","headword":"mamma","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mummy; mum","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlia plōrat et Aemiliam vocat: 'Mamma!","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"mandare","latin":"mandāre","headword":"mandāre","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to order; entrust (+ dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"mandatum","latin":"mandātum, -ī","headword":"mandātum","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"command; order","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iuppiter vērō, ubi haec audīvit, Mercurium sīc alloquitur et haec mandat: 'Age vāde, fīlī, et dēfer mea dicta per aurās ad ducem Dardanium, quī nunc Karthāgine morātur neque fītūrōrum prōmissa respicit.","reading":"NŪNTIUS DEŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"mane","latin":"māne","headword":"māne","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.; adverb","posGroup":"noun","english":"morning; in the morning; early","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Prīma pars diēī est māne, pars postrēma vesper.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"latin":"Sed iam māne est, nam gallus canit.","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"manipulus","latin":"manipulus, -ī","headword":"manipulus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"maniple; company of soldiers","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ita renovātum foedus, indictumque iūnioribus Latīnōrum 'ut diē certā ad lūcum Ferentīnae armātī frequentēs adessent.' Quī ubi ex omnibus populīs Latīnīs convēnēre, Tarquinius miscuit manipulōs ex Latīnīs Rōmānīsque, ut ex bīnīs singulōs faceret bīnōsque ex singulīs.","reading":"TURNUS HERDONIUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"mansuetudo","latin":"mānsuētūdō, -inis","headword":"mānsuētūdō","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gentleness; clemency","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hūmānitāte iam tanta est ut difficile dictū sit, utrum hostēs magis virtūtem eius pugnantēs timuerint an mānsuētūdinem victī dīlēxerint.","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"manus","latin":"manus","headword":"manus","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hand","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In bracchiō est manus, in crūre pēs.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Nōn modo vestīs, sed etiam faciēs et manūs et genua sordida sunt.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"mare","latin":"mare","headword":"mare","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sea","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Neptūnus natāre potest; is enim deus maris est. (Ōceanus Atlanticus est magnum mare.) Mercurius et Neptūnus deī Rōmānī sunt.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Italia inter duo maria interest, quōrum alterum, quod suprā Italiam situm est, 'mare Superum' sīve 'Hadriaticum' appellātur, alterum, īnfrā Italiam situm, 'mare Īnferum' sīve 'Tuscum'.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"margarita","latin":"margarīta","headword":"margarīta","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pearl","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce taberna Rōmāna, in quā gemmae et margarītae multae sunt.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"maritus","latin":"marītus","headword":"marītus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"husband","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius marītus Aemiliae est.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"latin":"Marītus et uxor iam nōn dē praeteritō colloquuntur, sed dē tempore futūrō.","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"masculinum","latin":"masculīnum","headword":"masculīnum","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"masculine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"masculinus","latin":"masculīnus","headword":"masculīnus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"masculine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Genera nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Quattuor.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Masculīnum, ut hic magister; fēminīnum, ut haec fēmina; neutrum, ut hoc scamnum; commūne, ut hic et haec sacerdōs.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"mater","latin":"māter","headword":"māter","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mother","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia est māter.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"materia","latin":"māteria","headword":"māteria","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"material; matter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lignum est māteria dūra, sed minus dūra quam ferrum.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"matrona","latin":"mātrōna","headword":"mātrōna","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"married woman; matron","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia mātrōna nōn erat, sed virgō septendecim annōrum, quae Rōmae apud parentēs suōs habitābat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"maturus","latin":"mātūrus","headword":"mātūrus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"ripe; mature","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēnsē Augustō frūmentum mātūrum est.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"mausoleum","latin":"mausōlēum, -ī","headword":"mausōlēum","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mausoleum; great tomb","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Claudiō Marcellō; āra Pācis, in quā sacerdōtēs virginēsque Vestālēs anniversārium sacrificium facere iussit; mausōlēum Augustī, id est monumentum in quō ossa prīncipis cremāta servantur.","reading":"VRBS MARMOREA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"me","latin":"mē","headword":"mē","letter":"m","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"me (acc.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus mē pulsat!'","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"medicus","latin":"medicus","headword":"medicus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"doctor; physician","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Medicus ad hominem aegrum venit eumque sānum facit.","reading":"SĀNVS ET AEGER","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"medius","latin":"medius","headword":"medius","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"middle; middle of","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Digitus medius nimis magnus est.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"Diēī prīmō mēnsis Iūliī \"kalendae Iūliae\" nōmen est; is est diēs annī medius.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"mehercle","latin":"mehercle","headword":"mehercle","letter":"m","pos":"interjection","posGroup":"interjection","english":"by Hercules!","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nusquam igitur scrīptum invenīre est — apud idōneōs quidem scrīptōrēs — aut 'mehercle' fēminam dīcere aut 'mecastor' virum; 'edepol' autem, quod iūs iūrandum per Pollūcem est, et virō et fēminae commūne est.","reading":"DĒ IVRE IVRANDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"mel","latin":"mel","headword":"mel","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"honey","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ego vīnum dulce amō; semper mel vīnō misceō.' Statim minister mel apportat, quod Paulā in pōculum suum fundit. (Mel est quod apēs ex flōribus quaerunt; nihil melle dulcius est.)","reading":"CĒNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"melior","latin":"melior","headword":"melior","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"better","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Certē Iūlius marītus melior quam Iuppiter est!","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"membrum","latin":"membrum","headword":"membrum","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"limb; member","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Bracchium membrum est et crūs membrum est.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"mens","latin":"mēns","headword":"mēns","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mind","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornelius: \" ... et decimo post mense filios geminos peperit, quorum alter fuit Hercules.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"mensa","latin":"mēnsa","headword":"mēnsa","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"table","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Sacculum tuum in mēnsā pōne!' Dāvus sacculum suum in mēnsā pōnit.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"mensis","latin":"mēnsis","headword":"mēnsis","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"month","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Annus in duodecim mēnsēs dīviditur, quibus haec sunt nōmina: Iānuārius, mēnsis prīmus; Februārius, secundus; Mārtius, tertius; Aprīlis, quārtus; Maius, quīntus; Iūnius, sextus; Iūlius, septimus; Augustus, octāvus; September, nōnus; Octōber, decimus; November, ūndecimus; December, mēnsis duodecimus ac postrēmus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"mentio","latin":"mentiō, -ōnis","headword":"mentiō","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mention","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tarquinium, ubi et Tarquinius Collātīnus, Egeriī fīlius, cēnābat, incidit dē uxōribus mentiō.","reading":"LŪCRĒTIA VIOLĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"mentiri","latin":"mentīrī","headword":"mentīrī","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to lie; tell a lie","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"mentitur","latin":"mentītur","headword":"mentītur","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"lies; deceives","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quod dīcit nōn vērum, sed falsum est: Mārcus mentītur.","reading":"MARCVS MENTĪTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"mercator","latin":"mercātor","headword":"mercātor","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"merchant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mercurius est deus mercātōrum. (Mercātor est homō quī emit et vēndit.) Mercurius imperia deōrum ad hominēs portat, is enim nūntius deōrum est.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Ex omnibus terrīs in portūs Italiae veniunt nāvēs, quae mercēs in Italiam vehunt. (Mercēs sunt rēs quās mercātōrēs emunt ac vēndunt.)","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"mercatus","latin":"mercātus, -ūs","headword":"mercātus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"market; fair","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Isthmiōrum lūdicrum aderat tempus, semper frequēns — cum propter spectāculī studium, tum quia Graeciae is mercātus erat; tum vērō nōn ad solitōs modo ūsūs undique convēnerant, sed exspectātiōne ērectī, quī deinde status futūrus Graeciae, quae sua fortūna esset.","reading":"ISTHMIA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"merces","latin":"mercēs","headword":"mercēs","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"goods; merchandise; fee; wages; pay; wage; rent; cargo","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ex omnibus terrīs in portūs Italiae veniunt nāvēs, quae mercēs in Italiam vehunt. (Mercēs sunt rēs quās mercātōrēs emunt ac vēndunt.)","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Ergō mihi mercēdem!' (Mercēs est pecūnia quam magister quoque mēnsē ā patribus discipulōrum accipit.","reading":"EPISTVLA AD PATREM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"mergere","latin":"mergere","headword":"mergere","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to sink; plunge","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ille cūrāvit ut nōs ē tempestāte servārēmur nēve mergerēmur — vel potius nōs ipsī, quī mercēs ēiēcimus.","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"mergit","latin":"mergit","headword":"mergit","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"plunges; dips; sinks","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus caput tōtum in aquam mergit atque etiam aurēs et capillum lavat.","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"mergor","latin":"mergor","headword":"mergor","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"be sunk; be drowned","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nauta, quī flūctibus iactātur ac mergitur: 'Flūctibus iactor ac mergor!","reading":"NAVTAE ET NEPTŪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"meridies","latin":"merīdiēs","headword":"merīdiēs","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"midday; noon; south","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hōra sexta, quae hōrā mediā est inter hōram prīmam et duodecimam, \"merīdiēs\" nōminātur.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"latin":"Partēs caelī sunt quattuor: oriēns et occidēns, merīdiēs et septentriōnēs.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"meritum","latin":"meritum, -ī","headword":"meritum","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"service; merit","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ac propter hoc meritum annōrum trium et vīgintī cōnsul est factus.","reading":"POST VRBEM CAPTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"merum","latin":"merum","headword":"merum","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pure; unmixed wine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nunc merum bibendum est!' Cornēlius: 'Tacendum est, nōn bibendum!","reading":"INTER PŌCVLA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"merus","latin":"merus","headword":"merus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"pure; undiluted","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"metit","latin":"mētit","headword":"mētit","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"reaps; harvests","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēnsē Augustō frūmentum mētītur et ex agrīs vehitur.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"metuit","latin":"metuit","headword":"metuit","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"fears; is afraid of","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dux exercituī imperat, exercitus ducī suō pāret, nam dux ab exercitū metuitur.'","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Mārcus magistrum metuit, Diodōrus enim magister sevērus est, quī discipulōs suōs virga verberat; eō modo magister sevērus discipulōs improbōs pūnīre solet.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"metus","latin":"metus, -ūs","headword":"metus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fear","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hās tantās virī virtūtēs ingentia vitia aequābant: inhūmāna crūdēlitās, perfidia plūs quam Pūnica, nihil vērī, nihil sānctī, nūllus deum metus, nūllum iūs iūrandum, nūlla religiō.","reading":"HANNIBAL IMPERĀTOR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"meus","latin":"meus","headword":"meus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"my; mine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornēlius: 'Cuius servus est Mēdus?' Iūlius: 'Mēdus servus meus est.' Cornēlius: 'Estne Dāvus servus tuus?' Iūlius: 'Dāvus quoque servus meus est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Ecce sacculus meus.'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"migrare","latin":"migrāre","headword":"migrāre","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to move; migrate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"miles","latin":"mīles","headword":"mīles","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"soldier","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilius mīles est.","reading":"DĒ FAMILIĀ ET NŌMINIBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Nec vērō ūllus mīles legiōnārius ā tergō vulnerātus est.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"miliarium","latin":"mīliārium, -ī","headword":"mīliārium","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"milestone","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rōmānōs saepe vīcit, usque ad quīntum mīliārium urbis accessit, oppugnātūrus etiam patriam suam (lēgātīs quī pācem petēbant repudiātīs), nisi ad eum māter Veturia et uxor Volumnia ex urbe vēnissent, quārum flētū et dēprecātiōne superātus remōvit exercitum.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"militia","latin":"mīlitia, -ae","headword":"mīlitia","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"military service; warfare","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec Rōmulō rēgnante domī mīlitiaeque gesta sunt.","reading":"ROMVLVS CONSECRATVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"mille","latin":"mīlle","headword":"mīlle","letter":"m","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"a thousand","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In capitulō prīmō mīlle vocābula sunt.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"minae","latin":"minae, -ārum","headword":"minae","letter":"m","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"threats","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"minister","latin":"minister","headword":"minister","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"servant; waiter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aliī servī, quī ministrī vocantur, cibum parātum ē culīnā in trīclīnium portant.)","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"minor","latin":"minor","headword":"minor","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"smaller","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus maior est quam Iūlia et minor quam Mārcus.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"minos","latin":"Mīnōs","headword":"Mīnōs","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"Minos; king of Crete","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus: \"Nōnne rēx Mīnōs Thēseum cum Ariadnā fugientem persecūtus est?\"","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"minotaurus","latin":"Mīnōtaurus","headword":"Mīnōtaurus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"the Minotaur","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Nārrābō tibi tabulam dē Thēseō et Mīnōtaurō' inquit Syrā, et sīc nārrāre incipit.","reading":"TABVLĀ POSTVLĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"mirabilis","latin":"mīrābilis","headword":"mīrābilis","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"wonderful; marvellous","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum rēx īrātus cēpit Daedalum, quī fīlum cōnfēcerat et Ariadnae dederat, eumque in labyrinthum inclūdī iussit ūna cum eius Īcarō fīliō; vērum pater et fīlius mīrābilī modō ē labyrinthō fūgērunt.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"miraculum","latin":"mīrāculum, -ī","headword":"mīrāculum","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wonder; miracle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī cum dēscendere ad animōs nōn posset sine aliquō dīvīnō mīrāculō, simulat sibi cum deā Ēgeriā nocturnōs sermōnēs esse: eius monitū sē sacra quae dīs acceptissima essent institutere, et sacerdōtēs suōs cuique deōrum praeficere.","reading":"NVMA POMPILIVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"mirari","latin":"mīrārī","headword":"mīrārī","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to wonder at; be surprised","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra: 'Nōlī hoc mīrārī: Mārcus forem frangere cōnātur, quod aliter exīre nōn potest.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"miratur","latin":"mīrātur","headword":"mīrātur","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"wonders at; admires","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Īcarus dēspiciēns multitūdinem īnsulārum mīrātus est: \"Ō, quot parvae īnsulae in marī ingentī sunt!\" Daedalus vērō \"Illae īnsulae\" inquit \"haud parvae sunt, quamquam parvae esse videntur.","reading":"ĪCARVS IN MARE CADIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"miscere","latin":"miscēre","headword":"miscēre","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to mix","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"miser","latin":"miser","headword":"miser","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"wretched; unhappy","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ergō Iūlius miser erat et nocte male dormiēbat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"latin":"Puella misera ab humilī lītore in altum saxum ascendit, unde prōspiciēns nāvem Thēseī procul in marī vīdit.","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"miseratio","latin":"miserātiō, -ōnis","headword":"miserātiō","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed postquam Persea cōnsulī 'rēgem Paulō salūtem' lēgisset, miserātiōnem omnem stultitia ignōrantis fortūnam suam exēmit.","reading":"PERSEVS CAPTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"misericordia","latin":"misericordia, -ae","headword":"misericordia","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pity; compassion","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam hōc ferē sīc fierī solēre accēpimus, ut rēgum afflīctae fortūnae facile multōrum opēs alliciant ad misericordiam, maximēque eōrum quī aut rēgēs sunt aut vīvunt in rēgnō, ut iīs nōmen rēgāle magnum et sānctum esse videātur.","reading":"DĒ MAGNITŪDINE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"mithridaticus","latin":"Mithridāticus, -a, -um","headword":"Mithridāticus","letter":"m","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"of Mithridates","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Annō urbis conditae sescentēsimō sexāgēsimō secundō prīmum Rōmae bellum cīvīle commōtum est, eōdem annō etiam Mithridāticum.","reading":"BELLVM MITHRIDĀTICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"mitigare","latin":"mītigāre","headword":"mītigāre","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to soften; calm","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed ipse Rōmulus circumībat animōsque eārum mītigābat hīs dictīs: \"Hoc factum est ob patrum vestrōrum superbiam, quī cōnūbium Rōmānīs negāvērunt.","reading":"SABINAE RAPTAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"mittere","latin":"mittere","headword":"mittere","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to send","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"mittit","latin":"mittit","headword":"mittit","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sends","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"moderator","latin":"moderātor, -ōris","headword":"moderātor","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ruler; controller","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Deinde subter mediam ferē regiōnem Sōl obtinet, dux et prīnceps et moderātor lūminum reliquōrum, mēns mundī et temperātiō, tantā magnitūdine ut cūncta suā lūce lūstret et compleat.","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"modius","latin":"modius, -ī","headword":"modius","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"peck; a measure of grain","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"modus","latin":"modus","headword":"modus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mood; manner","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"moenia","latin":"moenia, -ium","headword":"moenia","letter":"m","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"walls (of a city)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Moenia Rōmāna antīqua septem collēs sīve montēs complectuntur, quōrum haec sunt nōmina: Palātium, Capitōlium, Aventīnus, Caelius, Esquiliae, Vīminālis, Quirīnālis.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"},{"latin":"Ab urbe oppugnandā Poenum absterruēre cōnspecta moenia.","reading":"MĀGŌ NV̄NTIVS VICTŌRIAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"moles","latin":"mōlēs, -is","headword":"mōlēs","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mass; huge bulk","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"mollit","latin":"mollit","headword":"mollit","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"softens","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"monere","latin":"monēre","headword":"monēre","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to warn; advise","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"monet","latin":"monet","headword":"monet","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"warns; reminds; advises","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic diēs mē monet dē mercēde quam mihi dēbēs: quārē Mārcus hodiē mercēdem nōn tulit?","reading":"EPISTVLA ADVENIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"latin":"Nam ille cāsus tuus melius tē monet quam ūlla tabula!\"","reading":"ĪCARVS IN MARE CADIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"monitus","latin":"monitus, -ūs","headword":"monitus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"warning; instruction","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī cum dēscendere ad animōs nōn posset sine aliquō dīvīnō mīrāculō, simulat sibi cum deā Ēgeriā nocturnōs sermōnēs esse: eius monitū sē sacra quae dīs acceptissima essent institutere, et sacerdōtēs suōs cuique deōrum praeficere.","reading":"NVMA POMPILIVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"mons","latin":"mōns","headword":"mōns","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mountain","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In campō est collis. (Collis est mōns parvus.) In colle arbor est.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"monstrat","latin":"mōnstrat","headword":"mōnstrat","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"points out; shows","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ō, quam pulchra sunt illa ōrnāmenta!\" Lȳdia tabernam Albīnī digitō mōnstrat.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"monstrum","latin":"mōnstrum","headword":"mōnstrum","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"monster; portent","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra: 'At tāle mōnstrum tē terrēbit, Quīnte.'","reading":"TABVLĀ POSTVLĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"mordere","latin":"mordēre","headword":"mordēre","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to bite","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Canis īrātus dentēs ostendit ac fremit: \"Rrrr...!\" nec vērō tabellārium mordēre potest, quod catēna retinētur.","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"mori","latin":"morī","headword":"morī","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to die","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hominēs mortālēs nāscuntur ac moriuntur, immortālīs semper vīvit.","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"moribundus","latin":"moribundus, -a, -um","headword":"moribundus","letter":"m","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"dying","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cuī mē moribundam dēseris?","reading":"NŪNTIUS DEŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"mors","latin":"mors","headword":"mors","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"death","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nāvis, quā Athēniēnsēs illūc vehēbantur, vēla ātra gerēbat, nam eō colōre significātur mors.'","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"mortalis","latin":"mortālis","headword":"mortālis","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"mortal","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hominēs mortālēs nāscuntur ac moriuntur, immortālīs semper vīvit.","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"mortuus","latin":"mortuus","headword":"mortuus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"dead","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī spīrat vīvus est, quī nōn spīrat est mortuus.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Puer quiētus super lectum iacet ut mortuus.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"multi","latin":"multī","headword":"multī","letter":"m","pos":"adjective (pl.)","posGroup":"adjective","english":"many","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In Galliā et in Germāniā multī sunt fluviī.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"multus","latin":"multus","headword":"multus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"much; many","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"mundus","latin":"mundus","headword":"mundus","letter":"m","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"clean; neat","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus, postquam vestem mūtāvit, mundus redit et mātrem salūtat.","reading":"MARCVS MENTĪTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"munire","latin":"mūnīre","headword":"mūnīre","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to fortify; build (a wall)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"munitio","latin":"mūnītiō, -ōnis","headword":"mūnītiō","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fortification","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postrēmō omnī bellō Latīnō Medulliam compulsō, aliquamdiū ibi variā victōriā pugnātum est, nam urbs tūta mūnītiōnibus praesidiōque validō firmāta erat.","reading":"BELLVM LATINVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"munus","latin":"mūnus","headword":"mūnus","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gift; service","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hoc sōlum mihi optō.\" Bacchus autem, etsī rēgem avārum mūnus pessimum optāsse cēnsēbat, tamen prōmissum solvit.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"murmur","latin":"murmur, -uris","headword":"murmur","letter":"m","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"murmur","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quārtō post diē quam cum rēge est pugnātum, cum in circō lūdī fierent, murmur repentē populum tōtā spectācula pervāsit 'pugnātum in Macedoniā et dēvictum rēgem esse'; dein fremitus incrēvit; postrēmō clāmor, plausus, velut certō nūntiō victōriae allātō, est exortus.","reading":"PERSEVS VICTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"murus","latin":"mūrus, -ī","headword":"mūrus","letter":"m","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wall","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Circum Rōmam est mūrus antīquus.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Sed et turris ingēns imminebat, et mūrus, ut in suspectō locō, ēmūnītus erat, et iuventūs dēlēcta ubi plūrimum perīculī ac timōris ostendēbātur ibi vī maiōre obsistēbat.","reading":"SAGVNTVM OPPVGNĀTVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"mutabilis","latin":"mūtābilis, -e","headword":"mūtābilis","letter":"m","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"changeable; fickle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Varium et mūtābile semper fēmina!' Sīc fātus noctī sē immiscuit ātrae.","reading":"ROGUS DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"mutare","latin":"mūtāre","headword":"mūtāre","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to change","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cui Orontēs: 'Stultē id quaeris,' inquit. 'Midās enim terram, lignum, ferrum manū tangendō in aurum mūtāre poterat, ac famē et sitī moriēbātur, cum cibus quoque et pōtiō, simul atque ā rēge tācta erat, aurum fieret.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"mutat","latin":"mūtat","headword":"mūtat","letter":"m","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"changes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus Dāvum sequitur in cubiculum, ubi cruōrem et sordēs ē faciē, manibus, genibus lavat ac vestīmenta mūtat.","reading":"MARCVS Ā PATRE INTERROGĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"mutatio","latin":"mūtātiō, -ōnis","headword":"mūtātiō","letter":"m","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"change; reversal","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec Graecō sermōne Perseō; Latīnē deinde suīs: 'Exemplum īnsigne cernitis' inquit 'mūtātiōnis rērum hūmānārum.","reading":"PERSEVS ANTE CONSVLEM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"nancisci","latin":"nancīscī","headword":"nancīscī","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to get; obtain","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tē autem permagnum est nancīscī ōtiōsum, hōc praesertim mōtū reī pūblicae.' Tum Scīpiō: 'Atquī nactus es, sed mēhercule ōtiōsiōrem operā quam animō.' Et ille: 'At tū vērō animum quoque relaxāre oportet.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"narrat","latin":"nārrat","headword":"nārrat","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"tells; relates","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn sōlum dēlectandī causā vērum etiam monendī causa nārrātur tabulā dē Daedalō, nam quod illī puerō accidit, idem omnibus accidere poterit, nisi patrī suō pāret.","reading":"ĪCARVS IN MARE CADIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"nasus","latin":"nāsus","headword":"nāsus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"nose","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra nōn est fēmina pulchra, neque pulcher est nāsus eius, sed foedus est.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Puella sē in speculō videt et sē interrogat: 'Estne foedus nāsus meus?' Nāsus eius autem fōrmōsus nōn est.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"natat","latin":"natat","headword":"natat","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"swims","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Piscis quī natat caudam movet.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"natio","latin":"nātiō, -ōnis","headword":"nātiō","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"people; nation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī vērum est — quod nēmō dubitat — ut populus Rōmānus omnēs gentēs virtūte superārit, nōn est īnfitiandum Hannibalem tantō praestitisse cēterōs imperātōrēs prūdentiā, quantō populus Rōmānus antecēdat fortitūdine cūnctās nātiōnēs.","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"naufragium","latin":"naufragium, -ī","headword":"naufragium","letter":"n","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shipwreck","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cōnsulēs cum victrīcī classe redeuntēs circā Siciliam naufragium passī sunt.","reading":"BELLVM PŪNICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"nauta","latin":"nauta","headword":"nauta","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sailor","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is quī nāvigāre vult adit nautam quī bonam nāvem habet.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Nauta, quī flūctibus iactātur ac mergitur: 'Flūctibus iactor ac mergor!","reading":"NAVTAE ET NEPTŪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"navalia","latin":"nāvālia, -ium","headword":"nāvālia","letter":"n","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dockyards","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilius Regillus, quī praefectōs classis Antiochī nāvālī proeliō dēvīcerat, nāvālem triumphum dūxit.","reading":"PERSEVS VICTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"navicularius","latin":"nāviculārius, -ī","headword":"nāviculārius","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shipowner; shipper","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Maiōrēs nostrī saepe prō mercātōribus aut nāviculāriīs nostrīs iniūriōsius tractātīs bella gessērunt — vōs, tot mīlibus cīvium Rōmānōrum ūnō nūntiō atque ūnō tempore necātīs, quō tandem animō esse debētis?","reading":"DĒ GENERE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"navigare","latin":"nāvigāre","headword":"nāvigāre","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to sail","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quod autem paulum aquae est in Tiberī, magnae nāvēs in eō flūmine nāvigāre nōn possunt.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Mēdus et Lȳdia ventō secundō per mare Īnferum nāvigāre pergunt ad fretum Siculum (id est fretum quō Sicilia ab Italiā disiungitur).","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA IN NĀVĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"navigat","latin":"nāvigat","headword":"nāvigat","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sails","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nec ūllīs perīculīs ā nāvigandō dēterrentur nautae.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"navis","latin":"nāvis","headword":"nāvis","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ship","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pars nāvis posterior puppis dīcitur.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Nāvis, quā Athēniēnsēs illūc vehēbantur, vēla ātra gerēbat, nam eō colōre significātur mors.'","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"-ne","latin":"-ne","headword":"-ne","letter":"n","pos":"particle","posGroup":"particle","english":"(turns a sentence into a question)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ne","latin":"nē","headword":"nē","letter":"n","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"that not; lest","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī hoc vērum est, prīnceps omnium deōrum est deus tuus; neque enim ūllus deus Rōmānus hominem mortālem ab Īnferīs suscitāre potest; nē Iuppiter quidem tantam potestātem habet, etsī ille deus maximus habētur.\"","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"ne ... quidem","latin":"nē ... quidem","headword":"nē ... quidem","letter":"n","pos":"particle","posGroup":"particle","english":"not even","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quoniam igitur propter vim atque multitūdinem praedōnum nē mare Tuscum quidem tūtum erat, frūmentī ex Siciliā et ex Āfricā Rōmam advehēbātur.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"nebula","latin":"nebula, -ae","headword":"nebula","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cloud; mist","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūr dextrās iungere nōn licet ac vērē colloquī?' At Venus Aenēam et Achāten gradientēs nebulā circumfūdit, nē quis eōs cernere neu contingere posset.","reading":"VENUS GENETRĪX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"necessitas","latin":"necessitās, -ātis","headword":"necessitās","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"necessity; compulsion","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed rem immātūram nisi per necessitātem aperīre nōluerat.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"nefas","latin":"nefās","headword":"nefās","letter":"n","pos":"noun n. indecl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"crime against divine law","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Spērāsne, perfide hospes, tē tantum nefās dissimulāre posse et meā terrā clam dēcēdere?","reading":"NŪNTIUS DEŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"negat","latin":"negat","headword":"negat","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"denies","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus, quī iam nōn audet mentīrī, nihil negat, sed omnia fatētur: 'Rēctē dīcis, pater.","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"neglegens","latin":"neglegēns","headword":"neglegēns","letter":"n","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"careless; neglectful","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itane īnfantēs suōs neglegit?","reading":"PĀSTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"negotiator","latin":"negōtiātor, -ōris","headword":"negōtiātor","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"trader; businessman","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quibus rēbus Micipsa tametsī initiō laetus fuerat exīstimāns virtūtem Iugurthae rēgnō suō glōriae fore, tamen, postquam hominem adulēscentem — exāctā suā aetāte et parvīs līberīs — magis magisque crēscere intellegit, vehementer eō negōtiō permōtus multa cum animō suō volvēbat.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"negotium","latin":"negōtium","headword":"negōtium","letter":"n","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"business; task","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornēlius: 'Nōnnumquam tē vīsere voluī, nec prius urbem relinquere potuī prae multīs et magnīs negōtiīs meīs.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"nepos","latin":"nepōs, nepōtis","headword":"nepōs","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"grandson; descendant","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ipse meā manū mortem inveniam!\" Tālia dīcēns fīxus eōdem locō haerēbat, dum fīlius et parvus nepōs omnisque domus multīs cum lacrimīs eī suādent nē omnēs suōs sēcum perderet!","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"neptunus","latin":"Neptūnus","headword":"Neptūnus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"Neptune; god of the sea","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Servā mē, Neptūne, quī prope ades, quamquam nec vidēris nec audīris ab hominibus.' Neptūnus: 'Flūctibus iactāris, nauta, nec vērō mergeris!","reading":"NAVTAE ET NEPTŪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"neque","latin":"neque","headword":"neque","letter":"n","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"and not; nor","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius Quīntum nōn audit neque venit.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"neuter","latin":"neuter","headword":"neuter","letter":"n","pos":"pronoun; adjective","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"neither (of the two); neuter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Uterque puer cubat in cubiculō parvō, neuter in cubiculō magnō.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"neutrum","latin":"neutrum","headword":"neutrum","letter":"n","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"neuter","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"neve","latin":"nēve","headword":"nēve","letter":"n","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"and not; nor","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ille cūrāvit ut nōs ē tempestāte servārēmur nēve mergerēmur — vel potius nōs ipsī, quī mercēs ēiēcimus.","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"latin":"Hāc fābulā monēmur ut semper bonō animō sīmus nēve umquam dē salūte dēspērēmus.","reading":"FĀBVLA ARĪONIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"nidus","latin":"nīdus","headword":"nīdus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"nest","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In hāc arbore nīdus est.' Accurrit Quīntus.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"niger","latin":"niger","headword":"niger","letter":"n","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"black","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pāstor nōn sōlus est in campō, nam canis niger cum eō est et centum ovēs: ūna ovis nigra et ūndēcentum ovēs albae.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"nimbus","latin":"nimbus, -ī","headword":"nimbus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"storm-cloud","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postquam in altum prōvectae sunt nāvēs nec iam ūllae terrae appārēbant, nimbus repentīnus solem occultāvit imbrem tempestātemque afferēns.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"nimis","latin":"nimis","headword":"nimis","letter":"n","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"too; too much","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pretium ānulī est sēstertiī centum!\" Lȳdia: \"Dā huic tabernāriō centum sēstertiōs!\" Mēdus: \"Id nimis magnum pretium est!","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"nisi","latin":"nisi","headword":"nisi","letter":"n","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"unless; if not","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nisi dīī nōs iuvābunt, numquam vīvī ēgrediēmur.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"},{"latin":"Nec vērō ego vīvō nisi cotīdiē bonō vīnō fruor.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"nix","latin":"nix","headword":"nix","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"snow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hieme nōn sōlum imber, sed etiam nix dē caelō cadit.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"latin":"Hodiē manē vestīmenta Mārcī munda erant atque tam candida quam nix nova, nunc vērō sordida et ūmida sunt.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"nobilitas","latin":"nōbilitās, -ātis","headword":"nōbilitās","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"nobility; high birth","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"nocere","latin":"nocēre","headword":"nocēre","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to harm (with dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"nocet","latin":"nocet","headword":"nocet","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"harms; does harm to","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Neque enim vīneīs magis prōdest quam sōl et calor, nec iīs magis nocet quam imber et frīgus.” Iūlius: “Calor sōlis nōn ipse per sē efficit ut vīnum bonum sit.","reading":"PĀSTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"nodus","latin":"nōdus, -ī","headword":"nōdus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"knot; bond","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Illī autem octō cursūs, in quibus eadem vīs est duōrum, septem efficiunt distīnctōs intervāllīs sonōs, quī numerus rērum omnium ferē nōdus est.","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"nomen","latin":"nōmen","headword":"nōmen","letter":"n","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"name; noun","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōmen patris est 'Iūlius', mātris 'Aemilia'; 'Quīntus' est nōmen frātris, 'Iūlia' sorōris.","reading":"DĒ FAMILIĀ ET NŌMINIBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"nominativus","latin":"nōminātīvus","headword":"nōminātīvus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"nominative","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Cāsus nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Sex.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Nōminātīvus, genetīvus, dativus, accūsātīvus, vocātīvus, ablātīvus.","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"non","latin":"nōn","headword":"nōn","letter":"n","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"not","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aegyptus in Eurōpā nōn est, Aegyptus in Āfricā est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"nonae","latin":"nōnae","headword":"nōnae","letter":"n","pos":"noun (f. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"the Nones (fifth or seventh day)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Diēs nōnus ante Īdūs dīcitur \"nōnae\" (nōnae Iānuāriae: diēs quīntus Iānuāriī; nōnae Februāriae: diēs quīntus Februāriī; nōnae Mārtiae: diēs septimus Mārtiī; cet.).","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"nonaginta","latin":"nōnāgintā","headword":"nōnāgintā","letter":"n","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"ninety","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In eō nōnāgintā sēstertiī īnsunt.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"nonne?","latin":"nōnne?","headword":"nōnne?","letter":"n","pos":"particle","posGroup":"particle","english":"(introduces a question expecting \"yes\")","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōnne fōrmōsus est nāsus meus?' Iūlia: 'Immō foedus est!","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"nos","latin":"nōs","headword":"nōs","letter":"n","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"we","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Audītisne id quod dīcō?' Tum Sextus et Titus 'Id quod dīcis' inquiunt 'vērum nōn est: nōs iānuam pulsāmus cum ad lūdum venīmus, et magistrum salūtāmus cum eum vidēmus.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"noscere","latin":"nōscere","headword":"nōscere","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to get to know","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dum hic sōlus cubō, nihil nōscere possum, etsī omnia scīre cupiō.'","reading":"SYRA NĀRRAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"novem","latin":"novem","headword":"novem","letter":"n","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"nine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"novus","latin":"novus","headword":"novus","letter":"n","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"new","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce duo librī Latīnī: liber antīquus et liber novus.","reading":"LIBER TVVS LATĪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"nox","latin":"nox","headword":"nox","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"night","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nox est tempus ā vesperō ad māne.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"latin":"Ō, quam longa nox est!","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"noxa","latin":"noxa, -ae","headword":"noxa","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"guilt; harm","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cōnsōlantur aegram animī āvertendō noxam ab coāctā in auctōrem dēlictī: 'mentem peccāre, nōn corpus, et unde cōnsilium fūerit, culpam abesse.' 'Vōs' inquit 'vīderitis quid illī dēbeātur!","reading":"RĒGĒS EXĀCTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"nubere","latin":"nūbere","headword":"nūbere","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to marry (a man)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Catullus Lesbiam uxorem ducere cupiebat, nec vero illa Catullo nupsit, etsi affirmabat 'se nulli alii viro nubere malle.' Mox vero poeta de verbis eius dubitare coepit:","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"nubes","latin":"nūbēs","headword":"nūbēs","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cloud","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In caelō nūlla nūbēs vidētur.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"nudus","latin":"nūdus","headword":"nūdus","letter":"n","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"naked; bare","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puer iam nūdus nōn est.","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"nullus","latin":"nūllus","headword":"nūllus","letter":"n","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"no; none","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nūllus servus adest.'","reading":"SCAENA TERTIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"num?","latin":"num?","headword":"num?","letter":"n","pos":"particle","posGroup":"particle","english":"(introduces a \"no\" question)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Num Crēta oppidum est?","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"numerat","latin":"numerat","headword":"numerat","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"counts","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"numerosus","latin":"numerōsus, -a, -um","headword":"numerōsus","letter":"n","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"numerous; many","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūliō Caesare et Marciō Philippō cōnsulibus sescentēsimō quīnquāgēsimō nōnō annō ab urbe conditā, cum prope alia omnia bella cessārent, in Ītaliā gravissimum bellum Picentēs, Marsī Paelīgnīque mōvērunt, quī, cum annīs numerōsīs iam populō Rōmānō oboedīrent, tum lībertātem sibi aequam asserere coepērunt.","reading":"BELLVM SOCIĀLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"numerus","latin":"numerus","headword":"numerus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"number","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"III quoque numerus est.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Hic magister eum interpellat: 'Necesse nōn est omnēs numerōs dīcere; ā vīgintī dīc decimum quemque numerum tantum, Tite!'","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"nummus","latin":"nummus","headword":"nummus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"coin","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce nummus tuus, Dāve!' Iūlius ūnum nummum pōnit in sacculō Dāvī.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"nuntiare","latin":"nūntiāre","headword":"nūntiāre","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to announce; report","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Īdibus Maiīs dēmum ex itinere Rōmam revertī, unde hodiē veniō.' Iūlius: 'Ergō vōs mihi aliquid dē rēbus urbānīs novissimīs nūntiābitis.' Cornēlius: 'Et tū nōs docēbis dē rēbus rūsticīs, ut agricola studiōsus et dīligēns.'","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"nuntius","latin":"nūntius","headword":"nūntius","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"messenger; news","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"nuptiae","latin":"nūptiae, -ārum","headword":"nūptiae","letter":"n","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"marriage; wedding","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"nurus","latin":"nurus, -ūs","headword":"nurus","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"daughter-in-law","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"nutrire","latin":"nūtrīre","headword":"nūtrīre","letter":"n","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to suckle; nourish","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"nutrix","latin":"nūtrīx (nutricis)","headword":"nūtrīx","letter":"n","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"nurse; wet-nurse","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mulier quae aliēnum īnfantem alit nūtrīx appellātur.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"nutus","latin":"nūtus, -ūs","headword":"nūtus","letter":"n","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"nod; downward pressure","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"o!","latin":"ō!","headword":"ō!","letter":"o","pos":"interjection","posGroup":"interjection","english":"oh!","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"oblivisci","latin":"oblīvīscī","headword":"oblīvīscī","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to forget","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Midās — nec vērō certus sum; semper nōmina oblīvīscor, nam mala memoria mihi est.'","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"obliviscitur","latin":"oblīvīscitur","headword":"oblīvīscitur","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"forgets (with gen.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Montēs aurī feminis pollicentur, tum prōmissa oblīvīscuntur ac fēminās sine causā dēserunt!","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"oboedire","latin":"oboedīre","headword":"oboedīre","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to obey (+ dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quis est ille dominus tuus cui mare et ventī oboedīre videntur?\"","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA IN NĀVĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"latin":"Iūliō Caesare et Marciō Philippō cōnsulibus sescentēsimō quīnquāgēsimō nōnō annō ab urbe conditā, cum prope alia omnia bella cessārent, in Ītaliā gravissimum bellum Picentēs, Marsī Paelīgnīque mōvērunt, quī, cum annīs numerōsīs iam populō Rōmānō oboedīrent, tum lībertātem sibi aequam asserere coepērunt.","reading":"BELLVM SOCIĀLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"obrepere","latin":"obrēpere","headword":"obrēpere","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to creep up secretly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Manlius Rōmae, quī Gallōs in obsidiōne Capitōliī obrēpentēs per ardua dēpulerat, convictus est cōnsilium dē regnō occupandō iniisse damnātusque capitis ē saxō Tarpēiō, ut M.","reading":"SŌCRATĒS ET CAMILLUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"obscurus","latin":"obscūrus","headword":"obscūrus","letter":"o","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"dark","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vīlla tōta obscūra et quiēta est.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"obsidio","latin":"obsidiō, -ōnis","headword":"obsidiō","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"siege; blockade","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Manlius Rōmae, quī Gallōs in obsidiōne Capitōliī obrēpentēs per ardua dēpulerat, convictus est cōnsilium dē regnō occupandō iniisse damnātusque capitis ē saxō Tarpēiō, ut M.","reading":"SŌCRATĒS ET CAMILLUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"},{"latin":"Obsidiō deinde per paucōs diēs magis quam oppugnātiō fuit, dum vulnus ducis cūrārētur; per quod tempus ab apparātū operum ac mūnītiōnum nihil cessātum.","reading":"SAGVNTVM OPPVGNĀTVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"obsidis","latin":"obsidis, -is","headword":"obsidis","letter":"o","pos":"noun m./f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hostage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī ubi in Āfricam trānsiērunt, acceptīs quōs imperāverant trecentīs obsidibus et armīs omnibus īnstrūmentīsque bellī, cum ex auctōritāte patrum iubērentur in alium locum sēdēs transferre, dum ā marī decem mīlia passuum nec minus recessissent, Carthāginiēnsēs indignitāte reī ad bellum compulsī sunt.","reading":"BELLVM PVNICVM TERTIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"obtrectare","latin":"obtrectāre","headword":"obtrectāre","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to disparage; attack in words","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ennius, mox et iūxtā Caecilius et Terentius, et subinde Pācuvius, et continuō Pācuviō iam sene Accius, clāriorque tunc in poēmatis tragicī Rōmānī eōrum obtrectandīs Lūcīlius fuit.","reading":"PHILIPPVS ĀD LŪCĪLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"obtruncare","latin":"obtruncāre","headword":"obtruncāre","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to cut down; slaughter","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī tibi certum est Trōiae peritūrae tē tuōsque addere, patet iānua mortī: iam aderit Pyrrhus sanguine Priamī cruentus, quī fīlium cōram patre, tum patrem ipsum ad āram obtruncāvit!","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"obtunsus","latin":"obtūnsus, -a, -um","headword":"obtūnsus","letter":"o","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"blunted; dull","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn obtūnsa adeō gestāmus pectora Poenī.","reading":"DĪDŌ RĒGĪNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"occasio","latin":"occāsiō, -ōnis","headword":"occāsiō","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"opportunity; favourable moment","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dum Crustumīnī atque Antemnātēs occāsiōnem exspectant, Caenīnēnsēs nimis impatientēs per sē ipsī in agrum Rōmānum impetum faciunt.","reading":"SPOLIA OPIMA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"occasus","latin":"occāsus, -ūs","headword":"occāsus","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"setting (of the sun)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Post sōlis occāsum in lītus ēgressī sunt et fessī somnō sē dedērunt; sed mediā nocte Palīnūrus, cum ventum secundum caelumque serēnum vidēret, signum proficīscendī dedit.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"occidens","latin":"occidēns","headword":"occidēns","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"west","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Partēs caelī sunt quattuor: oriēns et occidēns, merīdiēs et septentriōnēs.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"occidere","latin":"occidere","headword":"occidere","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to kill","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"occidit","latin":"occīdit","headword":"occīdit","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"kills","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum Thēseus, fīlum Ariadnae post sē trahēns, labyrinthum intrāvit ac sine morā Mīnōtaurum in mediā parte exspectantem petīvit, quem post brevem pugnam gladiō occīdit.","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"occurrere","latin":"occurrere","headword":"occurrere","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"meet; run up to","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum vērō Syrā, quae eō ipsō tempore peristȳlum intrat ūna cum Iūlia, dominae in ōstiō occurrit.","reading":"DĒ SORŌRE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"oceanus","latin":"ōceanus","headword":"ōceanus","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ocean","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Num ōceanus Atlanticus parvus est?","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"octo","latin":"octō","headword":"octō","letter":"o","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"eight","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"octoginta","latin":"octōgintā","headword":"octōgintā","letter":"o","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"eighty","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tanta gemma sōla octōgintā sēstertiīs cōnstat.\" Mēdus: \"Num ānulus sine gemmā vīgintī tantum sēstertiīs cōnstat?\" Albīnus nōn respondet.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"oculus","latin":"oculus","headword":"oculus","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"eye","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"odisse","latin":"ōdisse","headword":"ōdisse","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to hate","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"odium","latin":"odium, -ī","headword":"odium","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hatred","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce duo versus qui mentem poetae dolentem ac dubiam inter amorem et odium demonstrant:","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"},{"latin":"Hic autem, velut hērēditāte relictum, odium paternum ergā Rōmānōs sīc cōnservāvit ut prius animam dēpōneret quam id dēposuerit — quī quidem, cum patriā pulsus esset et aliēnārum opum indigeret, numquam dēstiterit animō bellāre cum Rōmānīs.","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"offensa","latin":"offēnsa, -ae","headword":"offēnsa","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"offence; resentment","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deinde, cum minus agrī esset quam quod dīvidī posset sine offēnsā etiam plēbis — quoniam eōs ad cupiditātem amplum modum spērandī incitāverat — lēgem sē iūgerum prōmulgātūrum ostendit: 'ut iīs quī Semprōniā lēge agrum accipere dēbērent, pecūnia quae rēgis Attalī fuisset dīviderētur.' Hērēdem autem populum Rōmānum relīquerat Attalus, rēx Pergamī, Eumenis fīlius.","reading":"LĒGĒS AGRĀRIAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"offensio","latin":"offēnsiō, -ōnis","headword":"offēnsiō","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"reverse; disaster","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc in illō ipsō malō gravissimāque bellī offēnsiōne L.","reading":"DĒ MAGNITŪDINE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"officium","latin":"officium","headword":"officium","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"duty; job","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sīve īnfāns valet sīve aegrōtat, māter ipsa eum cūrāre et alere dēbet — hoc est mātris officium!\" Iūlius: \"Tūne ipsa īnfantem tuum lacte tuō āles?\" Aemilia: \"Profectō īnfantem meum ipsa ālam.","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"latin":"Nē servō quidem iniūriam facere oportet, sed necesse est servōs īnfīdōs aut fugitīvōs sevērē pūnīre; nec enim quidquam nisi poena sevēra eius generis servōs ā maleficiīs dēterrēre atque in officiō tenēre potest.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"olim","latin":"ōlim","headword":"ōlim","letter":"o","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"once; long ago; formerly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'In īnsulā Crēta ōlim vīvēbat mōnstrum terribile, Mīnōtaurus, cui caput taurī, corpus virī erat.","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"latin":"Ōlim cūncta maria tam īnfēstā erant praedōnibus ut nēmō nāvigāret sine maximō perīculō mortis aut servitūtis.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"omen","latin":"ōmen, -inis","headword":"ōmen","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sign; omen","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī postquam nūllus erat, ēvānuit quidem tamquam certae reī gaudium, ōmen tamen laetum īnsidēbat animīs.","reading":"PERSEVS VICTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"},{"latin":"Ea lēgātiō, velut ōmen, grāta patribus, acerba Carthāginiēnsibus fuit.","reading":"BELLVM PVNICVM TERTIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"onus","latin":"onus, oneris","headword":"onus","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"burden; load","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum Aenēās, cum iam strepitus flammārum propius audīrētur, \"Ergō, cāre pater\" inquit, \"in umerōs meōs tē impōnam; ipse tē portābō, nec mihi grave erit hoc onus.","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"operarius","latin":"operārius, -ī","headword":"operārius","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"workman; labourer","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Intentus perficiendō templō, fabrīs undique ex Etrūriā accītīs, nōn pecūniā sōlum ad id pūblicā est ūsus, sed operāriīs etiam ex plēbe.","reading":"GABIĪ DOLŌ CAPTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"operit","latin":"operit","headword":"operit","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"covers","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In Germāniā hiemēs frīgidiōrēs sunt quam in Italiā: altā nive operītur tōta terra et lacūs glaciē operiuntur; hieme Germānī puerī super glaciem lacuum lūdere possunt.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"opes","latin":"opēs, -um","headword":"opēs","letter":"o","pos":"noun (f. pl.); noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wealth; riches; resources","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dantur opes nullis nunc nisi divitibus. —","reading":"DĒ MĀRTIĀLĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"},{"latin":"Mezentius, quī iam inde ab initiō minimē laetus fuerat orīgine novae urbis, et tum opēs Latīnōrum nimium crēscere rēbātur, statim societātem cum Rutulīs iūnxit Latīnīsque bellum intulit.","reading":"TRŌIĀNĪ ET LATĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"opifex","latin":"opifex, -icis","headword":"opifex","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"craftsman; worker","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"opinio","latin":"opīniō, -ōnis","headword":"opīniō","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"opinion; belief","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Erat enim metus iniectus iīs nātiōnibus quās numquam populus Rōmānus neque lacessendās bellō neque temptandās putāvit; erat etiam alia gravis atque vehemēns opīniō quae per animōs gentium barbarārum pervāserat: aurī locuplētissimī et religiōsissimī dīripiendī causā in eās ōrās nostrum esse exercitum adductum!","reading":"DĒ MAGNITŪDINE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"opperiri","latin":"opperīrī","headword":"opperīrī","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to wait for","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī āēr tranquillus est, necesse est ventum opperīrī. (Ventus est āēr quī movētur.) Cum nūllus ventus super mare flat, tranquillum est mare; cum magnus ventus flat, mare turbidum est.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"oppidum","latin":"oppidum, -ī","headword":"oppidum","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"town","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Brundisium oppidum est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Castra sunt mīlitum oppidum.'","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"opportunitas","latin":"opportūnitās, -ātis","headword":"opportūnitās","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"opportunity; advantage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"opportunus","latin":"opportūnus, -a, -um","headword":"opportūnus","letter":"o","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"suitable; exposed to","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ipse ācer, bellicōsus; at is quem petēbat quiētus, imbellis, placidō ingeniō, opportūnus iniūriae, metuēns magis quam metuendus.","reading":"CIRTA OBSESSA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"oppugnare","latin":"oppugnāre","headword":"oppugnāre","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to attack; besiege","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quibus oppugnandīs quia haud dubiē Rōmāna arma movēbantur, in Olcādum prius fīnēs indūxit exercitum, ut nōn petīsse Saguntīnōs, sed fīnitimīs domitīs gentibus tractus ad id bellum vidērī posset.","reading":"HANNIBAL IMPERĀTOR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"oppugnat","latin":"oppugnat","headword":"oppugnat","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"attacks","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Germānī exercitum nostrum oppugnant.'","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"oppugno","latin":"oppugnō","headword":"oppugnō","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to attack","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Prope cotīdiē aut Germānī castra nostra oppugnāvērunt aut nōs impetūs fēcimus in illōs.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"optimus","latin":"optimus","headword":"optimus","letter":"o","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"best","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia Iūlium 'optimum' appellat.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"opulentus","latin":"opulentus, -a, -um","headword":"opulentus","letter":"o","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"wealthy; powerful","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Interim Turnus Rutulīque, cum rēbus suīs diffīderent, ad Etrūscōs Mezentiumque, rēgem eōrum, cōnfūgerant, quī Caere, opulentō tum oppidō, imperābat.","reading":"TRŌIĀNĪ ET LATĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"ora","latin":"ōra","headword":"ōra","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"coast; shore","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec omnia oppida in ōra maritima sita sunt. (Ōra maritima est fīnis terrae, unde mare incipit.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"oraculum","latin":"ōrāculum, -ī","headword":"ōrāculum","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"oracle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque Delphōs, ad maxumē inclutum in terrīs ōrāculum, mittere statuit.","reading":"TEMPLUM IOVIS ET ŌRĀCULUM DELPHICUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"oratio","latin":"ōrātiō","headword":"ōrātiō","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"speech; sentence","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"orator","latin":"ōrātor, -ōris","headword":"ōrātor","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"orator; speaker","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ante Comitium est locus superior, ex quō ōrātōrēs verba faciunt ad populum.","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"oriens","latin":"oriēns","headword":"oriēns","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"east; the rising sun","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ea pars caelī unde sōl oritur dīcitur oriēns.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"origo","latin":"orīgō, -inis","headword":"orīgō","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"origin; beginning","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"oriri","latin":"orīrī","headword":"orīrī","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to rise","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dum ille loquitur, Mēdus occidentem spectat et nūbēs ātrās procul suprā mare orīrī videt; simul mare tranquillum esse dēsinit. 'Nōn serēnum est caelum,' inquit, 'Ecce nūbēs ātrae ...' Gubernātor statim loquī dēsinit et nūbēs spectat; tum caelum aspiciēns exclāmat: 'Quid (malum!) hoc est?","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"ornamentum","latin":"ōrnāmentum","headword":"ōrnāmentum","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ornament; piece of jewellery","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Gemmae et margarītae sunt ōrnāmenta.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"ornat","latin":"ōrnat","headword":"ōrnat","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"adorns; decorates","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ānulus digitum Aemiliae ōrnat, margarītae collum eius ōrnant.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"ortus","latin":"ortus, -ūs","headword":"ortus","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rising (of the sun)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"os","latin":"ōs","headword":"ōs","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mouth; bone","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In capite sunt oculī et aurēs, nāsus et os.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Facile os frangere potuistī.'","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"osculatur","latin":"ōsculātur","headword":"ōsculātur","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"kisses","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius uxōrem ōsculātur et 'Ō Aemilia' inquit, 'mea uxor!","reading":"AMOR IŪLIĪ ET AEMILIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"osculum","latin":"ōsculum","headword":"ōsculum","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"kiss","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia virō suō ōsculum dat.","reading":"ROSA IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"ostendit","latin":"ostendit","headword":"ostendit","letter":"o","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"shows; points out","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Albīnus eōs salūtat et margarītās in līneā ante oculōs Lȳdiae tenet: Albīnus Lȳdiae margarītās ostendit.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"Linguam ostende!\" Syra: \"Quid dīcit medicus?\" Aemilia: \"Medicus Quīntum os aperīre atque linguam ostendere iubet.\" Quīntus os aperit atque medicō linguam ostendit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"ostiarius","latin":"ōstiārius","headword":"ōstiārius","letter":"o","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"doorkeeper","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pater fīliōs salūtat: 'Salvēte, fīliī!' et ā fīliīs salūtātur: 'Salvē, pater!' Iūlius ambulat ad ōstium, quod ab ōstiāriō aperītur.","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"latin":"Servus cuius officium est forēs aperīre et claudere ac vīllam dominī cūstōdīre, ōstiārius vel iānitor appellātur.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"ostium","latin":"ōstium","headword":"ōstium","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"door; entrance; mouth (of a river)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In vīllā sunt duo ōstia: ōstium magnum et ōstium parvum.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Mēdus autem Rōmae est ante ōstium Lȳdiae.","reading":"MĒDVS ET CORNĒLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"otium","latin":"ōtium","headword":"ōtium","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"leisure; free time","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ovis","latin":"ovis","headword":"ovis","letter":"o","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sheep","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pāstor nōn sōlus est in campō, nam canis niger cum eō est et centum ovēs: ūna ovis nigra et ūndēcentum ovēs albae.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Equus et asinus, leō et lupus, canis et ovis bēstiae sunt.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"ovum","latin":"ōvum","headword":"ōvum","letter":"o","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"egg","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pabulum","latin":"pābulum, -ī","headword":"pābulum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fodder; feed; food","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Italia est terra fertilis, sed multa loca nōn arantur nec ūllās frūgēs ferunt praeter herbās; iīs locīs ovēs, porcī, bovēs pāscuntur, nam herba pecoris pābulum est, et facilius est pecus pāscere quam colere.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"},{"latin":"Cum undique Numantiam obsidiōne clausisset et obsessōs fame vidēret urgērī, hostēs quī pābulum exierant vetuit occīdī, quia dīceret 'vēlōcius eōs absumptūrōs frūmentī quod habērent, sī plūrēs fuissent.' Numantīnī fame coāctī ipsī sē per vicem trāicientēs trucīdāvērunt.","reading":"HISPĀNIA PĀCĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"paelex","latin":"paelex, -icis","headword":"paelex","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"concubine","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"paene","latin":"paene","headword":"paene","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"almost; nearly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nec longum tempus nōbīs reliquum est ad vīvendum, cibus noster paene cōnsūmptus est.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"pagina","latin":"pāgina","headword":"pāgina","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"page","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In LINGVĀ LATĪNĀ sunt multae pāginae et multa capitula: capitulum prīmum, secundum, tertium, cētera. 'IMPERIVM ROMANVM' est titulus capitulī prīmī.","reading":"LIBER TVVS LATĪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"pallescere","latin":"pallēscere","headword":"pallēscere","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to grow pale","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pallidus","latin":"pallidus","headword":"pallidus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"pale","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Interim Mārcus, cuius vultūs ad nōmen magistrī commūtāvit, pallidus et tremēns patrem legentem intuētur.","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"latin":"Tum mercātor, cum gubernātōrem pallidum videat, \"Bonō animō es!\" inquit.","reading":"NĀVIS PRAEDŌNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"pallium","latin":"pallium","headword":"pallium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cloak; mantle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homō territus ex ōstiō cēdere cōnātur, sed canis īrātus pallium eius dentibus prehendit et tenet.","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"palma","latin":"palma","headword":"palma","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"palm (of victory); prize","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed plerumque is qui victus est occiditur, victor vero palmam accipit, dum spectatores delectati clamant ac manibus plaudunt.\"","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"paludamentum","latin":"palūdāmentum, -ī","headword":"palūdāmentum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"commander’s cloak","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cui soror virgō, quae dēspōnsa ūnī ex Curiātiīs fuerat, obvia ante portam Capēnam fuit, cognitōque super umerōs frātris palūdāmentō spōnsī, quod ipsa cōnfēcerat, solvit crīnēs et flēbiliter nōmine spōnsum mortuum appellat.","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"palus","latin":"palūs, -ūdis","headword":"palūs","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"marsh; swamp","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"panis","latin":"pānis","headword":"pānis","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bread","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cibus pāstōris est pānis, quī inest in saccō.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Ante eōs in parvā mēnsā pānis et mala sunt.","reading":"DISCESSVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"papaver","latin":"papāver, -eris","headword":"papāver","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"poppy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi inambulāns tacitus summa papāverum capita dīcitur baculō dēcussisse.","reading":"GABIĪ DOLŌ CAPTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"parcere","latin":"parcere","headword":"parcere","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to spare (+ dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"parentes","latin":"parentēs","headword":"parentēs","letter":"p","pos":"noun (m. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"parents","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus sē malum puerum fuisse fatētur ac simul prōmittit sē posthāc bonum puerum futūrum esse, semper sē parentibus paritūrum esse neque umquam in viā pugnātūrum neque in lūdō dormītūrum esse — id quod saepe antehāc prōmīsit!","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"parere","latin":"pārēre","headword":"pārēre","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"obey; to obey (+ dat.); to obey (with dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"paret","latin":"pāret","headword":"pāret","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"obeys; obeys (with dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Venī in hortum, Iūlia!' Iūlia imperat: 'Claude ōstium!' Ancilla pāret.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"parit","latin":"parit","headword":"parit","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"gives birth to; lays","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Canis nōn ōva, sed pullōs vīvōs parit.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"parricidium","latin":"parricīdium, -ī","headword":"parricīdium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"murder of a parent","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nec nocte nec interdiū virum conquiēscere patī, nē grātuīta praeterita parricīdia essent: \"nōn sibi dēfuisse marītum cum quō tacita servīret; dēfuisse virum quī sē rēgnō dignum esse putāret, quī meminisset sē esse Prīscī Tarquiniī fīlium, quī habēre quam spērāre rēgnum māllet!\"","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"},{"latin":"Roscium parricīdiī reum clārissimā ōrātiōne dēfendit, eōque patrōciniō maximam laudem meruit.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"pars","latin":"pars","headword":"pars","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"part","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Nōmen quid est?' Discipulus: 'Pars ōrātiōnis cum cāsū, corpus aut rem propriē significāns; aut enim ūnīus nōmen est et proprium dīcitur, aut multōrum et appellātīvum.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"particeps","latin":"particeps, -cipis","headword":"particeps","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"sharing in; partaking of","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed et in rēgnīs nimis expertēs sunt cēterī commūnis iūris et cōnsiliī; et in optimātium dominātū vix particeps lībertātis potest esse multitūdō, cum omnī cōnsiliō commūnī ac potestāte careat; et cum omnia per populum geruntur, quamvīs iūstum atque moderātum, tamen ipsa aequābilitās est inīqua, cum habet nūllōs gradūs dignitātis...'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"participium","latin":"participium","headword":"participium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"participle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"partior","latin":"partior","headword":"partior","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"share; divide (deponent)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī vōs sex assēs aequē partīminī, quot tibi sunt?' Mārcus: 'Pecūniam meam exiguam nōn largior nec partior cum aliīs!'","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"partus","latin":"partus, -ūs","headword":"partus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"birth; offspring","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Addit scelerī scelus: stirpem frātris virīlem interimit, frātris fīliae Reae Silviae, cum virginem Vestālem eam lēgisset, perpetuā virginitāte spem partūs adimit.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"parvulus","latin":"parvulus","headword":"parvulus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"little; tiny","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Parvulī quī nōndum fārī possunt īnfantēs dīcuntur.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"parvus","latin":"parvus","headword":"parvus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"small; little","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tiberis nōn est fluvius magnus, Tiberis fluvius parvus est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"pascit","latin":"pāscit","headword":"pāscit","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"grazes; feeds","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque pecus maiōris pretiī est quam frūmentum, et quī pecus pāscit plūs pecūniae facit quam quī agrōs colit.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"passer","latin":"passer","headword":"passer","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sparrow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lucernis accensis, Iulius librum Catulli proferri iubet, tum \"Incipiam\" inquit \"a carmine de morte passeris quem Lesbia in deliciis habuerat:","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"passivum","latin":"passīvum","headword":"passīvum","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"passive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"passivus","latin":"passīvus","headword":"passīvus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"passive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Genera verbōrum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Quattuor.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Āctīva, passīva, neutra, dēpōnentia.'","reading":"DĒ VERBŌ ET ADVERBIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"passus","latin":"passus","headword":"passus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pace; step","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Aemilius in castrīs habitat mīlle passūs ā fīne imperiī.","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"pastor","latin":"pāstor","headword":"pāstor","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shepherd","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic vir, quī in campō ambulat, pāstor Iūliī est.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Pāstōrēs Āfricae leōnēs timent, nam leōnēs nōn sōlum ovēs pāstōrum edunt, sed etiam pāstōrēs ipsōs!","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"pater","latin":"pater","headword":"pater","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"father","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pater est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"patera","latin":"patera, -ae","headword":"patera","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"libation-bowl","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum fīdissimus pater Anchīsēs magnam pateram merō implēvit atque in celsā puppī stāns deōs invocāvit: \"Dī maris et terrae tempestātumque potentēs, ferte viam ventō facilem et spīrāte secundō!\"","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"paterfamilias","latin":"paterfamiliās","headword":"paterfamiliās","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"head of the household","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ante decem annōs Iūlius paterfamiliās nōn erat, tunc enim nec uxōrem nec līberōs habēbat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"pati","latin":"patī","headword":"patī","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to endure; suffer","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puerum Rōmānum sine lacrimīs dolōrem patī decet.'","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"patria","latin":"patria","headword":"patria","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"homeland; fatherland","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Germānia est patria Germānōrum, ut Rōmā patriā est.'","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Mēdus, quī Graecus est, in patriam suam redīre vult.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"patrimonium","latin":"patrimōnium, -ī","headword":"patrimōnium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"inherited property; patrimony","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed Tarquiniō Collātīnō statim sublāta est dignitās; placuerat enim 'nē quisquam in urbe manēret quī Tarquinius vocārētur.' Ergō acceptō omnī patrimōniō suō ex urbe migrāvit, et locō ipsīus factus est P.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"patrocinium","latin":"patrōcinium, -ī","headword":"patrōcinium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"legal defence; patronage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Roscium parricīdiī reum clārissimā ōrātiōne dēfendit, eōque patrōciniō maximam laudem meruit.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"patruus","latin":"patruus, -ī","headword":"patruus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"paternal uncle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pauci","latin":"paucī","headword":"paucī","letter":"p","pos":"adjective (pl.); adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"few","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In Arabiā nōn multī, sed paucī fluviī sunt et pauca oppida.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"paucitas","latin":"paucitās, -ātis","headword":"paucitās","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fewness; small number","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Praecipuē ita patrum numerō imminūtō, statuit nūllōs in patrēs legere, ut paucitāte ipsā senātus contemptior esset.","reading":"L. IŪNIUS BRŪTUS, LĪBERĀTOR POPULĪ RŌMĀNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"pauper","latin":"pauper","headword":"pauper","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"poor","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pater Aemiliae erat homō pauper, quī ūnam domum exiguam possidēbat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"pavor","latin":"pavor, -ōris","headword":"pavor","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"panic; dread","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum vērō cūnctī Trōiānī novō pavōre perturbantur, et \"Laocoontem poenās meritās Minervae dedisse\" dīcunt, \"quod hasta scelerāta sacrum rōbur laeserit.\" Conclāmant omnēs \"simulācrum equī in arcem Minervae dūcendum esse.\" Ergō parte mūrōrum dēstrūctā māchina illa hostibus armātīs plēna magnō labōre in urbem trahitur fūnibus, dum puerī puellaeque carmina sacra canunt et fūnem manū contingere gaudent.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"pax","latin":"pāx, pācis","headword":"pāx","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"peace","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cēterum nihilo eī pāx tūtior fuit: barbarus eum quīdam palam obtruncāvit.","reading":"IŪS IŪRANDVM HANNIBALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"pectus","latin":"pectus","headword":"pectus","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"chest; breast","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sub collō est pectus.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"peculatus","latin":"pecūlātus, -ūs","headword":"pecūlātus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"embezzlement","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Scīpiō Asiāticus, frāter Āfricānī, pecūlātūs accūsātus damnātusque cum in vincula et carcerem dūcerētur, Ti.","reading":"PERSEVS VICTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"pecunia","latin":"pecūnia","headword":"pecūnia","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"money","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In sacculō eius est pecūnia.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"pecuniosus","latin":"pecūniōsus","headword":"pecūniōsus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"rich; wealthy","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eae quae magnam pecūniam habent multa ōrnāmenta emunt.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"pecus","latin":"pecus","headword":"pecus","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cattle; flock","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Italia est terra fertilis, sed multa loca nōn arantur nec ūllās frūgēs ferunt praeter herbās; iīs locīs ovēs, porcī, bovēs pāscuntur, nam herba pecoris pābulum est, et facilius est pecus pāscere quam colere.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"pedes","latin":"pedes, peditis","headword":"pedes","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"foot-soldier","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Aemilius pīlum tantum fert, is enim pedēs est, nōn eques.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Pedestre magna iam ex parte certāmen factum erat; ācrius tamen quam diūtius pugnātum est, pulsīque Rōmānī equitēs terga vertunt.","reading":"CANNAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"peior","latin":"pēior","headword":"pēior","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"worse","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nēmō deōrum peior marītus est quam Iuppiter, neque ūlla dea peior uxor est quam Venus.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"pellere","latin":"pellere","headword":"pellere","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to drive (out)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōlī iterum mē forās in imbrem pellere!\" Iānitor, postquam canem vīnxit, \"Nōn ego\" inquit, \"sed hic canis tē forās pepulit.","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"penna","latin":"penna","headword":"penna","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"feather","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Ecce omnia habeō quae necessāria sunt ad hōc opus: pennās, cēram, ignem.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"pensum","latin":"pēnsum","headword":"pēnsum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"exercise; task","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pentameter","latin":"pentameter","headword":"pentameter","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pentameter (five-foot verse)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"penuria","latin":"pēnūria, -ae","headword":"pēnūria","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"want; scarcity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Scīpiōnī, summō virō, placuisse; ob eāsdem artēs ā Micipsā, nōn pēnūriā līberōrum, in rēgnum adoptātum esse.","reading":"CIRTA OBSESSA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"per","latin":"per","headword":"per","letter":"p","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"through","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus prope Rōmam est; iam mūrī Rōmānī ab eō videntur et porta Capēna. (Is quī viā Latīnā venit per portam Capēnam Rōmam intrat.) Cūr Rōmam it Mēdus?","reading":"MĒDVS ET CORNĒLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"percontari","latin":"percontārī","headword":"percontārī","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to ask; inquire","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tarquinius pretium percontātus est.","reading":"LIBRĪ SIBYLLĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"percontatio","latin":"percontātiō, -ōnis","headword":"percontātiō","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"interrogation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Prima percontātiō fuit 'quā subāctus iniūriā contrā populum Rōmānum bellum tam īnfestō animō suscēpisset, quō sē rēgnumque suum ad ultimum discrīmen addūceret?' Cum, respōnsum exspectantibus cūnctīs, terram intuēns diū tacitus flēret, rūrsus cōnsul:","reading":"PERSEVS ANTE CONSVLEM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"percutere","latin":"percutere","headword":"percutere","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to strike; knock; hammer","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At subitō silentium clāmōre et strepitū maximō rumpitur, nam Mārcus in cubiculō suō, quod iuxtā cubiculum Quīntī est, magnā vōce clāmat et forem manibus pedibusque percutit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"perduellio","latin":"perduelliō, -ōnis","headword":"perduelliō","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"treason","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēx, nē ipse rem tam trīstem iūdicāret ac secundum iūdicium suppliciī auctor esset, cōnsiliō populī advocātō, \"Duumvirōs\" inquit, \"quī Horātiō perduelliōnem iūdicent, secundum lēgem faciō.\" Horrenda lēgis verba haec erant: \"Duumvirī perduelliōnem iūdicent.","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"perfidia","latin":"perfidia, -ae","headword":"perfidia","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"treachery","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dīmicātum est enim nōn magis cum hostibus quam — quae dīmicātiō maior atque perīculōsior est — cum prōditiōne ac perfidiā sociōrum.","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"},{"latin":"Hās tantās virī virtūtēs ingentia vitia aequābant: inhūmāna crūdēlitās, perfidia plūs quam Pūnica, nihil vērī, nihil sānctī, nūllus deum metus, nūllum iūs iūrandum, nūlla religiō.","reading":"HANNIBAL IMPERĀTOR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"perfidus","latin":"perfidus, -a, -um","headword":"perfidus","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"treacherous; faithless","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Spērāsne, perfide hospes, tē tantum nefās dissimulāre posse et meā terrā clam dēcēdere?","reading":"NŪNTIUS DEŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"perfugium","latin":"perfugium, -ī","headword":"perfugium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"refuge; shelter","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hiemis enim, nōn avāritiae perfugium maiōrēs nostrī in sociōrum atque amīcōrum tēctīs esse voluērunt.","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"pergere","latin":"pergere","headword":"pergere","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"continue; go on; to continue; proceed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Somnus virō industriō necessārius est!\" Aemilia īrāta: \"Nōlī pergere!\" inquit, \"Plūra ā tē audīre nōlō!\" atque iterum ad ōstium versūs īre incipit.","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"periculum","latin":"perīculum","headword":"perīculum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"danger","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōlīte vērō cēnsēre nōs iam extrā perīculum esse.","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"peristylum","latin":"peristȳlum","headword":"peristȳlum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"peristyle; colonnaded garden court; colonnaded court; colonnade","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Etiam peristȳlum magnum et pulchrum in vīllā est. 'Peristȳlum' est vocābulum Graecum.","reading":"ĀTRIVM ET PERISTȲLVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Māter nōn est apud fīliōs, ea in peristȳlō est; illīc virum suum exspectat.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"perit","latin":"perit","headword":"perit","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"perishes; is lost","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"peritus","latin":"perītus, -a, -um","headword":"perītus","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"skilled; expert","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"permutatio","latin":"permūtātiō, -ōnis","headword":"permūtātiō","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"exchange","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Post haec mala Carthāginiēnsēs Regulum ducem, quem cēperant, petīvērunt ut Rōmam proficīscerētur et pācem ā Rōmānīs obtinēret ac permūtātiōnem captīvōrum faceret.","reading":"BELLVM PŪNICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"pernicies","latin":"perniciēs, -ēī","headword":"perniciēs","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"destruction; ruin","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Et duce Xanthippō, quī ā Lacedaemoniīs missus fuerat, Rōmānōrum dux Regulus victus est ultimā perniciē.","reading":"BELLVM PŪNICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"perniciosus","latin":"perniciōsus, -a, -um","headword":"perniciōsus","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"destructive; ruinous","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Perniciōsum admodum hoc bellum fuit.","reading":"BELLVM SOCIĀLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"perrogare","latin":"perrogāre","headword":"perrogāre","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to ask in order; poll (the senate)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum lēgātī ex Āfricā cum ōrātōribus Carthāginiēnsium et Gulussā redīssent dīcerentque 'et exercitum sē dēprehendisse et classem Carthāgine dēprehendisse', perrogārī sententiās placuit.","reading":"BELLVM PVNICVM TERTIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"persequi","latin":"persequī","headword":"persequī","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to pursue; chase","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tempestās quidem dēsiit, sed multa alia perīcula nōbīs impendent: ut saxa quibus nāvēs franguntur, vorāginēs in quās nāvēs merguntur, praedōnēs maritimī quī nāvēs persequuntur, ut mercēs et pecūniam rapiant nautāsque occīdant.","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"latin":"Amīcī nostrī in marī Tuscō nāvigantēs tālēs praedōnēs audācissimōs nāvem suam persequī arbitrantur.","reading":"IN MARĪ TVSCŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"persona","latin":"persōna","headword":"persōna","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"character; person","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Persōnae: Iūlia, Mārcus, Quīntus.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Magister: 'Prōnōmen quid est?' Discipulus: 'Pars ōrātiōnis quae prō nōmine posita tantundem paene significat persōnamque interdum recipit.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"perterritus","latin":"perterritus","headword":"perterritus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"terrified","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Neptūnum invocō, quod ille dominus maris ac tempestātum est.' Nautā perterritus tempestātem venientem opperītur.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"pes","latin":"pēs","headword":"pēs","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"foot","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In bracchiō est manus, in crūre pēs.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Quīntus dormīre nōn potest, quod et caput et pēs eī dolet.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"pessimus","latin":"pessimus","headword":"pessimus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"worst","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inter omnēs deōs deāsque Iuppiter pessimus marītus est ac Venus pessima uxor.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"pessum dare","latin":"pessum dare","headword":"pessum dare","letter":"p","pos":"phrase","posGroup":"other","english":"to ruin; destroy utterly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quae rēs plērumque magnās cīvitātēs pessum dedit, dum alterī alterōs vincere quōvīs modō et victōs acerbius ulcīscī volunt.","reading":"CĪVITĀS DĪLACERĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"pestilentia","latin":"pestilentia, -ae","headword":"pestilentia","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"plague; pestilence","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nāvibus in lītus subductīs, iuvenēs Trōiānī iam novam urbem aedificābant et arva nova colēbant, cum foeda pestilentia hominēs miserōs afficere coepit, et simul sōl flagrāns agrōs siccōs adeō torrēbat ut nec herbam nec frūmentum ferre possent.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"pharetra","latin":"pharetra, -ae","headword":"pharetra","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"quiver","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Integer vītae scelerisque pūrus / nōn eget Maurīs iaculīs neque arcū / nec venēnātīs gravidā sagittīs, / Fusce, pharetrā,","reading":"INTEGER VĪTAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"philosophus","latin":"philosophus, -ī","headword":"philosophus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"philosopher","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūxtā ea tempora Empedoclēs Agrigentīnus in philosophiae nātūrālis studiō flōruit.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"pietas","latin":"pietās, -ātis","headword":"pietās","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"duty; piety","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"piger","latin":"piger","headword":"piger","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"lazy; idle; slow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī discere nōn vult atque in lūdō dormit, piger esse dīcitur.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"latin":"Nōn oportet sē comparāre cum discipulō pigerrimō ac stultissimō!","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"pilleus","latin":"pilleus, -ī","headword":"pilleus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cap of a free man","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi eī in carpentō sedentī cum uxōre aquilā repente dēlāpsa pilleum aufert, superque carpentum volitāns rūrsus, velut dīvīnitus missa, capitī aptē repōnit; inde sublīmis abit.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"pilum","latin":"pīlum","headword":"pīlum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"javelin","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Mīles est vir quī scūtum et gladium et pīlum fert.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"pirata","latin":"pīrāta","headword":"pīrāta","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pirate","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed frūstrā hoc optō, nam iam illī pīrātae eam spem mihi ēripient, idque eādem diē quā ab amīcā meā dēsertus sum!\"","reading":"DĒ VĒRĪS AMĪCĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"pirum","latin":"pirum","headword":"pirum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pear","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vidēte, puerī: hic saccus plēnus est pirōrum.' Iūlius duo pira ē saccō sūmit: 'Ecce pirum tuum, Mārce, et tuum, Quīnte.' Pater fīliīs suīs pira dat.","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"piscator","latin":"piscātor","headword":"piscātor","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fisherman","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Paucīs post diēbus aliquis piscātor in eōdem marī piscem cēpit quī tam fōrmōsus erat ut piscātor eum nōn ēderet, sed tyrannō dōnāret.","reading":"ĀNVLVS POLYCRATIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"piscis","latin":"piscis","headword":"piscis","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fish","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Piscis neque ālās neque pedēs habet.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"placidus","latin":"placidus, -a, -um","headword":"placidus","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"calm; gentle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magna virī virtūs et gentis honōs in animō versātur, vultus verbaque haerent in pectore, neque cūra membris placidam quiētem dat.","reading":"FLAMMA AMŌRIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"planus","latin":"plānus","headword":"plānus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"plain; clear","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"plaudere","latin":"plaudere","headword":"plaudere","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to clap; applaud","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Illo occiso spectatores plaudere desierunt ac lugere coeperunt.\"","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"plebs","latin":"plēbs, -bis","headword":"plēbs","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"the common people; the plebeians","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nē huic fāmae plēbs crēderet, Proculus Iūlius, senātor nōbilissimus, in cōntiōnem prōdiit.","reading":"ROMVLVS CONSECRATVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"plenus","latin":"plēnus","headword":"plēnus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"full","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Vidēte, puerī: hic saccus plēnus mālōrum est.'","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"plerumque","latin":"plērumque","headword":"plērumque","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"mostly; generally","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed plerumque is qui victus est occiditur, victor vero palmam accipit, dum spectatores delectati clamant ac manibus plaudunt.\"","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"plorat","latin":"plōrat","headword":"plōrat","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"cries; weeps","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iam Iūlia nōn cantat, sed plōrat: 'Uhuhū!'","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"pluralis","latin":"plūrālis","headword":"plūrālis","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"plural","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Numerī nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Duo.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Singulāris, ut hic magister; plūrālis, ut hī magistrī.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"plusquamperfectum","latin":"plūsquamperfectum","headword":"plūsquamperfectum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pluperfect (tense); pluperfect","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"poculum","latin":"pōculum","headword":"pōculum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cup","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pōculum tollēns 'Ergō bibāmus!' inquit, 'Hoc vīnum factum est ex optimīs ūvīs meārum vīneārum.","reading":"CĒNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"},{"latin":"Hic pōculum tollit Orontēs et exclāmat: 'Vīvat fortissimus quisque!","reading":"INTER PŌCVLA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"poema","latin":"poēma, -atis","headword":"poēma","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"poem","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Archilochum autem Nepōs Cornēlius trādit, Tullō Hostīliō Rōmae regnante, iam tunc fuisse poēmatis clārum et nōbilem.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"poena","latin":"poena","headword":"poena","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"punishment; penalty","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nē servō quidem iniūriam facere oportet, sed necesse est servōs īnfīdōs aut fugitīvōs sevērē pūnīre; nec enim quidquam nisi poena sevēra eius generis servōs ā maleficiīs dēterrēre atque in officiō tenēre potest.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"pollens","latin":"pollēns, -entis","headword":"pollēns","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"strong; powerful","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī ubi prīmum adolēvit, pollēns vīribus, decōrā faciē, sed multō maximē ingeniō validus, nōn sē luxuī neque inertiae corrumpendum dedit, sed, utī mōs gentis illīus est, equitāre, iaculārī, cursū cum aequalibus certāre; et, cum omnēs glōriā anteīret, omnibus tamen cārus esse.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"pollere","latin":"pollēre","headword":"pollēre","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to be strong; prevail","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pollicetur","latin":"pollicētur","headword":"pollicētur","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"promises","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Id tibi polliceor.'","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"pollicitatio","latin":"pollicitātiō, -ōnis","headword":"pollicitātiō","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"promise; offer","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eā tempestāte exercitū nostrō fuēre complūrēs novī atque nōbilēs, quibus dīvitiae bonō honestōque potiōrēs erant, factiōsī domī, potentēs apud sociōs, clārī magis quam honestī; quī Iugurthae nōn mediocrem animum pollicitandō accendēbant, 'sī Micipsa rēx occidisset, fore utī sōlus imperiī Numidiae potīrētur: in ipsō maximam virtūtem, Rōmae omnia vēnālia esse!'","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"pomerium","latin":"pōmērium, -ī","headword":"pōmērium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sacred city boundary","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Verberātō vel intrā pōmērium vel extrā pōmērium!\"","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"pompa","latin":"pompa, -ae","headword":"pompa","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"procession; parade","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fūriō Pācilō cōnsulibus, Metellus in Siciliā Afrōrum ducem cum centum trīgintā elephantīs et magnīs cōpiīs venientem superāvit, vīgintī mīlia hostium cecīdit, sex et vīgintī elephantōs cēpit, reliquōs errantēs per Numidās, quōs in auxilium habēbat, collēgit et Rōmam dēdūxit ingentī pompā, cum elephantōrum numerus omnia itinera implērent.","reading":"BELLVM PŪNICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"pondo","latin":"pondō","headword":"pondō","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"by weight","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornēlium Rūfīnum, quī bis cōnsul et dictātor fuerat, senātū mōvērunt: causamque istī notae subscrīpsērunt 'quod eum comperissent argentī factī cēnae grātiā decem pondō lībrās habēre.'","reading":"PHILIPPVS ĀD LŪCĪLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"pondus","latin":"pondus, -eris","headword":"pondus","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"weight","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ponit","latin":"pōnit","headword":"pōnit","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"puts; places","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Sacculum tuum in mēnsā pōne!' Dāvus sacculum suum in mēnsā pōnit.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Sūmite cēterās rosās eāsque in aquā pōnite!\" Puerī cēterās quattuor rosās sūmunt et cum iīs discēdunt.","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"pontifex","latin":"pontifex, -icis","headword":"pontifex","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"priest; pontifex maximus","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūxtā aedem Vestae est ātrium Vestae, id est domus Vestālium, et Rēgia, domus pontificis maximī, in quā ōlim rēgēs Rōmānī habitāvisse dīcuntur. (Pontifex maximus est summus sacerdōs, quī cēterīs omnibus sacerdōtibus Rōmānīs praefectus est; sacerdōtum negōtium est sacrificia facere atque rēs dīvīnās cūrāre.)","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"pontus","latin":"pontus, -ī","headword":"pontus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sea","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"populares","latin":"populārēs, -ium","headword":"populārēs","letter":"p","pos":"noun m. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fellow citizens; one’s own people","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Īra vulgī Albānī, quod tribus mīlitibus fortūna pūblica commissa erat, ingenium dictātōris corrūpit, et quoniam rēcta cōnsilia haud bene ēvēnerant, prāvīs cōnsiliīs reconciliāre populārium animōs coepit.","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"popularis","latin":"populāris, -e","headword":"populāris","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"popular; of the people","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Illa autem est cīvitās \"populāris\" (sīc enim appellant) in quā in populō sunt omnia.'","reading":"DĒ TRIBUS GENERIBUS RĒRUM PŪBLICĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"porcus","latin":"porcus","headword":"porcus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pig","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: \"Et tū tam sordidus es quam porcus!","reading":"MARCVS Ā PATRE INTERROGĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"porta","latin":"porta","headword":"porta","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gate","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In mūrō Rōmānō duodecim portae sunt.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Quattuor portae per vallum in castra dūcunt.","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"portat","latin":"portat","headword":"portat","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"carries","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syrus saccum portat et Lēander quoque saccum portat: Syrus et Lēander duōs saccōs in umerīs portant.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Puerī saccōs plēnōs, quī ā servīs portantur, vident et interrogant: 'Quid inest in saccīs?' Iūlius respondet: 'In saccō quem Lēander portat māla īnsunt.","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"portentum","latin":"portentum, -ī","headword":"portentum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"portent; prodigy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cuius cīvēs Rōmānī aliī super aliōs trucīdentur, exsulātum eant, bona āmittant: quid speī meliōris Latīnīs portendī?","reading":"TURNUS HERDONIUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"porticus","latin":"porticus, -ūs","headword":"porticus","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"colonnade; portico","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūxtā aedem Dīvī Vespasiānī est porticus duodecim dīs et deābus cōnsecrāta, quōrum simulācra aurāta in porticū stant.","reading":"AEDĒS FORĪ RŌMĀNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"portuosus","latin":"portuōsus, -a, -um","headword":"portuōsus","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"full of harbours","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In dīvīsiōne, quae pars Numidiae Mauretaniam attingit, agrō virīsque opulentior, Iugurthae trāditur; illam alteram, quae portuōsior et aedificiīs magis exōrnāta erat, Adherbal possēdit.","reading":"ADHERBAL RŌMAM PROFĪCĪSCITUR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"portus","latin":"portus","headword":"portus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"harbour; port","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Alia oppida maritima quae magnōs portūs habent sunt Brundisium, Arīminum, Genua, Puteolī.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"poscit","latin":"poscit","headword":"poscit","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"asks for; demands","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus frīget, quod corpus eius nūdum est (id est sine vestīmentīs); itaque Mārcus vestīmenta sua ā servō poscit: 'Dā mihi tunicam et togam!","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"positivus","latin":"positīvus","headword":"positīvus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"positive (degree)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Comparātiōnis gradūs quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Trēs.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Positīvus, ut doctus; comparātīvus, ut doctior; superlātīvus, ut doctissimus.' Magister: 'Quae nōmina comparantur?' Discipulus: 'Appellātīva dumtaxat quālitātem aut quantitātem significantiā.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"possidet","latin":"possidet","headword":"possidet","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"owns; possesses","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pater Iūliī, quī iam mortuus est, magnam pecūniam habēbat multāsque vīllās magnificās possidēbat praeter domum Rōmānam: is homō dīves erat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"post","latin":"post","headword":"post","letter":"p","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"after; behind","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ursus est ante Iūlium, Dāvus post eum est.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"posteri","latin":"posterī, -ōrum","headword":"posterī","letter":"p","pos":"noun m. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"descendants","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Haec īnsula Trōiānōs fessōs in tōtum portum recēpit, ibīque deus Apollō, quem pius Aenēās in vetere templō adōrābat, novam terram Trōiānīs et posterīs eōrum pollicitus est.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"posteritas","latin":"posteritās, -ātis","headword":"posteritās","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"posterity; future generations","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīn etiam sī cupiat prōlēs illa futūrōrum hominum deinceps laudēs ūnius cuiusque nostrum ā patribus acceptās posterīs prōdere, tamen propter ēluviōnēs exustiōnēsque terrārum, quās accidere tempore certō necesse est, nōn modo nōn aeternam, sed nē dīturnam quidem glōriam assequī possumus.'","reading":"ANGUSTIAE TERRĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"posticum","latin":"posticum, -ī","headword":"posticum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"back door","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēx ipse nocte mediā cum tribus cōnsciīs fugae per posticum aedium in propinquum cubiculō hortum atque inde, māceriam aegrē trānsgressus, ad mare pervēnit.","reading":"PERSEVS CAPTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"postquam","latin":"postquam","headword":"postquam","letter":"p","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"after; when","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nunc dēmum, postquam heri ad vīllam Tusculānam rediī, paulum requiēscere possum et amīcōs vīsere.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"postremus","latin":"postrēmus","headword":"postrēmus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"last; final","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Annus in duodecim mēnsēs dīviditur, quibus haec sunt nōmina: Iānuārius, mēnsis prīmus; Februārius, secundus; Mārtius, tertius; Aprīlis, quārtus; Maius, quīntus; Iūnius, sextus; Iūlius, septimus; Augustus, octāvus; September, nōnus; Octōber, decimus; November, ūndecimus; December, mēnsis duodecimus ac postrēmus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"postulare","latin":"postulāre","headword":"postulāre","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"demand; ask for","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quōmodo īnfāns, quī fārī nōn potest, postulat?","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"postulat","latin":"postulat","headword":"postulat","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"demands; asks","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōlī ā mē postulāre ut tantum pecūniae statim solvam!","reading":"PĀSTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"potens","latin":"potēns, -entis","headword":"potēns","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"powerful","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"potentia","latin":"potentia, -ae","headword":"potentia","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"power; might","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quanta erit potentia Poenōrum, quanta glōria tua, sōlor, sī cum duce Trōiānōrum tē coniūnxeris!","reading":"FLAMMA AMŌRIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"potest","latin":"potest","headword":"potest","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"can; is able","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Canis volāre nōn potest.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Homō quī ventrem malum habet cibum sūmere nōn potest, neque is sānus, sed aeger est.","reading":"SĀNVS ET AEGER","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"potio","latin":"pōtiō","headword":"pōtiō","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"drink","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn sōlum dē cibō et pōtiōne est sermō convīvārum.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"potiri","latin":"potīrī","headword":"potīrī","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to seize; possess (with abl.)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"praeceps","latin":"praeceps, -cipitis","headword":"praeceps","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"headlong; steep","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Illa dolōs dīrumque nefās in pectore versat… Nōn fugis hinc praeceps, dum praecipitāre potestās?","reading":"ROGUS DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"praeceptum","latin":"praeceptum, -ī","headword":"praeceptum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"order; instruction","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hōrum in concursū Bīthȳnī Hannibalis praeceptō ūniversī nāvem Eumenis adoriuntur.","reading":"APVD PRŪSIAM ET MORS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"praeco","latin":"praecō, -ōnis","headword":"praecō","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"herald; crier","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inde, omnibus perculsīs pavōre, in rēgiā sēde prō cūriā sedēns patrēs in cūriam per praecōnem \"ad rēgem Tarquinium\" cōgī iussit.","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"praeda","latin":"praeda, -ae","headword":"praeda","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"booty; prey; plunder","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hinc portum repetīvit et praedam omnibus sociīs partītus est.","reading":"LĪTUS ĀFRICAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"latin":"Victor exercitus in hīberna opulentā praedā Carthāginem Novam est dēductus.","reading":"HANNIBAL IMPERĀTOR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"praedium","latin":"praedium","headword":"praedium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"estate; country property","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius, quī nūper ex urbe in praedium suum Albānum venit, circā agrōs et vīneās suās ambulat.","reading":"VĪNEAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"praedives","latin":"praedīves, -itis","headword":"praedīves","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"very rich","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum, sīcut praedīxerat, fūsus fugātusque esset Rōmānus exercitus et duae cohortēs ab hoste obsidērentur, cum paucīs equitum turmīs in saltum reversus līberāvit eās et incolumēs redūxit.","reading":"BELLVM PVNICVM TERTIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"praedo","latin":"praedō","headword":"praedō","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"robber; pirate","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tempestās quidem dēsiit, sed multa alia perīcula nōbīs impendent: ut saxa quibus nāvēs franguntur, vorāginēs in quās nāvēs merguntur, praedōnēs maritimī quī nāvēs persequuntur, ut mercēs et pecūniam rapiant nautāsque occīdant.","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"latin":"Certē nāvis praedōnum est.","reading":"NĀVIS PRAEDŌNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"praeesse","latin":"praeesse","headword":"praeesse","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to be in charge of (+ dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Uter nostrum in culīnā praeest?","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"praemium","latin":"praemium","headword":"praemium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"reward","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Profectō magnum praemium dabō eī quī servum meum fugitīvum hūc retrāxerit.' Cornēlius: 'Quantum pecūniae dabis?","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"praepositio","latin":"praepositiō","headword":"praepositiō","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"preposition","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"praesidium","latin":"praesidium, -ī","headword":"praesidium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"garrison; guard","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi modicō praesidiō relictō, ēgressus cum omnibus cōpiīs partem mīlitum locīs occultīs sedēre in īnsidiīs iussit, ipse cum parte māiōre atque omnī equitātū profectus ad ipsās prope portās Fīdēnārum accēdēns hostēs ad pugnam excit.","reading":"FIDENATES ET VEIENTES VICTI","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"praeteritus","latin":"praeteritus","headword":"praeteritus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"past; gone by","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Marītus et uxor iam nōn dē praeteritō colloquuntur, sed dē tempore futūrō.","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"praetexta","latin":"praetexta, -ae","headword":"praetexta","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"purple-bordered toga","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is cum in opere et arāns esset inventus, sūdōre dētersō togam praetextam accēpit, et caesīs hostibus līberāvit exercitum.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"praetura","latin":"praetūra, -ae","headword":"praetūra","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"praetorship","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"prave","latin":"prāvē","headword":"prāvē","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"wrongly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus (parva vōce ad Titum): 'Magister dīcit mē prāvē scrībere: ergō litterās meās legere potest.'","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"pravus","latin":"prāvus","headword":"prāvus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"wrong; perverse; crooked","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"precatur","latin":"precātur","headword":"precātur","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"prays; begs","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pretiosus","latin":"pretiōsus","headword":"pretiōsus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"precious; valuable; expensive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōnnūllī in terrās aliēnās nāvigant, quod mercēs pretiōsās nautīs crēdere nōlunt, sīcut mercātor ille Rōmānus quī eādem nāve vehitur quā Mēdus et Lȳdia.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"latin":"Ante convīvium trīclīnium flōribus exōrnātur et vestis pretiōsa super lectōs sternitur.","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"pretium","latin":"pretium","headword":"pretium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"price; value","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Albīnus: \"Hic ānulus centum nummīs cōnstat.\" Mēdus: \"Quid?\" Albīnus: \"Pretium huius ānulī est centum sēstertiī.\" Mēdus: \"Centum sēstertiī?","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"Ipse Gāius Iūlius Caesar, cum adulēscēns ex Italiā Rhodum nāvigāret, ā praedōnibus captus est nec prius līberātus quam ingēns pretium solvit.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"primores","latin":"prīmōrēs, -um","headword":"prīmōrēs","letter":"p","pos":"noun m. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"leading men; chiefs","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum īnstrūctae aciēs cōnstitissent, priusquam signum pugnandī darētur, prōcessit Latīnus inter prīmōrēs ducemque advenārum ēvocāvit ad colloquium.","reading":"TRŌIĀNĪ ET LATĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"primum","latin":"prīmum","headword":"prīmum","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"first","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus prīmum manus lavat, deinde faciem.","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"primus","latin":"prīmus","headword":"prīmus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"first","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"principium","latin":"prīncipium","headword":"prīncipium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"beginning","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce principium carminis quod scripsit ad amicam secum in circo sedentem:","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"probus","latin":"probus","headword":"probus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"good; honest; well-behaved","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus puer probus nōn est; Mārcus est puer improbus!'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Exclāmat magister: 'Ō discipulōs improbōs ...!' Sextus: 'Num ego discipulus improbus sum?' Magister: 'Immō tū probus es discipulus, Sexte, at Mārcus et Quīntus et Titus improbī sunt!'","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"procella","latin":"procella, -ae","headword":"procella","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"storm; squall","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Utinam ego quoque in campīs Īliacīs animam prō patriā effūdissem!' Dum tālia verba iactat, rapida procella vēla scindit fluctūsque ad caelum tollit.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"procerus","latin":"prōcērus, -a, -um","headword":"prōcērus","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"tall; long","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Erat eō tempore in nōbīs summa grācilitās et īnfirmitās corporis, prōcērum et tenue collum; quī habitus et quae fīgūra nōn procul abesse putātur ā vītae perīculō, sī accēdit labor et laterum magna contentiō.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"procreare","latin":"prōcreāre","headword":"prōcreāre","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to beget; bring forth","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is Aenēam Silvium prōcreat; is deinde Latīnum Silvium.","reading":"ALBA CONDITA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"procul","latin":"procul","headword":"procul","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"far; far off; at a distance","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Brundisium nōn est prope Rōmam, sed procul ab Rōmā: via Appia longa est.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Ovis, quae iam procul ā pāstōre cēterisque ovibus abest, neque caelum neque sōlem suprā sē videt.","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"prodest","latin":"prōdest","headword":"prōdest","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is useful to; does good to","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Neque enim vīneīs magis prōdest quam sōl et calor, nec iīs magis nocet quam imber et frīgus.” Iūlius: “Calor sōlis nōn ipse per sē efficit ut vīnum bonum sit.","reading":"PĀSTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"prodigium","latin":"prōdigium, -ī","headword":"prōdigium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"portent; wonder","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tālia exclāmāns omnem domum gemitū complēbat — cum subitō mīrābile prōdigium vīsum est: namque inter manūs maestōrum parentum lūmen in summō culminī appāruit, neque flamma puerō nocēbat!","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"proditio","latin":"prōditiō, -ōnis","headword":"prōditiō","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"betrayal; treason","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Igitur, prius in bellō pācem, sīc in pāce bellum quaerēns, quia suae cīvitātī vīrēs dēesse cernēbat, ad bellum palam gerendum aliōs concitat populōs, ipse clam prōditiōnem parat.","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"proelium","latin":"proelium, -ī","headword":"proelium","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"battle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ante proelium dux exercitiīs mīlitēs suōs hortātur ut fortiter pugnent.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"latin":"Prīnceps in proelium ībat, ultimus proeliō excēdēbat.","reading":"HANNIBAL IMPERĀTOR","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"proficisci","latin":"proficīscī","headword":"proficīscī","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to set out; depart","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inter eōs hominēs quī nāvēs cōnscendunt est Mēdus, quī ex Italiā proficīscitur cum amīcā suā Lȳdia.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"proficiscitur","latin":"proficīscitur","headword":"proficīscitur","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sets out; departs","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ariadna igitur, antequam Thēseus labyrinthum intrāvit, ad eum accessit et sīc loquī coepit: 'Contrā Mīnōtaurum sōlus proficīscī nōn potes.","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"profugus","latin":"profugus, -a, -um","headword":"profugus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"fugitive; exiled","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eō tempore Euander, Mercuriī et Carmentis fīlius, profugus ex Arcadiā, regiōne Peloponnēsī mediā, in Italiam vēnit cum parvā manū Graecōrum; cui Faunus, rēx benignus, montem, quem ille posteā Palātium appellāvit, et arva colenda dedit.","reading":"ABORĪGINĒS ET RĒGĒS LATIĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"proles","latin":"prōlēs, -is","headword":"prōlēs","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"offspring; descendants","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"promittit","latin":"prōmittit","headword":"prōmittit","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"promises","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hoc vōbīs prōmittō, pater et māter!","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"promulgare","latin":"prōmulgāre","headword":"prōmulgāre","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to publish (a bill); propose","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Prōmulgāvit et aliam lēgem agrāriam, quā sibi lātius agrum patefaceret: 'ut iīdem triumvirī iūdicārent quā pūblicus ager, quā prīvātus esset.'","reading":"LĒGĒS AGRĀRIAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"pronomen","latin":"prōnōmen","headword":"prōnōmen","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pronoun","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"prope","latin":"prope","headword":"prope","letter":"p","pos":"preposition; adverb","posGroup":"preposition","english":"near; close to; near (with acc.); close by","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ōstia est prope Rōmam.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"In viā prope tabernam Albīnī vir et fēmina ambulant.","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"propinquus","latin":"propinquus","headword":"propinquus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"near; neighbouring","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra: \"Tum factum est id quod necesse erat accidere: ignis sōlis propinquī cēram, quā pennae iūnctae et fīxae erant, mollīvit et pennās ussit.","reading":"ĪCARVS IN MARE CADIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"proprius","latin":"proprius","headword":"proprius","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"proper; one’s own","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Nōmen quid est?' Discipulus: 'Pars ōrātiōnis cum cāsū, corpus aut rem propriē significāns; aut enim ūnīus nōmen est et proprium dīcitur, aut multōrum et appellātīvum.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"prora","latin":"prōra, -ae","headword":"prōra","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"prow (of a ship)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Rōstra\" nōmen est huius locī, quia rōstrīs nāvium captārum ōrnātur (\"rōstrum\" enim vocantur eae hastae ferreae quae ē prōrā nāvis longae eminent velut rōstrum avis).","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"proscribere","latin":"prōscrībere","headword":"prōscrībere","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to proscribe; outlaw","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam dum Sulla Achāiā atque Asiā Mithridāten vincit, Marius, quī fugātus erat, et Cornēlius Cinna, ūnus ex cōnsulibus, bellum in Ītaliā reparāvērunt, et ingressī urbem Rōmam nōbilissimōs ē senātū et cōnsulārēs virōs interfēcērunt, multōs prōscrīpsērunt, ipsīus Sullae domō ēversā fīliōs et uxōrem ad fugam compulērunt.","reading":"BELLVM CĪVĪLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"prosequi","latin":"prōsequī","headword":"prōsequī","letter":"p","pos":"verb (dep.)","posGroup":"verb","english":"to honour; praise; to escort","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"protinus","latin":"prōtinus","headword":"prōtinus","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"at once; immediately","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tālibus verbīs nauta mercātōrem maestum cōnsōlārī cōnātur, sed frūstrā, nam ille prōtinus \"Nōlī mē monēre\" inquit, \"quī ipse imperāvistī ut mercēs meae iacērentur!\"","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"protrahere","latin":"prōtrahere","headword":"prōtrahere","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to draw out; prolong","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tertiō quoque eī et quārtō dēlātus est cōnsulātus, quia bellum Cimbricum prōtrahēbātur.","reading":"BELLVM CIMBRICVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"provehi","latin":"prōvehī","headword":"prōvehī","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to sail forward; be carried on","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"provincia","latin":"prōvincia","headword":"prōvincia","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"province","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hispānia et Syria et Aegyptus prōvinciae Rōmānae sunt.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Germānia est magna terra nōn procul ā Galliā; Galliā autem prōvincia Rōmāna est, ut Hispānia, Syria, Aegyptus.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"provocatio","latin":"prōvocātiō, -ōnis","headword":"prōvocātiō","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"appeal to the people","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum Horātius \"Ad populum prōvocō\" inquit.","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"prudens","latin":"prūdēns","headword":"prūdēns","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"prudent; wise","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Discipulus quī nec stultus nec piger est, sed prūdēns atque industrius, multās rēs ā magistrō discere potest.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"prudenter","latin":"prūdenter","headword":"prūdenter","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"wisely; sensibly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius frontem contrahit et 'Agricola' inquit 'ipse nōn sum, sed multīs agricolīs praesum ac dīligenter cūrō ut colōnī agrōs meōs bene cōlant.' Orontēs, quī vīta rūstica nōn fruitur, 'Prūdenter facis' inquit 'quod agrōs ipse nōn colis.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"prudentia","latin":"prūdentia, -ae","headword":"prūdentia","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"practical wisdom; good sense; foresight","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum 'dē aliīs rēbus assentīre sē veteribus Gabīnīs' dīceret, identidem bellī auctor esse et in eō sibi praecipuam prūdentiam assūmere 'quod utrīusque populī vīrēs nōvisset scīretque invīsam profectō superbiam rēgiam cīvibus esse.' Ita cum sēnsim ad rebellandum prīmōrēs Gabīnōrum incitāret et ipse cum prōmptissimīs iuvenum praedātum īret, dictīs factīsque omnibus ad fallendum aptīs, ad ultimum dux bellī legitur.","reading":"GABIĪ DOLŌ CAPTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"},{"latin":"Sī vērum est — quod nēmō dubitat — ut populus Rōmānus omnēs gentēs virtūte superārit, nōn est īnfitiandum Hannibalem tantō praestitisse cēterōs imperātōrēs prūdentiā, quantō populus Rōmānus antecēdat fortitūdine cūnctās nātiōnēs.","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"pruina","latin":"pruīna, -ae","headword":"pruīna","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hoar-frost","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cernis autem eandem terram quasi quibusdam redimītam et circumdatam cingulīs, ē quibus duōs maximē inter sē dīversōs et caelī verticibus ipsīs ex utrāque parte subnīxōs obriguisse pruīnā vidēs, medium autem illum et maximum sōlis ārdōre torrērī.","reading":"ANGUSTIAE TERRĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"publicanus","latin":"pūblicānus, -ī","headword":"pūblicānus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tax-farmer; publican","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vērum tamen illīs imperātōribus laus est tribuenda, quod ēgērunt, venia danda, quod relīquērunt, proptereā quod ab eō bellō Sullam in Italiam rēs pūblica, Mūrēnam Sulla revocāvit.","reading":"DĒ GENERE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"pudens","latin":"pudēns, -entis","headword":"pudēns","letter":"p","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"modest; chaste","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pudicitia","latin":"pudīcitia, -ae","headword":"pudīcitia","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"modesty; chastity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quō terrōre cum vīcisset obstinātam pudīcitiam, libīdō victrīx abiit.","reading":"LŪCRĒTIA VIOLĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"pudor","latin":"pudor","headword":"pudor","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shame","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōnne tē pudet hoc fēcisse?","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"puella","latin":"puella","headword":"puella","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"girl","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlia est puella Rōmāna.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"puer","latin":"puer","headword":"puer","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"boy","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus est puer Rōmānus.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"pueritia","latin":"pueritia, -ae","headword":"pueritia","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"childhood","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tantum tamen opēs Latīnōrum crēverant — maximē victīs Etrūscīs — ut ne morte quidem Aenēae nec deinde inter rēgnum muliebre et Ascaniī pueritiam aut Etrūscī aut ūllī aliī fīnitimī arma movēre ausī sint.","reading":"ALBA CONDITA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"puerulus","latin":"puerulus, -ī","headword":"puerulus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"little boy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Pater meus' inquit 'Hamilcar, puerulō mē, utpote nōn amplius novem annōs nātō, in Hispāniam imperātor proficīscēns Carthāgine Iovī Optimō Maximō hostiās immolāvit.","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"pugna","latin":"pugna","headword":"pugna","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fight; battle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sextus, quī maior est quam cēterī discipulī, cum Mārcō et Titō pugnāvit et ab iīs pulsātus est.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"latin":"Tabulās mūtāvī inter pugnam.'","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"pugnat","latin":"pugnat","headword":"pugnat","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"fights; does battle","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eques est mīles quī ex equō pugnat; quī pedibus pugnat pedēs est.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Mārcus: 'Certē malus puer fuī, sed posthāc bonus puer futūrus sum: semper vōbīs paritūrus sum, numquam pugnātūrus sum in viā neque umquam in lūdō dormītūrus sum.","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"pugnator","latin":"pugnātor, -ōris","headword":"pugnātor","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fighter; soldier","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In Siciliā contrā eōs pugnātum est, et Ap.","reading":"BELLVM PŪNICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"pugno","latin":"pugnō","headword":"pugnō","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to fight","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ante proelium dux exercitiīs mīlitēs suōs hortātur ut fortiter pugnent.","reading":"EXERCITVS RŌMĀNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"pugnus","latin":"pugnus","headword":"pugnus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fist","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pulcher","latin":"pulcher","headword":"pulcher","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"beautiful; handsome; lovely; fine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hortus Iūliī pulcher est, quia in eō sunt multae et pulchrae rosae līliaque.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Equus quī Cornēlium vehit pulcher est.","reading":"MĒDVS ET CORNĒLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"pulchre","latin":"pulchrē","headword":"pulchrē","letter":"p","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"finely; beautifully","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister suam cuique discipulō tabulam reddit, prīmum Sextō, tum Titō, postrēmō Mārcō, atque 'Pulchre et rēctē scrībis, Sexte,' inquit, 'Facile est tālēs litterās legere.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"pullus","latin":"pullus","headword":"pullus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"chick","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pulmo","latin":"pulmō","headword":"pulmō","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lung","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In pectore cor et pulmōnēs sunt.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"pulsare","latin":"pulsāre","headword":"pulsāre","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to knock; strike","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pulsat","latin":"pulsat","headword":"pulsat","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"hits; strikes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus Iūliam pulsat.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Sanguis eī dē nāsō fluit, quod Mārcus ā Sextō pulsātus est.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"pulsus","latin":"pulsus, -ūs","headword":"pulsus","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"push; impulse","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"pulvis","latin":"pulvis, -eris","headword":"pulvis","letter":"p","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dust","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ut vērō iam fragor tēctōrum quae dīruēbantur in ultimīs urbis partibus audiēbātur, pulvisque velut nūbe omnia implēverat, Albānī tēcta in quibus nātus quisque ēducātusque erat relinquentēs exiērunt.","reading":"ALBA DIRVTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"punctum","latin":"pūnctum, -ī","headword":"pūnctum","letter":"p","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"point; dot","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iam ipsa terra ita mihi parva vīsa est ut mē imperiī nostrī, quō quasi pūnctum eius attingimus, paenitēret.","reading":"MORS ET VĪTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"punire","latin":"pūnīre","headword":"pūnīre","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to punish","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nē servō quidem iniūriam facere oportet, sed necesse est servōs īnfīdōs aut fugitīvōs sevērē pūnīre; nec enim quidquam nisi poena sevēra eius generis servōs ā maleficiīs dēterrēre atque in officiō tenēre potest.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"punit","latin":"pūnit","headword":"pūnit","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"punishes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"puppis","latin":"puppis","headword":"puppis","letter":"p","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stern (of a ship)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pars nāvis posterior puppis dīcitur.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"purus","latin":"pūrus","headword":"pūrus","letter":"p","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"clean","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"putat","latin":"putat","headword":"putat","letter":"p","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"thinks; supposes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed Syra eum mortuum esse putat, quod eum spīrāre nōn audit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"quadriennium","latin":"quadriennium, -ī","headword":"quadriennium","letter":"q","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"period of four years","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam post aliquantum nūllōs placuit fierī, et quadriennium in urbe ita flūxit ut potestātēs ibi maiōrēs nōn essent.","reading":"POST VRBEM CAPTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"},{"latin":"Quadrienniō cum gravī tamen calamitāte hoc bellum tractum est.","reading":"BELLVM SOCIĀLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"quadrigae","latin":"quadrīgae, -ārum","headword":"quadrīgae","letter":"q","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"team of four horses","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Duābus admōtīs quadrīgīs, in currūs eārum ligat Mettium.","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"quae","latin":"quae","headword":"quae","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"who; which (f.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quae est puella quae plōrat?","reading":"SCAENA TERTIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"quae?","latin":"quae?","headword":"quae?","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"who? (f. sg.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quae est māter Mārcī?","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"quaerit","latin":"quaerit","headword":"quaerit","letter":"q","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"seeks; looks for","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lupus in silvā cibum quaerit, dum pāstor et canis ovem nigram quaerunt.","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"quaestura","latin":"quaestūra, -ae","headword":"quaestūra","letter":"q","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"quaestorship","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ūnum igitur annum, cum redissēmus ex Asiā, causās nōbilēs ēgimus, cum quaestūram nōs, cōnsulātum Cotta, aedīlitātem peteret Hortēnsius.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"quaestus","latin":"quaestus, -ūs","headword":"quaestus","letter":"q","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"gain; profit","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quis enim umquam aut obeundī negōtiī aut cōnsequendī quaestūs studiō tam brevī tempore tot loca adīre, tantōs cursūs cōnficere potuit, quam celeriter Cn.","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"quam","latin":"quam","headword":"quam","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"whom; which (f. acc.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puella quam Mārcus pulsat est Iūlia.","reading":"SCAENA TERTIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"quamquam","latin":"quamquam","headword":"quamquam","letter":"q","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"although","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mīnōs, quamquam celeriter nāvigāvit, nōn tam celer fuit quam Thēsēus neque eum cōnsequī potuit.","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"quantus","latin":"quantus","headword":"quantus","letter":"q","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"how great; how big","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quantum est pretium illīus ānulī?\" Mēdus ānulum post Albīnum digitō mōnstrat.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"quartus","latin":"quārtus","headword":"quārtus","letter":"q","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"fourth","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ānulus satis magnus est et ad digitum convenit, nam digitus quārtus nōn tantus est quantus digitus medius.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"quattuor","latin":"quattuor","headword":"quattuor","letter":"q","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"four","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"In oppidō Tusculō est sine Aemiliā, sed cum servīs quattuor.","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"-que","latin":"-que","headword":"-que","letter":"q","pos":"enclitic","posGroup":"other","english":"and (attached to a word)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"quem","latin":"quem","headword":"quem","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"whom; which (m. acc.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puer quem Aemilia verberat est Mārcus.","reading":"SCAENA TERTIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"querella","latin":"querella, -ae","headword":"querella","letter":"q","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"complaint; reproach","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēsine querellīs tuīs et mē et tē incendere!","reading":"QUERELLA DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"queritur","latin":"queritur","headword":"queritur","letter":"q","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"complains; laments","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mercātor ad gubernātōrem accēdēns multīs cum lacrimīs queritur: \"Heu, mē miserum!","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"qui","latin":"quī","headword":"quī","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"who; which (m.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Puer quī parvam puellam pulsat improbus est!'","reading":"SCAENA TERTIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"qui?","latin":"quī?","headword":"quī?","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"who? (m. pl.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus quoque puer Rōmānus est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"qui/quae/quod","latin":"quī/quae/quod","headword":"quī/quae/quod","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"who; which","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"quia","latin":"quia","headword":"quia","letter":"q","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"because","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus respondet: 'Iūlia plōrat, quia Mārcus eam pulsat.'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Mēdus discēdit, quia is pecūniam dominī in sacculō suō habet!","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"quid?","latin":"quid?","headword":"quid?","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"what?","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quid est Crēta?","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Quī tabernam habet tabernārius est.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"quies","latin":"quiēs, -ētis","headword":"quiēs","letter":"q","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rest; quiet","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"quietus","latin":"quiētus","headword":"quiētus","letter":"q","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"quiet; still","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus quiētus in lectō suō cubat; is bene dormit.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"quinque","latin":"quīnque","headword":"quīnque","letter":"q","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"five","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Quīntus: \"Carpe rosās, Iūlia!\" Iūlia rosās carpit et cum quīnque rosīs ex hortō venit.","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"quinquennium","latin":"quīnquennium, -ī","headword":"quīnquennium","letter":"q","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"period of five years","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ibi cum multa dē administrandō imperiō dissererent, Iugurtha inter aliās rēs iacit 'oportere quīnquenniī cōnsulta et dēcrēta omnia rescindī, nam per eōs annōs Micipsam parum animō valuisse.' Tum 'idem' Hiempsal 'placēre sibi' respondit, 'nam ipsum illum tribus proximīs annīs adoptātiōne in rēgnum pervēnisse!' Quod verbum in pectus Iugurthae altius quam quisquam rātus erat dēscendit.","reading":"MORS HIEMPSALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"quis?","latin":"quis?","headword":"quis?","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"who? (m. sg.); who?","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus quoque puer Rōmānus est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Quī tabernam habet tabernārius est.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"quod","latin":"quod","headword":"quod","letter":"q","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"because","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hominēs ambulāre possunt, quod pedēs habent, neque volāre possunt, quod ālās nōn habent.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Magister interrogat: 'Cūr tū sōlus es, Sexte?' 'Ego sōlus sum, quod cēterī discipulī omnēs absunt,' respondet Sextus.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"quoque","latin":"quoque","headword":"quoque","letter":"q","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"also; too","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hispānia quoque in Eurōpā est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"quot?","latin":"quot?","headword":"quot?","letter":"q","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"how many?","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus quoque puer Rōmānus est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Quod ōrnāmentum?","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"quotannis","latin":"quotannīs","headword":"quotannīs","letter":"q","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"every year; yearly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque complūrēs adulēscentēs virginēsque quotannīs Athēnīs in Crētam mittēbantur, quī omnēs in labyrinthō ā mōnstrō illō saevō vorābantur.","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"rabies","latin":"rabiēs, -ēī","headword":"rabiēs","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fury; rage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"radius","latin":"radius, -ī","headword":"radius","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ray; spoke","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"radix","latin":"rādīx, -īcis","headword":"rādīx","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"root; foot (of a mountain)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ramus","latin":"rāmus","headword":"rāmus","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"branch","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rāmus quī nīdum sustinet nōn crassus, sed tenuis est.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"raro","latin":"rārō","headword":"rārō","letter":"r","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"rarely","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ex eō tempore rārō fit ut nāvis praedōnum in marī Internō appāreat, nam classēs Rōmānae, quae cūncta maria percurrunt, nāvēs mercātōriās atque ōram maritimam dīligenter tuentur.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"ratio","latin":"ratiō","headword":"ratiō","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"reason; account; explanation","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ovidius poeta, qui ingenium mulierum tam bene noverat quam ipsae mulieres, rationem reddit hoc versu: 'Spectatum veniunt, veniunt spectentur ut ipsae!'\"","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"recidere","latin":"recīdere","headword":"recīdere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to cut back; remove","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"recitare","latin":"recitāre","headword":"recitāre","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to recite","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus \"sē bonum discipulum fuisse\" dīxit, etsī in lūdō nec magistrum recitantem audīverat.","reading":"SYRA NĀRRAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"recitat","latin":"recitat","headword":"recitat","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"recites; reads aloud","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Item librum suum aperit magister ac recitāre incipit.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"recte","latin":"rēctē","headword":"rēctē","letter":"r","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"rightly; correctly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sextus ūnus ex tribus puerīs rēctē scrībit: HOMŌ OCVLŌS ET NASVM HABET.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"rector","latin":"rēctor, -ōris","headword":"rēctor","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ruler; governor","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Sit huic oppositus alter, bonus et sapiēns et perītus ūtilitātis dignitātisque cīvīlis, quasi tūtor et prōcūrātor reī pūblicae: sīc enim appelletur quīcumque erit rēctor et gubernātor cīvitātis.","reading":"DĒ VETERE RĒ PŪBLICĀ RŌMĀNĀ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"rectus","latin":"rēctus","headword":"rēctus","letter":"r","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"right; correct; straight","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"recumbere","latin":"recumbere","headword":"recumbere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to lie back; recline","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum puer aegrōtus in lectō recumbit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"recusare","latin":"recūsāre","headword":"recūsāre","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to refuse","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ubi iam ad antīquam domum patriam pervēnit, Anchīsēs pater, quem prīmum in altōs montēs portāre volēbat, ex patriā captā fugere recūsāvit.","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"reddere","latin":"reddere","headword":"reddere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to give back; return","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"reddit","latin":"reddit","headword":"reddit","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"gives back; returns","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus īrātus Titum pulsāre incipit, sed magister 'Dēsine, Mārce!' inquit, 'Titus tibi mālum dare nōn potest, at ego tibi mālum dare possum, nisi hic et nunc Titō librum reddis!' Mārcus Titō librum reddit.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"redimere","latin":"redimere","headword":"redimere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to ransom; redeem","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus: \"Ergō nūlla spēs est mihi, quī nec ipse pecūniam habeō nec amīcum tam pecūniōsum, ut mē ē servitūte redimere possit aut velit.\"","reading":"IN MARĪ TVSCŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"redit","latin":"redit","headword":"redit","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"returns; goes back","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus ad sellam suam redit, neque cōnsīdit, sed tacitus ante sellam stat. 'Audīsne, Mārce?","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"latin":"Marcō in cubiculum ductō atque inclūsō, Dāvus redit et 'Mārcus' inquit 'inclūsus est.","reading":"RESPŌNSVM IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"reficere","latin":"reficere","headword":"reficere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to rebuild; restore","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"regina","latin":"rēgīna, -ae","headword":"rēgīna","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"queen","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At ego, deōrum rēgīna Iovisque et soror et coniūnx, ūnā cum gente tot annōs bellum gerō!' Tālia animō incēnsō sēcum volvēns dea in Aeoliam, nimbōrum patriam, vēnit.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"regnum","latin":"rēgnum, -ī","headword":"rēgnum","letter":"r","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"kingdom; kingship","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Faunō mortuō, Latīnus, fīlius eius, rēgnum accēpit.","reading":"ABORĪGINĒS ET RĒGĒS LATIĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"regulus","latin":"rēgulus, -ī","headword":"rēgulus","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"petty king; prince","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"relaxare","latin":"relaxāre","headword":"relaxāre","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to relax; relieve","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tē autem permagnum est nancīscī ōtiōsum, hōc praesertim mōtū reī pūblicae.' Tum Scīpiō: 'Atquī nactus es, sed mēhercule ōtiōsiōrem operā quam animō.' Et ille: 'At tū vērō animum quoque relaxāre oportet.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"relinquere","latin":"relinquere","headword":"relinquere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to leave behind; leave (behind)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lȳdia collēs in quibus Rōmā sita est procul cernit et 'Valē, Rōma!' inquit, 'Nōn sine lacrimīs tē relinquō, nam tū altera patria es mihi.' Lȳdia vix lacrimās tenēre potest.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Certē mulierēs rārius ā līberīs suīs discēdunt ...\" Aemilia: \"Multae mātrēs īnfantēs suōs apud nūtrīcēs relinquunt, ego vērō manēbō apud īnfantem meum: numquam ab eō discēdam!","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"relinquit","latin":"relinquit","headword":"relinquit","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"leaves (behind); leaves behind; abandons","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ovis nigra ovēs albās relinquit et rīvum petit; aquam bibit ē rīvō, et in silvam intrat!","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Syra, postquam facta Mārcī nārrāvit, abīre vult, sed Quīntus: 'Nōlī mē relinquere!","reading":"TABVLĀ POSTVLĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"remigare","latin":"rēmigāre","headword":"rēmigāre","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to row","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Etsī nautae omnibus vīribus rēmigant, tamen illa nāvis, ventō secundō adiuvante, magis magisque appropinquat.","reading":"IN MARĪ TVSCŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"remissio","latin":"remissiō, -ōnis","headword":"remissiō","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"relaxation; easing","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eōque magis hoc eōs quibus eram cārus commovēbat, quod omnia sine remissiōne, sine varietāte, vī summā vōcis et tōtīus corporis contentiōne dīcēbam.'","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"remittit","latin":"remittit","headword":"remittit","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sends back","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Initiō Aemilia epistulās Iūliī legēbat nec dōna eius accipiēbat, sed omnia ad eum remittēbat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"remus","latin":"rēmus","headword":"rēmus","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"oar","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"reperire","latin":"reperīre","headword":"reperīre","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to find; discover","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornēlius: 'Etiam sī adhūc Rōmae latet, difficile erit servum fugitīvum in tantā urbe reperīre.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"reperit","latin":"reperit","headword":"reperit","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"finds","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Age! quaere ovem, canis, et reperi eam!' Canis ovem quaerit et vestīgia eius in terrā reperit, neque ovem ipsam reperit.","reading":"LPVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"reportare","latin":"reportāre","headword":"reportāre","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to carry back; win","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tria et trīgintā Cimbrīs signa sublāta sunt; ex hīs exercitus Mariī duo reportāvit, Catulī exercitus ūnum et trīgintā.","reading":"BELLVM CIMBRICVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"reprehendit","latin":"reprehendit","headword":"reprehendit","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"rebukes; scolds","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Foedē scrībitis, pigrī discipulī!' Magister Titum et Mārcum sevērē reprehendit.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"reprehendo","latin":"reprehendō","headword":"reprehendō","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"blame; rebuke","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam stultē et prāvē respondēs!' Magister Mārcum nōn laudat, sed reprehendit.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"resistere","latin":"resistere","headword":"resistere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to resist (+ dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is sōlus nōs tuērī potest.\" Gubernātor multīs verbīs Mēdō dissuādēre cōnātur nē gladium ēducat neu praedōnibus vī et armīs resistat.","reading":"IN MARĪ TVSCŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"respondeo","latin":"respondeō","headword":"respondeō","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"answer; reply","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Omnēs puerī simul respondent, nēmō eōrum manum tollit.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"respondet","latin":"respondet","headword":"respondet","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"answers; replies","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus respondet: 'Iūlia tē vocat.'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"restinguere","latin":"restinguere","headword":"restinguere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to extinguish; quench","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Parentēs expavidī ignem aquā restinguere properant; at pater Anchīsēs laetus Iovem invocat, subitōque fragōre ā laevā gravis tonat, et simul stēlla dē caelō lāpsa multā cum lūce per tenebrās currit.","reading":"ANCHĪSĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"restis","latin":"restis, -is","headword":"restis","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rope; cord","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"reus","latin":"reus, -ī","headword":"reus","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"accused man; defendant","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fit reus Bomilcar.","reading":"IVGVRTHA RŌMAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"reverti","latin":"revertī","headword":"revertī","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"return; to return","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ō miserōs nautās, quī numquam domum revertentur!","reading":"DĒ SORŌRE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"latin":"Aemilia ātrium intrāns hospitēs salūtat et marītum tardum excūsat: 'Iūlius tardē ex agrīs revertit quod nimis diū ambulāvit.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"revertitur","latin":"revertitur","headword":"revertitur","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"returns; comes back; turns back","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce puer quī ē lūdō domum revertitur.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"latin":"Brevī hūc redībō neque sine tē, Ariadna, in patriam revertar.","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"rex","latin":"rēx","headword":"rēx","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"king","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra: 'Rēx Mīnōs, quī tunc Crētam regēbat, paucīs annīs ante urbem Athēnās bellō expugnāverat.","reading":"DĒ MĪNŌTAVRŌ ET LABYRINTHŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"ridet","latin":"rīdet","headword":"rīdet","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"laughs; smiles","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus rīdet: 'Hahahae!'","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Diodōrus: 'Quid rīdētis, Tite et Sexte?' Titus: 'Rīdēmus, quod Mārcō dolet ... ' Diodōrus: 'Tacēte!","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"rigat","latin":"rigat","headword":"rigat","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"waters; irrigates","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aegyptus enim terra fertilissima est, quia sōlum eius aqua Nīlī rigātur.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"ripa","latin":"rīpa, -ae","headword":"rīpa","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bank; shore","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Urbs Rōma in rīpā Tiberis flūminis sita est vīgintī mīlia passuum ā marī.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"ritus","latin":"rītus, -ūs","headword":"rītus","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rite; religious custom","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"rivus","latin":"rīvus","headword":"rīvus","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stream; brook","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"robur","latin":"rōbur, -oris","headword":"rōbur","letter":"r","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hard wood; oak","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum vērō cūnctī Trōiānī novō pavōre perturbantur, et \"Laocoontem poenās meritās Minervae dedisse\" dīcunt, \"quod hasta scelerāta sacrum rōbur laeserit.\" Conclāmant omnēs \"simulācrum equī in arcem Minervae dūcendum esse.\" Ergō parte mūrōrum dēstrūctā māchina illa hostibus armātīs plēna magnō labōre in urbem trahitur fūnibus, dum puerī puellaeque carmina sacra canunt et fūnem manū contingere gaudent.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"robustus","latin":"rōbustus, -a, -um","headword":"rōbustus","letter":"r","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"strong; sturdy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quem cum vidēret domesticīs opibus minus esse rōbustum, conciliābat cēterōs rēgēs, adiungēbat bellicōsās nātiōnēs.","reading":"APVD PRŪSIAM ET MORS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"rogatio","latin":"rogātiō, -ōnis","headword":"rogātiō","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bill; proposed law","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum Carbō tribūnus plēbis rogātiōnem tulisset 'ut eundem tribūnum plēbis quotiēns vellet creāre licēret', rogātiōnem eius P.","reading":"LĒGĒS AGRĀRIAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"rogus","latin":"rogus, -ī","headword":"rogus","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"funeral pyre","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"romanus","latin":"Rōmānus","headword":"Rōmānus","letter":"r","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"Roman","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tusculum nōn oppidum Graecum, sed oppidum Rōmānum est.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"rosa","latin":"rosa","headword":"rosa","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rose","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In hortīs sunt rosae et līlia.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Iūlia, quae sōla est illīc, rosam ante nāsum tenet.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"rostrum","latin":"rōstrum, -ī","headword":"rōstrum","letter":"r","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"beak (of a ship); Rōstra; speaker's platform","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Rōstra\" nōmen est huius locī, quia rōstrīs nāvium captārum ōrnātur (\"rōstrum\" enim vocantur eae hastae ferreae quae ē prōrā nāvis longae eminent velut rōstrum avis).","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"ruber","latin":"ruber","headword":"ruber","letter":"r","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"red","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Color sanguinis est ruber.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"rubet","latin":"rubet","headword":"rubet","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"blushes; is red","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus, quī paulō ante ob timōrem pallēbat, iam rubet propter pudōrem.","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"ruina","latin":"ruīna, -ae","headword":"ruīna","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ruin; fall","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"rumor","latin":"rūmor","headword":"rūmor","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rumour; report","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūr nōn servum aliquem Rōmam mittis?' Iūlius: 'Servī sunt malī nūntiī: saepe falsōs rūmōrēs nūntiant.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"rumpere","latin":"rumpere","headword":"rumpere","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to break; burst","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tlēpolemus: \"Num canis catēnam ferream rumpere potest?","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"rumpit","latin":"rumpit","headword":"rumpit","letter":"r","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"breaks open; bursts","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Signum rumpe!' Iūlius signum rumpit et epistulam aperit.","reading":"EPISTVLA ADVENIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"rupes","latin":"rūpēs, -is","headword":"rūpēs","letter":"r","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rock; cliff","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ruptor","latin":"ruptor, -ōris","headword":"ruptor","letter":"r","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"breaker (of a treaty)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mettius ille est ductor itineris huius, Mettius īdem huius auctor bellī, Mettius foederis Rōmānī Albānīque ruptor!\"","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"ruri","latin":"rūrī","headword":"rūrī","letter":"r","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"in the country","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In urbe semper in negōtiō est, sed rūrī in ōtiō cōgitat dē urbānīs.","reading":"VĪNEAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"rursus","latin":"rūrsus","headword":"rūrsus","letter":"r","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"again; back","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlium vocāte, ancillae!\" Syra: \"Sed dominus in oppidō est.\" Aemilia: \"Ō, iam rūrsus abest Iūlius!\" Dēlia: \"Age!","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"rus","latin":"rūs","headword":"rūs","letter":"r","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"countryside; ruri = in the country","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Neque labōrat dominus, sed quiēscit, cum in praediō suō rūs quiētum et amoenum eum dēlectat.","reading":"VĪNEAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"rusticus","latin":"rūsticus","headword":"rūsticus","letter":"r","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"rustic; boorish","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tū tam pulchra es quam Helena...' Aemilia: '...et tū tam rūsticus quam Paris, quī inter pāstōrēs ēducātus erat!","reading":"INTER PŌCVLA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"rutilus","latin":"rutilus, -a, -um","headword":"rutilus","letter":"r","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"reddish; glowing","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deinde est hominum generī prosperus et salūtāris ille fulgor quī dīcitur \"Iovis\"; tum rutilus horribilisque terrīs quem \"Martium\" dīcitis.'","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"sacculus","latin":"sacculus","headword":"sacculus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"little bag; purse","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sacculus Iūliī nōn parvus est.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"saccus","latin":"saccus","headword":"saccus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sack; bag","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Saccī quōs Syrus et Lēander portant magnī sunt, sed saccus quem Syrus portat nōn tam magnus est quam saccus Lēandrī.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Vidēte, puerī: hic saccus plēnus mālōrum est.'","reading":"REDITVS IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"sacra","latin":"sacra, -ōrum","headword":"sacra","letter":"s","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sacred things; rites","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aliī eum ut dōnum Minervae, deae Trōiānīs benignae, sacrātum intrā mūrōs dūcī et in arce locārī iubēbant, aliī dōnum Graecōrum suspectum in mare praecipitandum et flammīs ūrendum esse cēnsēbant, aliī interiōrem equī partem īnspicere volēbant.","reading":"EQVVS TRŌIĀNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"sacrarium","latin":"sacrārium, -ī","headword":"sacrārium","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shrine; sanctuary","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Librī trēs, in sacrārium conditī, 'Sibyllīnī' appellātī.","reading":"LIBRĪ SIBYLLĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"sacrificium","latin":"sacrificium, -ī","headword":"sacrificium","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sacrifice","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ad hoc templum imperātor victor post triumphum ascendit, ut Iovī Optimō Maximō sacrificium faciat, dum ducēs hostium, quī in triumphō ante currum imperātōris ductī sunt, ad supplicium trāduntur.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"saeculum","latin":"saeculum","headword":"saeculum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"century; age","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Saeculum est centum annī.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"saevitia","latin":"saevitia, -ae","headword":"saevitia","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cruelty; savagery","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam cum aliīs urbānīs operibus intentum sē esse simulāret, Sextus, fīlius eius quī minimus ex tribus erat, trānsfūgit ex compositō Gabiōs patris in sē saevitiam nōn tolerandam querēns: 'rēgem iam ab aliēnīs in suōs vertisse superbiam et līberīs quoque īnsidiās parāre, nē quem hērēdem regnī relinquat; sē quidem inter tēla et gladiōs patris ēlāpsum nihil usquam sibi tūtum nisi apud hostēs L.","reading":"GABIĪ DOLŌ CAPTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"saevus","latin":"saevus","headword":"saevus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"savage; fierce","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"sal","latin":"sāl","headword":"sāl","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"salt","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Optima quidem est carō, sed sale caret.' Orontēs cibum sale aspergere solet, ut sitim augeat! (Sāl est māteriā albā quae in marī et sub terrā invenītur.)","reading":"CĒNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"salinae","latin":"salīnae, -ārum","headword":"salīnae","letter":"s","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"salt-pans","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Usque ad mare imperium prōlātum est et in ōre Tiberis Ōstia urbs condita, salīnae circā factae.","reading":"BELLVM LATINVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"salus","latin":"salūs","headword":"salūs","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"safety; welfare","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"salutat","latin":"salūtat","headword":"salūtat","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"greets; hails","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Salūtā dominum!' Servus dominum salūtat: 'Salvē, domine!' Dominus servum salūtat: 'Salvē, serve!'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Iam Iūlius in vīllā est et ab Aemiliā līberīsque laetīs salūtātur.","reading":"MĒDVS ET CORNĒLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"salvus","latin":"salvus","headword":"salvus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"safe; unharmed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"sanat","latin":"sānat","headword":"sānat","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"heals; cures","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Medicus est vir quī hominēs aegrōs sānat, sed multī aegrī ā medicō sānārī nōn possunt.","reading":"SĀNVS ET AEGER","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"sanguinulentus","latin":"sanguinulentus, -a, -um","headword":"sanguinulentus","letter":"s","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"bloody","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīs aliīsque increpandō iuvenem īnstīgat, nec conquiēscere ipsa potest, sī — cum Tanaquil, peregrīna mulier, duo continua rēgna virō ac deinceps generō dedisset — ipsa, rēgiō sanguine orta, nec dare nec adimere rēgnum posset.","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"sanguis","latin":"sanguis","headword":"sanguis","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"blood","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In corde est sanguis, quī per vēnās ad cor fluit.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Mārcus est, sed difficile est eum cognōscere, nam sordidus est et sanguis dē nāsō eius fluit.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"sanus","latin":"sānus","headword":"sānus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"healthy; well","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homō quī ventrem malum habet cibum sūmere nōn potest, neque is sānus, sed aeger est.","reading":"SĀNVS ET AEGER","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"sapientia","latin":"sapientia, -ae","headword":"sapientia","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wisdom","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Cēterum ante hōs tē, Iugurtha, quī aetāte et sapientiā prior es, nē aliter quid ēveniat prōvidēre decet.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"satis","latin":"satis","headword":"satis","letter":"s","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"enough","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Albīnus: \"Sed nōnāgintā nōn satis est.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"saxum","latin":"saxum","headword":"saxum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rock","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"scaena","latin":"scaena","headword":"scaena","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"scene; stage","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"scalpellum","latin":"scalpellum","headword":"scalpellum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"small knife; scalpel","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fabia: \"Quisnam vulneravit filium tuum?\" Aemilia: \"Medicus bracchium eius scalpello suo acuto secuit!","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"sceptrum","latin":"sceptrum, -ī","headword":"sceptrum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sceptre","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc rex Aeolus in vastō antrō ventōs tempestātēsque in vinculīs tenet; ipse rēx in celsā arce sedet sceptrum tenēns.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"scientia","latin":"scientia, -ae","headword":"scientia","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"knowledge; skill","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ego enim sīc existimō, in summō imperātōre quattuor hās rēs inesse oportēre: scientiam reī mīlitāris, virtūtem, auctōritātem, fēlīcitātem.","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"scindere","latin":"scindere","headword":"scindere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to tear; split","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At certē vestem scindere potuit: pallium meum novum, quod nūper magnō pretiō ēmī, scissum esse ā cane tuō?\" Iānitor: \"Istud pallium nōn est magnī pretiī, neque id nūper ēmptum esse crēdō.","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"scindit","latin":"scindit","headword":"scindit","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"tears; rips","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius rīdēns 'Rēctē dīcis' inquit, 'Ego enim pecūniam solvere nōlō: ergō solvere nōn possum!' Hoc dīcēns Iūlius epistulam magistrī scindit.","reading":"RESPŌNSVM IŪLIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"scio","latin":"sciō","headword":"sciō","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"know","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sextus manum tollēns: 'Ego respōnsum sciō,' inquit.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"sciscitari","latin":"scīscitārī","headword":"scīscitārī","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to ask; inquire","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum ex suīs ūnum Rōmam ad patrem mittit scīscitātum 'quidnam sē facere vellet?' Huic nūntiō — quia, crēdō, dubiae fideī vidēbātur — nihil vōce respōnsum est.","reading":"GABIĪ DOLŌ CAPTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"scopulus","latin":"scopulus, -ī","headword":"scopulus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rock; crag","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Nīmīrum haec est illa Charybdis\" inquit Anchīsēs, \"Hōs scopulōs, haec saxa horrenda Helēnus memorābat.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"scortum","latin":"scortum, -ī","headword":"scortum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"prostitute","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"scribere","latin":"scrībere","headword":"scrībere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"write","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"scribit","latin":"scrībit","headword":"scrībit","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"writes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quisque discipulus in tabulā suā scrībit eās sententiās quās magister eī dictat.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"scutum","latin":"scūtum","headword":"scūtum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shield","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Mīles est vir quī scūtum et gladium et pīlum fert.","reading":"MĪLES ET ARMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"secernere","latin":"sēcernere","headword":"sēcernere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to separate; set apart","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lēgātī Rōmānī ab Achaeīs pulsī sunt Corinthī, missī ut eās cīvitātēs quae sub dīcione Philippī fuerant ab Achāicō conciliō sēcernerent.","reading":"BELLVM ACHAEVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"secundus","latin":"secundus","headword":"secundus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"second; favourable (of wind)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"A est littera prīma (I), B littera secunda (II), C littera tertia (III). Γ littera Graeca est.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Nautae nec marī turbidō nec marī tranquillō nāvigāre possunt; itaque in portū ventum secundum opperiuntur. (Ventus secundus est ventus quī ā tergō flat.) Ventō secundō nāvēs ē portū ēgrediuntur: vēla ventō implentur ac nāvēs plēnīs vēlīs per mare vehuntur.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"sed","latin":"sed","headword":"sed","letter":"s","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"but","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syria nōn est in Eurōpā, sed in Asiā.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"sedes","latin":"sēdēs, -is","headword":"sēdēs","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"seat; dwelling","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rūrsus mōtanda est sēdēs, nōn licet tibi in hāc terrā cōnsīdere.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"seditio","latin":"sēditiō, -ōnis","headword":"sēditiō","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sedition; civil strife","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dēmarātī Corinthiī fīlius erat, quī ob sēditiōnēs domō profugus, cum Tarquiniīs forte cōnsēdisset, uxōre ibi ducta duōs fīliōs genuit.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"sella","latin":"sella","headword":"sella","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"chair; seat","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister intrāns Sextum sōlum in sellā sedentem videt.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"semen","latin":"sēmen","headword":"sēmen","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"seed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Agricola sēmen manū spargit.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"senator","latin":"senātor, -ōris","headword":"senātor","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"senator","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Senātus cōnstat ex sescentīs senātōribus, cīvibus nōbilissimīs, quī ante Caesaris aetātem summam potestātem in rē pūblicā Rōmānā tenēbant.","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"senatus","latin":"senātus, -ūs","headword":"senātus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"senate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūxtā basilicam Aemiliam, in eā forī parte quae dīcitur Comitium, locāta est Cūria, id est aedificium quō senātus Rōmānus convenīre solet.","reading":"FORUM RŌMĀNUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"},{"latin":"Quī cum lēgātīs in senātum intrōductīs dē rē pūblicā rettulissent, placuissetque 'mittī lēgātōs in Hispāniam ad rēs sociōrum īnspiciendās, quibus sī vidērētur digna causa, et Hannibalī dēnūntiārent ut ā Saguntīnīs, sociīs populī Rōmānī, abstinēret' — hāc lēgātiōne dēcrētā necdum missā, omnium spē celerius 'Saguntum oppugnārī' allātum est.","reading":"SAGVNTVM OPPVGNĀTVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"senectus","latin":"senectūs, -ūtis","headword":"senectūs","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"old age","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum vērō in diēs īnfēstior Tulliī senectus, īnfēstius rēgnum coepit esse.","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"sententia","latin":"sententia","headword":"sententia","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sentence; thought","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum vocābula coniunguntur, sententiae fīunt.","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"sepelire","latin":"sepelīre","headword":"sepelīre","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to bury","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aenēās, postquam ossa patris in monte Eryce sepelīvit, ex Siciliā atque ā sepulcrō genitōris dīgressus est.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"septem","latin":"septem","headword":"septem","letter":"s","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"seven","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"septentriones","latin":"septentriōnēs","headword":"septentriōnēs","letter":"s","pos":"noun (m. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"north","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Partēs caelī sunt quattuor: oriēns et occidēns, merīdiēs et septentriōnēs.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"sepulcrum","latin":"sepulcrum, -ī","headword":"sepulcrum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tomb; grave","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aenēās, postquam ossa patris in monte Eryce sepelīvit, ex Siciliā atque ā sepulcrō genitōris dīgressus est.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"sequi","latin":"sequī","headword":"sequī","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to follow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lȳdia eum sequitur.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"sequitur","latin":"sequitur","headword":"sequitur","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"follows","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"serenus","latin":"serēnus","headword":"serēnus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"clear; calm","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hodiē caelum serēnum et ventus secundus est.","reading":"PROFECTIŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"serit","latin":"serit","headword":"serit","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sows","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deinde agrī arantur et novum frūmentum seritur.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"sermo","latin":"sermō","headword":"sermō","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"conversation; talk","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sermō eōrum est dē rēbus futūrīs.","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"},{"latin":"Nōn sōlum dē cibō et pōtiōne est sermō convīvārum.","reading":"SERMŌ CONVĪVĀRVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"serpens","latin":"serpēns, -entis","headword":"serpēns","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"snake","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Imperāvit quam plūrimās venēnātās serpentēs vīvās colligī eāsque in vāsa fictilia conicī.","reading":"APVD PRŪSIAM ET MORS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"servare","latin":"servāre","headword":"servāre","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to save; keep; preserve","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ille cūrāvit ut nōs ē tempestāte servārēmur nēve mergerēmur — vel potius nōs ipsī, quī mercēs ēiēcimus.","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"servat","latin":"servat","headword":"servat","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"saves; preserves","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Gubernātor: \"Iactūra mercium nāvis servāta est.\" Mercātor: \"Rēctē dīcis: meae mercēs ēiectae sunt, ut nāvis tua salva esset!\" Gubernātor: \"Mercēs iēcimus ut nōs omnēs salvī essēmus.","reading":"MERCĀTOR ET GVBERNĀTOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"servator","latin":"servātor, -ōris","headword":"servātor","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"saviour","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quōrum agmen imperātor secūtus — prōsequentibus cūnctīs 'servātōrem' 'līberātōrem'que acclāmantibus — eādem quā vēnerat viā Elatēam rediit.","reading":"TRIVMPHVS FLĀMINĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"servitium","latin":"servitium, -ī","headword":"servitium","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"slavery; subjection","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nec hīs nec illīs perīculum suum ob oculōs versātur, sed pūblicum imperium servitiumque.","reading":"TRIGEMINORVM PVGNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"servitus","latin":"servitūs","headword":"servitūs","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"slavery","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ōlim cūncta maria tam īnfēstā erant praedōnibus ut nēmō nāvigāret sine maximō perīculō mortis aut servitūtis.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"servus","latin":"servus","headword":"servus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"slave; servant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus fīlius Iūliī nōn est, Mēdus est servus Iūliī.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Mēdus: 'Servus tuus Mēdus hīc est.' Iūlius servum suum Mēdum videt, Dāvum nōn videt.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"sestertius","latin":"sēstertius","headword":"sēstertius","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sesterce (a Roman coin)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Albīnus: \"Hic ānulus centum nummīs cōnstat.\" Mēdus: \"Quid?\" Albīnus: \"Pretium huius ānulī est centum sēstertiī.\" Mēdus: \"Centum sēstertiī?","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"},{"latin":"Ut scītis, ūnus sēstertius est quattuor assēs et ūnus dēnārius quattuor sēstertiī.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"severus","latin":"sevērus","headword":"sevērus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"strict; severe; stern","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus magistrum metuit, Diodōrus enim magister sevērus est, quī discipulōs suōs virga verberat; eō modo magister sevērus discipulōs improbōs pūnīre solet.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"latin":"Item Aemilia vultum Iūliī sevērum intuētur.","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"sex","latin":"sex","headword":"sex","letter":"s","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"six","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In vocābulō 'īnsula' sex litterae et trēs syllabae sunt: syllaba prīma 'īn-', secunda '-su-', tertia '-la'.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"siccus","latin":"siccus","headword":"siccus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"dry","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"significat","latin":"significat","headword":"significat","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"means; signifies","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Nōmen quid est?' Discipulus: 'Pars ōrātiōnis cum cāsū, corpus aut rem propriē significāns; aut enim ūnīus nōmen est et proprium dīcitur, aut multōrum et appellātīvum.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"signum","latin":"signum","headword":"signum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"statue; sign; seal; standard","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Omnēs pulchritūdinem tuam laudant.' Tum vērō fōrmam eius spectāns: 'At minus gracilis es quam tunc: eō enim tempore gracilior erās quam hoc signum Veneris.'","reading":"AMOR IŪLIĪ ET AEMILIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"latin":"Dominus cēram aspiciēns signum magistrī cognōscit — est enim parva eius imāgō — et 'Missā est' inquit 'ā magistrō Diodōrō.","reading":"EPISTVLA ADVENIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"silva","latin":"silva","headword":"silva","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"forest; wood","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ovēs in campō herbam edunt, et aquam bibunt ē rīvō, quī inter campum et silvam est.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Barbarī perterritī, quī impetum equitātūs sustinēre nōn possunt, arma ad terram iaciunt atque in magnās silvās fugiunt.'","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"simulacrum","latin":"simulācrum, -ī","headword":"simulācrum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"image; statue","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Postrēmō Domitiānus templum Iovis Capitōlīnī incendīō cōnsūmptum refēcit atque tantīs dīvitiīs exōrnāvit ut nihil magnificentius fierī posset: aurō et gemmīs splendet tēctum, quod plūrimīs columnīs ē marmore pulcherrimō factīs sustinētur; intus in cellā, templō clausus post forēs aurō opertās, ingēns simulācrum Iovis in altā sēde sedentis positum est.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"simultas","latin":"simultās, -ātis","headword":"simultās","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"enmity; feud","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Suspecta fuit, tamquam eī venēnum dēdidisset Semprōnia uxor — hinc maximē quod soror esset Gracchōrum, cum quibus simultās Āfricānō fuerat.","reading":"LĒGĒS AGRĀRIAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"sine","latin":"sine","headword":"sine","letter":"s","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"without (+ abl.); without","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia sine virō suō Iūliō in vīllā est.","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Sine animā nēmō potest vīvere.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"singularis","latin":"singulāris","headword":"singulāris","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"singular","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Numerī nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Duo.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Singulāris, ut hic magister; plūrālis, ut hī magistrī.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"sitis","latin":"sitis","headword":"sitis","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"thirst","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homō sex diēs cibō carēre potest, nec tamen famē moritur.' Iūlius: 'Dubitō num ego tam diū famem ferre possim.' Cornēlius: 'Id nōn negō, sed multō molestior est sitis quam famēs.'","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"socialis","latin":"sociālis, -e","headword":"sociālis","letter":"s","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"of allies; social","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam cum Sulla cōnsul contrā Mithridāten gestūrus bellum, quī Asiam et Achāiam occupāverat, mitterētur, isque exercitum in Campaniā paulisper tenēret, ut bellī sociālis — dē quō dīximus — quod intrā Ītaliam gestum fuerat, reliquiae tollerentur, Marius affectāvit ut ipse ad bellum Mithridāticum mitterētur.","reading":"BELLVM MITHRIDĀTICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"sociare","latin":"sociāre","headword":"sociāre","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to unite; associate","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"societas","latin":"societās, -ātis","headword":"societās","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"alliance; partnership","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mezentius, quī iam inde ab initiō minimē laetus fuerat orīgine novae urbis, et tum opēs Latīnōrum nimium crēscere rēbātur, statim societātem cum Rutulīs iūnxit Latīnīsque bellum intulit.","reading":"TRŌIĀNĪ ET LATĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"socius","latin":"socius, -ī","headword":"socius","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"ally; comrade","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"sol","latin":"sōl","headword":"sōl","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sun","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sōl in caelō est suprā campum.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"latin":"Aestāte diēs longī sunt, sōl lūcet, āēr calidus est.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"solet","latin":"solet","headword":"solet","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is accustomed to; usually does","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus, quī ante mē surgere solet, adhūc dormit!","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"solitudo","latin":"sōlitūdō, -inis","headword":"sōlitūdō","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"solitude; deserted place","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Vāstae tum in hīs locīs sōlitūdinēs erant.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"solium","latin":"solium, -ī","headword":"solium","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"throne","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"solus","latin":"sōlus","headword":"sōlus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"alone; only","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius nōn sōlus, sed cum Aemiliā et cum magnā familiā in vīllā habitat.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Iūlius sōlus nōn est, nam quattuor servī apud eum sunt.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"solvere","latin":"solvere","headword":"solvere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to untie; loosen; to pay; to loosen","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tlēpolemus in līmine resistēns \"Retinē canem!\" inquit, \"Nōlī eum solvere!","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"latin":"Sōlī quī magnam pecūniam solvere potuerant servitūte līberābantur.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"solvit","latin":"solvit","headword":"solvit","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"pays","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Colōnus est agricola quī nōn suōs, sed aliēnōs agrōs prō absente dominō colit et mercēdem dominō solvit prō agrīs.","reading":"VĪNEAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"somnium","latin":"somnium, -ī","headword":"somnium","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dream","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"somnus","latin":"somnus","headword":"somnus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sleep","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Īnfāns multās hōrās dormit, nōn sōlum nocte sed etiam diē; nam longus somnus īnfantī tam necessārius est quam cibus.","reading":"ĪNFANTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"sordes","latin":"sordēs","headword":"sordēs","letter":"s","pos":"noun (f. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"dirt; filth (plural)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus Dāvum sequitur in cubiculum, ubi cruōrem et sordēs ē faciē, manibus, genibus lavat ac vestīmenta mūtat.","reading":"MARCVS Ā PATRE INTERROGĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"sordidus","latin":"sordidus","headword":"sordidus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"dirty; filthy","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Manūs tuae sordidae sunt.'","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"latin":"Mārcus est, sed difficile est eum cognōscere, nam sordidus est et sanguis dē nāsō eius fluit.","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"soror","latin":"soror (sororis)","headword":"soror","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sister","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mihi soror nōn est.\" Iūliō silentē, Aemilia: \"Nōnne gaudēbis, Iuliiola\" inquit, \"sī parvulam sorōrem habēbis?\" Iūlia: \"Sorōrem habēre nōlō!","reading":"DĒ SORŌRE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"sors","latin":"sors, sortis","headword":"sors","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"lot; fate; oracle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"spargit","latin":"spargit","headword":"spargit","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"scatters; sprinkles","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Agricola sēmen manū spargit.","reading":"IN AGRĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"spatium","latin":"spatium, -ī","headword":"spatium","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"space; distance","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Castra locant, fossā circumdant, haud plūs quīnque mīlia passuum ab urbe — nam hoc spatium interest inter Rōmam et locum quī \"fossā Cluiliā\" ab nōmine ducis per aliquot saecula appellātus est, quoad nōmen vetustāte abolēvit.","reading":"TVLLVS HOSTILIVS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"species","latin":"speciēs, -ēī","headword":"speciēs","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sight; appearance","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trōiānī hanc speciem ferre nōn poterant et cūnctī in medium hostium agmen multitūdine ruēbant.","reading":"MORS PRIAMĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"spectaculum","latin":"spectāculum, -ī","headword":"spectāculum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"show; spectacle","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Id Rōmānī iuvenēs aegrē passī sunt, et haud dubiē ad vim spectāre rēs coepit.","reading":"SABINAE RAPTAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"spectator","latin":"spectātor","headword":"spectātor","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"spectator; onlooker","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Modo in amphitheatro certamen magnificum spectavi: plus trecenti gladiatores certabant.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"speculum","latin":"speculum","headword":"speculum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"mirror","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlia speculum sūmit et ante oculōs tenet.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"spelunca","latin":"spēlunca, -ae","headword":"spēlunca","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cave","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dīdō et dux Trōiānus in eandem spēluncam dēveniunt, dūcente Iūnōne.","reading":"VENĀTIŌ ET FĀMA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"spernere","latin":"spernere","headword":"spernere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to despise; reject","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nusquam benignē lēgātiō audīta est: adeō aliae gentēs Rōmānōs spernēbant ac simul tantam in mediō crēscentem mōlem metuēbant.","reading":"SABINAE RAPTAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"spes","latin":"spēs, speī","headword":"spēs","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hope","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iam vērō ea spēs omnis periit, nam flūctibus mersae sunt mercēs in quibus omnem spem posuerat.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"},{"latin":"Utrimque in pugnam prōcursum est; hinc spēs, hinc dēspērātiō animōs irrītābat.","reading":"SAGVNTVM OPPVGNĀTVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"sphaera","latin":"sphaera, -ae","headword":"sphaera","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sphere; globe","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum deinde Philus et Scīpiō et Tubērō parumper dē rēbus caelestibus disputāvissent — velut dē certīs et ratīs astrōrum mōtibus, quōs Archimēdēs Syrācūsiānus in globō sīve sphaerā aēneā arte mīrābilī effectā dēclārāvisse dīcitur — Laelius, quī eius modī disputātiōnēs tamquam inūtilēs contemnēbat, 'alia quaedam maiōra quaerenda esse' dīxit.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"spirat","latin":"spīrat","headword":"spīrat","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"breathes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homō vīvit, dum spīrat.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Quīntus autem spīrat, ergō mortuus nōn est.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"splendor","latin":"splendor, -ōris","headword":"splendor","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"brightness; splendour","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"spolia","latin":"spolia, -ōrum","headword":"spolia","letter":"s","pos":"noun n. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"spoils; armour stripped from a foe; booty","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēgem in proeliō obtruncat et spoliat.","reading":"SPOLIA OPIMA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"spoliare","latin":"spoliāre","headword":"spoliāre","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to strip; despoil","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rēgem in proeliō obtruncat et spoliat.","reading":"SPOLIA OPIMA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":42,"roman":"XLII","title":"War and Peace","slug":"bellum-et-pax"}]},{"id":"spondeus","latin":"spondēus","headword":"spondēus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"spondee (– –)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"sponsus","latin":"spōnsus, -ī","headword":"spōnsus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"betrothed man; fiancé","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cui soror virgō, quae dēspōnsa ūnī ex Curiātiīs fuerat, obvia ante portam Capēnam fuit, cognitōque super umerōs frātris palūdāmentō spōnsī, quod ipsa cōnfēcerat, solvit crīnēs et flēbiliter nōmine spōnsum mortuum appellat.","reading":"AMOR IMMATVRVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"statim","latin":"statim","headword":"statim","letter":"s","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"immediately; at once","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic Titus ad lūdum advēnit et iānuam pulsat antequam intrat: discipulus nōn statim intrat, sed prīmum iānuam pulsat; tum lūdum intrat et magistrum salūtat: 'Salvē, magister!' Magister: 'Ō Tite!","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"stella","latin":"stēlla","headword":"stēlla","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"star","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nocte sōl nōn lūcet, sed lūna et stēllae lūcent.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"sterilis","latin":"sterilis, -e","headword":"sterilis","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"barren; unable to bear children","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Carvīlius Rūga prīmus Rōmae dē amīcōrum sententiā dīvortium cum uxōre fēcit, quod matrimōniō sterilis esset iūrāssetque apud cēnsōrēs 'uxōrem sē līberum quaerundōrum causā habēre'; eōdemque annō Cn.","reading":"PHILIPPVS ĀD LŪCĪLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"sternere","latin":"sternere","headword":"sternere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to spread; lay out","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"stilus","latin":"stilus","headword":"stilus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pen; stylus","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"stipes","latin":"stīpes, -itis","headword":"stīpes","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stake; rough trunk","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"stirps","latin":"stirps, -pis","headword":"stirps","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"stock; lineage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Brevī stirps quoque virīlis ex novō mātrimōniō fuit, cui 'Ascanium' parentēs nōmen dedērunt.","reading":"TRŌIĀNĪ ET LATĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"strages","latin":"strāgēs, -is","headword":"strāgēs","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"slaughter; heap of slain","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Alterum intāctum ferrō corpus et gemināta victōria ferōcem in certāmen tertium dabat; alter, fessum vulnere fessum cursū corpus trahēns vīctusque frātrum ante sē strāge, victōrī obicitur hostī.","reading":"TRIGEMINORVM PVGNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"stramentum","latin":"strāmentum, -ī","headword":"strāmentum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"straw; thatch","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Palātium prīmum mūnītum est, sed ea moenia quadrāta, quibus Rōmulus, prīmus rēx Rōmānōrum, Palātium mūnīvisse dīcitur, iam prīdem periērunt, neque ūlla casa restat ex illā urbe antīquissimā, quae ā fōrmā moenium \"Rōma quadrāta\" appellābātur, praeter \"casam Rōmulī\" strāmentō tēctam.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"strepitus","latin":"strepitus","headword":"strepitus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"noise; racket; uproar","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"At subitō silentium clāmōre et strepitū maximō rumpitur, nam Mārcus in cubiculō suō, quod iuxtā cubiculum Quīntī est, magnā vōce clāmat et forem manibus pedibusque percutit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"stulte","latin":"stultē","headword":"stultē","letter":"s","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"stupidly","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"stultus","latin":"stultus","headword":"stultus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"stupid; foolish","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī cerebrum parvum habet stultus est.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"},{"latin":"Quī paulum aut nihil discere potest, stultus esse dīcitur.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"stuprum","latin":"stuprum, -ī","headword":"stuprum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shameful violation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"suadere","latin":"suādēre","headword":"suādēre","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to urge; persuade (with dat.)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"sub","latin":"sub","headword":"sub","letter":"s","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"under; beneath","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sub arbore autem umbra est.","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"subducere","latin":"subdūcere","headword":"subdūcere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to beach; draw up (ships)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nāvibus in lītus subductīs, iuvenēs Trōiānī iam novam urbem aedificābant et arva nova colēbant, cum foeda pestilentia hominēs miserōs afficere coepit, et simul sōl flagrāns agrōs siccōs adeō torrēbat ut nec herbam nec frūmentum ferre possent.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"subinde","latin":"subinde","headword":"subinde","letter":"s","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"soon after; repeatedly","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ennius, mox et iūxtā Caecilius et Terentius, et subinde Pācuvius, et continuō Pācuviō iam sene Accius, clāriorque tunc in poēmatis tragicī Rōmānī eōrum obtrectandīs Lūcīlius fuit.","reading":"PHILIPPVS ĀD LŪCĪLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"subsidium","latin":"subsidium, -ī","headword":"subsidium","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"help; relief","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Macedonēs quīque aliī in castrīs rēgiīs erant prīmō, dum procul nihil aliud quam turba et agmen apparēbat, Aetōlōs crēdere subsidiō venīre; cēterum, ut prīmum signa et arma ex propinquō cognita errōrem aperuērunt, tantus repentē pavor omnēs cēpit ut abiectīs armīs fugerent!","reading":"THERMOPYLAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"successus","latin":"successus, -ūs","headword":"successus","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"outcome; success","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Metellus variō successū contrā Sertōrium dīmicāvit.","reading":"BELLA NOVA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"succumbere","latin":"succumbere","headword":"succumbere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to yield; sink under","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nisi certum mihi esset nūllī virō mē coniugio iungere, postquam prīmus amor mē morte fefellit, huius ūnīus amōrī forsitan succumbere potuī!","reading":"FLAMMA AMŌRIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"sudor","latin":"sūdor, -ōris","headword":"sūdor","letter":"s","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sweat","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is cum in opere et arāns esset inventus, sūdōre dētersō togam praetextam accēpit, et caesīs hostibus līberāvit exercitum.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"sum","latin":"sum","headword":"sum","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"I am","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"sumit","latin":"sūmit","headword":"sūmit","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"takes (up); takes; picks up","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius: 'Sūme sacculum tuum et discēde, bone serve!' Dāvus sacculum suum sūmit et discēdit.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Sūmite cēterās rosās eāsque in aquā pōnite!\" Puerī cēterās quattuor rosās sūmunt et cum iīs discēdunt.","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"sunt","latin":"sunt","headword":"sunt","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"they are","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Italia et Graecia in Eurōpā sunt.","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}]},{"id":"superbia","latin":"superbia, -ae","headword":"superbia","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pride; arrogance","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn vēnimus ut praedam faciāmus — nōn tanta vīs nec tanta superbia victīs est.","reading":"DĪDŌ RĒGĪNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"superbus","latin":"superbus","headword":"superbus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"proud; arrogant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"At Caesar, vir superbus, cum id parum esse cēnsēret, quīnquāgintā talenta pīrātīs obtulit, simul vērō supplicium iīs minātus est!","reading":"CLASSIS RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"superlativus","latin":"superlātīvus","headword":"superlātīvus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"superlative","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Comparātiōnis gradūs quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Trēs.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Positīvus, ut doctus; comparātīvus, ut doctior; superlātīvus, ut doctissimus.' Magister: 'Quae nōmina comparantur?' Discipulus: 'Appellātīva dumtaxat quālitātem aut quantitātem significantiā.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"supinum","latin":"supīnum","headword":"supīnum","letter":"s","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"supine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"suppeditare","latin":"suppeditāre","headword":"suppeditāre","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to supply; furnish","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Commentābar dēclāmitāns — sīc enim nunc loquimur — idque faciēbam multum etiam Latīnē, sed Graecē saepius, vel quod Graeca ōrātiō plūra ōrnāmenta suppeditāns cōnsuētūdinem similiter Latīnē dīcendī afferēbat, vel quod ā Graecīs summīs doctōribus, Graecē dīcerem, neque corrigī possem neque docērī.'","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"supplex","latin":"supplex, -icis","headword":"supplex","letter":"s","pos":"adjective / noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"suppliant","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Posterō diē paulō ante sōlis ortum vir ignōtus extrēmā famē cōnfectus ē silvīs prōcessit atque supplex manūs ad lītus extendit; barbam horrentem gerēbat et sordidam scissamque vestem — at Graecus erat, quondam armātus adversus Trōiam missus.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"supplicatio","latin":"supplicātiō, -ōnis","headword":"supplicātiō","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"public thanksgiving","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sergiō praetōre, deinde ex auctōritāte patrum in cōntiōne sunt recitātae, et ob rēs prosperē gestās in diēs quīnque supplicātiōnēs dēcrētae.","reading":"PHILIPPVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"supra","latin":"suprā","headword":"suprā","letter":"s","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"above; over","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sōl in caelō est suprā campum.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"surgere","latin":"surgere","headword":"surgere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to get up; rise; to rise; get up","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque ē lectō surgere cōnātur, sed pēs dēnuō dolēre incipit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"latin":"In Iudaeā Iēsus nōn sōlum faciēbat ut caecī vidērent, surdī audīrent, mūtī loquerentur, vērum etiam verbīs efficiēbat ut mortuī surgerent et ambulārent.","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA IN NĀVĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"surgit","latin":"surgit","headword":"surgit","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"rises; gets up","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"surripere","latin":"surripere","headword":"surripere","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to steal","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Certum praemium statuere oportet.' Iūlius: 'Tantum quantum ille surripuit.' Orontēs: 'Centum tantum sēstertiōs?","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"surripit","latin":"surripit","headword":"surripit","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"steals","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūr nōndum mihi respondistī?\" Ita repente interrogātus Mēdus sē pecūniam ē sacculō dominī surripuisse cōnfitētur.","reading":"ĀNVLVS POLYCRATIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"suspicio","latin":"suspīciō, -ōnis","headword":"suspīciō","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"suspicion","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ad quem cum circum Arabiam lēgātī vēnissent Rōmānī quī dē eius voluntāte explōrārent darentque operam cōnsiliīs clandestīnīs ut Hannibalem in suspīciōnem rēgī addūcerent, neque id frūstrā fēcissent, idque Hannibal comperisset, tempore datō adiit ad rēgem, eīque cum multa dē fidē suā et odiō in Rōmānōs commemorāsset, hoc adiūnxit:","reading":"PUERITIA ET IŪS IŪRANDVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"sustineo","latin":"sustineō","headword":"sustineō","letter":"s","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to withstand; hold out","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nostrī, cum parātī essent ad castra dēfendenda, illum prīmum impetum facile sustinuērunt.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"suus","latin":"suus","headword":"suus","letter":"s","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"his; her; its (own)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"syllaba","latin":"syllaba","headword":"syllaba","letter":"s","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"syllable","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In vocābulō 'īnsula' sex litterae et trēs syllabae sunt: syllaba prīma 'īn-', secunda '-su-', tertia '-la'.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Hoc vocābulum amīca quīnque litterās habet et trēs syllabās: ā-mī-ca.","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"tabella","latin":"tabella","headword":"tabella","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"writing-tablet","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tabellam vōbīs ostendam.","reading":"MARCVS MENTĪTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"tabellarius","latin":"tabellārius","headword":"tabellārius","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"postman; letter-carrier; courier","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Extrā forēs stat tabellārius (sīc appellātur servus quī epistulās fert, nam anteā in tabellīs scrībēbantur epistulae).","reading":"TABELLĀRIVS AD IĀNVAM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"},{"latin":"Iānitor: 'Tabellārius advenit Tusculō.","reading":"EPISTVLA ADVENIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"taberna","latin":"taberna","headword":"taberna","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shop; tavern","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce taberna Rōmāna, in quā gemmae et margarītae multae sunt.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"tabernaculum","latin":"tabernāculum, -ī","headword":"tabernāculum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tent","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Consurrēxit cōnsul, iussīs sedēre aliīs, prōgressusque paulum introeuntī rēgī dextram porrēxit submittentemque sē ad pedēs sustulit nec attingere genua passus intrōductum in tabernāculum adversus advocātōs in cōnsilium cōnsīdere iussit.","reading":"PERSEVS CAPTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"tabernarius","latin":"tabernārius","headword":"tabernārius","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shopkeeper","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce taberna Rōmāna, in quā gemmae et margarītae multae sunt.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"tabula","latin":"tabula","headword":"tabula","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"writing tablet; writing-tablet; story; tale; picture; painted panel","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dāvus Mārcō librum et tabulam et stilum et rēgulam affert.","reading":"DISCESSVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"latin":"Mārcus librum et tabulam et cēterās rēs ferēns Tusculum ambulat.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"tacet","latin":"tacet","headword":"tacet","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is silent; is quiet","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tacē et audī!' Servus tacet.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"latin":"Aemilia: \"Tacēte, puerī improbī!","reading":"ROSAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"tangere","latin":"tangere","headword":"tangere","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to touch","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tangit","latin":"tangit","headword":"tangit","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"touches","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Dormī bene!\" Māter manum pōnit in fronte fīliī: frontem eius tangit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"tantum","latin":"tantum","headword":"tantum","letter":"t","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"only","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius rūrsus pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor ... novem, decem.' Numerus nummōrum nōn est centum, sed decem tantum.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"tantus","latin":"tantus","headword":"tantus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"so great; so big","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ānulus satis magnus est et ad digitum convenit, nam digitus quārtus nōn tantus est quantus digitus medius.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"tardus","latin":"tardus","headword":"tardus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"late; slow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nimis tardus est iste cocus!' Aemilia: 'Tuumne hoc negōtium est an meum?","reading":"TRĪCLĪNIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"taurus","latin":"taurus","headword":"taurus","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bull","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"te","latin":"tē","headword":"tē","letter":"t","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"you (acc.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus respondet: 'Iūlia tē vocat.'","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"tectum","latin":"tēctum","headword":"tēctum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"roof","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tēctum peristȳlī altīs columnīs sustinētur, inter quās tria pulchra signa stant: ūnum Iūnōnis, alterum Cupīdinis, tertium Veneris.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"}]},{"id":"tellus","latin":"tellūs, -ūris","headword":"tellūs","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"earth; land","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam ea quae est media et nōna, Tellūs, neque movētur et īnfima est et in eam feruntur omnia nūtū suō pondera.'","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"telum","latin":"tēlum, -ī","headword":"tēlum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"weapon; spear","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc Priamus, quamquam ipse mortem iam propinquam videt, īrā permōtus exclāmat: \"At prō tālī scelere dī caelestēs praemia dēbita reddant tibi, quī cōram patre fīlium foedē trucīdāvistī!\" Sīc fātus senex īnfirmus tēlum inūtile coniēcit, quod Pyrrhum laedere nōn potuit, sed nequīquam in clipeō haesit.","reading":"MORS PRIAMĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"temerarius","latin":"temerārius","headword":"temerārius","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"reckless; rash","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Sī altius volābimus, nōn sōlum Graeciam, sed paene tōtum orbem terrārum spectābimus\" inquit puer temerārius atque etiam altius sē levāvit.","reading":"ĪCARVS IN MARE CADIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"temere","latin":"temere","headword":"temere","letter":"t","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"rashly; at random","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"temeritas","latin":"temeritās, -ātis","headword":"temeritās","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rashness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Celeriter adulēscentem suā temeritāte implet.","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"temperantia","latin":"temperantia, -ae","headword":"temperantia","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"self-control; moderation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ac prīmum quanta innocentia dēbent esse imperātōrēs! quanta deinde in omnibus rēbus temperantia! quanta fide, quanta facilitāte, quanto ingeniō, quanta hūmānitāte!","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"temperatio","latin":"temperātiō, -ōnis","headword":"temperātiō","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"blending; moderation","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}],"examples":[{"latin":"'Deinde subter mediam ferē regiōnem Sōl obtinet, dux et prīnceps et moderātor lūminum reliquōrum, mēns mundī et temperātiō, tantā magnitūdine ut cūncta suā lūce lūstret et compleat.","reading":"CURSUS STELLĀRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":56,"roman":"LVI","title":"The Dream of Scipio","slug":"somnium-scipionis"}]},{"id":"tempestas","latin":"tempestās","headword":"tempestās","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"storm","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tempestās est magnus ventus quī mare turbat ac flūctus facit quī altiōrēs sunt quam nāvēs.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Mēdus vērō multum cōgitat dē verbīs Lȳdiae et dē tempestāte quae tam subitō cessāvit, postquam Lȳdia deum suum invocāvit.","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA IN NĀVĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"templum","latin":"templum, -ī","headword":"templum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"temple","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In monte Capitōlīnō, quī prae cēterīs sacer habētur, multa sunt aedificia sacra, quōrum clārissimum est templum Iovis Optimī Maximī.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"tempus","latin":"tempus","headword":"tempus","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"time; tense","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Centum annī vel saeculum est longum tempus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"tendere","latin":"tendere","headword":"tendere","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to stretch out; extend","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tenebrae","latin":"tenebrae","headword":"tenebrae","letter":"t","pos":"noun (f. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"darkness","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Libenter faciam\" inquit Iulius, \"sed iam nimis obscurum est hoc triclinium; in tenebris legere non possum.","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"tenet","latin":"tenet","headword":"tenet","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"holds; keeps","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tenuis","latin":"tenuis","headword":"tenuis","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"thin; slender","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rāmus quī nīdum sustinet nōn crassus, sed tenuis est.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"terget","latin":"terget","headword":"terget","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"wipes; dries","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlia oculōs et nāsum terget, rosam sūmit, ē cubiculō exit.","reading":"ROSA IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"tergum","latin":"tergum","headword":"tergum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"back (of the body); back","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Diodōrus, magister sevērus, tergum puerī virga verberat. (Tergum est posterior pars corporis.) Tergum dolet Mārcō, neque ille lacrimat, nam lacrimāre puerō Rōmānō nōn convenit.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"terra","latin":"terra","headword":"terra","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"earth; land","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Caelum est suprā terram.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"terrere","latin":"terrēre","headword":"terrēre","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to frighten","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"terror","latin":"terror, -ōris","headword":"terror","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"terror; fright","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In quāscumque terrās abdūcite!","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"tertius","latin":"tertius","headword":"tertius","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"third","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"testamentum","latin":"testāmentum, -ī","headword":"testāmentum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"will; testament","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nec diū superfuit fīliō pater; quī cum ignōrāns nurum ventrem ferre dēcessisset oblītus nepōtis in testāmentō, puerō egentī post avī mortem nātō ab inopiā \"Egēriō\" nōmen datum est.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"testis","latin":"testis","headword":"testis","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"witness","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"thalamus","latin":"thalamus, -ī","headword":"thalamus","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bedchamber","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Famulae eam collāpsam suscipiunt, in marmoreum thalamum referunt et in lectō pōnunt.","reading":"QUERELLA DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"theatrum","latin":"theātrum, -ī","headword":"theātrum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"theatre","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fabia: \"Ego ludos scaenicos praefero: malo fabulas spectare in theatro.","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"},{"latin":"Pompēius cōnsul amplissimum theātrum marmoreum aedificandum cūrāvit cum porticū et novā cūriā.","reading":"VRBS MARMOREA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"thermae","latin":"thermae, -ārum","headword":"thermae","letter":"t","pos":"noun f. pl.","posGroup":"noun","english":"public baths","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Agrippā, duce illūstrī quī classī Augustī praefectus erat, itemque magnae balneae quae ab eōdem thermae Agrippae vocantur.","reading":"VRBS MARMOREA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"thesaurus","latin":"thēsaurus, -ī","headword":"thēsaurus","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"treasure","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sed in somnīs Dīdōnī appāruit imāgō coniugis mortuī, quī mīrum in modum ōs pallidum tollēns āram cruentam et pectus suum vulnerātum nūdāvit et scelus rēgis omne patefēcit; tum uxōrī suāsit ut celeriter ex patriā excēderet, et simul veterēs thēsaurōs occultōs, ignōtum pondus aurī et argentī, mōnstrāvit.","reading":"VENUS GENETRĪX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"tigris","latin":"tigris, -is","headword":"tigris","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tiger","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"timet","latin":"timet","headword":"timet","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"fears; is afraid of","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mēdus nōn est apud dominum, nam is dominum īrātum timet.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Itaque ovis lupum nōn timet.","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"timidus","latin":"timidus","headword":"timidus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"timid; fearful","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus: 'Nōlī putāre mē puerum timidum esse!","reading":"TABVLĀ POSTVLĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"timor","latin":"timor","headword":"timor","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"fear","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pallet ob timōrem. (Quī timet, pallēre solet.)","reading":"MARCVS CŌNFITĒTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"tiro","latin":"tīrō, -ōnis","headword":"tīrō","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"new recruit; novice soldier","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Et cum Latīnī, quī ā Rōmānīs subāctī erant, mīlitēs praestāre nōllent, ex Rōmānīs tantum tīrōnēs lēctī sunt, factaeque legiōnēs decem; quī modus sexāgintā vel amplius armātōrum mīlia efficiēbat. (Parvīs adhūc Rōmānīs rēbus tanta tamen in rē mīlitārī virtūs erat.)","reading":"POST VRBEM CAPTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"titulus","latin":"titulus","headword":"titulus","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"title","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Titulus librī tuī est 'LINGVA LATINA'.","reading":"LIBER TVVS LATĪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"toga","latin":"toga","headword":"toga","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"toga","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus frīget, quod corpus eius nūdum est (id est sine vestīmentīs); itaque Mārcus vestīmenta sua ā servō poscit: 'Dā mihi tunicam et togam!","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"toga virilis","latin":"toga virīlis","headword":"toga virīlis","letter":"t","pos":"phrase","posGroup":"other","english":"the toga of manhood","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sūmptā togā virīlī, Marcus in forum ductus est ad Q.","reading":"M. TVLLIVS CICERŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"tollo","latin":"tollō","headword":"tollō","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"raise; lift","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quisque puer manum tollit, prīmum Sextus, tum Titus, postrēmō Mārcus.","reading":"IN LŪDŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"tonare","latin":"tonāre","headword":"tonāre","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to thunder","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"torrere","latin":"torrēre","headword":"torrēre","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to scorch; burn","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"torus","latin":"torus, -ī","headword":"torus","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"couch","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"trabs","latin":"trabs, trabis","headword":"trabs","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"beam; timber","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tradit","latin":"trādit","headword":"trādit","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"hands over; delivers","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce epistula quam illinc ad tē tulit.' Hoc dīcēns iānitor epistulam dominō suō trādit.","reading":"EPISTVLA ADVENIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":23,"roman":"XXIII","title":"The Teacher’s Letter","slug":"epistula-magistri"}]},{"id":"tragicus","latin":"tragicus, -a, -um","headword":"tragicus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"tragic; of tragedy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Inter haec tempora nōbilēs celebrēsque erant Sophoclēs ac deinde Eurīpidēs, tragicī poētae, et Hippocratēs medicus, et philosophus Dēmocritus, quibus Sōcratēs Athēniēnsis nātū quidem posterior fuit, sed quibusdam temporibus iīsdem vīxērunt.","reading":"SŌCRATĒS ET CAMILLUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"tragoedia","latin":"tragoedia, -ae","headword":"tragoedia","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tragedy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum Aeschylus Athēnīs tragoediārum poēta celebris fuit.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"traicere","latin":"trāicere","headword":"trāicere","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to cross; transport across; to cross over; transport","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tranquillus","latin":"tranquillus","headword":"tranquillus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"calm; still","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī āēr tranquillus est, necesse est ventum opperīrī. (Ventus est āēr quī movētur.) Cum nūllus ventus super mare flat, tranquillum est mare; cum magnus ventus flat, mare turbidum est.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"trans","latin":"trāns","headword":"trāns","letter":"t","pos":"preposition","posGroup":"preposition","english":"across","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Celsī sānē et arduī montēs Germāniam ab Italiā disiungunt, ac difficillimae sunt viae quae trāns Alpēs ferunt, sed tamen celer tabellārius idem iter quīndecim ferē diēbus cōnficere potest, ut tabellāriī pūblicī quibus ūtitur dux noster.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"transfuga","latin":"trānsfuga, -ae","headword":"trānsfuga","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"deserter","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Multī temere subeuntēs vāllum trānsfīxī sunt, et aut recessissent aut plūrēs cecidissent, nī M.","reading":"THERMOPYLAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"transfugere","latin":"trānsfugere","headword":"trānsfugere","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to desert; go over to the enemy","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nam cum aliīs urbānīs operibus intentum sē esse simulāret, Sextus, fīlius eius quī minimus ex tribus erat, trānsfūgit ex compositō Gabiōs patris in sē saevitiam nōn tolerandam querēns: 'rēgem iam ab aliēnīs in suōs vertisse superbiam et līberīs quoque īnsidiās parāre, nē quem hērēdem regnī relinquat; sē quidem inter tēla et gladiōs patris ēlāpsum nihil usquam sibi tūtum nisi apud hostēs L.","reading":"GABIĪ DOLŌ CAPTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":45,"roman":"XLV","title":"Rome Liberated","slug":"roma-liberata"}]},{"id":"transgredi","latin":"trānsgredī","headword":"transgredī","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to cross over; pass over","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Posteā Philippus ex īnsidiīs occīditur; et Alexander regnum adeptus ad subigendōs Persās in Asiam atque in Orientem trānsgressus est; plērāque parte Orientis subāctā, cum annōs ūndecim rēgnāvisset, obiit mortis diem.","reading":"PHILIPPVS ĀD LŪCĪLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"},{"latin":"Inde Pyrēnaeum trānsgreditur.","reading":"ITER HANNIBALIS IN ĪTALIAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"transitio","latin":"trānsitiō, -ōnis","headword":"trānsitiō","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"going over; desertion","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Antiochum timor incessit nē quās per imminentia iuga callēs invenīret ad trānsitum Rōmānus; nam Lacedaemoniōs quondam ita ā Persīs circuitōs fāma erat.","reading":"THERMOPYLAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"transitus","latin":"trānsitus, -ūs","headword":"trānsitus","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"crossing; passage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Saltum Pyrēnaeum trānsiit.","reading":"IN HISPĀNIAM ET AD ALPĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"transmarinus","latin":"trānsmarīnus, -a, -um","headword":"trānsmarīnus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"from across the sea; overseas","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Is mox ad Italiam vēnit, tumque prīmum Rōmānī cum trānsmarīnō hoste dīmicāvērunt.","reading":"PYRRHUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"tremere","latin":"tremere","headword":"tremere","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to tremble","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iānitor eum tremere animadvertit iterumque dērīdet: \"Quid tremis?","reading":"CANIS FERŌX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"trepidatio","latin":"trepidātiō, -ōnis","headword":"trepidātiō","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"panic; alarm","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tullus equitem clārā increpāns vōce, ut hostēs exaudīrent, redīre in proelium iubet: nihil trepidātiōne opus esse; ut suō iussū circumdūcī Albānum exercitum, ut Fīdēnātium nūda terga invādat!","reading":"METTII PERFIDIA AC SVPPLICIVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}]},{"id":"trepidus","latin":"trepidus, -a, -um","headword":"trepidus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"alarmed; trembling","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc mē sociī, dum trepidī fugiunt, in vastō Cyclōpis antrō dēseruērunt.","reading":"MŌNS AETNA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"tres","latin":"trēs","headword":"trēs","letter":"t","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"three","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"A, B, C sunt trēs litterae.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"tria","latin":"tria","headword":"tria","letter":"t","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"three (neut.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sparta, Delphī Tusculumque tria oppida sunt: duo oppida Graeca et ūnum oppidum Rōmānum.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"}]},{"id":"tribunal","latin":"tribūnal, -ālis","headword":"tribūnal","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"raised platform; tribunal","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Semprōnius Gracchus tribūnus plēbis, quī anteā Scīpiōnibus inimīcus fuerat, intercessit, et ob id beneficium Āfricānī fīliam dūxit.","reading":"PERSEVS VICTVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"tribunus plebis","latin":"tribūnus plēbis","headword":"tribūnus plēbis","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tribune of the plebs","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum et ipse sibi tribūnōs plēbis, quasi propriōs iūdicēs et dēfensōrēs, creāvit, per quōs contrā senātum et cōnsulēs tūtus esse posset.","reading":"CŌNSVLĒS ET DICTĀTŌRĒS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"tribus","latin":"tribus, -ūs","headword":"tribus","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tribe; territorial division","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī nōn dēduntur quae exposcit, diēbus tribus et trīgintā perāctīs bellum ita indīcit: \"Audī, Iuppiter, et tū, Iāne Quirīne, dīque omnēs caelestēs vōsque terrestrēs vōsque īnfernī, audīte: ego vōs testor populum Latīnum iniūstum esse neque iūs persolvere!","reading":"ANCVS MARCIUS REX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"tributum","latin":"tribūtum, -ī","headword":"tribūtum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tribute; tax","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tribūtum dīmidium eius quod pependissent rēgibus pendere populō Rōmānō.","reading":"MACEDONIA PRŌVINCIA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"triclinium","latin":"trīclīnium","headword":"trīclīnium","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"dining room","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hic Aemilia 'Necesse est' inquit 'paulisper famem sitimque ferre, dum cibus coquitur et trīclīnium exōrnātur.'","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"tridens","latin":"tridēns, -entis","headword":"tridēns","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"trident","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Properāte domum rēgīque vestrō haec dīcite: nōn illī datum esse imperium pontī saevumque tridentem, sed mihī!'","reading":"LĪTUS ĀFRICAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"triduum","latin":"trīduum, -ī","headword":"trīduum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"three days","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trīduum triumphāvit.","reading":"TRIVMPHVS FLĀMINĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"triennium","latin":"triennium, -ī","headword":"triennium","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"period of three years","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Praesūmpsērunt tamen tribūnī mīlitēs cōnsulārī potestāte iterum dignitātem, et triennium perseverāvērunt.","reading":"POST VRBEM CAPTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"triens","latin":"triēns, -entis","headword":"triēns","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"a third (of an as)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tristis","latin":"trīstis","headword":"trīstis","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"sad","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Itaque trīstis est Aemilia, quae frātrem suum amat.","reading":"DĒ FAMILIĀ ET NŌMINIBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"}]},{"id":"triticum","latin":"trīticum, -ī","headword":"trīticum","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wheat","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eōdem tempore potentissimus rēx Siciliae Hierō Rōmam vēnit ad lūdōs spectandōs et ducenta mīlia modiōrum trīticī populō dōnum praebuit.","reading":"BELLVM PŪNICVM PRĪMVM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}]},{"id":"triumphus","latin":"triumphus, -ī","headword":"triumphus","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"triumph; triumphal procession","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ad hoc templum imperātor victor post triumphum ascendit, ut Iovī Optimō Maximō sacrificium faciat, dum ducēs hostium, quī in triumphō ante currum imperātōris ductī sunt, ad supplicium trāduntur.","reading":"PALĀTIUM ET CAPITŌLIUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":36,"roman":"XXXVI","title":"Roma Aeterna","slug":"roma-aeterna"}]},{"id":"triumvir","latin":"triumvir, -ī","headword":"triumvir","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"one of three commissioners","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Gracchum frātrem et Appium Claudium socerum triumvirōs ad dīvidendum agrum creāret.","reading":"LĒGĒS AGRĀRIAE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"trux","latin":"trux, trucis","headword":"trux","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"savage; grim; fierce","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tu","latin":"tū","headword":"tū","letter":"t","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"you (sing.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister interrogat: 'Cūr tū sōlus es, Sexte?' 'Ego sōlus sum, quod cēterī discipulī omnēs absunt,' respondet Sextus.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"tueri","latin":"tuērī","headword":"tuērī","letter":"t","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to protect; guard","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Neque tamen classis Rōmāna omnēs nautās quī ubīque nāvigant tuērī potest.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"tugurium","latin":"tugurium, -ī","headword":"tugurium","letter":"t","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"hut; cottage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quī postquam in aedēs irrūpēre, dīversī rēgem quaerere, dormientēs aliōs, aliōs occurrentēs interficere, scrūtārī loca abdita, clausa effringere, strepitū et tumultū omnia miscēre — cum interim Hiempsal reperītur occultāns sē tuguriō mulieris ancillae, quō initiō pavidus et ignārus locī perfūgerat.","reading":"MORS HIEMPSALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"tumidus","latin":"tumidus, -a, -um","headword":"tumidus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"swollen; surging","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum omnēs hīs malīs perturbārentur, dī Penātēs, quōs Aenēās sēcum Trōiā extulerat, noctū in somnīs eī vīsī sunt ante lectum adstāre in līmine iānuae atque hīs dictīs cōnsōlārī: \"Nōs quī tē, Dardaniā incēnsā, per mare tumidum secūtī sumus, nōs īdem posterōs tuōs in caelum tollēmus imperiumque urbī eōrum dabimus.","reading":"Ē TRŌIĀ IN CRĒTAM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"tunica","latin":"tunica","headword":"tunica","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tunic","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus frīget, quod corpus eius nūdum est (id est sine vestīmentīs); itaque Mārcus vestīmenta sua ā servō poscit: 'Dā mihi tunicam et togam!","reading":"MANĒ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"turbidus","latin":"turbidus","headword":"turbidus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"rough; disturbed","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī āēr tranquillus est, necesse est ventum opperīrī. (Ventus est āēr quī movētur.) Cum nūllus ventus super mare flat, tranquillum est mare; cum magnus ventus flat, mare turbidum est.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"}]},{"id":"turgidus","latin":"turgidus","headword":"turgidus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"swollen; turgid","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Qui, cum Quintus heri de alta arbore cecidisset, pedem eius turgidum vix tetigit, sed misello puero sanguinem misit!","reading":"DĒ LŪDĪS ET SPECTĀCVLĪS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"turpis","latin":"turpis","headword":"turpis","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"ugly; shameful","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"turpiter","latin":"turpiter","headword":"turpiter","letter":"t","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"foully; shamefully","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tum vērō 'Nec sōlum,' inquit, 'prāvē et turpiter, sed etiam nimis leviter scrībis.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ SCRĪBVNT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"turris","latin":"turris, -is","headword":"turris","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tower","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tutor","latin":"tūtor, -ōris","headword":"tūtor","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"guardian","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Brevī Tarquinius cum Ancō rēge tam firmam amīcitiam iūnxit ut pūblicīs pariter ac prīvātīs cōnsiliīs bellō domīque interesset, et postrēmō tūtor etiam līberīs rēgis testāmentō īnstituerētur.","reading":"LVCVMO ET TANAQVIL","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"tutus","latin":"tūtus","headword":"tūtus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"safe","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"tuus","latin":"tuus","headword":"tuus","letter":"t","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"your (of one person); your; yours","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cornēlius: 'Cuius servus est Mēdus?' Iūlius: 'Mēdus servus meus est.' Cornēlius: 'Estne Dāvus servus tuus?' Iūlius: 'Dāvus quoque servus meus est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Mēdus: 'Servus tuus Mēdus hīc est.' Iūlius servum suum Mēdum videt, Dāvum nōn videt.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"tyrannis","latin":"tyrannis, -idis","headword":"tyrannis","letter":"t","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rule of a tyrant; tyranny","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Serviō autem Tulliō regnante, Pīsistratus Athēnīs tyrannus fuit, Solōne ante in exsilium voluntārium profectō, quoniam id eī praedīcentī nōn crēditum est.","reading":"INITIVM CHRONICŌRUM","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"tyrannus","latin":"tyrannus","headword":"tyrannus","letter":"t","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tyrant","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Nēmō tibi ānulum ita abiectum reddet — nisi forte tam fēlīx eris quam Polycratēs tyrannus Samius, cuius ānulus, quem ipse in mare abiēcerat, mīrum in modum inventus est nōn in fundō maris, sed in ventre piscis!\"","reading":"ĀNVLVS POLYCRATIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"ubi?","latin":"ubi?","headword":"ubi?","letter":"u","pos":"adverb","posGroup":"verb","english":"where?","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ubi est Italia?","reading":"LĒCTIŌ PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Ubi sunt cēterī nummī?","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"ulcisci","latin":"ulcīscī","headword":"ulcīscī","letter":"u","pos":"verb (dep.)","posGroup":"verb","english":"to avenge; punish","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quae rēs plērumque magnās cīvitātēs pessum dedit, dum alterī alterōs vincere quōvīs modō et victōs acerbius ulcīscī volunt.","reading":"CĪVITĀS DĪLACERĀTA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":51,"roman":"LI","title":"Scipio Aemilianus","slug":"scipio-aemilianus"}]},{"id":"ultrix","latin":"ultrīx, -īcis","headword":"ultrīx","letter":"u","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"avenging (goddess)","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ululatus","latin":"ululātus, -ūs","headword":"ululātus","letter":"u","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wailing; shriek","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Domus interior gemitū ac tumultū miscētur, penitusque magna ātria ululātū fēminārum resonant, cum mātrēs pavidae in aedibus errent īnfantēs suōs amplexae.","reading":"MORS PRIAMĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"umbra","latin":"umbra","headword":"umbra","letter":"u","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shade; shadow","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sub arbore autem umbra est.","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"umerus","latin":"umerus","headword":"umerus","letter":"u","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shoulder","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"umidus","latin":"ūmidus","headword":"ūmidus","letter":"u","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"wet; damp","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nūper Mārcus sōlus rediit, sed pater fīlium suum redeuntem vix cognōvit neque eum ōsculātus est ut solet, nam Mārcus nōn modo ūmidus erat quod per imbrem ambulāverat, sed etiam sordidus atque cruentus quod humī iacuerat et ā Sextō pulsātus erat.'","reading":"SYRA NĀRRAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"unda","latin":"unda, -ae","headword":"unda","letter":"u","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wave","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Notus vēla implēbat, nāvēs celeriter per undās vehēbantur quō ventus ferēbat.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"undequadraginta","latin":"ūndēquadrāgintā","headword":"ūndēquadrāgintā","letter":"u","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"thirty-nine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trīgintā et novem sunt ūndēquadrāgintā.","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"unguis","latin":"unguis, -is","headword":"unguis","letter":"u","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"claw; nail","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"universus","latin":"ūniversus, -a, -um","headword":"ūniversus","letter":"u","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"whole; entire","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ūniversus reliquus senātus ex urbe fugiēns ad Sullam in Graeciam vēnit ōrāns patriae subvenīret.","reading":"BELLVM CĪVĪLE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":53,"roman":"LIII","title":"Marius and Sulla","slug":"marius-et-sulla"}]},{"id":"unus","latin":"ūnus","headword":"ūnus","letter":"u","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"one","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius pecūniam numerat: 'Ūnus, duo, trēs, quattuor, quīnque, sex, septem, octō, novem, decem.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"urit","latin":"ūrit","headword":"ūrit","letter":"u","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"burns; scorches","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"ut","latin":"ut","headword":"ut","letter":"u","pos":"conjunction","posGroup":"conjunction","english":"that; in order that","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ut tempestās mare tranquillum turbāvit, ita verba Lȳdiae animum Mēdī turbāvērunt.","reading":"MĒDVS ET LȲDIA IN NĀVĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"uterque","latin":"uterque","headword":"uterque","letter":"u","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"each (of the two)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Uterque puer cubat in cubiculō parvō, neuter in cubiculō magnō.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"utilitas","latin":"ūtilitās, -ātis","headword":"ūtilitās","letter":"u","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"usefulness; advantage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"uva","latin":"ūva","headword":"ūva","letter":"u","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"grape","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"uxor","latin":"uxor (uxoris)","headword":"uxor","letter":"u","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wife","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius cum uxōre suā in peristȳlō ambulat.","reading":"MARĪTVS ET VXOR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"latin":"Iūlius adhūc in peristȳlō cum uxōre colloquitur.","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"vacuus","latin":"vacuus","headword":"vacuus","letter":"v","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"empty","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sacculus eius vacuus est.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"vadum","latin":"vadum, -ī","headword":"vadum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"shallow water; shoal","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"vagina","latin":"vāgīna, -ae","headword":"vāgīna","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"scabbard; sheath","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Imperiō dī ovantēs pāreāmus!' Hōc dīcēns ēnsem fulgentem ē vāgīnā ēripit et fūnēs incidit.","reading":"ROGUS DĪDŌNIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"vagire","latin":"vāgīre","headword":"vāgīre","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"cry; wail","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"vagitus","latin":"vāgītus, -ūs","headword":"vāgītus","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wail; infant cry","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cum aqua recēdēns alveum, in quō expositī erant puerī, in siccō relīquisset, lupa sitiēns ex montibus ad puerīlem vāgītum cursum flēxit.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"valet","latin":"valet","headword":"valet","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is well; is strong","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Alter ē duōbus puerīs valet, alter aegrōtat.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"}]},{"id":"validus","latin":"validus","headword":"validus","letter":"v","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"strong; powerful","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sextus tam validus est quam bōs!\"","reading":"MARCVS Ā PATRE INTERROGĀTVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"vallis","latin":"vallis","headword":"vallis","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"valley","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"vallum","latin":"vāllum","headword":"vāllum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rampart; wall","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Circum castra fossā et vallum longum et altum est.'","reading":"CASTRA ET PROELIVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":12,"roman":"XII","title":"The Roman Soldier","slug":"miles-romanus"},{"latin":"Quī cum arma cēpissent et vallum ascendissent, prīmō mīrābantur quamobrem mediā nocte ē somnō excitātī essent, cum extrā vallum omnia tranquilla esse vidērentur.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"vates","latin":"vātēs, -is","headword":"vātēs","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"prophet; seer","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Age, vāde, et factīs tuīs Trōiam ad caelum tollem!\" Quae postquam Helēnus vātēs dīvīnō ōre fātus est, dōna magnifica ad nāvēs ferrī iussit.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"vectigal","latin":"vectīgal, -ālis","headword":"vectīgal","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"tax; revenue","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Namque effēcit ex novīs vectīgālibus nōn sōlum ut esset pecūnia quae Rōmānīs ex foedere penderētur, sed etiam superesset quae in aerāriō repōnerētur.","reading":"RĒX CARTHĀGINE","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"},{"latin":"Bellum grave et perīculōsum vestrīs vectīgālibus ac sociīs ā duōbus potentissimīs rēgibus īnfertur, Mithridāte et Tigrāne, quōrum alter relictus, alter lacessītus occasionem sibi ad occupandam Asiam oblātam esse arbitrātur.","reading":"DĒ GENERE BELLĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"vehemens","latin":"vehemēns, -entis","headword":"vehemēns","letter":"v","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"violent; forceful","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quibus rēbus Micipsa tametsī initiō laetus fuerat exīstimāns virtūtem Iugurthae rēgnō suō glōriae fore, tamen, postquam hominem adulēscentem — exāctā suā aetāte et parvīs līberīs — magis magisque crēscere intellegit, vehementer eō negōtiō permōtus multa cum animō suō volvēbat.","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"vehiculum","latin":"vehiculum, -ī","headword":"vehiculum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"vehicle; carriage","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Foedum inhūmānumque inde trāditur scelus: Tullia per patris corpus carpentum ēgisse fertur, partemque sanguinis ac caedis paternae cruentō vehiculō tulisse ad Penātēs suōs virīque suī!","reading":"TVLLIA FEROX","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":44,"roman":"XLIV","title":"Kings and Queens","slug":"reges-et-reginae"}]},{"id":"vehit","latin":"vehit","headword":"vehit","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"carries; conveys","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Equus quī Cornēlium vehit pulcher est.","reading":"MĒDVS ET CORNĒLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"vehitur","latin":"vehitur","headword":"vehitur","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is carried; travels","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōnnūllī in terrās aliēnās nāvigant, quod mercēs pretiōsās nautīs crēdere nōlunt, sīcut mercātor ille Rōmānus quī eādem nāve vehitur quā Mēdus et Lȳdia.","reading":"IN MARĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"velox","latin":"vēlōx","headword":"vēlōx","letter":"v","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"swift; fast","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}],"examples":[{"latin":"\"Illa nāvis vēlōx nōs persequitur.","reading":"NĀVIS PRAEDŌNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":29,"roman":"XXIX","title":"To Sail Is Necessary","slug":"navigare-necesse-est"}]},{"id":"velum","latin":"vēlum","headword":"vēlum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"sail; cloth","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Brevī nāvis ē cōnspectū eius abiit neque iam ūllum vēlum in marī cernēbātur.","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"vena","latin":"vēna","headword":"vēna","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"vein","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In corde est sanguis, quī per vēnās ad cor fluit.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"venalis","latin":"vēnālis, -e","headword":"vēnālis","letter":"v","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"for sale; venal","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Eā tempestāte exercitū nostrō fuēre complūrēs novī atque nōbilēs, quibus dīvitiae bonō honestōque potiōrēs erant, factiōsī domī, potentēs apud sociōs, clārī magis quam honestī; quī Iugurthae nōn mediocrem animum pollicitandō accendēbant, 'sī Micipsa rēx occidisset, fore utī sōlus imperiī Numidiae potīrētur: in ipsō maximam virtūtem, Rōmae omnia vēnālia esse!'","reading":"IVGVRTHA ADULĒSCĒNS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":52,"roman":"LII","title":"Jugurtha","slug":"iugurtha"}]},{"id":"vendere","latin":"vēndere","headword":"vēndere","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to sell","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Neque praedōnēs inermēs occīdunt, cum eōs magnō pretiō servōs vēndere possint.\"","reading":"IN MARĪ TVSCŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"vendit","latin":"vēndit","headword":"vēndit","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sells","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Albīnus est tabernārius Rōmānus quī gemmās et margarītās vēndit.","reading":"TABERNA ALBĪNĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"venenatus","latin":"venēnātus, -a, -um","headword":"venēnātus","letter":"v","pos":"adj.","posGroup":"adjective","english":"venomous; poisonous","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Imperāvit quam plūrimās venēnātās serpentēs vīvās colligī eāsque in vāsa fictilia conicī.","reading":"APVD PRŪSIAM ET MORS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":49,"roman":"XLIX","title":"Hannibal","slug":"hannibal"}]},{"id":"venenum","latin":"venēnum, -ī","headword":"venēnum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"poison","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":46,"roman":"XLVI","title":"After the Kings Were Expelled","slug":"post-reges-exactos"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"venia","latin":"venia, -ae","headword":"venia","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pardon; favour","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Modo sacrificiīs ā dīs veniam pete!'","reading":"FLAMMA AMŌRIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":40,"roman":"XL","title":"Unhappy Dido","slug":"infelix-dido"}]},{"id":"venit","latin":"venit","headword":"venit","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"comes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūr nōn venit?' Aemilia Iūlium nōn videt.","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"venter","latin":"venter","headword":"venter","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"belly; stomach","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Īnfrā pulmōnēs sunt iecur et venter.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"ventitare","latin":"ventitāre","headword":"ventitāre","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to come often","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Āfricānus, hic Paulī fīlius, fēriīs Latīnīs Tūditānō cōnsule et Aquīliō, cōnstituisset in hortīs esse familiārissimīque eius ad eum frequenter per eōs diēs ventitātūrī sē esse dīxissent, Latīnīs ipsīs māne ad eum prīmus sorōris fīlius vēnit Q.","reading":"DĒ DUŌBUS SŌLIBUS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":55,"roman":"LV","title":"On the Republic","slug":"de-re-publica"}]},{"id":"ventus","latin":"ventus","headword":"ventus","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wind","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī āēr tranquillus est, necesse est ventum opperīrī. (Ventus est āēr quī movētur.) Cum nūllus ventus super mare flat, tranquillum est mare; cum magnus ventus flat, mare turbidum est.","reading":"MARE ET PORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"latin":"Nāvicula autem in mediō marī iactābātur flūctibus, erat enim ventus contrārius.","reading":"DĒ POTESTĀTE CHRĪSTĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"venumdare","latin":"vēnumdare","headword":"vēnumdare","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to sell","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In antīquīs annalibus memoria super librīs Sibyllīnīs haec prōdita est: anus hospita atque incōgnita ad Tarquinium Superbum rēgem adiit novem librōs ferēns quōs esse dīcēbat dīvīna ōrācula: 'eōs velle vēnumdarī'.","reading":"LIBRĪ SIBYLLĪNĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":47,"roman":"XLVII","title":"Greeks and Romans","slug":"graeci-et-romani"}]},{"id":"venustus","latin":"venustus","headword":"venustus","letter":"v","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"charming; graceful","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"et quantum est hominum venustiorum!","reading":"DĒ CATVLLŌ ET LESBIA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"ver","latin":"vēr","headword":"vēr","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"spring","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Tempora annī sunt quattuor: aestās et hiems, vēr et autumnus.","reading":"ANNVS ET MĒNSĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"verberare","latin":"verberāre","headword":"verberāre","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to beat; whip","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus: 'Estne verberātus Mārcus?","reading":"SYRA NĀRRAT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}]},{"id":"verberat","latin":"verberat","headword":"verberat","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"beats; whips","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Māter fīlium verberat: tuxtax, tuxtax...","reading":"SCAENA SECVNDA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Mārcus magistrum metuit, Diodōrus enim magister sevērus est, quī discipulōs suōs virga verberat; eō modo magister sevērus discipulōs improbōs pūnīre solet.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"verbum","latin":"verbum","headword":"verbum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"verb; word","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister discipulum interrogat: 'Partēs ōrātiōnis quot sunt?' Discipulus respondet: 'Octō.' Magister: 'Quae?' Discipulus: 'Nōmen, prōnōmen, verbum, adverbium, participium, coniūnctiō, praepositiō, interiectiō.'","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"vereor","latin":"vereor","headword":"vereor","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"fear (deponent)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lȳdia: 'Ego Neptūnum nōn vereor.","reading":"NAVTAE ET NEPTŪNVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"vereri","latin":"verērī","headword":"verērī","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to fear; respect; be afraid of","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":16,"roman":"XVI","title":"The Storm","slug":"tempestas"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":24,"roman":"XXIV","title":"The Sick Boy","slug":"puer-aegrotus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"versiculus","latin":"versiculus","headword":"versiculus","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"little verse","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Versiculos in me narratur scribere Cinna.","reading":"DĒ MĀRTIĀLĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":34,"roman":"XXXIV","title":"On the Art of Poetry","slug":"de-arte-poetica"}]},{"id":"vertex","latin":"vertex, -icis","headword":"vertex","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"whirlpool; summit; peak","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trēs in saxa latentia abripiuntur, trēs ab altō in vada feruntur, ūnam ante ipsīus Aenēae oculōs ingēns flūctus in puppim ferit atque ter circumagit, tum rapidus vertex eam vorat.","reading":"TEMPESTĀS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":39,"roman":"XXXIX","title":"Carthage","slug":"karthago"}]},{"id":"vertit","latin":"vertit","headword":"vertit","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"turns","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Syra nōn videt lacrimās Iūliae, nam puella sē nōn vertit.","reading":"LACRIMAE IŪLIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":7,"roman":"VII","title":"The Girl and the Rose","slug":"puella-et-rosa"}]},{"id":"verus","latin":"vērus","headword":"vērus","letter":"v","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"true","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"vesper","latin":"vesper","headword":"vesper","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"evening","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Prīma pars diēī est māne, pars postrēma vesper.","reading":"DIĒS ET NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":13,"roman":"XIII","title":"The Year and the Months","slug":"annus-et-menses"}]},{"id":"vestigium","latin":"vestīgium","headword":"vestīgium","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"trace; footprint","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In terrā inter arborēs sunt vestīgia lupī.","reading":"OVIS NIGRA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"vestis","latin":"vestis","headword":"vestis","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"garment; clothes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cūr vestis Mārcī ūmida est?","reading":"PVGNA IN VIĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}]},{"id":"vetare","latin":"vetāre","headword":"vetāre","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to forbid","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Nōn īdem est permittere ac nōn vetāre.","reading":"SERVVS FVGITĪVVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":31,"roman":"XXXI","title":"Between the Cups","slug":"inter-pocula"}]},{"id":"via","latin":"via","headword":"via","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"road; way; street","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"In Italiā multae et magnae viae sunt: via Appia, via Latīna, via Flāminia, via Aurēlia, via Aemilia.","reading":"VIA LATĪNĀ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"latin":"Quī viā Appiā Rōmā Brundisium it multōs pāstōrēs videt in campīs.","reading":"PĀSTOR ET OVĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":9,"roman":"IX","title":"The Shepherd and the Sheep","slug":"pastor-et-oves"}]},{"id":"victoria","latin":"victōria, -ae","headword":"victōria","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"victory","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hōc proeliō factō, dux victor, cum ā mīlitibus imperātor salūtātus esset, virtūtem nostram laudāvit quod contrā hostēs numerō superiōrēs fortissimē pugnāvissēmus; tot hominibus ūnō proeliō āmissīs, hostēs brevī arma positūrōs esse dīxit.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"},{"latin":"Odiīs etiam prope maiōribus certāvērunt quam vīribus, Rōmānīs indignantibus quod victōribus victī ultrō īnferrent arma, Poenīs quod superbē avārēque crēderent imperitātum victīs esse.","reading":"IŪS IŪRANDVM HANNIBALIS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}]},{"id":"videt","latin":"videt","headword":"videt","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"sees","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus Mārcum videt.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"}]},{"id":"vidua","latin":"vidua, -ae","headword":"vidua","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"widow","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Hīc iam incrēdibilis fāma iīs allāta est: Helēnum, Priamī fīlium, rēgnō Ēpīrī potītum esse atque Andromachēn, viduam Hectoris, uxōrem dūxisse!","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"vigilare","latin":"vigilāre","headword":"vigilāre","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"stay awake","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Sī aeger erit, ipsa eum cūrābō tōtamque noctem apud eum vigilābō; nēmō īnfantem aegrum tam bene cūrāre potest quam māter ipsa.\"","reading":"COLLOQVIVM PARENTVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":20,"roman":"XX","title":"Parents","slug":"parentes"}]},{"id":"vigilat","latin":"vigilat","headword":"vigilat","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"is awake; keeps watch; stays awake","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Bracchium quoque dolet Quīntō; itaque is nōn dormit, sed vigilat.","reading":"NOX","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":14,"roman":"XIV","title":"A New Day","slug":"novus-dies"},{"latin":"Immō vigilō et tē audiō, magister.' Item Sextus et Titus 'Neque nōs dormīmus' inquiunt, 'Vigilāmus et omnia verba tua audīmus.","reading":"DISCIPVLĪ DORMIENTĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"viginti","latin":"vīgintī","headword":"vīgintī","letter":"v","pos":"numeral","posGroup":"numeral","english":"twenty","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Albīnus: \"In hōc ōrnāmentō vīgintī margarītae magnae sunt.","reading":"ĀNVLVS GEMMĀTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":8,"roman":"VIII","title":"The Roman Tavern","slug":"taberna-romana"}]},{"id":"vilis","latin":"vīlis","headword":"vīlis","letter":"v","pos":"adjective","posGroup":"adjective","english":"cheap","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Rōmae igitur ex summā inopiā repente maxima frūmentī cōpia facta est ac pānis tam vīlis fuit quam anteā fuerat — id quod populō Rōmānō grātissimum fuit.","reading":"PRAEDŌNĒS MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":32,"roman":"XXXII","title":"The Roman Fleet","slug":"classis-romana"}]},{"id":"vilitas","latin":"vīlitās, -ātis","headword":"vīlitās","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"cheapness","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Pompēiō omnium rērum ēgregiārum exempla sūmantur: quō diē ā vōbīs maritimō bellō praepositus est imperātor, tanta repentē vīlitās ex summā inopiā et cāritāte reī frūmentāriae cōnsecūta est ūnīus hominis spē ac nōmine, quantam vix in summā ūbertāte agrōrum dīturna pāx efficere potuisset.","reading":"DĒ IMPERĀTŌRE DĒLIGENDŌ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":54,"roman":"LIV","title":"Pompey the Great","slug":"pompeius-magnus"}]},{"id":"villa","latin":"vīlla","headword":"vīlla","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"country house; villa; estate","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce vīlla et hortus Iūliī.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"},{"latin":"Vīlla Iūliī est prope Tusculum.","reading":"IŪLIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":6,"roman":"VI","title":"The Latin Road","slug":"via-latina"}]},{"id":"vincire","latin":"vincīre","headword":"vincīre","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to chain; tie up","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iānitor intrā iānuam sedet cum cane, quī prope tam ferōx est quam lupus; itaque necesse est eum catēnā vincīre.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"vincit","latin":"vincit","headword":"vincit","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"conquers; defeats","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":21,"roman":"XXI","title":"The Pupils’ Fight","slug":"pugna-discipulorum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"vinco","latin":"vincō","headword":"vincō","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to conquer; defeat","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"vinculum","latin":"vinculum, -ī","headword":"vinculum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bond; chain","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ecce virgō Cassandra crīnibus passīs ā templō Minervae — ubi Aiax, Oīleī fīlius, eī vim attulerat — trahēbātur, frūstrā oculōs ardentēs ad caelum ērigēns; nam tenerās manūs vincula tenēbant.","reading":"MORS PRIAMĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":37,"roman":"XXXVII","title":"Troy Captured","slug":"troia-capta"}]},{"id":"vinea","latin":"vīnea","headword":"vīnea","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"vineyard","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Agrī in quibus vītēs crēscunt vīneae dīcuntur.","reading":"VĪNEAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}]},{"id":"vinum","latin":"vīnum","headword":"vīnum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ex ūvīs mātūrīs vīnum efficitur.","reading":"VĪNEAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"},{"latin":"Magnum bonum est vīnum.' Cornēlius: 'Nēmō negat vīnum aquā iūcundius esse, tamen aquam bibere mālō quam sitim patī.","reading":"ADVENTVS HOSPITVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":30,"roman":"XXX","title":"The Dinner Party","slug":"convivium"}]},{"id":"vir","latin":"vir","headword":"vir","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"man; husband","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlius vir Rōmānus est.","reading":"FAMILIA RŌMĀNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":2,"roman":"II","title":"The Roman Family","slug":"familia-romana"},{"latin":"Iūlius est vir Aemiliae, fēminae pulchrae.","reading":"VĪLLA ET HORTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":5,"roman":"V","title":"The Villa and the Garden","slug":"villa-et-hortus"}]},{"id":"virga","latin":"virga","headword":"virga","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"rod; cane","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus magistrum metuit, Diodōrus enim magister sevērus est, quī discipulōs suōs virga verberat; eō modo magister sevērus discipulōs improbōs pūnīre solet.","reading":"IN LŪDVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"},{"latin":"Magister īrātus virgam tollēns: 'Tacēte, puerī!' inquit, 'Nōnne virgam meam verēminī?' Mārcus: 'Nōs nec tē nec virgam tuam verēmur!'","reading":"MARCVS REPREHENDITVR","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":17,"roman":"XVII","title":"Difficult Numbers","slug":"numeri-difficiles"}]},{"id":"virginitas","latin":"virginitās, -ātis","headword":"virginitās","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"virginity","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Addit scelerī scelus: stirpem frātris virīlem interimit, frātris fīliae Reae Silviae, cum virginem Vestālem eam lēgisset, perpetuā virginitāte spem partūs adimit.","reading":"RŌMULUS ET REMUS NĀTĪ","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]},{"id":"virgo","latin":"virgō","headword":"virgō","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"maiden; virgin","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Aemilia mātrōna nōn erat, sed virgō septendecim annōrum, quae Rōmae apud parentēs suōs habitābat.","reading":"ANTE DECEM ANNŌS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":19,"roman":"XIX","title":"Husband and Wife","slug":"maritus-et-uxor"},{"latin":"Ariadna igitur in lītus dēscendit atque hūc et illūc currēns cum lacrimīs capillum et vestem scindēbat, ut eae quae maerent agere solent — ita maerēbat virgō quae ā virō, quem ante omnēs amābat, sōla erat inter ferās īnsulae sīcut agnus timidus inter lupōs.'","reading":"THĒSEVS ET ARIADNA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":25,"roman":"XXV","title":"Theseus and the Minotaur","slug":"theseus-et-minotaurus"}]},{"id":"virtus","latin":"virtūs, -ūtis","headword":"virtūs","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"courage; excellence","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":48,"roman":"XLVIII","title":"The Second Punic War","slug":"bellum-punicum-secundum"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"viscera","latin":"viscera","headword":"viscera","letter":"v","pos":"noun (n. pl.)","posGroup":"noun","english":"internal organs","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Cor, pulmōnēs, iecur, venter sunt vīscera hūmāna.","reading":"CORPVS HŪMĀNVM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"vitis","latin":"vītis","headword":"vītis","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"vine","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":27,"roman":"XXVII","title":"Country Matters","slug":"res-rusticae"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"vivere","latin":"vīvere","headword":"vīvere","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to live","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ego Rōmae vīvere mālō quam in Graeciā.\"","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"vivit","latin":"vīvit","headword":"vīvit","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"lives; is alive","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Homō vīvit, dum spīrat.","reading":"DEĪ ET HOMINĒS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Medicus: \"Puer spīrat et cor eius palpitat.\" Aemilia gaudet quod fīlius vīvit.","reading":"QVĪNTVS AEGRŌTVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":11,"roman":"XI","title":"The Human Body","slug":"corpus-humanum"}]},{"id":"vocabulum","latin":"vocābulum","headword":"vocābulum","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"word","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Fluvius et oppidum vocābula Latīna sunt.","reading":"LITTERAE ET NVMERĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":1,"roman":"I","title":"The Roman Empire","slug":"imperium-romanum"},{"latin":"Litterae sunt aut vōcālēs aut cōnsonantēs: vōcālēs sunt Ā, Ē, I, Ō, V, Y; cēterae sunt cōnsonantēs. (Etiam I et V cōnsonantēs sunt in vocābulīs IAM, VEL, vōs, QVAM, cet.)","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"vocalis","latin":"vōcālis","headword":"vōcālis","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"vowel","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quaeque syllaba vōcālem habet, ergō numerus syllabārum et vōcālium īdem est.","reading":"LITTERAE LATĪNAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":18,"roman":"XVIII","title":"Latin Letters","slug":"litterae-latinae"}]},{"id":"vocat","latin":"vocat","headword":"vocat","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"calls","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlia Aemiliam vocat: 'Māter!","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":3,"roman":"III","title":"The Naughty Boy","slug":"puer-improbus"},{"latin":"Mēdus Dāvum vocat: 'Dāve!' sed Dāvus Mēdum nōn audit neque venit.","reading":"SCAENA PRĪMA","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":4,"roman":"IV","title":"Master and Slaves","slug":"dominus-et-servi"}]},{"id":"vocativus","latin":"vocātīvus","headword":"vocātīvus","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"vocative","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Magister: 'Cāsus nōminum quot sunt?' Discipulus: 'Sex.' Magister: 'Quī?' Discipulus: 'Nōminātīvus, genetīvus, dativus, accūsātīvus, vocātīvus, ablātīvus.","reading":"PARTĒS ŌRĀTIŌNIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":35,"roman":"XXXV","title":"The Art of Grammar","slug":"ars-grammatica"}]},{"id":"volat","latin":"volat","headword":"volat","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"flies","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Avis quae volat ālās movet.","reading":"BĒSTIAE","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Intuēre illam aquilam quae in magnum orbem circum carcerem nostrum volat!","reading":"NĀRRĀTIŌ INCIPIT","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":26,"roman":"XXVI","title":"Daedalus and Icarus","slug":"daedalus-et-icarus"}]},{"id":"volucris","latin":"volucris, -is","headword":"volucris","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"bird","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Trēs diēs totidemque noctēs nāvēs caecae errābant, quoad quārtō diē in lītora Strophadum dēlātae sunt. (Strophades dīcuntur duae parvae īnsulae in marī Ioniō sitae.) Inde pulsī ab Harpyīs, mōnstrīs foedissimīs quibus corpora volucrum, vultūs virginum sunt, ad septentriōnēs cursum tenuērunt.","reading":"ANDROMACHĒ ET HELĒNVS","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":38,"roman":"XXXVIII","title":"Pious Aeneas","slug":"pius-aeneas"}]},{"id":"voluptas","latin":"voluptās, -ātis","headword":"voluptās","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"pleasure","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Lūdicrum deinde ita raptim perāctum est ut nūllīus nec animī nec oculī spectāculō intentī essent — adeō ūnum gaudium praeoccupāverat omnium aliārum sēnsum voluptātum.","reading":"ISTHMIA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":50,"roman":"L","title":"Greece Liberated","slug":"graecia-liberata"}]},{"id":"vorago","latin":"vorāgō","headword":"vorāgō","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"whirlpool","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Brevī nāvigābimus per fretum Siculum, ubi ab utrāque parte magnum perīculum impendet nautīs: ab ōrā Italiae saxa perīculōsa, quibus Scyllā nōmen est, ab ōrā Siciliae vorāgō terribilis quae Charybdis vocātur.","reading":"PERĪCVLA MARIS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":28,"roman":"XXVIII","title":"Dangers of the Sea","slug":"pericula-maris"}]},{"id":"vos","latin":"vōs","headword":"vōs","letter":"v","pos":"pronoun","posGroup":"pronoun","english":"you (pl.)","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Mārcus (ad Sextum et Titum): 'Vōs iānuam nōn pulsātis cum ad lūdum venītis, nec magistrum salūtātis cum eum vidētis.","reading":"MARCVS IMPROBVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":15,"roman":"XV","title":"The Teacher and the Pupils","slug":"magister-et-discipuli"}]},{"id":"vox","latin":"vōx","headword":"vōx","letter":"v","pos":"noun f.","posGroup":"noun","english":"voice","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Quīntus: 'Audī: Iūlia vōcem pulchram habet.' Mārcus: 'Vōx eius nōn pulchra est!'","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"},{"latin":"Vōx tua difficilis est audītū, quod forēs intersunt.\" Tabellārius: \"Mihi nōmen est Tlēpolemus, sīcut iam dictum est.","reading":"TABELLĀRIVS AD IĀNVAM","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"vulcanus","latin":"Vulcānus","headword":"Vulcānus","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"Vulcan; god of smiths","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Deus fabrōrum est Vulcānus.","reading":"IĀNVA ET ŌSTIĀRIVS","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":22,"roman":"XXII","title":"Beware of the Dog","slug":"cave-canem"}]},{"id":"vulgus","latin":"vulgus, -ī","headword":"vulgus","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"the crowd; common people","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":43,"roman":"XLIII","title":"Rome and Alba","slug":"roma-et-alba"}],"examples":[]},{"id":"vulnero","latin":"vulnerō","headword":"vulnerō","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"to wound","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ipse sagitta in bracchiō laevō vulnerātus sum, sed vulnus meum leve est, multī graviōra vulnera accēpērunt.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"vulnus","latin":"vulnus","headword":"vulnus","letter":"v","pos":"noun n.","posGroup":"noun","english":"wound","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Ipse sagitta in bracchiō laevō vulnerātus sum, sed vulnus meum leve est, multī graviōra vulnera accēpērunt.","reading":"EPISTVLA AEMILIĪ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":33,"roman":"XXXIII","title":"The Roman Army","slug":"exercitus-romanus"}]},{"id":"vult","latin":"vult","headword":"vult","letter":"v","pos":"verb","posGroup":"verb","english":"wants; wishes","sources":[{"book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Iūlia pilam tenet et cum puerīs pilā lūdere vult, neque iī cum puellā lūdere volunt; puerī enim nīdōs quaerunt in arboribus.","reading":"IN HORTŌ","book":"Familia Romana","bookSlug":"familia-romana","number":10,"roman":"X","title":"Beasts and Men","slug":"bestiae-et-homines"}]},{"id":"vultur","latin":"vultur, -uris","headword":"vultur","letter":"v","pos":"noun m.","posGroup":"noun","english":"vulture","sources":[{"book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}],"examples":[{"latin":"Priorī Remō auspicium vēnisse dīcitur: sex vulturēs; iamque nūntiātō auspiciō, duplex numerus Rōmulō sē ostendit.","reading":"RŌMA CONDITA","book":"Roma Aeterna","bookSlug":"roma-aeterna","number":41,"roman":"XLI","title":"Origins","slug":"origines"}]}]

